ally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287441#post1287441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did Altered Carbon style body/gender swapping in fiction become a sensitive issue while I whiled away the eons in my sarcophagus-sanctum? I didn\u2019t even know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure, I had no idea this was a problem at all. We should probably stop derailing this lets read thread though, unless Isator doesn\u2019t mind. We can put it into its own thread otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T00:19:13-08:00","id":1287445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287443#post1287443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not sure, I had no idea this was a problem at all. We should probably stop derailing this lets read thread though, unless Isator doesn\u2019t mind. We can put it into its own thread otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, and apologies for the derailment.<br /> <br /> Prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T00:37:13-08:00","id":1287448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287441#post1287441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did Altered Carbon style body/gender swapping in fiction become a sensitive issue while I whiled away the eons in my sarcophagus-sanctum? I didn\u2019t even know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The complaint about Altered Carbon was whitewashing rather than anything about trans issues; a Japanese character is played by a tall, blonde, white guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T02:28:52-08:00","id":1287461,"title":"","content":"I mean, I would expect Lunars to be protected from dysphoria in general, when shapeshifting. <br /> <br /> Like, [spoiler] probably feels more comfortable in female forms now than he ever did when he was mortal. He's got his true form, it's awesome. But he's a lunar and there's no need to wear it all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T02:42:03-08:00","id":1287463,"title":"","content":"I'm actually more interested in the psychological effects of turning into animals than other humans, which are a lot more different from the Lunars' base form than different human forms are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T03:00:04-08:00","id":1287468,"title":"","content":"I am going to put a pin in this subject, and when the book is fully released and I have finished it, return to it with a dedicated thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287403#post1287403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From how you expressed it, it sounded like the solars still had their mates, but also were bonded with all the Lunars to a varying extent which sounds fairly poly to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nono, what I meant, and what the book basically said, is that the war having created a coherent sense of a Lunar Society, which then proceeded to collectively reach terms with the Solar Exalted, is what provided the stabilizing effect that facilitated their common transformation, even for the ones who did not personally engage in a (symbolic) marriage. That it was a cultural affect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T03:08:10-08:00","id":1287470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a mandatory school subject and required for a number of job types (almost everything government related), and it's not taught well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much why most (not all) of my Welsh friends dislike Welsh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say that it's not helped by being very different from English, but they don't have this problem on the continent, do they? It's just a bad curriculum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Irish is more different from English than Germanic or Latin languages. It's still Indo-European, but it's probably much harder to learn for an English speaker than German, Dutch, French, etc (Dutch and Danish are the easiest for English speakers).<br /> <br /> Also, while some countries in Europe don't teach English well (some do), the students are often motivated by external factors; pop stars they like, TV shows, computer games. I doubt many Irish students are really keen on understanding an Irish computer game.<br /> <br /> Though I can well believe it's taught badly. Foreign languages often are in secondary schools (though I may be biased; we ESL teachers are quite snooty towards the way foreign languages are taught in British schools, and I imagine Irish is done the same way).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it\u2019s helpful to introduce the Silver Pact as a middle way between complex organisations and going it alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that makes the most sense as a presentation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, start off with a bit of history, a bit of background for why the Silver Pact is the way it is, coloured with some namedrops for ancient wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the history parts were very good; both in terms of namedrops, style, the process of history (2nd ed just went Primordial War, High First Age, Contagion, now, with little in between), and having famous characters who are now dead (2nd ed had Ingosh, but that's it). And most of those historical characters were quite interesting (though I'd like to have known their totem animals).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of jargon is welcome for cases where a lack of good terminology would feel a bit stale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually didn't like the jargon. I feel it's something players will continually forget or not use. <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the last vestiges of monogamy in the Exalted universe, given that the Realm has a lot of polyamorous and frequently bisexual relationships</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, I don't think I've ever actually seen any polyamorous relationships in the Dragonblood stuff. I don't think &quot;living in an arranged marriage but having a lover&quot; really counts as polyamarous.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't really see what being bisexual has with not being monogamous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though in retrospect it seems weird that Solars and Lunars would have a pair-bond thing going on, given that the Unconquered Sun and Luna had, at various points, Gaia, Merela, one of the Maidens (I think), and some others that I might have forgotten as a part of their relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unconquered Sun and Luna were never even together really.<br /> The UCS had all kinds of (female) lovers; handmaidens, goddesses, Merelea, the Maidens. Not really Luna.<br /> Luna was with Gaia.<br /> <br /> Basically, I don't think the Solar-Lunar bond is supposed to evoke a romantic relationship between Luna and the UCS.<br /> <br /> I'd also point out that the very first reference to the Solar Bond is Gilgamesh and Enkidu, not something romantic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll need to revise the initial sidebar appearance of Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi for clarity. The intent is that while they Exalted in the First Age, they weren't yet famous luminaries and heroes when the Usurpation took place, so they were overshadowed by other First Age Lunars in the early days of the Silver Pact. But with the loss of more well-known Lunar champions, Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi had an opportunity to step up to leadership roles in the Pact</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading their later descriptions, and coming back to the early descriptions, that did make sense to me (and it makes a lot of sense), but I misunderstood when I first read about them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T04:43:17-08:00","id":1287478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287470#post1287470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Irish is more different from English than Germanic or Latin languages. It's still Indo-European, but it's probably much harder to learn for an English speaker than German, Dutch, French, etc (Dutch and Danish are the easiest for English speakers).<br /> <br /> Also, while some countries in Europe don't teach English well (some do), the students are often motivated by external factors; pop stars they like, TV shows, computer games. I doubt many Irish students are really keen on understanding an Irish computer game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I meant to revise that a bit. I was kind of thinking about Basque. It's only spoken fluently by a minority of Basque people, but it's a much larger minority than speaks Irish.<br /> <br /> That and European multi-lingualism for languages besides English (even if they still have the advantage of being closely related).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T05:08:10-08:00","id":1287483,"title":"","content":"Solar bond section\u2014did the whole white-washed \u201chostage/spouse\u201d thing created to end a war not strike people as a bit discomfiting? Not so Much that it happened but the way the text kind of took it in stride and moved on. Did I wildly misread this?<br /> <br /> I started reading this hoping to see how you (or anyone) reacted to that part.<br /> <br /> Kinda hope there tends to be more variance (which is suggested by some passages, especially the ones that mentions some Lunars fighting for the bronze faction in the usurpation) in their opinion regarding the solar deliberative and the vision of bronze. It also would be kinda neat if there was at least one actually bronze faction lunar wandering around heaven with some very complicated emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T05:21:44-08:00","id":1287487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287483#post1287483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar bond section\u2014did the whole white-washed \u201chostage/spouse\u201d thing created to end a war not strike people as a bit discomfiting? Not so Much that it happened but the way the text kind of took it in stride and moved on. Did I wildly misread this?<br /> <br /> I started reading this hoping to see how you (or anyone) reacted to that part.<br /> <br /> Kinda hope there tends to be more variance (which is suggested by some passages, especially the ones that mentions some Lunars fighting for the bronze faction in the usurpation) in their opinion regarding the solar deliberative and the vision of bronze. It also would be kinda neat if there was at least one actually bronze faction lunar wandering around heaven with some very complicated emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't pick up on it as being a hostage situation, nor any sort of surrender in particular.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T05:29:18-08:00","id":1287490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287483#post1287483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar bond section\u2014did the whole white-washed \u201chostage/spouse\u201d thing created to end a war not strike people as a bit discomfiting? Not so Much that it happened but the way the text kind of took it in stride and moved on. Did I wildly misread this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dare I say this might be somewhat coloured by the flavour of it from previous editions?<br /> I certainly read it more as an EU-esque 'The wars between us have been so utterly devastating and tragic how can we make sure it doesn't happen again?' approached on roughly equitable terms than a terms of surrender deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T05:34:33-08:00","id":1287493,"title":"","content":"No, this was definitely something mutually agreed upon. The lunars were the ones who took the brunt of the changes, true -they are the ones who can feel the bond, and they are the ones most able to exploit it via charms - but this is likely because the lunar exaltation has always been the more malleable of the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T05:47:15-08:00","id":1287499,"title":"","content":"I took it as medieval political marriages to unite two warring sides. Like how William the Conqueror's son married the Princess of the English, or how Henry VII married one of the last female Yorkist claimants. Or to take a less one-sided example, stuff like Ferdinand and Isabella.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T06:23:45-08:00","id":1287513,"title":"","content":"Also, there is at least one Solar charm that protect less against Lunar mates (Stubborn Boar Defense, ), so it's not entirely a one-way thing. It should've been more though, but the question would be how to balance such a thing. I'm curious what the Lunar book has to say about that from a Lunar charm perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T07:21:17-08:00","id":1287522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287493#post1287493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, this was definitely something mutually agreed upon. The lunars were the ones who took the brunt of the changes, true -they are the ones who can feel the bond, and they are the ones most able to exploit it via charms - but this is likely because the lunar exaltation has always been the more malleable of the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not 100% opposed to how it\u2019s presented, as long as the bond isn\u2019t a leash\u2014 but it seems to be, at least, a thing that predisposes the lunar to be loyal to her solar partner. <br /> <br /> Why it\u2019s not explicitly a \u2018hostage\u2019 in a litteral sense it does seem like a concession of surrender insofar as the solars are not stated to have undergone fundamental spiritual changes as a result of the peace. But yeah, I don\u2019t have enough info to make a judgement yet\u2014 the tone just felt... light and uncomplicated for a thing which was, to my mind, neither light nor uncomplicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T07:23:12-08:00","id":1287523,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm pretty sure they covered that one by saying the bond doesn't have to be a positive intimacy.<br /> <br /> Lunars can feel however they like towards their solar. All the bond demands is that they <i>feel</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T07:30:35-08:00","id":1287524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287523#post1287523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I'm pretty sure they covered that one by saying the bond doesn't have to be a positive intimacy.<br /> <br /> Lunars can feel however they like towards their solar. All the bond demands is that they <i>feel</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I read, all it says is that the Lunars were usually supportive of their solar mates who reincarnated but not always. This is pretty vague and not something many conclusions can be drawn from. Also I\u2019m not making a hard point here\u2014 like I\u2019ve said. I definitely didn\u2019t mean to send the thread off the rails. Just was curious if anyone felt it was a bit... glossy in its tone when addressing that point. <br /> <br /> My feeling was one of slight caution not disagreement. <br /> <br /> Seems like most people didn\u2019t see it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T07:43:30-08:00","id":1287532,"title":"","content":"... I have no time for conversation. Maybe when I'm done.<br /> <br /> (Partly driven by the concern of people still talking about things past where I have read)<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> Now, continuing with chapter two. Always helpful for a group to clarify its aims.<br /> <br /> Fairly standard, gather and train the young Lunars, help one another out, seek to gather people behind you and break down the threat of the Realm. As usual, I like how it includes a reference to them employing a method based on guile and misdirection, rather than direct (even if stealthy) force. I also like how a lot of our new Lunars from the core are recurring names now; they\u2019ll supplant Leviathan yet!<br /> <br /> Ah, good, each goal is receiving elaboration. Let\u2019s see how they handle the youths.<br /> <br /> Good range of mundane and supernatural methods for becoming aware of the appearance of a new Lunar there; I\u2019m particularly imagining something like in the Lion, Witch, Wardrobe movie with the trees, having a relay system of minor spirits to transmit information along very long distances. I\u2019d say it should also be helpful to emphasize that, yes, going to find a new Lunar entails going far out of one\u2019s way, while laying out the compelling motivations to do so.<br /> <br /> I always thought it was good for the corebook to present the idea that the Pact doesn\u2019t use force, or even obligation, to bring in new recruits when they think the world at large will educate them, and I like how that\u2019s expanded on here with the idea that a young Lunar spending an indeterminate time on their own can even come back with unique and beneficial insight and methods. That being said\u2026 a couple of these paragraphs are highly repetitive in a manner distinct from a simple misprint. Leaving that aside, it\u2019s an effectively and plausibly accommodating picture of the Pact\u2019s process, and I think the most interesting thing is the point on how recruitment can often be facilitated by the simple awe of a powerful rescuing Lunar.<br /> <br /> Now, sidebar concerned with the Sidereals\u2026 ah, it\u2019s just comparing tracking methods. Sidereal aid to the Wyld Hunt provides precision, while Lunars can have shapes to give them the edge in speed (flying probably helps particularly; cover the kind of distance that an unladen swallow could).<br /> <br /> Okay, mutual aid society. Approached in a freeform manner, probably determined by circumstance and the personalities involved, with some of the incentive coming from the prestige entailed by being open to a great number and variety of tasks. The book keeps referring to council, which seems like occasions where a number of qualified Lunars gather to arbitrate a dispute (or perhaps more likely, several that have gathered to be heard at a designated time and order). As for the prospective forms of repayment, I think the notion of bringing desired animals to be hunted stands out as particularly Lunar, and the benefits are obvious. It\u2019s got to suck for the animal involved though; hunted once, trussed up and dragged who knows how far, and then hunted again to the death. Also the idea that debts can be repaid by long-term respect, that sounds like it would be a practical way to maintain decorum without overburdening too many Lunars. I like how the details of the consequences for exploiting or not honouring the system are multifaceted, including circumstances where there are people that can get away with it.<br /> <br /> Ah finally, detailing these councils. Not just for arbitration, but varied decision-making as required of local circumstances, as well as just an opportunity to get together with Lunars and share what they have in common. I imagine that, given the somewhat loose standards for the rank of shaman-ya, the arrangements of councils can have a unique plasticity. Heh, given the description of expectations for hospitality, I can also imagine that many Lunars are drawn to participate in council just for the sake of being offered access to those luxuries at somebody else\u2019s expense, especially if many Lunars are often otherwise more hard living. I\u2019d been wondering about Leviathan, so here\u2019s a first really major revision to him, a more socially active leader, harnessing the distinct wealth of Luthe to put on a show; I like the image of him leading Lunars in the shape of oceanic predators in grand hunts particularly. Somehow, he\u2019s still overshadowed by Amatha Kinslayer\u2019s councils undertaken in plain sight, attended by Lunars in disguise. If nothing else, that feels like a real horror story scenario for, say, an impromptu visiting Dynast, the sudden or gradual realisation that you\u2019ve walked into the hyena\u2019s den. A bit of storytelling advice should tide people over until a dedicated book, and it presents an interesting picture of how to interact with the process while not yet being a big player in proceedings. I particularly like the emphasis on the idea that it\u2019s not the best suited to having Persuade actions navigating varied Intimacies, and bargaining is the better option.<br /> <br /> For the interpersonal protocols\u2026 I\u2019ve had thoughts in the past about outright prohibitions against violence against other Lunars, but the framing of it here is less objectionable to me, and in the context of conflict resolution via council rulings I can see sufficiently compelling alternatives (still including duels) as to be unconcerned. The image of the process for executing particularly criminal former members of the Pact entailing hunting them down feels like something intended to insult and degrade, giving the organisation a nice bit of grit.<br /> <br /> Now, warring against the Realm. I\u2019d say it\u2019s good to focus the attention almost entirely on those who partake of the Shogunate\u2019s legacy, rather than Dragon Blooded as a whole, if only to make them feel less indiscriminately hostile. Given the contention of the subject, it\u2019s also useful to detail the various grievances that can be caused by Realm policy, even beyond the boundaries of their more direct power. I can even picture some Lunars embellishing that a little bit for some more distantly removed people, with the aid of their silver tongues.<br /> <br /> I like how the sidebar frames the matter of trying to assassinate Dragon Blooded on their home turf, both in terms of describing the obstacles and the problems that can be entailed by succeeding, while the focus is on the need to be discriminating rather than a straightforward \u201cit won\u2019t work, don\u2019t do it\u201d.<br /> <br /> Aaaand this should redress some concerns, a dedicated section to some of the successes of the Silver Pact. Ah, my initial take was that it would be a list, but a description of the standards and overall model makes more sense for this placement. Let\u2019s see\u2026 ah yes, we saw some of this before. The reference to being a threat that curtailed the territorial ambitions of the Scarlet Empress and the like. What I like from the first few paragraphs is that sense that for many of the Lunars, it\u2019s better to extend the length and range of conflicts than going for the small decisive victories, which feels like it lends another reason to be conservative with assassinations; why eliminate a major general early on when you can keep doing enough damage to make them chase you, prolonging the wasteful expense of the process over years? It puts me in mind of things I\u2019ve been reading recently about European warfare of the 17th and 18th centuries, and what they could do to national finances. I think the term \u201cwar of attrition\u201d too often conjures the image of two forces grinding away at one another until one has run out of bodies, disregarding the idea of one that keeps effectively running away from the other, until somebody can\u2019t pay for their armies anymore (or the process of doing so is ruinous to an economy or political body). It's an interesting finalisation of the long promised picture of the Silver Pact\u2019s grand strategy, even if it ends on the note of how the return of Solars throws some of its viability into doubt.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there\u2019s even more detailing for the different kinds of approach. First off, I think the sidebar effectively covers the benefits and drawbacks of asymmetrical, decentralized warfare. Yes, the description of attrition takes about the same tack as I described above, and it\u2019s helpful to be specific about what it actually means for the Realm to be infrastructure dependent. Even the point about where Dragon Blooded come from, look back at how What Fire Has Wrought described the processes and resources dedicated to gathering them, educating them, matching them to one another. If they weren\u2019t facing an enemy that could draw a significant mortality rate, would the Realm be so concerned with maximizing Exaltation rates? Perhaps not, and it\u2019s another strain on the system. And what\u2019s especially useful is to describe this all in terms of the Realm more than the Dragon Blooded; Terrestrial Exalted could also function in this manner (many outcaste bandits clearly do), but they can\u2019t exercise empire like that. If they were competing against Lunars directly in that arena, they\u2019d be at a disadvantage, and besides that there\u2019s the question of whether Dragon Blooded not operating as an empire is even something the Lunars would find as objectionable.<br /> <br /> Heh, I initially misread the line about the resources of tending to wounded soldiers meaning that the Realm is incentivized to merely abandoning them, but I can see now that the point is for Lunars to leave more wounded (who the Realm ends up with some obligation to care for) than dead (who can merely be replaced from the vast population). And then there\u2019s the point about how outright defeat may draw an overwhelming reprisal, or make them stay within their safe boundaries, or shift focus, and it\u2019s preferable to the long term strategy to keep things drawn-out indefinitely, perpetuating the vicious cycle.<br /> <br /> And finally a sidebar clarifying on a distinction between the relative professionalism of Realm legions and the likely excesses of auxiliaries that they\u2019re dependent on. The point about how Dynasts generally don\u2019t have a need to heavily engage in plunder in their own right\u2026 that effectively offsets some of my own prior ideas, as well as providing a bit of background as to why the Realm might employ a system of purchased commissions.<br /> <br /> Oh, there\u2019s more, let me just range ahead a bit\u2026 the other two approaches are less heavy, so I\u2019ll finish the stuff about Silver Pact warfare and then take a break before moving on to the group composition stuff.<br /> <br /> Ah I see, the rest was focused primarily on the logistical results of Lunar action, and here\u2019s the layout of the various things they can actually do; lend their power to commanding small bodies of troops deep into enemy territory, personal combat prowess, and shapeshifting to attack, infiltrate and foment severe paranoia, as well as their mystical powers to apply more indirect and esoteric pressure. And yeah, under circumstances like this, I can see the benefit of detailing the challenges that opponents can bring against them, right down to the more mundane but effective measures that can be employed by powerful and wealthy mortals.<br /> <br /> And finally (really this time) a sidebar for more dedicated focus to the occult side of warfare. What interests me here is something to provide some clarity to the recurring point about Lunar mystics being able to draw upon strange secrets, the forgotten workings and lost monsters that their power and placement might find and direct against the Realm.<br /> <br /> So, next is defensive withdrawal\u2026 which feels like a slightly misleading description of what sounds a lot more like fortification. In any case, there are a few implications for this, in my eyes primarily noting that there are instances where the Lunar relationship with dominions is more benevolent (for those who balk at the callousness of spending them on weakening the Realm), and applying their talents towards presiding over zones of prosperity. It puts me in mind of many disproportionately powerful small states, such as island kingdoms, little strategically and economically powerful duchies that are able to heavily fortify themselves, and city states (often located at the tips of peninsulas) that serve as major financial centres.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, I\u2019ve got a picture of that Lunar I came up with for BrilliantRain\u2019s White Elephant eventually becoming enamoured enough of that little kingdom to take up residence to adopt it as a dominion of this kind.<br /> <br /> And the last of them is their open warfare, for the Turin Turambar\u2019s among the Silver Pact. Most of it is the fairly basic needs of such a force and the point of how often it fails against the considerable advantages of the Realm, so it seems primarily beneficial as an option that many Lunars might explore in the Time of Tumult. In any case, it\u2019s right and proper to have a sidebar pointing out that conventional and asymmetrical warfare are more of a continuum than a binary, and Lunars dedicated to either approach can utilise some of the other (conversely, one can see a few examples of the Realm employing some irregulars to great effect, such as the strategies of House Tepet).<br /> <br /> Last of all is the point on what the endgame is, which is about what I expected; a few vaguely defined possibilities, held off on for the sakes of focusing on the present and preserving the unity of the movement (an understandable and perhaps unavoidable point that has nevertheless been the bane of many a revolutionary group). Even within those limits\u2026 I have my own biases about what the Pact might be capable of, or what it\u2019s preferable for them to do, so it\u2019s good to be reminded that actual characters would have a greater variety of visions for the future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T07:44:30-08:00","id":1287533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287524#post1287524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like most people didn\u2019t see it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you see any of the previews?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T08:17:40-08:00","id":1287541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287533#post1287533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you see any of the previews?</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the backer preview that I\u2019m discussing now and the ones posted to the onyx path website proper\u2014 not that I can clearly recall why?<br /> <br /> Also, I didn\u2019t mean for that to be sarcasm if it scans that way it\u2019s only because of the tonal limitations of typing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T08:39:28-08:00","id":1287545,"title":"","content":"I mean, the Solar Bond preview described the mechanical implementation of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T09:01:30-08:00","id":1287553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287545#post1287545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the Solar Bond preview described the mechanical implementation of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of respect for your thread\u2019s integrity I won\u2019t go into this overmuch. I read that yes\u2014 and I don\u2019t have a problem per say, but the genesis of the bond was the end of a violent struggle and the preview (neither of them) really goes into the ramifications of the institution of the bond or what it was intended to accomplish other than to talk about it in cursory terms. That\u2019s all I was getting at and all I was wondering if you or anyone found curious.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll spin this off into another thread after more of the preview has been released if no one else does. Sorry for the digression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T11:46:18-08:00","id":1287605,"title":"","content":"Now, see if I can\u2019t finish the chapter. Next up are the shahan-yas, the leaders and luminaries of the Pact who exert significant influence on its agendas and priorities (with a useful note on not everybody having universal recognition for their claim on the title).<br /> <br /> First up is our old hand Ma-Ha-Suchi. I want to put one point straight up front; I had formed a strong impression from the corebook that Ma-Ha-Suchi was not strictly a member of the Silver Pact in his own right, and thought there was a lot that was beneficial to that image which I became attached to but in this context, with how the preceding chapter has set the Silver Pact and the experience of a lot of its elders up, as well as some of the particulars of his own history, having him in here as basically an honoured retiree works and I\u2019m good with it. With that established, let\u2019s see the particulars.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, started off as a widely beloved champion in the later First Age, but finds his old ideals having no place in his current environment. Was the type who viewed the Lunars as the only legitimate inheritors of the Realm with the removal of the Solars and made a lot of his name fighting the Shogunate to that effect. Used the typical Silver Pact playbook with beastfolk armies, seducing Exalted generals, destroying old infrastructure and forging alliances between Lunar elder and mortal nation alike, dreaming of establishing a new Realm. Then Great Contagion happened, he becomes disenchanted with his struggle in the face of seeming powerlessness in the face of the eschaton, and the fact that even after all of that the enemy Dragon Blooded pulled back together and established a whole new Realm of their own. The final nail came from allies centred around his dear friend Raksi ultimately rejecting his vision of a new Realm, and after a severe internal struggle became completely spent and retreated to seclusion in his Nameless Lair.<br /> <br /> Ah, some things about his response to the Time of Tumult have been clarified; he\u2019s seeing it as the time of miracles, and with reinvigoration is starting to try rebuilding forces and reclaim his old contacts, in hopes of striking out at the opportune moment to establish significant power over the East and maybe try and get that Lunar Realm project back on track.<br /> <br /> What do I think\u2026 well, he\u2019s come through with a lot more of his corebook portrayal intact than he did in First Edition. Nah, in all seriousness, it\u2019s fine, I can see some compelling drama in the image of an old passion being stirred back to life (especially if playing a circle that has been within his orbit since enough time before the start of the Tumult to see the difference), and a bit more activity directed towards the future.<br /> <br /> Oh there\u2019s more\u2026 hmm, basically structuring shahan-yas in a similar manner to describing Great\u2026 Houses\u2026 anyway, what about the pact relations. Doesn\u2019t tend to meet or attend council personally, and it would take something major to make him host a council. Still has the major falling out with Raksi, to the point of shunning her and avoiding contact with anybody associated, which is generally a fun take on the old point about how they were always major Lunar elders in relatively close proximity and seemingly no connection. But not completely isolated, and I think it\u2019s very effectively humanising to give such a lofty character some specific friends and correspondences, including the artistic subjects of interest therein.<br /> <br /> Heh, something is fun in the image of him having a passing interest in a marginalized group that kind of aligns with his goals and sensibilities, while their own leader finds that attention to be threatening. And otherwise he\u2019s still got some of the creepy hermit stuff I was liking in the fact that other visitors will almost never get a direct audience with him. I like the image that I\u2019m getting of visiting the Nameless Lair, and Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s presence lingers as a tense pressure (informed by the certainty that he\u2019s somewhere on the premises) while never actually seeing or speaking to him.<br /> <br /> Hehehe: \u201cTo those in attendance of the Third Age ball, Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2026 has more important things to attend to. Therefore, I will be observing in his place\u201d<br /> <br /> Ohhh Lord, I\u2019m just remembering that the actual Great Houses were so long that I could only write two at a time (per day? I\u2019ll check back later). How long has all of this been\u2026 seven hundred words? Eh, see how long my energy and attention can last.<br /> <br /> Oh, the Shadow Fang Vanguard sidebar misled me, there\u2019s still a bunch left. Okay, keep going, keep going. The sidebar is no different than the first time I saw it in preview, so to reiterate I like the idea of a more firmly organised faction that is also a weird outlying cult that a lot of the others give a wide berth, plus the idea of a second generation on top and a First Age elder as advisor.<br /> <br /> Despite what I said about a similar skeletal structure to the Great Houses, of course a lot of the substance is very different, and a description of the mentorship styles and standards comes across as an especially distinct and valuable one. So up until recently, he\u2019s only been taking on occasional students recommended from other trusted fellows, who can then expect to learn social engineering, intrigue and warfare through command of beastfolk reavers, from a teacher that is brusque and stoic, but not outright cruel. Huh, he\u2019s kind of like a less murderous Pai Mai\u2026 yeah, that boosts this new profile up a fair bit for me. His teaching method is also informed by the desire to have Lunars that can work in the organized manner that would drive a new Realm, and in spite of his own withdrawal he still has friends, supporters and admirers throughout the pact that independently support his positions and ambitions. That idea is especially interesting, I hadn\u2019t considered something like that even back in the core (mind, I had no sense of what his overall worldview was). <br /> <br /> And his adherents\u2026 is it weird that Kathaka puts me in mind of the protagonist of The Fault in Our Stars, with that thing of being disappointed to find your hero is really a crotchety bastard? I like the juxtaposition between giving her compelling motives as regards her teacher, casting herself in a close familial role and desperate for his praise, and the opening description of her as a bully, suggesting that she\u2019s not actually very pleasant as a person. Likewise the complexity underlying his position as teacher fond of her but not altogether having faith in her, continuously seeking to test if she\u2019s actually in it for the cause rather than just attachment to him, and worried that the changing times will prove she\u2019s not up to it. Yeah, stuff like this, this is a good way to include First Age characters without the whole story warping around or buckling beneath them, I think.<br /> <br /> Who else is there\u2026 aww, that Ranotis na-Raya is rather adorable, with the retaining a close working relationship with his factor father and seeing Ma-Ha-Suchi in exceptionally Romantic terms and having a playful rapport with him, reciprocated by a teacher that, for all his taciturn stylings, sees a lot of potential that he\u2019s actively cultivating, while also trying to drive a wedge between him and his mortal family lest they cause a conflict of interest or split priorities.<br /> <br /> Anja Silverclaws, you\u2019ve got some tough acts to follow, what are you up to this time around\u2026 ahh, her focus on Thorns remains, and is harnessed in an interesting new way with her not actually being devoted to the shahan-ya or his dreams, his proximity and short-term plans just seen as useful to her own goal of liberating the city, while he\u2026 I\u2019m guessing he lets her in primarily because her drives and actions constitute a strongly motivated asset in making strategic inroads into the East (and might be less exhausting to have around than the other two wanting to get through to him), even if he rates the Mask of Winters as a lower priority than the Realm and the Solars.<br /> <br /> What I like with these write-ups, is that it\u2019s creating a picture of a complex social dynamic that is more close-knit and personally driven than the Great Houses, which I think can generate a lot of interest in wanting to play Lunars of a specific school just to associate with them and be witness to and participants of the tangle of their lives. Yeah, overall this is a very good way to do this with them, and also gives me a lot of hope for the Deathlords in the future.<br /> <br /> A few moments ago I remembered how it actually came down to only writing on one House at a time, so I\u2019ll save Raksi for a bit later. Hopefully it won\u2019t be too long, so long as there aren\u2019t eleven shahan-yas to read into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T12:21:31-08:00","id":1287627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287524#post1287524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I read, all it says is that the Lunars were usually supportive of their solar mates who reincarnated but not always. This is pretty vague and not something many conclusions can be drawn from. Also I\u2019m not making a hard point here\u2014 like I\u2019ve said. I definitely didn\u2019t mean to send the thread off the rails. Just was curious if anyone felt it was a bit... glossy in its tone when addressing that point. <br /> <br /> My feeling was one of slight caution not disagreement. <br /> <br /> Seems like most people didn\u2019t see it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, given the preview makes it clear the Lunar decides what the Bond is, this seems like a non-issue. The reason most Lunars were supportive of their mates was because their mates were worthy of support. If anything, the sheer flexibility of the Bond makes it seem like a threat hung over the Solars: &quot;You piss us off, our very souls will become a weapon to bring you to justice and cleave off your Exaltation to give to someone worth it.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you've played Tales of Berseria*, the relationship between Artorius and Velvet seems like a good example of how terrifying it is to a Solar half a soured Bond is**. Before the Scarlet Night, Velvet respects Artorius as a mentor and friend, with some implication she's tempted to replace her dead sister as his spouse. After the Scarlet Night and Artorius kills Velvet's actual brother in a ritual to save the world***, and Velvet gets thrown in a prison to snack on monsters for three years, she comes out a force of absolutely merciless nature who's become so angry she loops right back around to coolly pragmatic and rational about systematically destroying everything Artorius worked for and treasures.<br /> <br /> * I'd say Berserk, but Artorius is way more Solar than Griffith in power, goals, and personality. Because fuck Griffith.<br /> ** On the off chance Eleanor isn't the other half of this Bond, which progesses in the exact opposite direction of souring.<br /> *** For certain values of &quot;saving&quot; and &quot;world&quot;, of course. There's a reason Velvet is the player character and the story looks askance at Hard Men Making Hard Decisions While Hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T12:26:16-08:00","id":1287629,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, when I saw a sidebar titled &quot;Storytelling councils&quot;, I presumed that it would describe councils dedicated to recounting the history of the Silver Pact and the legends of its accomplished members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T13:29:23-08:00","id":1287652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287627#post1287627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, given the preview makes it clear the Lunar decides what the Bond is, this seems like a non-issue. The reason most Lunars were supportive of their mates was because their mates were worthy of support. If anything, the sheer flexibility of the Bond makes it seem like a threat hung over the Solars: &quot;You piss us off, our very souls will become a weapon to bring you to justice and cleave off your Exaltation to give to someone worth it.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you've played Tales of Berseria*, the relationship between Artorius and Velvet seems like a good example of how terrifying it is to a Solar half a soured Bond is**. Before the Scarlet Night, Velvet respects Artorius as a mentor and friend, with some implication she's tempted to replace her dead sister as his spouse. After the Scarlet Night and Artorius kills Velvet's actual brother in a ritual to save the world***, and Velvet gets thrown in a prison to snack on monsters for three years, she comes out a force of absolutely merciless nature who's become so angry she loops right back around to coolly pragmatic and rational about systematically destroying everything Artorius worked for and treasures.<br /> <br /> * I'd say Berserk, but Artorius is way more Solar than Griffith in power, goals, and personality. Because fuck Griffith.<br /> ** On the off chance Eleanor isn't the other half of this Bond, which progesses in the exact opposite direction of souring.<br /> *** For certain values of &quot;saving&quot; and &quot;world&quot;, of course. There's a reason Velvet is the player character and the story looks askance at Hard Men Making Hard Decisions While Hard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Didn't think about it being a threat, that's good.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you are good to us, we will be the greatest ally you can ever hope to have, but if you stray we will house an arcane hatred that cannot be extinguished.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T14:54:48-08:00","id":1287685,"title":"","content":"Okay, one more, and then probably finish tomorrow. What of Raksi?<br /> <br /> Right off the bat, there\u2019s the focus on her as formidable in a courtly sense in addition to being a fearsome monster queen; the idea that she resides in decadent splendour has always been present, but I often felt as though the focus was minimal, even perfunctory, especially in Second Edition, contrasted here where it\u2019s made a strong part of her internal dichotomy. The idea that she cultivates uncertainty about herself already makes her more interesting than I found her in the past. Really, she has nowhere to go but up; for a character that books kept trying to present as scary and impressive, I don\u2019t think I ever really saw a genuine instance where she wasn\u2019t treated like a punchline.<br /> <br /> Moving on\u2026 I don\u2019t know why I\u2019m struggling to think of something to say about the paragraph describing how there are some people close enough to know that the revelry and cruelty is disingenuous. What\u2019s easier is the point about how her reign over her worshippers is so prosperous with her applications of sorcery that even her strong opponents in the Silver Pact can\u2019t deny it. People have often wanted such things from a Lunar ruler, I wonder how many might have thought it would wind up with Raksi. I wonder if the use of such a modern sounding term as \u201cTotal Control Zone\u201d is meant to evoke a sense that she\u2019s running things in accordance with a more advanced First Age model.<br /> <br /> Now this is interesting, the idea that in the First Age she applied her talents to esoterica that wasn\u2019t really a source of acclaim, but then provided the basis for her providing all kinds of benefits to the cause of the Silver Pact, such as reshaping the Castes and unleashing powerful sorcerous horrors upon the Realm. I also think it\u2019s worthwhile to have this point that the image she projects being disingenuous doesn\u2019t mean that it\u2019s something she\u2019s conflicted over; narratively, it\u2019s okay for her to still come down as a monster.<br /> <br /> Still, I do like the fact that she\u2019s still kind of isolated from the Pact as a whole. She\u2019s a bit more involved than the picture that I had contrived for myself, but I still kind of think that her ultimate motive remains the same; that she wants to have her own slice of the world to herself to revel and engage in her studies, she just pursues that by means of promoting it as the ideal for the whole Pact.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s diversifying her method of greeting other Lunars, even when they\u2019re the rivals that she wants to put off balance with atrocities. Sure, the description of her doing such things just to get a social edge is likely to still outrage people, but at least it\u2019s up front about it here so nobody mistakes her meaning. I also like how even when she\u2019s dispensing with the big Queen of Fangs theatrics in the presence of allies, she puts on grand sorcerous displays ala Zorayas. I\u2019ve got this odd sense that, after having been overlooked in the First Age, she has a certain need to be seen. And then there\u2019s her opposite attitude to Ma-Ha-Suchi, going out of her way to mess with him if she can.<br /> <br /> Obviously her mentorship focused on various occult and sorcerous subjects, so the most important part is going into the attitude around it, including how a student might win their way into her good graces and past all of the monster queen shenanigans. Like Ma-Ha-Suchi, I think it\u2019s good to humanise her by drawing attention to the idea that she has some genuine close friends. It\u2019s not said here, but I would find it consistent with the rest that her tutelage can also include developing a sense of self-reliance and a desire for independent authority.<br /> <br /> Huh, Raksi\u2019s write-up seems to be just plain shorter than Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s. Either that or she\u2019s a more straightforward character in general, even if she\u2019s more complex than in the past. I\u2019m not complaining, it\u2019s just a curious reversion.<br /> <br /> Anyway, what of her adherents. She\u2019s got a major enforcer who still hasn\u2019t earned his way to being invited past her fa\u00e7ade in Dark Eyes, an emissary to carry proclamations to her subjects and get people to try and transform themselves into apefolk. I\u2019m thinking that if Raksi is more politically and administratively active, a lot of her relationships with adherents come from that angle rather than the greater intimacy between Ma-Ha-Suchi and his few students. Hence the interesting element of him having inadvertently become a separate object of veneration to a subset of her subjects, his leveraging that to shape them towards one of his ideals, as well as his own anxiety based on not fully understanding his teacher.<br /> <br /> The story of Weyna Who-Sees-Much makes me think that another useful element of the prohibiton against excessive violence against one another might help a younger Lunar feel secure when calling at a more powerful one in the heart of their domain. Heh, oh dear, it didn\u2019t entirely work out for her, even if the infant child is probably grateful for the chance to not only live, but have an Exalted parent obligated to do the best for her.<br /> <br /> Ahh, here\u2019s something interesting that I think has hardly, if ever, been seen before; a Lunar that was a beastperson before Exalting, as well as being an adherent more from complementary agenda than direct stewardship. It\u2019s an interesting confluence that this character, whose altruism would probably be laudable to a lot of readers, draws real and meaningful inspiration from one of the worst monsters in the setting.<br /> <br /> So, overall, I think Raksi does a good job, both in refining her prior concepts and serving as a distinct contrast in style to her former best friend.<br /> <br /> Calling it a night for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:47:50-08:00","id":1287716,"title":"","content":"Ma-Ha-Suchi's new version is actually interesting. I know I should have, but I kinda didn't expect that.<br /> <br /> His old portrayal, while it certainly has it's place, was so over-the-top cartoonish that I never managed to get any use out of him, that wasn't &quot;generic lunar warlord, but worse and ancient&quot;.<br /> Everything that I found even remotely interesting (even if only because of how shocking all of it came together) about old Ma-Ha-Suchi is easy to transfer to any generic new NPC. I think nothing at all was lost and a lot was gained with this awesome version.<br /> <br /> I haven't read Raksi myself yet, but I really hope I get the same thing out of her. I had her as a villain in two games, but people just couldn't care about anything about her once the baby-eating was known about her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:06:46-08:00","id":1287726,"title":"","content":"I am definitely loving this editions version of Raksi better then the last since she actually has some depth now (even if she is still morally deplorable since serving babies on a platter to troll your enemies is still serving a baby on a freaking platter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:21:01-08:00","id":1287736,"title":"","content":"Huh. So I was thinking that 3e Raksi was still pretty bad and that going from &quot;she's just insane&quot; to &quot;it's a social experiment bro&quot; wasn't a big improvement. Then I went back and actually re-read her 2e description and <i>wow</i> it's horrifying how much of an improvement 3e is over 2e.<br /> <br /> Mind you, she's still not much better than Eric Cartman in my eyes with her deeds to get a 'social edge' or 'unbalance' people. At least you can interact with her kinda now rather than just... have her be there? But the rhetorical question still remains, why would you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:30:23-08:00","id":1287771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287736#post1287736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. So I was thinking that 3e Raksi was still pretty bad and that going from &quot;she's just insane&quot; to &quot;it's a social experiment bro&quot; wasn't a big improvement. Then I went back and actually re-read her 2e description and <i>wow</i> it's horrifying how much of an improvement 3e is over 2e.<br /> <br /> Mind you, she's still not much better than Eric Cartman in my eyes with her deeds to get a 'social edge' or 'unbalance' people. At least you can interact with her kinda now rather than just... have her be there? But the rhetorical question still remains, why would you?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean aside from the part where failure to excercise proper decorum and visit when you go through her territory leads to someone who acts like <i> that</i> just to screw with people deciding to respond to someone being rude and insulting her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:30:25-08:00","id":1287772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287736#post1287736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. So I was thinking that 3e Raksi was still pretty bad and that going from &quot;she's just insane&quot; to &quot;it's a social experiment bro&quot; wasn't a big improvement. Then I went back and actually re-read her 2e description and <i>wow</i> it's horrifying how much of an improvement 3e is over 2e.<br /> <br /> Mind you, she's still not much better than Eric Cartman in my eyes with her deeds to get a 'social edge' or 'unbalance' people. At least you can interact with her kinda now rather than just... have her be there? But the rhetorical question still remains, why would you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because she is arguably the best teacher of sorcery an aspiring lunar sorcerer can get for starters. Also good for a solar sorcerer to if they could somehow manage to convince her to take them on (she doesn't seem to be mad she can't get adamant circle sorcerery and she isn't batshit insane so it would be easier then in 2E, at least).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:43:50-08:00","id":1287777,"title":"","content":"Raksi is absolutely a terrible person, but she's also a better character for having coherent and meaningful motivations, ideology and engaging in methods of pursuing them, as well as a political presence that can range beyond her. She can have a greater variety of impacts in games that way.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't look on serving babies as an affectation to offend as a better motive, or even a deeper one, but as a more Lunar operation (in the sense of that manner and tone of manipulation).<br /> <br /> That being said, part of my point before is that the framing allows the babies to be one choice among many, adjusted to suit exactly how far one wants her to go.<br /> <br /> Two other considerations: <br /> <br /> If she primarily does it to unwanted guests, they don't necessarily actually eat the baby.<br /> <br /> If the net result is that fewer of those meet her, then fewer such outrages might occur.<br /> <br /> These can at least be rationalisations employed by Lunars who get the red carpet rolled out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T18:40:50-08:00","id":1287792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287777#post1287777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two other considerations:<br /> <br /> If she primarily does it to unwanted guests, they don't necessarily actually eat the baby.<br /> <br /> If the net result is that fewer of those meet her, then fewer such outrages might occur.<br /> <br /> These can at least be rationalisations employed by Lunars who get the red carpet rolled out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I had similar thoughts. Weyna's blurb about how she spoke out and was rewarded with Raksi's respect makes me think Raksi doesn't really give a damn about the baby being eaten, just that it draws out a reaction from someone. Like, I can still totally see her actually eating a baby, actually carrying out that threat, but not really for its own sake, not something she'd do when nobody's watching - that still makes her a crazy monster, but a more palatable one than previous depictions.<br /> <br /> Also, I find it fucking hilarious how she literally went 'Ok, it's your baby now, I'm the godmother.' Your Baby Now Prana, the secret Lunar followup to My City Now Declaration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24165-parabola","name":"Parabola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T19:02:00-08:00","id":1287798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287736#post1287736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the rhetorical question still remains, why would you?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why we have a bunch of adherents as examples.<br /> <br /> The question of why would people in opposition to her approach her is answered through descriptions of her achievements and capabilities, and the fact that Lunars passing through the Total Control Zone are obligated to do so.<br /> <br /> It <i>might</i> be answered again if Lunars are obligated to repay favours that they didn't ask for, that unambiguously helped them. <br /> <br /> Oh, also, as a prestigious shahan-ya with a big fancy city, Raksi can probably host some prominent councils. You can not go, but then you're not adding your voice to questions concerning all of the local Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T19:30:56-08:00","id":1287804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287777#post1287777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi is absolutely a terrible person, but she's also a better character for having coherent and meaningful motivations, ideology and engaging in methods of pursuing them, as well as a political presence that can range beyond her. She can have a greater variety of impacts in games that way.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't look on serving babies as an affectation to offend as a better motive, or even a deeper one, but as a more Lunar operation (in the sense of that manner and tone of manipulation).<br /> <br /> That being said, part of my point before is that the framing allows the babies to be one choice among many, adjusted to suit exactly how far one wants her to go.<br /> <br /> Two other considerations:<br /> <br /> If she primarily does it to unwanted guests, they don't necessarily actually eat the baby.<br /> <br /> If the net result is that fewer of those meet her, then fewer such outrages might occur.<br /> <br /> These can at least be rationalisations employed by Lunars who get the red carpet rolled out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quite. Raksi is no longer an example of Wyld corruption that has mysteriously been allowed to survive. She just ran out of fucks to give around the Shogunate and decided that if she needed to be a monster, by Luna she's going to be a goddamned <i>legend.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T20:01:57-08:00","id":1287821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287736#post1287736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. So I was thinking that 3e Raksi was still pretty bad and that going from &quot;she's just insane&quot; to &quot;it's a social experiment bro&quot; wasn't a big improvement. Then I went back and actually re-read her 2e description and <i>wow</i> it's horrifying how much of an improvement 3e is over 2e.<br /> <br /> Mind you, she's still not much better than Eric Cartman in my eyes with her deeds to get a 'social edge' or 'unbalance' people. At least you can interact with her kinda now rather than just... have her be there? But the rhetorical question still remains, why would you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Raksi from 1e would have been an improvement over 2e. It's one of those bars that 2e managed to lower instead of tiptoeing over or swerving around. As for comparisons to Eric Cartman, a big part of what makes him objectionable is utilizing pre-existing systemic racism and other forms of structural bigotry to beat other characters down, so I would measure that as a very far comparison, what with it being hard to imagine those fitting into Exalted. A bit even farther so for a Lunar out some ways from an empire that controls most practical perceptions of her to the outside world, to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T20:59:49-08:00","id":1287833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287771#post1287771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean aside from the part where failure to excercise proper decorum and visit when you go through her territory leads to someone who acts like <i> that</i> just to screw with people deciding to respond to someone being rude and insulting her?</div> </div> </div> </div>As opposed to being favored by her and getting the opportunity to take care of the live infant she tried to feed to someone? Or getting front row seats to the torture of prisoners in front of guests?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287821#post1287821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Raksi from 1e would have been an improvement over 2e. It's one of those bars that 2e managed to lower instead of tiptoeing over or swerving around. As for comparisons to Eric Cartman, a big part of what makes him objectionable is utilizing pre-existing systemic racism and other forms of structural bigotry to beat other characters down, so I would measure that as a very far comparison, what with it being hard to imagine those fitting into Exalted. A bit even farther so for a Lunar out some ways from an empire that controls most practical perceptions of her to the outside world, to boot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more thinking of the whole 'cooked some guy's parents and fed them to him because of a slight against him' bit when I was referencing Cartman, which feels in line with what Raksi is doing. What I was trying to get at with the Cartman comparison was that she's someone with whom you want to interact with as little as possible. She's probably just as interested in hurting you as helping you (see: the added responsibilities for someone who has earned her 'respect').<br /> <br /> Yes, I know there are reasons that you would have to interact with her. It's why I said the question was rhetorical - the only reason you interact with her is because you don't have another choice. And I don't mean 'no other choice' in a compelling 'work-with-an-enemy-for-a-common-good' way. She's not a person playing the part of a monster, she's a monster who tries to convince you that she's just 'acting' while actually doing horrific things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","user":"Cactuar","date":". 02-14-2019, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T21:43:05-08:00","id":1287843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287833#post1287833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was more thinking of the whole 'cooked some guy's parents and fed them to him because of a slight against him' bit when I was referencing Cartman, which feels in line with what Raksi is doing. What I was trying to get at with the Cartman comparison was that she's someone with whom you want to interact with as little as possible. She's probably just as interested in hurting you as helping you (see: the added responsibilities for someone who has earned her 'respect').</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right. It's been so long since I watched it, and his character slid so much toward just being outright racist as time went on that I forgot about that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, I know there are reasons that you would have to interact with her. It's why I said the question was rhetorical - the only reason you interact with her is because you don't have another choice. And I don't mean 'no other choice' in a compelling 'work-with-an-enemy-for-a-common-good' way. She's not a person playing the part of a monster, she's a monster who tries to convince you that she's just 'acting' while actually doing horrific things. </div> </div> </div>And there's probably another layer where she's moving something out of your line of sight at least part of the time, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T22:14:43-08:00","id":1287853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287833#post1287833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As opposed to being favored by her and getting the opportunity to take care of the live infant she tried to feed to someone? Or getting front row seats to the torture of prisoners in front of guests?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And considers herself the godparent of said infant.Face it you insult your boss by being insobordinate in front of an enemy/rival on the grounds of not liking what's being served as dinner tends to not go over well. Raksi giving Weyna the kid is a pretty good outcome considering when she decided to demonstrate possession of a bloody spine. Not to mention that kid could surprisingly do worse than having the ancient sorcerer queen/ godmonster as your god-parent.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of her behavior, at least part of her edge is being a Gen 1 Lunar allienating her is probably something most Lunars are heavily advised against on the grounds that she has been around a long time, has a lot of power and knowledge, and probably more than a few figure if she doesn't hate you then she might be willing to ease up on the horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 02-14-2019, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T02:50:57-08:00","id":1287895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parabola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287792#post1287792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I had similar thoughts. Weyna's blurb about how she spoke out and was rewarded with Raksi's respect makes me think Raksi doesn't really give a damn about the baby being eaten, just that it draws out a reaction from someone. Like, I can still totally see her actually eating a baby, actually carrying out that threat, but not really for its own sake, not something she'd do when nobody's watching - that still makes her a crazy monster, but a more palatable one than previous depictions.<br /> <br /> Also, I find it fucking hilarious how she literally went 'Ok, it's your baby now, I'm the godmother.' Your Baby Now Prana, the secret Lunar followup to My City Now Declaration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kinda thing a being that eats human infants as a type of weird job interview is far more terrible than one that does it for sustenance or even enjoyment. Think about the value judgment that\u2019s occurring in the first place.<br /> <br /> Not that I generally disagree about Rakshi this edition. I found the changes to her to be some of my fav parts of the preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T03:36:12-08:00","id":1287902,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I liked Ma-Ha-Suchi more than Rakshi, but I'm not sure why.<br /> Maybe it's just because he's a sympathetic character and she's not...<br /> Rakshi is actually perfect for her role in the setting (the baby-eating monster to show that the Wyld Hunt isn't entirely wrong). But somehow I didn't find her compelling.<br /> I didn't really dislike her write-up, but nor was I enthusiastic about it. I guess I liked it more than Leviathan, but less than Ma-Ha-Suchi and the other three (who I won't discuss yet as Isator hasn't got that far yet).<br /> Perhaps it's because Rakshi is 1st/2nd edition Rakshi but written better, whereas Ma-Ha-Suchi is essentially a whole new character who just looks like and has the same name as an old character. <br /> <br /> I also didn't find her ideology compelling as a Shan-Ya. I mean, I can see why a sorcerer would become her adherant, or a Lunar who wants her protection. But a Lunar who believes in her anarchist vision of independent Lunars isn't likely to want to serve another Lunar.<br /> I mean, I can see why more Lunars agreed with her than Ma-Ha-Suchi. But not that they'd want to become her adherants, compared to Lunars who believe in Lunar unity becoming adherants of Ma-Ha-Suchi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T05:55:15-08:00","id":1287912,"title":"","content":"Hehehe<br /> <br /> &quot;Raksi, we're supposed to be on vacation!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't know about you, but I'm having a lovely time here.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You toppled a Hundred Kingdoms government, Raksi!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The people have spoken. Viva la resistance!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You pushed the resistance leader into a giant fan!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He was a traitor and a scoundrel.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He was trying to stop you from pushing other people into a giant fan.&quot;<br /> <br /> {thump}<br /> <br /> &quot;Oho, that was a foot. I appear to have swallowed an entire person.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That would be the inn bartender.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, that explains why my mojito is taking so long.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It was horrifying! Your mouth unhinged like a snake.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wow, that sounds pretty awesome.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't go anywhere with you Raksi!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That hurt my feelings. Now we're both in the wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I wanna go home. We're leaving.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;In that case I should probably mention that I filled our luggage with orphan meat.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What?!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well I'm building a meat dragon, and not just any meat will do.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You know what, forget it; I'm not even shocked any more.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Aww, that's no fun.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This has become the norm for you, Raksi.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll have to try harder next time.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Please don't.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I feel like I've been issued a challenge.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Raksiiii...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's too late now... you.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I totally don't remember your name.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We've known each other for a thousand years, Raksi!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And what an impression you've made.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;My name is Ma-Ha-Suchi!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I said my name is Ma-Ha-Suchi.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh. I thought you were a woman.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why would you think that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mostly the voice. Are you sure?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course I'm sure!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, if you'll excuse me...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T07:37:28-08:00","id":1287934,"title":"","content":"Levels of monstrosity:<br /> <br /> &quot;I eat babies to survive; their suffering is irrelevant to me.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I eat babies for fun; their suffering is the entire point.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I eat babies just to fuck with people; their suffering is simultaneously irrelevant to me AND the entire point.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T08:24:24-08:00","id":1287944,"title":"","content":"Ah, I knew there was something I intended to address before posting the next part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287902#post1287902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also didn't find her ideology compelling as a Shan-Ya. I mean, I can see why a sorcerer would become her adherant, or a Lunar who wants her protection. But a Lunar who believes in her anarchist vision of independent Lunars isn't likely to want to serve another Lunar.<br /> I mean, I can see why more Lunars agreed with her than Ma-Ha-Suchi. But not that they'd want to become her adherants, compared to Lunars who believe in Lunar unity becoming adherants of Ma-Ha-Suchi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, maybe Lunars that are really obstinate and kind of dumb about it. Raksi's philosophy is evidently about sovereignty, not isolationism, so there are still viable ways for them to interact in ways that include some deference.<br /> <br /> I would find that a young Lunar would want to study under her so that they can actually learn the skills to let them actually govern and safeguard their dominions effectively before going off to do it. Raksi doesn't believe in every Lunar for themselves, and leaving others to flounder ineffectually is a good way to find herself surrounded by hostility. <br /> <br /> I mean, she wants other Lunars to be <i>good</i> at fighting the Realm. Presumably, a lot of younger Lunars want to be good at that as well. Is pride in their self-determination worth more than that?<br /> <br /> And describing her ideology as anarchist is quite silly, or at least betrays a fundamental misunderstanding of the term. An anarchist Lunar would be against any authorities, not saying that all of the Lunars should be one. The Shadow Deliberative were anarchist, given how they dissolved themselves after destroying the government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T08:36:46-08:00","id":1287946,"title":"","content":"Now, let\u2019s see how one of the new guys holds up.<br /> <br /> Okay, gonna disregard having seen that Caul preview a year ago for a moment\u2026 oh hey, here\u2019s a highly prominent and successful Lunar leader who specifically originated in the Shogunate. I like the previous two shahan-yas, but we certainly need more younger ones to drive home the point about the First Agers not being the driving force of the Pact.<br /> <br /> Now, for something actually new; I spent a long time thinking of Oka as being external to the Pact, but ultimately like the group being portrayed as something that is diverse and accommodating enough that his personal crusade of open warfare is valid within them, as well as providing the background for many others to flock to him for greater or lesser tours. What I find particularly interesting is that he reflects that same accommodation back on those who join him, not gatekeeping or proselytizing to them. It helps create the picture of what would be so personable and attractive about him that would attract so many, particularly in contrast to the prior, older ones. Come to that\u2026 I\u2019m forming a picture, let\u2019s see where it goes\u2026<br /> <br /> So yeah, his whole thing about having repeatedly faked his death, in extremely public ways. Quite apart from being a fun reversal of the old adage that Lunars only ever accomplished things by dying in the process, it\u2019s another nice way of creating a distinctly Lunar kind of accomplishment (I mean, sure, a Solar could probably do some of it, but it feels less readily as a signature move for one of their luminaries). Alluding to his experience with the disappeared Caul helps add some mystical weirdness to him, although what I find most interesting there is the timeline; if he was born into the Shogunate, but the Caul vanished shortly after the Usurpation, he was most likely not a Lunar for very long when he went with it, helping cement his endurance as not just a feat of immense power. And I\u2019m bemused by the contrast with the prior Lunars, being more widely admirable but having less personal intimacy. I actually particularly like the idea of a Full Moon who has an inclination towards obscure ritual and contemplation of mystery.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019m reading the line about the military advantages of the Caul being under Pact relations is to show that his military action is not just about the war itself, but making a big show to demonstrate the potential to other like-minded Lunars. Possibly also sometimes Lunars that aren\u2019t as desirous of such battle on the whole, but still sometimes want a theatre to cut loose in. Oh, but I like the addition of others arguing that he\u2019s emboldening Lunars in their own theatres to engage in strategies that are less functional there. All of this so far has been doing a lot of the same good work as the Great House write-ups, creating meaningful structures for actual politics and intrigue and actual, functional factionalisation. Right now I\u2019m picturing a scenario in which Raksi, jerk that she is, is being unrestrained in condemning the desires of some enthusiastic Lunars in council, which doesn\u2019t bely her actually being kind of in the right, or at least well motivated. I\u2019m taking from the description of Oka\u2019s own take on things that, for the most part, he\u2019s not strongly partisan in the sense of having no issues with shahan-yas that maintain a focus on the attrition warfare, only rejecting those who have rejected him outright. There\u2019s a description of Leviathan here, but I\u2019ll hold off on considerations about him until his own write-up, and just infer that while the Black Lion has no issue with attrition, he\u2019s a lot less fond of those that opt for defensive withdrawal.<br /> <br /> Hmm, my picture of him is evolving a bit from Brian Blessed to Sean Boromir (particularly the scene from Two Towers Extended Edition where we actually get a direct picture of Boromir as a great captain of Gondor).<br /> <br /> It makes sense that his instruction is both fairly comprehensive and multi-faceted in pursuit of the many avenues of an active war, and impersonal when he\u2019s got a lot of other responsibilities to attend to. I can actually imagine some Lunars seeking his tutelage just for the range of educational topics rather than personal investment in the war (even if they do become obligated during their tenure to take part in it). It\u2019s also interesting to get this picture of how Sha\u2019a Oka is experienced by others, especially that idea that when drawn into conversation he\u2019s only partially present. I find something strangely relatable in a lot of the arrangement.<br /> <br /> After the prior two, I\u2019m also interested to see what it\u2019s like to have a Lunar\u2019s prominent adherents consist themselves of older and more prestigious Lunars who serve as lieutenants. Let\u2019s see what they have\u2026 heh, Oka\u2019s undying commitment\u2026 anyway, yes, I think there\u2019s some goof stuff from the outset with Third Daughter of the Leaves, with her perhaps not altogether metaphorical description of focusing anger in excess of her years into attacks of witchcraft, as well as specifically being less loyal to His Divine Lunar Presence than the actual war to control the Realm.<br /> <br /> Skathra Venomchild sounds a lot like somebody from the Contagion era, and I like the description of how and why they\u2019re so close to Sha\u2019a Oka, as well as that particular expression of being a Lunar Exalt (by which I\u2019m referring to the ecstatic madness). There\u2019s an intriguing sense of backstory in the idea that nobody has shown them the sort of kindness or understanding that Oka has. On top of all this, the description of revelling in violence and terror suggests that they\u2019re not exactly a nice person, so it\u2019s fun to come with that at the end of all of the more sympathetic stuff.<br /> <br /> Sandswept Garda-Empress is fine, although less interesting to me than most of the other described adherents so far; nothing wrong with that, and her place and purpose are still clear. But then there\u2019s the very interesting idea of a Lunar who not only still identifies as one of the Lintha, but an actual intermediary between the Silver Pact and a local branch of the Family. That presents an insight into a way in which the Pact might maintain alliances with external groups while preserving the integrity of its own system. Likewise I think there\u2019s something strong in the idea of Flowers Unbending in the Storm being truly loyal, but still having a major disagreement that has caused her to act a bit subversively.<br /> <br /> And it helps to convey the scope of Oka\u2019s legend to make some references to Lunars far afield that still have a connection, whether it be a former student off doing their own thing or somebody pledged to his belief system without any kind of personal connection.<br /> <br /> My ultimate assessment of Oka is that he gives a good feel for a Lunar that is at the head of a system that is large and complex, something informed by him but beyond him. The other two had that to an extent, but even with Raksi it felt a bit smaller and closer, primarily like living in a tense household. Oka\u2019s school radiates out from him, extending feelers to the furthest reaches of Creation and knitting together a variety of personalities and interests. Between that and the focus on how indirect he often is even when he\u2019s not pretending to be dead\u2026 it\u2019s good at giving him presence without him needing to be around. It\u2019s a good approach, and it\u2019s executed well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T11:34:53-08:00","id":1288012,"title":"","content":"Anyway, my thoughts on the previewed Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Chimera Soul Expression: Heh, who would have thought that we'd ultimately get a chimerism without any flash? I mean that in the best way possible, that it's proper for it to be a basic meat-and-potatoes thing for a bit of character customisation. I do wonder if the definition of mutations in the book proper will be a bit more comprehensive, or if this simple one says all that is needed.<br /> <br /> Hybrid-Body Transformation: Between Eska's write-up and ensuing discussion, the function of this one has been known for ages, but I do like the particular language employed to convey the accommodation in the appearance. I was never very enthusiastic about Deadly Beastman Transformation in the past, but when the idea is that it's just about overlaying some animal traits on the human form, that those Merits can include anything with physical benefit, and none of them need to be dedicated to appearance, I'm much happier with something providing a suite of mutations.<br /> <br /> Totem Beast Embodiment: I like that idea for how a Lunar might harness and apply the power of an animal they possess the shape of, especially for how the Protean keyword provides both an incentive to do it in animal shape and a process for expressing the power while still in a human form. I wonder if Lunar free Excellencies can also raise the die-cap by stunting.<br /> <br /> Ohh, an Essence 5 Charm, what more impressive shit do they have...<br /> <br /> Silver Ripple Mirage: Uh-huh, so obviously Lunars have a preceding Charm to turn into images in reflective surfaces. It's fun that it's not only a more witchy power, but one under a Changing Moon Attribute. For the Charm itself, I've always thought that dematerialization was a bit of an awkward fit for Lunars, but what sells this one is the particular process and image, something more rooted in the Lunar milieu to keep it from feeling like part of a generic grab bag. The image of momentary physicality and being able to slip back into reflections also lends itself to Lunars engaging in some freaky avenues of attack, and the ways in which it might shape the behaviour of enemies. I also think it's interesting and useful to create novel methods of fighting against it within the Charm itself.<br /> <br /> Wolf Devours Shepherd: Another nice simple one to invoke some of that predatory image, as well as show the benefit of the Totemic Keyword for diversifying characters.<br /> <br /> Debt of Borrowed Skin: Like the other Charms for alternative sacred hunts, I appreciate how this one doesn't let the Lunar off easy, with the requirement for the payment in exchange for the shape needing to be a big deal rather than just a trivial endeavour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:38:53-08:00","id":1288041,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Silver Ripple Mirage influenced (in Creation) the Dragon-Blood Occult Charm that allows you to See Dematerialized Spirits <i>in a reflective surface</i>. I can see the combat now, an elder Lunar is attacking Mnemon or someone using Silver Ripple Mirage and all you see is her throwing her cup around and acting like a drunk maniac, when she's actually fighting for her life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T15:24:23-08:00","id":1288099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1288041#post1288041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Silver Ripple Mirage influenced (in Creation) the Dragon-Blood Occult Charm that allows you to See Dematerialized Spirits <i>in a reflective surface</i>. I can see the combat now, an elder Lunar is attacking Mnemon or someone using Silver Ripple Mirage and all you see is her throwing her cup around and acting like a drunk maniac, when she's actually fighting for her life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that's always been how Dragon Blooded Occult worked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T18:35:48-08:00","id":1288132,"title":"","content":"All right, show me Leviathan.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit, while I can see the intention behind contrasting the modern day roving sea monster Leviathan with him having once been the top admiral of the Realm navy, something about that backstory never really moved me. I don\u2019t really have an elaborate reason to prefer the idea that he was always a Lunar whose activity was more master ocean predator and preferred to live out there in that, I just do.<br /> <br /> \u2026.Is the implication that Leviathan is trans?<br /> <br /> Anyway, still has the element of severe grief over losing his mate, but\u2026 is kind of both less and more of a weirdo about it. He\u2019s still retreated from society to just protect Luthe while spending all of his time as a giant orca, and doing so for a <i>long</i> time, but at least he\u2019s not terrorising the descendants of the city\u2019s Dragon Blooded and violently murdering any who Exalt\u2026 I presume.<br /> <br /> I like how he\u2019s tied into that revised history of expansion to the West only being relatively recent, and how it\u2019s framed as a bridge too far for him (as well as a bit of delving too deep and awakening an ancient horror). From the description of Luthe, I\u2019m getting the image of a city that would be on an open war footing but for the limits of being under miles of water, but is nevertheless doing a lot of damage there, at least until the enemy is weak enough to emerge en masse and launch a true invasion. I think there\u2019s something especially fun in the idea of a lot of younger Lunars finding the appearance of this powerful First Age elder really abrupt and hard to get a read on, while the few others who knew him are excited the prospect of him getting back in the game. Kind of a Dark Knight Returns thing going on there.<br /> <br /> And that lends itself to a rather interesting twist on the image of the overwhelmingly powerful elder; somebody that is really old, but nevertheless has a huge amount of catching up to do and hasn\u2019t quite recovered his social skills. Especially the idea that he maintains an open invitation for Sha\u2019a Oka despite the rejection, but the rejection might make any actual meeting between them go poorly. And I enjoy that his side of reconnecting with the other survivors of the first generation amounts to them being the only people he has left that he can properly relate to, except being separated from the context of them for more than a thousand years means that he\u2019s out of the loop in the many complications in their relationships that have cropped up since, and he can\u2019t figure out which one to consolidate while breaking ties with the rest. It\u2019s kind of\u2026 relatable, but also alien. This idea that Leviathan has been away from his humanity for so long, but has a need and desire for connecting with some of his peers, in a manner that amounts to him having a significant struggle. It both makes me empathise for him, and is a surprisingly elegant way of curtailing the extremes of his potential power.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve got to say, so far the book has done a very good job on capitalising on the sense of how old a lot of these people are. Which for the First Age ones in particular, seems to often amount more to a liability, whether it be an excessive focus on the long view of things or having accumulated more bad blood and bitter memories than they can effectively handle. I\u2019m picturing Tayan Silver-Crowned to convince Feather Drenched to place himself under her authority simply by effectively making that argument to him.<br /> <br /> And all of that seems to come with some pros and cons for him as a teacher; he seems overly reliant on his old prestige drawing more experienced Lunars that can actually function as the mentors to any youths that wind up with him. But it otherwise makes him a lot less partisan than even the Black Lion, and possibly more effective on that front if he should effectively marshal all of his resources; the ocean provides a lot of resources and strategic avenues, and if the right collection of Lunars should manage to get a distribution network going\u2026 yes, I could imagine such a thing in the future greatly magnifying the power of the Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> Hmm, is it worth pulling my copy of Scroll of Exalts out of a box not a meter and a half away to remind myself exactly what Swims in Shadows was like in the previous Edition\u2026 ah screw it. Just a second\u2026 okay, that backstory of having been a deep diving shaman who Exalted by pushing himself down far in search of a spirit willing to fight off shark boy, discovered his god was an old Lunar, and started applying his prior skills to proselytizing to spirits on Lunar behalf is actually pretty neat. Assuming there\u2019s no comprehensive overhaul later, I\u2019m going to view this writing as a supplement for the new context rather than rewrite. As to that content, yeah, I like Leviathan\u2019s context emerging in a Lunar who already had a teacher becoming enamoured of him, splitting his service between them, and finding himself in the awkward position of the former one expecting him to function as a go-between.<br /> <br /> It seems like Leviathan\u2019s abrupt entry lends itself well to a lot of divided loyalties, with one of the Black Wave Reavers being like-minded and owing a personal debt, but keeping that to himself when his circle mate is a dedicated follower of Oka. I think that\u2019s good for giving a sense of the Silver Pact\u2019s cross sections of philosophy through distant adherents that end up more closely associating. Like I said before, this is how you do factions.<br /> <br /> Ah good, another beastfolk Lunar. Oh, Gjalla makes for a nice change of pace with a much more mercenary, opportunist Lunar who\u2019s only in it for access to the ancient super city and personal treasure and giving her family a place of unimaginable luxury and security to dwell in, while being singularly unimpressed with Leviathan himself. I really like her; she makes me want stories of Luthe\u2019s disastrous downfall that have never so much as crossed my mind before. Not out of malice, of course, but imagine how dramatic it would be!<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know about anybody else, but Leviathan as a shahan-ya brings a lot of really interesting new dynamics to the character and the Silver Pact as a whole to me, and I could see a lot of really cool and fun stuff coming out of it. Even just as a basis for a lot of undersea adventures, whether based in Luthe or with that as an element that other people have to deal with. Hell, Luthe as being on a war footing while also a uniquely secure and beneficial home base for Lunars makes that city more intriguing than it\u2019s ever been (hence why I care enough for me to want it dramatically destroyed). When I talked about wanting the book to give me something that I hadn\u2019t known I would always want, this right here is what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> And thinking some more over Sha\u2019a Oka\u2019s perspective, I also think it\u2019s good and valuable to have at least one major figure look on Leviathan\u2019s return and be really pissy at him not having contributed earl\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh dang, Luthe is underwater Wakanda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T19:14:10-08:00","id":1288143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1287912#post1287912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hehehe<br /> <br /> &quot;Raksi, we're supposed to be on vacation!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't know about you, but I'm having a lovely time here.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You toppled a Hundred Kingdoms government, Raksi!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The people have spoken. Viva la resistance!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You pushed the resistance leader into a giant fan!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He was a traitor and a scoundrel.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He was trying to stop you from pushing other people into a giant fan.&quot;<br /> <br /> {thump}<br /> <br /> &quot;Oho, that was a foot. I appear to have swallowed an entire person.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That would be the inn bartender.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, that explains why my mojito is taking so long.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It was horrifying! Your mouth unhinged like a snake.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wow, that sounds pretty awesome.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't go anywhere with you Raksi!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That hurt my feelings. Now we're both in the wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I wanna go home. We're leaving.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;In that case I should probably mention that I filled our luggage with orphan meat.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What?!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well I'm building a meat dragon, and not just any meat will do.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You know what, forget it; I'm not even shocked any more.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Aww, that's no fun.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This has become the norm for you, Raksi.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll have to try harder next time.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Please don't.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I feel like I've been issued a challenge.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Raksiiii...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's too late now... you.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I totally don't remember your name.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We've known each other for a thousand years, Raksi!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And what an impression you've made.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;My name is Ma-Ha-Suchi!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I said my name is Ma-Ha-Suchi.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh. I thought you were a woman.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why would you think that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mostly the voice. Are you sure?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course I'm sure!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, if you'll excuse me...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did you just make reference to LAMAS WITH HATS?! <br /> Best Valentines Day gift ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T22:06:45-08:00","id":1288170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026.Is the implication that Leviathan is trans? </div> </div> </div>I assumed it meant he was a scrawny manlet before he exalted, its kind of vague (which may or may not be on purpose).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:01:36-08:00","id":1288180,"title":"","content":"The answer was apparently yes.<br /> <br /> {slap slap}<br /> <br /> <br /> All right, if a quarter of the Charms chapter is being put up this soon, then I\u2019d best see if I can\u2019t polish off this chapter within the next few hours, because that is going to be an ordeal. I would personally prefer a longer window in-between previews to have some breathing room, but what are you going to do?<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay Amatha, fingers crossed for showing me a shahan-ya from the Realm era\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, snap, can\u2019t get more Realm era than \u201cactual child of a Great House founder\u201d.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve wondered, sometimes, if the new layout of the Realm might lend itself to some abusive husbands when they find themselves with wives they rank higher than. And when it\u2019s the actual child of Cynis, well, sounds like a nasty situation all around. Good on her to flee from that, although I do find something indefinably creepy in the idea that the first shape she acquired was that of her husband\u2019s sister (even if she applied it to canny use).<br /> <br /> Wait a moment\u2026 this whole time I\u2019ve been presuming that Amatha Kinslayer was Yena Bone-Breaker from the core book. Okay, adjusting some expectations\u2026<br /> <br /> So yeah, just a general saboteur with a more personal grudge against the Realm and one of its Houses. I actually see an interesting hint of the Cynis worldview in her aspirations to profaning the Scarlet Throne. And of course, as a child of Cynis, she\u2019ll likely be Well-Bred, lending itself to having her own Dragon Blooded child\u2026 ah, my head was initially going in the direction of the daughter being with her, but no, she was left behind. Given the description of how Amatha brought her up, there\u2019s got to be some lingering bitterness there in having been abandoned, even apart from the Anathema thing.<br /> <br /> Oh my, Amatha\u2019s sisters are still running the House, aren\u2019t they? I\u2019ve got to imagine that her identity as a Lunar is not widely known, since it seems like it would be a strong recurring disgrace for a trio of matriarchs. I\u2019m getting this weird picture of her as a Lunar that thrives on dysfunction.<br /> <br /> I guess it makes sense that a younger Lunar would have a less elaborate description of Pact relations, even if she has a bit of a head start in political dealings from that Dynastic upbringing\u2026 which ironically also holds her back, because she\u2019s dealing with people that would hold a Dynastic upbringing (and left behind descendants as a source of possible conflict of interest) against her. And then that upbringing also instils a sense of pride that means she responds to the snubs by being an incorrigible prankster in council\u2026 yes, definitely lives for the dysfunction. I like her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> After a bunch of much older Lunar mentors with various\u2026 issues with aloofness, it\u2019s nice to see one who is more self-critical and puts up confident fronts, and it helps that she has a genuinely valuable set of insights and frames of reference. That she\u2019s also a very sink-or-swim kind of teacher and tries to cultivate a wild abandon, maybe even a certain joie-de-vivre, also makes it seem like the experience of learning from her would be more dynamic, even fun for the Lunars involved.<br /> <br /> Now, some of those in question\u2026 I think it\u2019s cute to have the aristocrat bringing up an urchin in whom she sees a lot of potential, especially that idea that they make an educational game of promoting opposing social trends as a weapon against satrapies. I also think it speaks well of Amatha that she sees higher value in having Nida speak openly against her in council than having somebody in line behind her; like Ma-Ha-Suchi putting up with students that irritate him, it paints a helpful picture of a Silver Pact where contrary relationships don\u2019t need to be inhibited by power differences.<br /> <br /> Trasenji Yilean\u2019s backstory is interesting enough, but he\u2019s less of a vibrant character than Nida. And now, let\u2019s see if this book can finally redeem Strength-of-Many\u2026 hmm, unfortunately not really. He\u2019s got a bit more interplay with other Lunars within this setup for the Silver Pact (and maybe something mildly interesting in being apart from the society as a whole), but still has little deviation or elaboration from his one note of fighting slavery. He can\u2019t even have an interesting dynamic with Amatha, only associating with her because the grudge with House Cynis is relevant to his interests, and not even being a proper student. Set among the rest of these, he comes off as especially bland; if this book can\u2019t figure out a way to make the character a bit more interesting, I\u2019m afraid nothing can.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Amatha\u2019s write-up felt shorter than the others, maybe for the chapter winding down\u2026 keep going.<br /> <br /> All right, a completely new person that I had not mistaken for somebody else at all, Ruksara-Who-Remembers (probably a Dune style \u201cliving archive through rote memorisation\u201d thing).<br /> <br /> Okay, no ambiguity over Rukhsara being trans. So her prior incarnation being a Lunar with in impeccable memory and millenia of experience means that Rukhsara\u2019s experience of past life information is\u2026 a lot more extreme than the norm. Presumably, even if she\u2019s only getting a fraction of it, it\u2019s still far more than she\u2019s yet capable of processing. Interesting. And in the meantime she\u2019s putting her power to good use with getting some ancestral homelands back and trying to shore them up against retaliation, while mortal and Exalted adherents argue that she should take a more aggressive stance.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m guessing\u2026 that her school is structured in terms of the vast repository of information that she is, creating more variation in her students and resulting issues with difference in desired approach to the Pact\u2019s mission statement. I\u2019ve actually got an interesting image now in which her investment in her clan means that many of its mortal members form close rapports through common cause with her students.<br /> <br /> Her status in the Pact owing to what\u2019s provided by her former incarnation is interesting, particularly Raksi\u2019s uncommon delicacy. Oh wait, Aqadar\u2026 I think I remember from the Fajad preview\u2026 he\u2019s got some kind of big tower, doesn\u2019t he? And a rapport with another Lunar in a similar boat. It\u2019s a very peculiar approach to depicting one Lunar\u2019s Pact relations, broadly well-received but with some particularly intense and personal bonds. In the lack of overt description of political agenda, I\u2019m seeing a sense that she\u2019s had to be more dedicated to investing in her personal project and managing her inheritance; I can imagine that lack of affiliation helps with general popularity (the reference to a preference for gradually grinding down notwithstanding).<br /> <br /> Yes, I find my prior suppositions corroborated by the description of her teaching style. It\u2019s all about getting them to provide benefits to her people, and a more mutual approach to forming policies on various frontiers.<br /> <br /> Ho-oh lord yes, are her adherents tied into her clan, right down to a Lunar becoming her grandson-in-law. Somehow, I kept seeing the picture of Lunar dominions as very solitary affairs, and even with the preview of the Lunar schools\u2026 I\u2019ve never given much consideration for dominions with multiple Lunars, and some of the implications. And still always imagining them as so distant from the inhabitants, rather than including instances of them being important as some of the few places where Lunars don\u2019t need to hide. The funny thing is that this approach is doing more for making such locales and societies interesting and vibrant than the Thousand Streams River, in base concept or provided example, ever did.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s this asshole, one excessively devoted Echo-Prince Piyo that is of the opinion her mentor is not living up to her status and determined to have her adopt a more opulent splendour. See Strength-of-Many, why can\u2019t you be more like Piyo? Followed by one No Trouble Zhang, who\u2026 takes a similar path to a very different conclusion, concerned almost entirely with acquiring his teacher\u2019s occult lore. This lad strikes me as somebody mostly opposed to the Realm in the abstract; too dedicated to the goal in its own right, rather than driven by an underlying reason for it. He strikes me as a bit ruthless, possibly to the point of amorality; no trouble indeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, finally, a little section on some of The Rest.<br /> <br /> Yyyep, Aqadar is the one with that creepy tower. Kind of a terrifying sorcerer mendicant, way too focused on securing vengeance. Bit of background for Tayan\u2019s purpose in making and leading the Vanguard, with her own military origin and its value in having inflicted damage on the Shogunate enemy.<br /> <br /> Ah, so Feather Drenched isn\u2019t somebody under direct authority so much as a kind of consigliere, although the point about maybe lacking clarity from too much grief could still stand. I can actually see the relationship being mutually beneficial; Tayan gets the highly valued expertise on the Sidereals (which probably goes a long way towards helping such a close concentration of Lunars keep afloat), Feather gets somebody that can pursue her vengeance in a more structured, efficient manner. And sure, nice to see a Lunar with a lot more focus on their side of the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> Okay, you\u2019ve got your name, your presence in some of the art and comic story, a connection to a spider Lunar I enjoy, and like\u2026 half of a good design, show me something worthwhile to tie it all together Sublime Danger\u2026 rrriigght, basically a Lunar who applies her power and nature as a high-level thrill seeker, barely concerned with the political disposition of Creation, and is just philosophical about it as to take on the like-minded and put them through their paces (or maybe she just finds it amusing), with a touch of having designs on her mate that would make Yo-yo boy\u2019s quest probably not end in a manner most to his liking. Yeah, she\u2019s all right; I\u2019m imagining a personality of a kind I think is fun, and for all that the book ultimately dashed my dreams and built something better from the shards, there might as well be at least one prominent Lunar who desires only complete freedom and to live a life of intrigue and adventure.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve got the interesting presentation of a former duo of shahan-yas who worked together in the esoteric region of the Dreaming Sea, utilizing a combination of mundane and mystical means to harass the Realm\u2019s interests in the area, divided now over a question of whether to destroy Prasad or splinter it off into a rival of the Blessed Isle. And finally, one more for the first generation with Ul the Burning Eye, who has taken Lunar grievances to the greatest extremes and plots comprehensive genocide of the Terrestrial Exalted (and presumably all mortals who carry sufficient quantities of their bloodlines).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a smidge left, but\u2026 here I\u2019ll call it another night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T10:01:31-08:00","id":1288309,"title":"","content":"Okay, finally finish off, and then\u2026 on to the Charms. :S<br /> <br /> <br /> Silver Pact\u2019s relations with external powers. Being what it is, there\u2019s no unified idea or policy, just a broad consensus with lots of personal variations, seemingly informed by a rather proprietary attitude towards their grudge with the Realm.<br /> <br /> Now, what\u2019s the definition of an independent Lunar? Err, bpperr\u2026 so, you can still get favours and connections, which is a bit more association than I would expect. I guess then to be an independent means having neither hostility to the Realm, adherence to a shahan-ya or participation in councils, as well as possibly disregarding some of their customary standards of relation. The example of how Yena Bone-Breaker handled an independent who incurred her wrath gives a certain sense that relations between those and the Silver Pact\u2026 kind of favours the independent, depending on perspective. It\u2019s at least interesting that the Pact has such a strong interest in being attractive to other Lunars as to consistently treat them with a delicate hand.<br /> <br /> Heh, my perspective on Ma-Ha-Suchi having not been a member of the Silver Pact was not entirely incorrect, it just lacked some elaborating details. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That kind of variation in perspective does help to emphasize the informality in the group, anyway.<br /> <br /> What about (presumably non-Realm) Dragon Blooded? So as long as it\u2019s not somebody claiming a descent from the Shogunate or otherwise engaged in extending territorial power, most Lunars are willing to approach them with caution. I\u2019m actually imagining the reluctance to do things in the long-term as ultimately more beneficial to the Dragon Blooded in the equation, if that kind of thing can bring the wrath of the Realm down on a group less equipped to withstand it. And some loners can even find places in mixed circles or schools, although the circumstances and attitudes that might prolong this into allied family groups are probably still exceedingly unlikely. Still, it\u2019s nice that the attitude to Dragon Blooded is fairly accommodating, and focused on treating with them as peers rather than just a resource to cultivate and harness.<br /> <br /> So with Sidereals, on the whole they\u2019re in the same boat, in a manner that complicates interactions with independent Lunars. Whatever I may have said about it in the past, I ultimately think it\u2019s a good thing for Lunars that understand the nuances of Heavenly politics to have a willingness to engage with those who aren\u2019t complicit in their persecution when they have common cause, even if there are some less well-versed Lunars that basically attack on sight. That the Gold Faction is trying to put feelers out helps strengthen the sense of credibility for the Lunars, and apart from their uncertainty about what they want with the Solars, I think it\u2019s clever for there to be Lunars that are wary of such communications just because it might give them away to the Bronze Faction. The funny thing is, now more than ever, a Silver Faction would make sense (although still perhaps a stretch; possibly too many Lunars have gone too far for even independent Sidereals to want to entrust Creation to them).<br /> <br /> And now for the Solars themselves; I was worried that the chapter wouldn\u2019t get around to bringing them up. Throughout the Second Age, the few survivors seem to have been a marginal, if weighted consideration, especially for their mates. It seems to me that those Solars didn\u2019t transform the overall landscape, just generally serving as a circumstantial wild card element, either beneficial or concerning depending on the details. But now they\u2019ve returned on the whole, and the Lunar plans have become disrupted. Too many Solars that might have their own contrary agendas, too many older Lunars who aren\u2019t willing to let the Solars be on the top of the pyramid again, and the tumult of a lot more revived bonds and associated powerful emotions; if Lilith is anything to go by, that\u2019s going to be the roughest on those few Lunars that actually remember having mates and have had to spend <i>all</i> of that time with their absence. Suddenly, I have a picture of many of Leviathan\u2019s adherents and allies specifically working to prevent the reincarnation of his mate from reaching him, lest it disrupt his limited early momentum.<br /> <br /> Right, so there were Lunars in a position to gather early warning of the Abyssals even before their grand reveal, and since them most of them are in a position of waiting and seeing and judging by first contact, but for the realisation that some of them are the subject of Solar Bonds. Anja Silverclaws\u2019 attitude was already more compelling, and I think the idea of giving her an Abyssal mate effectively compounds that. Ahh, and the point about the ongoing vendetta against the Realm makes a good point about a priority that may decide in Abyssal favour, possibly to the Lunars\u2019 disadvantage.<br /> <br /> And now, we\u2019re getting our unofficial introduction to the Infernal Exalted of Third Edition, before their proper debut in the Storytelling Guide. Oh, it\u2019s\u2026 literally three sentences. Well, isn\u2019t my face red. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Okay, so most have no idea, just a few have been determined by mystical intelligence gathering, a rumour and a distant name insufficient to form any solid opinion on their implications, and so few encounters that almost none of them have revived their Bond through an Infernal. I\u2019m suddenly reminded of how the origin of the term Green Sun Prince was in Ingosh Silverclaws last vision, and I\u2019m kind of attached to that little bit of trivia.<br /> <br /> Exigents are reinforced as having too much variety to form a common standard, albeit with a focus on a few examples that have distinctly made common cause with the Pact. While Liminals are too diffuse to form a common standard, and a lot of the impetus seems to be on their side, in whether they want the assistance of Lunar magic or are opposed to its use in harnessing the dead improperly. I like the examples that we get, Withari\u2019s Child finding a useful refuge with Ul in exchange for enduring his weirdness, Dreams-of-Rain being kind of caught in the crossfire of Pact conflict with the Dynasty such that he\u2019s got a grudge against the Lunar that did it, and any others that get in his way.<br /> <br /> Ahh, I had kind of forgotten about the Getimians, even though there\u2019s been a lot of questions about how their fight with the Sidereals might interact with the Lunar conflict. Sooo\u2026 right, they had high hopes at the first appearance, but learning that Rakan Thulio is their leader has poisoned that well too much. So the best that can be managed is trying to direct encountered Getimians to disrupt Sidereal plans in ways beneficial to Lunars, as such opportunities arise.<br /> <br /> All right, getting to the bottom of the list now. The Guild has enough presence and power to be a major consideration, while also being structured in a manner resilient against Lunar infiltration, and motivated in a manner that makes it more tool than friend. Where the Guild undermines the Realm, it\u2019s unmolested or supported, where it helps or takes liberties with dominions it gets to feel the brunt of some Lunar anger. I\u2019ve been liking how many of these come with focused examples, it keeps feeling like a good lesson taken from Masters of Jade, and here that gets a full confluence with an example of a factor who made an exchange agreement with one of Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s crew, up until she also took up with a Realm satrap and is being used by the Lunar as a source of disinformation. I\u2019d say that\u2019s all about what one would expect of the Guild, itself being too diffuse to heavily politicize dealing with it.<br /> <br /> Most of the spirit stuff is fairly standard as any policies towards them go, although the Lunars maybe get a bit of an edge from how the opposition has a dedicated policy of managing and suppressing spirits. For examples, I like the manner in which Aqadar provides assistance to Fajad\u2019s spirit prophets, even if his intentions are largely self-serving. The most interesting is the idea that there are Lunars who seek a particularly strong affinity with those gods under Luna\u2019s purviews, whether motivated by spiritual considerations or the sense that their patron gives them an inroad. Tethys on the Untrammeled Path is one that I view as the more understated and well-written elements of Glories of the Most High, so I like seeing her brought back in, and I find something delightfully weird in the idea of an eclipse god being a giant god-bat.<br /> <br /> Who\u2019s left\u2026 among the dead, there are plenty of ghosts that would simply flock to Lunars as powerful figures that can aid and protect them (probably helped a bit by Lunars having had some of the strongest affinity for the dead through necromancy in the Second Age), as well as some having the benefits of their associated living being under Lunar dominions. And the plain fact of many Lunars having lived long enough to have enduring friendships among the dead. I like how creepy the associations of the example Lunars are, one offering their powerful blood in exchange for secrets, the other using victims of the common enemies as fuel to unleash dreadful weapons in vengeance. I am curious about how, between this and the Abyssal section, the Deathlords don\u2019t seem to be on the Silver Pact\u2019s radar.<br /> <br /> Being almost entirely detached from the Wyld now, the Fair Folk seem like a much more marginal concern for the Silver Pact. It seems to me that what violence is dedicated towards them is primarily motivated by the memory of the Balorian Crusade and desire to not allow it to be repeated, I feel both for the sake of protecting the world and not letting them interrupt Lunar vengeance again. Other than that, they\u2019re just another potential weapon against the Realm, albeit one whose history and appetites can draw severe reservations, and a fine line against going too far for most to tolerate. It\u2019s a bit less specificity towards the Raksha than I might have expected, but I have no strong attachment to that and the Lunars certainly have a lot else on their plate.<br /> <br /> And the very last of them all is some standards for the interaction with various regional powers. It\u2019s obviously not a question for the Silver Pact as a whole, instead a matter of how people with their agendas, as well as schools, might deal with their proximity. The Confederation of Rivers is a big deal to Lunars throughout the East, divided by ones who see it primarily as an extension of Lookshy and thus a target, and ones who want to encourage and strengthen its members to counterbalance the Shogunate remnant-state (see, factions!). The Dreaming Sea certainly seems like it would be a particular hotbed of powers to deal with, with interesting multi-faceted schemes such as turning Prasad\u2019s rivals against one another so that those Dragon Blooded are freed up to rebel against the Realm, contrasted with Lunars who view those rivals as more tolerable and allies against a feeler of Realm power in the region. The idea of Lunars being so entangled in the local politics enhances the Dreaming Sea\u2019s mystique to me, particularly with the idea that some of them are as at cross-purposes as the Silver Pact will allow. I\u2019m particularly imagining some princes of the states and empires recognising this dispute, and actively playing Lunars against one another for the benefit of their own power; like, say, a leader of Volivat delicately getting benefits from both, in the hopes of rising to dominance over both Ysyr <i>and</i> Prasad. And we already knew about some of Sha\u2019a Oka\u2019s association with the Lintha, although it\u2019s a nice place to reintroduce Ten Stripes, and good to point out that more distant Lunars might have protectorates that would benefit more from fighting the Lintha off.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the end of chapter two, a very strong thesis statement on the Lunars, and full of delightful personalities, agendas and methodologies. I think that even for people who don\u2019t quite like this direction, the strength of this portrayal can\u2019t be denied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T10:13:48-08:00","id":1288317,"title":"","content":"Okay, four days until the next manuscript preview. How long is this Charms preview?<br /> <br /> ..... Sixty two pages.<br /> <br /> aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T10:50:42-08:00","id":1288326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1288317#post1288317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, four days until the next manuscript preview. How long is this Charms preview?<br /> <br /> ..... Sixty two pages.<br /> <br /> aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey I am enjoying your review so far. If doing all 62 pages is too much you could always just do general impressions on the different sections? Or just cover your personal favorites? Anyway I look forward to reading your thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:42:18-08:00","id":1288342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1288326#post1288326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If doing all 62 pages is too much</div> </div> </div> </div>Silence!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">you could always just do general impressions on the different sections? Or just cover your personal favorites?</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered such an approach to What Fire Has Wrought, somewhere down the line. It left a bad taste in my mouth. I am maniacally committed.<br /> <br /> And these are Lunar Charms! Lunars! How long have we waited for them to fulfill their destiny?<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's wonderwall.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE<br /> Okay, I think I can at least get through the Intro and Universal Charms before having to wade through all of that rich, syrupy pudding.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the fact that it launches right into it reflects how the final product will look. I would at least expect a bit of a thesis statement on the nature of Lunar powers, for the purpose of establishing a brand and a standard.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I find it interesting that the Excellency establishes itself as Attribute + Ability first, before elaborating on the caveats. No, wait, that\u2019s describing the rolls that can be enhanced. Perhaps I\u2019m a little disoriented for this\u2026 {sheepish grin} I mean, of course, the idea was always a second Attribute, not an Ability.<br /> <br /> Oh dear, this is inane. Pick it back up, pick it back up\u2026<br /> <br /> I wonder what the ultimate implications of being able to add a dice cap on top of Charms to enhance soak or damage might be, whether it\u2019s limiting those ones or making those prominent areas for Lunars. While considering how broad the Excellencies can be, I\u2019d say that it makes sense for the conditions of getting them to be a bit more restrictive.<br /> <br /> The conditions for what kinds of action are enhanced make sense\u2026 so it appears, for the time being, they came down in favour of combination with Martial Arts, that should be interesting.<br /> <br /> And for the moment, no new Keywords (although the ones we do have remain rather impressive).<br /> <br /> So, quickly get out the Universals.<br /> <br /> Chimera Soul Expression and Hybrid Body Transformation have already been seen, so I have nothing more to say about them. And Shifting Beast Nature\u2026 it\u2019s a curious thing. The option for an additional suite of mutations for the hybrid form does seem appropriate, and making it a wholly separate Charm with the minimum requirement\u2026 it\u2019s a very functional thing, if ultimately not too flashy. Mind\u2026 I\u2019m getting into the idea of even a young Lunar having a pair of forms specialised for different purposes, and there\u2019s some interesting potential in that.<br /> <br /> I take it that Life of the Hummingbird provides the option of getting the shape of a killed (or wounded) being without undergoing a proper sacred hunt, at the cost of being only temporary. I actually think this is very interesting for the greater versatility it can lend a Lunar, letting the shapeshifting function in a more improvisational manner. Particularly, I\u2019m seeing a Lunar using it when backed into a corner that their current Charms and powers aren\u2019t suited to; I can imagine more than a few being dragged back to the Blessed Isle who got ahold of a rodent or insect, chomped it down, and slipped their bonds. Very neat.<br /> <br /> And the previously hinted at Many-Faced Moon Transformation, the ultimate in personal customisation. Even within its limits, the fact that it can be applied to <i>any</i> of a Lunars forms gives them ever more versatility in alteration for disguise and identity. I find it to be very elegant.<br /> <br /> Hmm, an initiative cost for Quicksilver Second Face\u2026 ah, the reflexive shapeshifting. I like how the initiative system gives it something to keep from superseding the slower path, as well as setting a variable limit on its frequency in a turn. It lets the image of dancing among a number of shapes breathe a bit more, helping lend a unique texture to how they might fight.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s Perfected Hybrid Interaction, a distinctly more limited approach to applying mutations from throughout the heart\u2019s blood library, but with the benefit of its own versatility; it appears to me that each purchase does not need to provide all four dots from the same animal. So it brings some of the addition in, without making the hybrid form feel redundant, and I appreciate that.<br /> <br /> Hmm, the manner in which mutations can stack like that feels especially interesting when articulated through the example of a beastperson. I\u2019m picturing that hawkwoman having the totem of a bat or a large bee, and the idea that her enhanced hybrid body wings combine the traits of both (even if a bird totem leading to especially impressive and majestic wings is also fitting).<br /> <br /> Given my prior thoughts on how the hybrid body might represent a number of specialisations in the transformation, I\u2019m interested in Changing Phases Transformation making that deeper with Attribute reassignments, although I would view that as apparently being mandatory as part of the cost for it. It\u2019s possible to give the change to both hybrid bodies if there\u2019s two, but I think that it might be worth keeping one\u2019s original Attribute layout for one of them.<br /> <br /> Hmm, and then Constant Quicksilver Rearrangement lets one assume a stance to shapeshift on the cheap. I get a fun impression of that as representing the general idea of a Lunar\u2019s growing familiarity and mastery of their essential power, more than a Charm in its own right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmm, so the Charms that let one have especially large and small spirit shapes aren\u2019t universal\u2026 I\u2019ll be interested to find out their location.<br /> <br /> Anyway, finish off with the first properly introduced Essence 5 Charm, Behemoth-and-Flea Mastery. Right, interesting, provide a limited capacity to reflexively shift into a huge or tiny form, unless using it to go into other giant or small forms respectively. Given the Essence, I\u2019m going to suppose that such a rapid alteration (with mote discount) is particularly formidable.<br /> <br /> So I like how the Universal Charms are taking the basic shapeshifting stuff and giving a lot of it some shine, effectively filling out and defining some of the basic (and likely very common) Lunar tools.<br /> <br /> I am\u2026 going to take a break tomorrow, and see if I can power through the first two Attributes on the remaining days. Eh, one a day, can\u2019t be that bad.<br /> <br /> I'm going to devote the time to one of my other passions; playing Xenoblade Chronicles.<br /> <br /> And also writing about that in exceeding detail. 30+ hours of gameplay translated into fifty <i>thousand</i> words of review and commentary!<br /> <br /> And counting...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T12:15:31-08:00","id":1288355,"title":"","content":"With the large number of dots one can get from charms I am very hopeful that the Lunars' merit section will have a substantial selection to choose from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T12:17:58-08:00","id":1288357,"title":"","content":"Behemoth and Flea Mastery is so god damned cool. That\u2019s my new #1 favourite way to destroy a building in Exalted now, to instantly kaiju out the roof. Double points if you\u2019re a flying kaiju and leave all 4 walls intact.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: also the ability to add to damage and soak is awesome. It\u2019s expensive as all hell but if you need to your dame can be insane, it might even spike over solar damage for withering attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-15-2019, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:44:12-08:00","id":1288467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The answer was apparently yes. </div> </div> </div>The answer to what was yes? Whether Leviathan was born female but their true self was a manly muscle mountain which they became on exalting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:03:56-08:00","id":1288478,"title":"","content":"Kelly Pederson asked Vance on Tuesday if Leviathan was trans, and was told yes.<br /> <br /> (The preferred terminology would be that Leviathan was assigned female at birth, and... it seems a bit odd to use they/them pronouns when the character is only ever described with he/him.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:10:02-08:00","id":1288483,"title":"","content":"Is occasionally using gender neutral pronouns something thats really worth commenting on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:22:48-08:00","id":1288490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1288483#post1288483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is occasionally using gender neutral pronouns something thats really worth commenting on?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a discussion specifically about a character's gender identity? It stands out a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]