alue":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T21:04:28-08:00","id":1288512,"title":"","content":"I see, I misread it and thought you were. My apologies for the overreaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T03:09:48-08:00","id":1288557,"title":"","content":"So Isator, now that you've read all the Shahan-Yas, do you have any favourites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T07:08:06-08:00","id":1288591,"title":"","content":"Do Lunars have a Charisma Charm that, when they are wrongfully imprisoned, plays Sarah McLachlan's &quot;Angel&quot; until the captors feel sad and let the Lunar go free? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T10:12:21-08:00","id":1288633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1288557#post1288557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Isator, now that you've read all the Shahan-Yas, do you have any favourites?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They are all interesting and compelling in distinct ways that shape different kinds of stories. They're unlike the Great Houses in that school and person are too intertwined to elevate an individual separate from the surrounding system, like with Mnemon.<br /> <br /> The closest I could get is in judging ones as significantly rising in my estimation from prior portrayals, in which case it would be Leviathan and Luthe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T11:37:15-08:00","id":1288659,"title":"","content":"Reading your description of Amatha caused me to imagine her as a murderous version of Miss Frizzle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T12:29:59-08:00","id":1288681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1288659#post1288659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading your description of Amatha caused me to imagine her as a murderous version of Miss Frizzle.</div> </div> </div> </div>{eyes widening}<br /> <br /> Octopus totem...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T11:47:17-08:00","id":1288962,"title":"","content":"I think that it\u2019s fitting that the arrangement in alphabetical order should start things off with Appearance, the originally unwanted child of Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Heart-Drinking Allure has already been seen in preview, the first of our new sacred hunt Charms, and I\u2019ll reiterate here my preference for it being a bit more strictly conditional to ensure that it doesn\u2019t crowd out the basic hunt. I sincerely hope that a lot of concerns are relieved by the sidebar being explicit that the necessary intimacy does not need to be sexual in nature.<br /> <br /> Ohh, that\u2019s right, every Attribute is getting at least one method, isn\u2019t it? So they go first, and then the rest are divided by broad application. So let\u2019s see what they can do for Influence.<br /> <br /> Glance-Oration Technique, for sophisticated communication through body language that can overcome language barriers. This one primarily interests me just in the territory that it\u2019s extending the umbrella of Appearance over; it\u2019s a bit non-descript, but that\u2019s entirely acceptable in such a low level Charm. It already starts to differentiate a bit more with a follow-up, Argument-Eclipsing Shadow, based on using beauty or menace to disrupt somebody else\u2019s influence, made more pointed with the distant possibility of immediately forming a powerful Tie. And it\u2019s going deeper still with Reflection Gazes Back, where a person trying to get a read on the Lunar becomes powerfully open to being beguiled or threatened by them. What I like about these Charms is that, while some feel roughly analogous to things that Solars might do, they still end up not quite feeling Silver Solar because the descriptions and functions of them actually do feel more like preternatural extrapolations of what description is described as being (form in combination with deliberate poise), which also gets to feel like a low level of precise and deliberate body control (even if elements like actual communication and a person\u2019s failings in a roll making them more susceptible put the Essence into it).<br /> <br /> Okay, different branch from Glance-Oration Technique for Predator-and-Prey Mirror, letting a Lunar alternately project an impression of being somebody socially threatening to the target or somebody that <i>they</i> would feel powerful or in control in the presence of. I feel it\u2019s lending validation to my speculation that Lunars would have a fair few to create phony Intimacies, as it were, and the prey posture does put me in mind of ideas I\u2019ve had in the past about Lunar body control letting them do things like certain portrayals of Superman. What especially interests me in this is the fact of it being a scene-long Charm that lets you shift freely, and the implications that has for a Lunar who goes back and forth during the course of a single encounter. That feels like it can be a distinctly Lunar way of interacting with people; not just leveraged for advantage, but just basic presentation or being. Also nicely draws something from the idea of a mercurial personality.<br /> <br /> Ah, and Glance-Oration has yet another branch to Perfect Symmetry; for years, I\u2019ve been wondering if they were ever going to fulfil that statement about the never realised Lunar errata of Charm trees that would resemble sea urchins. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for this Charm\u2026 just the basic (but powerful) extra dot of Appearance, with a nice sideline of making its prerequisite free for the duration. Most I can say about this is liking the image conveyed by the combination of the enhancement creating a base for even more precise body control.<br /> <br /> So, a new root, and our first official Protean Charm with Feral Smile Tactic; double 9s to threaten or instil fear, or use to drain Initiative from somebody who already has such a Tie towards their current shape. What I find interesting about this one is having never considered the possibility for Protean Charms (probably exclusively the social ones) to not merely provide an enhancement or alternative, but to actually capitalise upon the base use. So you\u2019ve got a Charm for making somebody fear you, that you can then continuously apply while in that shape to make efficacious threats to them. What I like about this is not just the way in which it ties animal shapeshifting to a social power, but bringing us into the significance of Lunars having multiple human shapes that a given person might have different relationships to. It\u2019s laying the groundwork for a thing I\u2019ve been thinking of for a while; that such shapes aren\u2019t merely about what standing is attached to the person you got them from, but can be used as the basis for cultivating a base of connections and identity, to be adorned or discarded at will.<br /> <br /> Out of that Charm we get another two paths into Outburst-Provoking Posture and Terrifying Bestial Visage. The former inducing outrage in the Lunar\u2019s cocksure attitude, modelled as intilling certain negative Ties alongside successful influence in general (I\u2019m not entirely clearly, but it seems to work on any witness to the influence, and possibly many at once), as well as penalising their mental and social rolls from how distracted they are; this I like for both the sense of personal image control and being a bit of a troll. The latter functioning both to enhance rolls to threaten and instil fear (with non-Charm dice if in a predatory shape), and inflict the person so affected with a block against initiating hostilities. I\u2019m guessing that with a Charm such as this, the Lunar has the option of assuming the animal shape in the course of the scene to make their threatening action (which it ought to be, shapeshifting should include a capacity to make a point as well as disguise), and still benefits from the block when they resume any other form. It\u2019s a nice bit of paralytic intimidation tactic there, and I particularly like the encouragement to shapeshift in the middle of conversation.<br /> <br /> Now back to something a bit more benign (as well as Appearance covering something a bit Linguistics related), Peacock Quill Flourish\u2026 oh, that\u2019s interesting, the idea of making writing so evocative of the memory of a person\u2019s look that they get to apply Appearance bonus in a roll where it normally wouldn\u2019t apply. Leaving aside the mechanical advantage, I think that\u2019s a very interesting way to realise a Lunar being able to manifest power through writing. I am guessing from the sidebar, though, that written stuff isn\u2019t a common channel for Lunar influence; I kind of hope so, for the sake of some stuff concerning the whole thing about Attribute Charms.<br /> <br /> Another base is in Seductive Moonlit Dream, the more positive counterpoint to Feral Smile, doubling 9s for rolls of seduction or instilling things like love and desire, and through Protean potentially improving the Appearance bonus against people with those Ties. What, no love for animal shapes? Way to kink shame, writers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (In all seriousness, for anybody who thought that it was appropriate, it has to be the most trivial house rule)<br /> <br /> Thinking more about the process of distinguishing between the Lunar and a given shape\u2026 I\u2019m thinking that if a Lunar is known to be themselves even while in an alternative shape that is recognised as being them (either through familiarity or direct witness), Intimacies apply across all recognised shapes, whereas if a shape is being utilised as a disguise, they only apply towards that identity. It raises an interesting question to me about how to resolve Ties towards a disguise and false identity (not exclusively, but very pertinent to Lunars) if that ruse should be unveiled. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s a rules thing as much as a story one, depending on the demeanour of the tricked person and how much the revealed character can convince that the thing the Tie was towards was their true self underneath the trappings. I think it has potential for interesting and dramatic stories, even without being leveraged into bigger things.<br /> <br /> It also gives me an image of a Lunar who conducts a relationship with somebody who knows them for themselves through a different shape every meeting. Like, even if the fellow isn\u2019t familiar with that shape, the Lunar can introduce themselves through briefly flaring their anima. It would be an interesting and off-putting social demeanour.<br /> <br /> Anyway, carrying on, the old Lunar standby of pheromones is here in Alluring Scent Technique. After a lot of the more heavily mystical stuff, I do actually like something that is a bit more rooted in the physical with wind conditions affecting the range, and the animalistic quality of it being tied to common species. I also think it\u2019s interesting how it doesn\u2019t put full control in the Lunar\u2019s hands, being dependent on pre-existing feelings, so it can\u2019t just be \u201carouse anybody you meet\u201d; I particularly like the idea of being able to reduce the effect of Minor Ties against Lunars.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m just skipping ahead a bit to check something\u2026 right, I\u2019m decided to approach these sub-categories of Attributes the way that I did for Terrestrial Abilities, one entry devoted to each. I still intend to finish each Attribute in a day right now, but not going to pack the entirety of Appearance into a single post.<br /> <br /> Moving on (maybe pick up the pace a bit), Attention-Demanding Presence\u2026 ah right, that fun idea of being the centre of attention, drawing all eyes on them to weaken general Perception, and another possibility of instantly forming a Tie if their rolls go poorly. It\u2019s funny how it\u2019s a Mute Charm to make a character dazzle.<br /> <br /> Mysterious Stranger Intimation can build off of the curiosity provoked by pheromones to cultivate further attractive mystery for the sake of improving Guile\u2026 oh, it\u2019s a Permanent enhancement, okay. Also extends the range, both spacially and across species barriers, creates a mild, circumstantial compulsion to act on the resulting curiosity in a fitting manner\u2026 yes, I like this idea of exuding pheromones as a way for a Lunar to be surrounded in an aura that drags attention along with them. Both in form and function, it feels very much like them.<br /> <br /> And the already previewed Divine Paramour\u2019s Embrace, to give the Lunar even more positive association through being able to bolster and reinforce others, especially their Mate. I wonder\u2026 if the Essence minimum is lower here than in the preview. As I said before, the thing I like most about this is the sense of placing the power in the hands of the Lunar, but not being a predatory thing.<br /> <br /> Finally, an Essence 2 Charm; I was starting to wonder if they would all be 1. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It\u2019s getting off to a strong start with a name like Devil-Queen Rapture, and it\u2026 oh that\u2019s interesting, so it\u2019s a kind of ecstasy arising from their own social success, being able to reap motes back from it. I\u2019d never considered such a thing as a Charm for anybody, although it feels particularly suited to Lunars. The more I think about it, the more I\u2019m fascinated by what it says about the experience of being a Lunar, and how it might shape behaviour.<br /> <br /> Heh, Hunted Stag Majesty letting a Lunar respond to ambush with a flash of beauty or horror to throw them off; it\u2019s a nice idea for a Lunar counter to such a thing, and the sense of mythology behind the name, and I think the mechanical resolution of making an influence roll that can automatically block the ambush if successful is very vivid.<br /> <br /> Irresistible Silver Spirit goes a bit back to the body language stuff with the ability to make seduction attempts stealthily, that\u2019s nice and straightforward. Let\u2019s see, Protean Charm Honeyed Lips Inquiry allows for adding questions that are hard to not answer directly and honestly to highly successful seduction attempts, with an existing Defining Tie to the Lunar removing one of the conditions for resistance. I\u2019m liking this line of giving Lunars social Charms that can layer a few effects atop one another, especially bringing more out of seduction. It\u2019s like a thing of Luna\u2019s seductiveness being a base through which Lunars can accomplish a wider range of tasks.<br /> <br /> Hmm, wonder where Lion-Mouse Inversion can go from Predator-and-Prey Mirror\u2026 ah, that\u2019s neat, convey some of that sense to alter people\u2019s perceptions of another person that the Lunar interacts with. Feels like another kind of outsider social shaping thing. I\u2019m not entirely sure what the last line means\u2026 can the person being interacted with otherwise be made to see <i>themselves</i> within those boxes?<br /> <br /> Argent Muse Approach is a nice synthesis of some of the previous trends, namely support for another and pulling in an Intimacy from success, conveyed through the general \u201call eyes on me\u201d thing. I also like the social implications of standing at the side of another, and being so compelling that it makes them look better. Where Kneeling Lion Auspice does something similar, enhancing instil attempts to create positive Ties to somebody the Lunar likes; also my first new Bond Charm, making Decision Points necessary to resist forming the Tie. And then Eye-Catching Appeal goes and lets them basically apply a kind of social Defend Other action to intercept and redirect read intentions actions against allies, an influence that is harder for the reader to resist if they\u2019re already strongly inclined towards the Lunar\u2019s shape. So far, I\u2019m liking the implementation of this thing of Appearance as a means of making the Exalt really hard to ignore.<br /> <br /> Ah, so Myriad Graces Appeal enhances the capacity to improve the Excellency with stunts to\u2026 ooh, add that bonus to the Appearance benefit to social influence, that seems very powerful. And Incomparable Paragon Assurance lets them meditate to enhance Appearance? How does that compare to the prior Charm\u2026 right, so the prior one was immediate and enhanced another Charm, this one can add yet another dot to the Attribute, and lets Appearance provide extra dice in social rolls where it normally wouldn\u2019t. Nice bit of synergy there.<br /> <br /> Further enhancement to the pheromones is in New Friend Aroma, with a surcharge to change the emotional context for strangers from curiosity to friendliness and a desire to make overtures, helping add a distinct method of fitting in wherever they take root.<br /> <br /> Heh, I like the name of Obsession-Building Prana to go with that effect of instantly resetting failed seduction or threaten rolls and weakening the Intimacy benefits to Resolve a bit, further penalising Resolve if they have a strong Tie to the Lunar. Plus the facet of the unignorable presence of leaving an endurance presence in their minds.<br /> <br /> Starts going in a different direction again with Perfect Fear Scent, weakening Resolve against threats and relevant fear-based Charms, and creating an aura of fear that is difficult to fight or argue through; its Protean benefit of being used reflexively in an appropriate animal shape that wins Join Battle seems particularly useful for a Simple Charm. Then there\u2019s the charmingly named Inchoate Horror Embodiment, to do a bit of a Boggart thing of shifting through myriad shapes until getting at one that is close to their strongest fear\u2026 ahh, I see, it\u2019s a threaten roll that will automatically benefit from the character\u2019s strongest fearful Intimacy, without needing to already know it (and refunding a bit for characters that don\u2019t have such a fear). I like the description of how it might go for more abstract fears, as well as the whole Protean notion around the possibility that the Lunar is already the target\u2019s greatest fear.<br /> <br /> So, what does Wasp-and-Termite Dance do\u2026ohh, finally a Totemic Charm. Anyway, this can- ah, right, we\u2019re back into communication stuff, this one letting the Lunar function as a kind of conduit for a whole group of indeterminate size to communicate through such indirect means, although such diffusion makes it easier for outsiders to realise that something is amiss. Oh, and the Solar Bond can serve as an even more powerful channel for communication, letting them speak telepathically over tens of miles, which I think would make for some very nice interpersonal scenes. Obviously to get it as a Charisma Charm, you need the spirit shape of a eusocial organism; thinking on that, I\u2019m struck more with the nice choice of representing the forms of silent communication through things like scent and dance.<br /> <br /> Hmm, what mystical place of mystery is within Essence 3\u2019s Moon Beckons Tide? Ah, to summon people with appropriate positive Ties to their side from a long distance, improving their ability to make such the approach, and with a bit more Appearance lets them call even strangers who fit certain designated parameters. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s too coercive, I think the idea of them having a more dream-like quality is a good fit to Lunars, and I think there can be something alternately profound and really creepy in feeling a certain tugging impulse that brings you upon a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Not far now.<br /> <br /> Resplendent Soul Reflection, a bit more demanding in the prerequisites. Aww, the description of that opening line is nice. Heh, even if the application is a bit sinister, using the enchanted reflection to leverage influence against the enthralled person. In any case, this actually feels like the most witch Lunar Charm so far.<br /> <br /> Totem Beast Embodiment has already been seen, nice way of invoking animal forms. And back to fear with Divine Terror Avatar, spending motes, Willpower and initiative in order to make enemies with Ties of fear (don\u2019t even need to be strong ones) to make them incapable of attacking and drain their initiative if they don\u2019t run away, and even requires a Decision Point to resist it. And it\u2019s scene long and all. I guess Lunars have to be among the more effective exploiters of fear, particularly effective from all the ways they have to improve cultivating it. There have to have been more than a few armies that were beaten just from a solitary Lunar standing in terrifying mien before them (a nice culmination to a campaign of harassing attacks, especially if they go for things like leaving mutilated bodies to be seen), and can probably clear the odd town neighbourhood by making all the regular people flee.<br /> <br /> Heh, the names are starting to become rather elaborate. There\u2019s Visage Great and Terrible, said to impress the image of the Lunar deep in a target\u2019s mind, rendering it more difficult across several fronts to get them to overturn seductive or threatening influence (and it\u2019s Instant, so the Lunar doesn\u2019t bear any burden from doing so). Followed by Passion-Unbinding Bacchanalia (finally getting some of that Dionysian hero vibe I see), to inspire powerful primal urges of lust or fear in large crowds; the fear can be focused on something other than the Lunar with a stunt, and sets people fleeing in a panicked mob that won\u2019t stop until they\u2019re far away, and the lust side\u2026 is more subtle and carefully designated, focused on characters losing a sense of decorum, propriety or reservation rather than becoming mindless or predatory, as well as a compulsion to engage in displays to attract amorous attention if it can\u2019t be acquired otherwise. I think that wording covers the problem bases while still having a meaningful impact. Either way, it\u2019s got an unusual basis for resistance, depending on how high a character\u2019s Willpower is, and it\u2019s a very interesting Charm for something, well, more specifically Luna idealised to put out on people.<br /> <br /> Into Essence 4 now, starting with All-Consuming Obsession. Hmm, have any of these actually been Psyche Charms so far\u2026 I think I\u2019d have noticed. So, the first Psyche Charm. A Tie of fear or lust is instilled, and the person afflicted with it becomes incapable of effectively processing anything else, making everyday experience feel like a weird dream-like haze. And this damn thing is Instant, the Lunar doesn\u2019t need to commit anything and it can last forever unless resisted. And the only method for that resistance is for the Intimacy to be eroded, which can\u2019t be done without assistance, and even then has powerful barriers against it. This sounds like a very potent method to mess somebody up, for purposes of attack or sabotage.<br /> <br /> Eternal Companion\u2019s Embrace is quite expensive, what does it buy for that cost? Ah jeez, using seduction on a Tied person to inflict an Obsession that not only focuses them on the love of the Lunar, but can gradually wear away their affections towards anybody else, and eventually starts building a Principle of not wanting to share intimacy with anybody besides the Lunar. It makes changing the attitude towards the Lunar more costly and difficult, and that\u2019s only a first step towards the long road to recovering from the Obsession. I\u2019m all for Charms that do some dubious stuff, really messing around with people\u2019s relationships and emotions and general psychology, and even I find this one particularly nasty. It\u2019s good stuff.<br /> <br /> Oh dear, what is Soul-Scarring Monstrosity going to follow it up with? Errr, same general principle as above, but for instilling fear that breeds Paranoia, wears down other positive Ties with the terror that loved ones might just be disguises of the Lunar, and eventually builds a Principle of never feeling safe. Has the same difficult process to escape from. Yeah, this one is kind of worse, ehe hehe {nervous laughter} Nice\u2026 job. Hmm.<br /> <br /> Okay, bring it home with the Essence 5 Charms. Beauty to Break All Hearts, commit motes indefinitely to make all characters with strong loving Ties to have penalties to Resolve and increase the necessary Willpower to resist the Lunar\u2019s influence, and weakens their attempts to act contrary to the Lunar\u2019s will, known or speculated upon, and need Decision Points to be able to attack them. Under such an influence, weakening the Tie becomes impossible without particularly firm evidence that the Lunar has personally harmed the subject or something they have a Defining Intimacy to, and it has a Protean effect to have the same power (at the greatly limited scope of being seen by the subject) when the Tie is not to the Lunar\u2019s true identity, but one of their human shapes. I think this one is interesting for having a broad and enduring scope, without completely superseding a lot of prior Charms that are more focused.<br /> <br /> And finally, Devil Body, Terror Face, which has similar effect oriented towards fear, although not an exact mirror. Penalties to Resolve from fear are doubled, characters suffer from nightmares that require a difficult Integrity roll to reclaim Willpower at night, and eroding the Ties require successfully asserting themselves against the Lunar or their projects. The Lunar also gets to use some other fear Charms at premium costs. The Protean effect is about the same, but extend to animal shapes.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the Influence Charms. I think they\u2019re a very good showing so far; Appearance is redeemed quite a ways with interesting, distinctive and often powerful Charms (even at lower Essence), and even as a subcategory it\u2019s fairly broad while still keeping on message. It\u2019s actually interesting to see such diverse applications within such a category, effecting emotions, drawing attention, and even communications. I myself have a fondness for there only being one focused on writing, how it doesn\u2019t need to feel out of place but also doesn\u2019t obligate including a whole bunch of other ones (although I suppose there might be in some of the other Attributes). I\u2019m very interested to see the rest a little bit later (looking at the layout, I\u2019m hoping that there\u2019s not as much left to the other categories).<br /> <br /> Aw jeez, that took up 4,000 words? I might need to think of a different way to divide these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T12:03:17-08:00","id":1288966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it\u2019s lending validation to my speculation that Lunars would have a fair few to create phony Intimacies, as it were,</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if Appearance has more than Charisma and Manipulation.<br /> <br /> The beautiful and terrifying, after all, subconsciously give you an immediate reaction more than, say, the manipulative.<br /> <br /> Manipulation on the other hand, seems more about leveraging things your target already thinks to control their behaviour.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:15:43-08:00","id":1289011,"title":"","content":"Okay; the rest exhausted me, but I\u2019m determined to keep to my schedule, and there are a lot fewer Subterfuge Charms, I checked.<br /> <br /> First up is Subtle Silver Declaration, controlling concealment of the Tell. I\u2019m feel I won\u2019t be able to fully appreciate it until I see complete Tell rules and details, but for the time being it seems like low anima (but not no anima? Maybe it\u2019s a matter of anima increasingly revealing Tell) has it almost perfectly concealed, with those familiar having their attempts to find it weakened, and higher anima not automatically showing it and also weakening attempts to find it. Perhaps the Tell works as no anima: unseen, can be spotted by people that know of it, dim make it a bit more apparent to the unfamiliar, glowing shines a light on it. It\u2019s probably a little useful, but not to the point of being mandatory (even if literally every Lunar is capable of buying it).<br /> <br /> Shifting Penumbra Stance is back as a nice kind of disguise by obscuring in light, and I think its interesting that some forms of read intentions can still figure things about them out, and how beating the Lunar\u2019s roll only gives you awareness of the kind of Exalt. Ah, and Essential Mirror Nature, to help improve some of their disguise against figures such as Dragon Blooded. Let\u2019s see\u2026 Caste Mark and anima change appearance for some other Exalt, they keep their banner but it takes minor necessary cosmetic changes (probably hardly a problem, since many others can include some animal stuff). Ah, and they can alternatively do some god or fae stuff, even if they can\u2019t shapeshift into those. It\u2019s Protean, so you can get it to last longer if you\u2019ve got the shape of a particular Exalt to imitate (including taking their iconic banner), and Totemic so that a spirit shape with natural mimicry can take it with Manipulation.<br /> <br /> Moon\u2019s Hidden Face is curious. I guess it\u2019s a case for if you want to keep your hybrid body on standby, but want to retain discretion, or else you\u2019re a Lunar who naturally possesses mutations. Sprit shapes with camouflage get to learn it as Manipulation. I think I may want to seek some dev clarity on how this might be employed.<br /> <br /> Huh, I\u2019d wondered if Changing Plumage Mastery might return if it wasn\u2019t a Universal Charm. Oh, but it does use Many-Faced Moon as a prerequisite (makes sense for something that takes on a bit of its old function). So, it\u2019s a permanent extension of transformative prowess, allowing for alternately assuming a boring, forgettable appearance that is hard to recall or investigate, going back and forth between being Hideous as desired, freely changing the appearance of clothing (with the amusingly rare Appearance + Craft roll for making especially lavish changes, and can commit some motes to substitute their scent for that of another form. I\u2019m interested in digging out my copy of Manual: Lunars (the only of my Second Edition Manuals that isn\u2019t a pdf currently in my reach) to see how it compares to prior writing; I have the vague impression that it\u2019s overcome some shortcoming or made a bit of an in-joke.<br /> <br /> One of the Herd can be used to blend in with even a small group so long as one acts the part, only discernible through their Tell; The Totemic effect lets it be Manipulation for mimicry animals, although I have a mild impression it might include things like zebras. Then there\u2019s Scent-of-All-Nations Attitude, which is actually a bit reminiscent of a previewed Solar Charm that never made it to the final product, with that effect of causing strangers who encounter them to automatically assume they share a culture, or else present oneself as belonging to a specific one, and benefiting from associated positive Intimacies. It can be seen through with read intentions or profile character to discern information contradicting that identity, although doing so for one aping a specific culture is more difficult. What I like particularly is the flavour text saying that people gather the impression of shared background from things like subtle cues, and completely overlook stuff like language and appearance; it\u2019s just fun to imagine a Southerner going around with, say, an icewalker tribe who accepts them as a fellow without question. I was never too into the worldwalker thing for Lunars, but if it\u2019s manifesting in ways like this I\u2019ve no problem. It\u2019s Totemic in the same manner as the prior Charms.<br /> <br /> Up to Essence 2, and Enticing Butterfly Trick, that name sounds familiar\u2026 in with the pheromones again. Did we see this before, the effect also seems familiar\u2026 actually, I think it\u2019s vaguely similar to a Terrestrial Charm. So let\u2019s see if I have this straight, a Lunar concealing tracks or evidence can spray it with pheromones, people working to uncover them get a whiff and risk having a Tie instilled, which can also inflict a penalty on actually figuring out the lead. I\u2019m glad that something reminiscent of yet another Ability has been rolled into the mix, and a kind of animalistic thing to be put down behind a Lunar trying to evade detection. I can also see some characters that would deliberately draw attention and run, just to lure people into the little pheromone bombs.<br /> <br /> Subtle Chameleon Practice is something that Lunars would be absolutely remiss without, getting some of that Randall-style of skin concealment (although mechanically modelled in a way that isn\u2019t absolute), and a nice Protean effect to let it overlay and improve the camouflage of other animals; I like that sense of the two kinds of skin modification blending together to shore up one another\u2019s limits.<br /> <br /> Ah, and another delightfully witch-like one in the expected Mirror Slip Trick; literally merge with a reflective surface, becoming highly stealthy and difficult to effect. I was wondering about how vulnerable the actual object would be, but that\u2019s covered by the Lunar\u2019s Essence shoring up the structure; I had a mind that clear water was a bad idea for being messed up with ripples, but it seems a strong Lunar would give even that a bit of hardy surface tension. It\u2019s actually interesting to fix of this being applied to stealth, considering that Creation is likely to have few silver-backed glasses of the kind we\u2019re familiar with; most mirrors are going to be polished metal, which even at the best quality will produce a somewhat murky image (although the idea of lurking in the back or the corner of even clear mirrors is effectively creepy). A bit of higher Essence lets them move between different mirrored surfaces, and it even has an obscure use of functioning as a means of escape if some other power traps them in such a surface.<br /> <br /> Cuckoo\u2019s Nest Hospitality, that sounds rather ominous. Ah, it\u2019s basically similar to Scent-of-All-Nations, but for being assumed in a social role of prominence rather than a particular group, and letting it broadly function akin to a Minor Tie in addition to any relevant pre-existing ones for a given character. Its weakness is about the same as using Scent to imitate a specific nation, it only lasts a day but doesn\u2019t need its Willpower cost paid consecutively to maintain, and is Totemic for mimicry.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Fickle Lady\u2019s Shifting Star starting Essence 3\u2026 I think it\u2019s both more specific and less comprehensive than it (or its closest analogue) might have been in the past. It builds off of Essential Mirror Trick, and extends the deception to divinatory or scrying magic. I like some of the odd places it can extend to, such as making a power that only responds to a specific individual or type open for a properly disguised Lunar, even if it\u2019s primarily for things like keeping a Sidereal from foreseeing you doing something out of keeping with what you\u2019re pretending to be. And with everything it can do, it\u2019s fine to be unable to stop something that specifically breaks through disguises. Mimicry Totemic.<br /> <br /> Dreams-and-Expectations Stance\u2026 ah yes, another brought in from Glories, the one to let you be seen as the individual most expected or desired, modelled as a disguise roll with double 8s (I think it\u2019s good to differentiate from full shapeshifting), and very difficult to see through. It can even be used to maintain multiple disguises to different observers simultaneously, although keeping them from figuring out something amiss has to be a bit of a balancing act (if helped by the difficulty in seeing through it). At this point, it would be easier to say what Charms are <i>not</i> Totemic.<br /> <br /> Ideal-Made-Flesh Apotheosis is another means of raising Appearance through meditation, and even removes the Willpower cost of one of the prior Appearance-raising Charms. So that\u2019s three now which can do that, capable of giving a Lunar a particularly formidable Appearance, and all kinds of Charms that capitalise on that. It\u2019s certainly one way to set these Attribute Exalted apart from the Solar capacity to raise Appearance. Not Totemic.<br /> <br /> Huh, that\u2019s very new and strange, a Charm to make Lunars completely undetectable to taste and smell in Shadow Wisp Sublimation. The flavour text is a bit whimsical, but the effect is actually remarkably powerful, being infallible even against magic to enhance them. Then there\u2019s Moon-in-Well Emanation for\u2026 huh, that\u2019s really strange, making a god in their image by pulling out their reflection; wonder what the theological implications of that are. The mirror god has one of each level of the Lunar\u2019s Intimacies (with associated memories at their leisure, and otherwise a blank slate), all of their non-magical or social traits, and a decent mote pool. In addition to Materialize, Hurry Home and Mirror Slip Trick (which can be used for free), the player and Storyteller design a number of additional Charms depending on the strength of the Lunar\u2019s Essence, and able to grow stronger as the Lunar does as well as the passage of stories in which it played a major part; they even get to retain those Charms if recreated by the Lunar. For a final uncanny detail, bringing their reflect to life means the Lunar doesn\u2019t have it (must lead to persisting legends that Anathema on the whole have no reflections), and only returns slowly if the spirit is destroyed, with recreation only being possible when the reflection returns. I know it\u2019s only one Attribute in, but I feel as though all of the more wordy Lunar Charms so far have been a good deal more focused and personal than comparable ones for other Exalted. Not Totemic.<br /> <br /> Now, subterfuge\u2019s Essence 4, and what does Clover Can\u2019t Be Found do now\u2026 penalises trying to see through stealth, disguise or notice the Tell, and Ties that motivate the person to find the Lunar actually <i>weaken</i> their perceptions. That kind of turning strength into weakness and undermining other efforts\u2026 it\u2019s reminiscent of another old idea for Lunars, but somehow everything is holding together coherently. Ah jeez, in an animal shape with camouflage the damn thing saps successes. Got to be really hard to find Lunars at this level. Not Totemic.<br /> <br /> Shifting Constellation Raiment builds off of Dreams-and-Expectations Stance and Fickle Lady\u2019s Shifting Star to enhance the former prereq with the effect of the latter, without needing Essential Mirror Nature. Furthermore\u2026 this is very strange, the Star interference with magical effects such as individually calibrated locks respond in ways that the observer desires or expects, rather than what it would do for the identity of the disguise, although doing so can actually give the game away, so it\u2019s a bit of a balancing act.<br /> <br /> And Silver Ripple Mirage\u2026 I\u2019ve already talked about. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, the Subterfuge Charms are also interesting, and often delightfully weird. It\u2019s still relatively early, but I think the Lunars are making a strong showing so far for variety with a good thorough line.[/spoiler]<br /> <br /> Won\u2019t take too long to go through the last few of these Appearance Charms. Jeez I\u2019m tired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:29:25-08:00","id":1289017,"title":"","content":"One with the Herd makes me want to go play Assassins Creed 2 (when it started working with <i>any</i> crowd instead of just with some monks you dressed similarly to for the very reason of blending into groups of them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T19:19:22-08:00","id":1289061,"title":"","content":"Now, quickly finish Appearance off with the warfare Charms. Might have been judged a curious fit in the past, but hey, it\u2019s one of the Attributes that can be rolled for command actions. I\u2019ll be interested if they all strictly feel like they\u2019d go with War.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Start with Glorious Battle Presence, allowing some failed dice to be rerolled, and possibly gain Initiative if the result turns up well. Finally seeing a break from Totemic Charms for mimic animals, with the alternative Attribute of Strength for those with a pack hunter spirit shape; wolf, claw strider, various kinds of squid\u2026 I wonder if the discount for Caste or Favoured is necessarily worth it here, given you\u2019d still need a decent Appearance to make a good roll, but then maybe\u2026 hmm, I want to say that you might have an incentive to stunt Strength into your Excellency, but doesn\u2019t having the Appearance Excellency imply either a discounted Attribute or high rating\u2026 ah, no I misread it before, you don\u2019t need it at a rating if you\u2019ve got a few Charms in it, so a Lunar with two of the most basic Appearance Charms could use the Excellency to enhance their command actions, and then add their Strength to it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Wolf Devours Shepherd, a Charm to penalise commanders trying to order battle groups that see the Lunar (I like how they don\u2019t actually need to be fighting <i>against</i> the Lunar), and weaken them if the resulting roll fails. In other words, a scary Lunar off in the distance makes troops less receptive to instructions from their commander, and when they don\u2019t hear it properly they start to become restless and uncoordinated. Apart from the basic concept, I like how the Lunar hardly has to do anything, their mere visible presence capable of being a disruptive influence; I think that sets it apart from some of the image of action in any similar Solar Charm. And hey, warfare without War, delightful.<br /> <br /> Building from that is Panicked Herd Incitement, targeting the battle group itself when it tries to do anything, penalising it with fear, and causing the beginnings of rout if their action fails. Protean effect allows shapes with strong Ties of fear to remove successes instead of dice. Again, Lunar just has to be seen, doesn\u2019t have to do anything else, doesn\u2019t have to be under attack. I really like this idea that part of how a Lunar might conduct war is by basically conducting themselves like a fearsome spectre or omen of doom; a hooded, hatted and cloaked figure wandering the margins, a grim black dog on the crest of a hill, a lone raiton circling overhead and cawing incessantly. The troops see these omens, it awakens a nameless dread in their hearts, and it just takes one bad manoeuvre to have them feeling as though they\u2019re cursed or hunted and start disintegrating.<br /> <br /> The last two Charms were also Totemic, of course.<br /> <br /> Victorious Beat-King Spirit takes things along a different path. A more conventional path, by the looks of things, being able to reflexively make rally actions upon successfully landing attacks, with their own success capable of enhancing the roll (generously including 10s from both hit and damage rolls to determine the bonus). Followed by Diving Hawk Inspiration, following the logic of a Lunar\u2019s haste into battle guiding followers by allowing them to apply 10s from their Join Battle as successes to their battle group, with a high enough result letting them add a reflexive order action. Deviating from the last several, that one can be taken as a Dexterity Charm by group hunter totems.<br /> <br /> Now it\u2019s Essence 2, and Panicked Herd Incitement gets to develop into Pride-Scattering Approach, which actually does specify and invoke the Lunar being an opponent in battle, allowing attacks by themselves or associated army to benefit from a bonus success on a damage roll, increasing difficulty if that causes a rout check, and penalising attempts to rally if the enemy does start to flee, with Protean human and animal shapes weakening the rout check further. Given the order of activation, it seems like a bit of a gamble, but potentially one with some big returns.<br /> <br /> Oof, Rank-Sundering Carnage sounds nasty. Represents the idea that successful attacks are opening holes in the ranks to let friendly troops in by allowing half of the successes on a withering damage roll to be given as bonus dice to the troops who attack immediately. I like the image of a Lunar being like a heavy weight swinging away against the front line of an opposing army, or the idea that a Lunar can confer the benefits of good command just by being a roving force of destruction. It gives a nice image to the efficacy of some Lunar guerrilla armies.<br /> <br /> Argent Battle Exemplar lets a Lunar that has successfully attacked to automatically use excess successes as the result of a reflexive command roll, although doing so can remove them from something like a damage roll where they might have applied. So there\u2019s still the element of a Lunar Appearance-based commander giving orders, but they feel like they can function as a kind of instinct emerging from successful individual fighting prowess. I mean, Appearance is supposed to represent leading an army by example from the front anyway, but I like to extrapolate from this that the Lunar is doing so with a bit more precision (even apart from it being not just looking good at the front, but out of how well they land strikes).<br /> <br /> Oh, hey, it doesn\u2019t actually have to be used when the Lunar and troops are fighting a battle group, and if they are the Lunar doesn\u2019t even need to pay motes for it. Yeesh, that makes it sound particularly nasty to fight certain kinds of Lunar, if they\u2019re doing that to your army with impunity.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s the Essence 3 Charm Silver-Maned Warlord Glory, allowing the Lunar who is shining with their anima to employ that in being the standard for their troops, using it as the metric for bonus dice to command roles and an army\u2019s rout checks. On top of that, there\u2019s the option once per scene to expend some anima in order to reset rally for numbers actions, with the idea of pulling back together even far-fling troops. And those dice bonuses are <i>scene</i> long, with a relatively small commitment of motes. It\u2019s interesting how this resolves some of the old issues with such extended bonuses by being very conditional and variable.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the last of the warfare Charms. I feel as though my assessment of them can\u2019t be summarised more readily than what I said throughout.<br /> <br /> What <i>does</i> warrant summary is the end of the Appearance Charms. What I find most remarkable here is what it introduces about Lunar Charms as a whole, and a possibility that I had never before fully conceived of, fully visualised; that a single Attribute could encompass such range and diversity that a Lunar could conceivably focus entirely on that one Attribute, and have a large array of powers, with varied effects and applications and imagery, available to explore. Social adaptation and engagement, emotional cultivation, being the centre of attention, disappearing completely from attention, multiple identities, repulsing attack, sabotaging armies and leading troops.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s just from being a Pretty Kitty. Appearance 5 alone opens a huge vista of narrative worlds for a Lunar to explore.<br /> <br /> I finally understand how you do them as diversity and adaptability Exalted. In aggregate, the Charmset as a whole might not include a wider range than that of something like the Solars, but for an individual Lunar, the cross-section of competencies represented by the smaller investment in a small number of Attributes permits a higher capacity to be diverse and adaptable as a distinct example of a Lunar.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s quite remarkable, and I enjoy seeing it play out. Stuff like this is why I was averse to those playtest threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:03:50-08:00","id":1289096,"title":"","content":"A few thoughts I had on possible implications for the nature of Lunar social prominence and government, and the form of their competencies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levie, post: 22405467, member: 55610</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to go back and compare at some point, but I rudimentarily think it might contrast distinctly with a lot of Solar social Charms that are predicated on things like reading into and harnessing existing social systems, and arguing to people on matters of Principle, as well as cultivating forms of dedication to and being impressed with the Solar's person. I think there may be a lot of things to allow a Solar to govern or be a champion of people more systemically, allowing projection of power beyond their direct person.<br /> <br /> I've not yet seen the Charisma Charms, but just comparing Appearance to that there's a sense that a Lunar can be an extremely compelling presence, but it kind of necessitates them <i>being</i> present; they'd have to distribute themselves around in order to effectively exert influence, and the scope or form of that influence that they can precisely control or plan for might end up being limited.<br /> <br /> It paints an interesting picture of what some dominions might be like, and what prospective Lunar governance of the world could be.<br /> <br /> Mind, there could still be room for Attributes such as the No Moon ones to add some variations or additions. Still, some of this points to another interesting difference; for a Solar or Terrestrial, whatever things like Bureaucracy, Presence or Socialize say about their formats of government and social prominence, they're all consolidated. If you've got one of those Abilities, you've got its whole package. Other Attributes might make up for synergistic things that Appearance lacks, but it means that you need to stretch further afield to cover all of those bases (possibly barring the right spirit shape).<br /> <br /> So it's also a way of realising the idea of Lunars actually often being a bit more generalist, but in a more interesting manner than them not being good at any specific thing. Rather, with an Attribute such as Appearance, the Lunar can be good at a number of things, and be <i>very</i> good at them, but not be good at every <i>part</i> of any given field. You're very good at commanding armies from the front in battle, and sabotaging enemy morale, but don't have anything at all for strategems or siege engines. You could develop Intelligence to get at anything that might empower those, but is it not more convenient, more <i>you</i> to develop skills at infiltrating a society or becoming a celebrity?<br /> <br /> Heh, the ironic thing is that specialising in a small number of Attributes makes a Lunar an extreme generalist.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:27:12-08:00","id":1289116,"title":"","content":".....I will be very curious to see your reaction to some of the Charisma charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:50:02-08:00","id":1289188,"title":"","content":"I am so frustrated with the rate at which stuff is being put out. It is too much too quickly. It's going to start becoming overwhelming. There was nothing wrong with sequentially putting out a couple of chapters each week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T08:38:29-08:00","id":1289194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289188#post1289188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am so frustrated with the rate at which stuff is being put out. It is too much too quickly. It's going to start becoming overwhelming. There was nothing wrong with sequentially putting out a couple of chapters each week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it largely the same if it's 9 chapters over 4 weeks in 4 chunks or in 10 chunks? It's the same content over 30ish days, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T08:56:55-08:00","id":1289198,"title":"","content":"As there are 9 chapters, and the charms chapter is massive, I think they wouldn't be able to get it out in 4 weeks.<br /> <br /> But I can understand, when you're trying to write and analyse every detail, that's it's pretty overwhelming.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:02:21-08:00","id":1289199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289198#post1289198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As there are 9 chapters, and the charms chapter is massive, I think they wouldn't be able to get it out in 4 weeks.<br /> <br /> But I can understand, when you're trying to write and analyse every detail, that's it's pretty overwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is supposedly the same length as DBs and they got it out in 4 weeks. Even if the proportions are different, the total amount of content should be the same. So I don't think it'll be an issue, it's just in digestible chunks this time instead of a short novel once a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:47:03-08:00","id":1289212,"title":"","content":"Fair point.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I can't wait a whole week to get more. And at the same time, it did take me ages to get through the chapters they released for DB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:45:09-08:00","id":1289230,"title":"","content":"All right, Charisma. Got a tough act to follow, but I\u2019m interested to see what expansions to the Lunar social suite might provide. I\u2019m going to divide the Influence Charms at the end of Essence 2, just to make it more manageable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Already seen the Heart\u2019s Blood Charm, so skipping right past that to Argent Songbird Voice. Fairly basic Charm to modify addressing crowds, although the idea of changing the function of the Excellency strikes me as having interesting possibilities. Poised Lion Attitude seems to already getting to something more expansive even if it functions simply; reflexively making influence rolls, what might that look like?<br /> <br /> Despite the name, Arrogant Lion Bearing is the start of a new cascade, and is the first Attribute replacement Charm, allowing this one to be used to calculate Resolve, and I like how it uses the idea of such comparison through force of personality to have the option to increase Resolve in the face of less charismatic people. Then another root with Beast-King Dictates, allowing failures on influence rolls to get somebody to do something to be re-rolled; the Protean effect is interesting in being something that could thoroughly belong to the Lunar\u2019s default form and identity, expanding the parameters for dice re-rolls.<br /> <br /> And from that is Guiding the Flock, to double 9s on rolls to get people to act in a manner according to the standards of their own culture, with a handy little sidebar to provide an expansive definition of what qualifies as a culture, as well as what I think is a pretty good guideline on how to approach influencing a group\u2019s customs in play. I\u2019m remembering some things from previews, some that gave me a notion of Lunars effectively guiding people from a position as outsiders.<br /> <br /> Ahh, Herd-Strengthening Invocation, that was the one. Being able to cultivate a Principle towards a custom that can only be beneficial, by way of either praise or criticism. I\u2019m interested in trying to think through scenarios in which a Lunar who hates a culture would want to instil in its people a stronger value for one of its customs; maybe a form of sabotage if it\u2019s viewed as detrimental, maybe trying to get people to see its shortcomings. It invites intrigue, if nothing else.<br /> <br /> Heh, I\u2019d forgotten to consider things to interact with animals. Pack-Calling Cry which basically does what it says on the tin (albeit only with one animal at a time). I\u2019d also say that it is fairly accommodating with getting a large or slightly magical animal. I enjoy it having a bit of an uncanny edge in the way that the animal can arrive with unnatural speed. Personally, I\u2019m imagining it being particularly interesting for the Lunars of Luthe, but that might just be because I\u2019m picturing a clever little cephalopod or cetacean being very confused by why it\u2019s going and how it\u2019s suddenly becoming so much faster. Or maybe just a Lunar impressing a date by calling a nice bird to their side and having it perform a quirky trick.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Untamed Soul Unity, to form a familiar bond of up to two dots between an animal and a person (not necessarily the Lunar). That it functions much more strongly when used to benefit a Solar Mate, being able to make the bond permanent from the beginning and can connect a three-dot one, has me thinking in terms of one of the possible values they can provide being as a kind of intermediary between man and beast.<br /> <br /> Back to the bottom with Charismatic Lunar Trick to give double 9s for rolls based around providing emotions, especially for something the Lunar is feeling themselves. I find that a bit resonant with some of the Appearance stuff, that for all of Lunar dissembling there\u2019s something powerful that they can convey about what is sincere or meaningful about themselves. Or they can encourage a bit of that exposure in another through Rapture of the Nightingale, lowering their Guile if a Lunar inspires emotions that might naturally reveal their intent through resonance or interference.<br /> <br /> Crowd-Inciting Fervor also seems particularly strong as something revolutionary <i>or</i> Dionysian by inspiring those who hear the Lunar to feel rage and direct it at something they\u2019re naturally inclined against, with caveats against necessary Intimacies and requiring a Decision Point to not do so. I like the idea of ways in which this can be applied, whether it be helping people to get over fear or decorum or any other such restraint in order to feel allowed to express their frustrations or outraged, or inflicting anarchy by having a community just explode in the multiple directions of their individual rancour (especially if it\u2019s a Lunar that has been going around spreading such things beforehand).<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, Soul-Baring Testament is a Charm purely dedicated to the Solar Mate, and feels the most reminiscent so far of the old Background by providing dice to enhance influence rolls in line with the mate, as well as making it harder for others in future to disregard them. Mind, the Protean effect makes it wonderfully strange with the idea of the Lunar being able to benefit from the Resolve penalty if they\u2019re using the Charm while looking like their own mate. I\u2019ll also note the fun implications on how the Charm doesn\u2019t mandate positivity; if you don\u2019t like your Mate, you still get bonuses from going around trying to convince people that the Solar is a jerk and act against them. I wouldn\u2019t even view this still ending up with a Resolve penalty against that Exalt in future to be contradictory, with a few ideas metaphysical and interpersonal behind why the Lunar might still convey a bit of susceptibility: \u201cI agree this Solar is a jerk\u2026 but there does seem to be something a bit interesting about them\u201d.<br /> <br /> Beast-God Idolatry provides the first Charm to benefit a Lunar\u2019s crafting, and I think there\u2019s something wonderfully egotistical in the idea of a Lunar imbuing an object crafted in their image (for any of the multifarious values that can have) with a capacity to instil a Tie to the person depicted. Doesn\u2019t have to be positive either, so you could always use it to cultivate fear for your own benefit, or hatred of a still living prey that you want to sabotage.<br /> <br /> Shining Moon-Child Mark, that was previewed as well. As I said back then, it strikes me as the ultimate realisation of something suggested back in the days of Lunar errata, albeit less violent and less specifically amorous. I also like the sense that it has a certain confluence between the general thesis of Charisma as an Attribute and an animalistic quality of marking your territory, albeit in a more understated, mystical manner.<br /> <br /> Hard-Nosed Denial Style functions as an interesting kind of social clash, resisting an argument with an immediate counter that also has a capacity to make the other side respect your conviction. This one covers a couple of the trends that the Charms have been making good use of so far, dealing with problems sideways, Charms that are multi-faceted and able to convey an influence underneath their more direct function. It\u2019s neat.<br /> <br /> Oh, that was Essence 2. Okay, halfway along, more or less.<br /> <br /> Next there\u2019s Silver Soul Conviction, again with the Lunar\u2019s displays of themselves; ah, it\u2019s like that Appearance Charm, success reaping back motes, just this time for influence to uphold an Intimacy (if to a Solar mate, treated as maximum or one step higher). Yes, keep going with this idea that a Lunar can be empowered by revelry in their success, in living their truth, a surge of spiritual energy.<br /> <br /> Lightning-Calling Challenge builds upon Crowd-Inciting Fervor in a novel way; rather than inspiring anger towards what people have reason to be angry at, call all of that shit towards the Lunar herself. In particular for the sake of making hostiles incapable of attacking anybody other than themselves; I particularly like the way that interacts with area-of-effect attacks, that idea that they can only be made if the Lunar will also be hit. I like the way that it models the resistance, the sense that you\u2019re not actually overcoming the anger but ignoring the impulse to attack the Lunar specifically, and it\u2019s still a distraction from other endeavours. And there\u2019s a Protean effect to harness a pre-existing rage or hate to make the impulse harder to resist, and more distracting if it is.<br /> <br /> Now, Heart-Stirring Expression, a broader kind of emotional incitement, but still a kind of lunatic fervour, what with balancing the bonus to non-physical action in complement against making it harder to focus on oppositional action. I\u2019m curious, it\u2019s an Instant Charm and no other time span is suggested\u2026 perhaps the base inspire influence rules would provide more insight.<br /> <br /> It looks like it\u2019s going a bit bigger with Creation-Spanning Passion\u2026 so first, a bonus is provided when a Lunar is trying to guide somebody that they love, hate or otherwise with the same feelings in response, as well as making it easier to strengthen an existing form of that Tie. From there, there\u2019s how strong Ties allow both individuals to have divinatory dreams about one another (although a Solar mate shares those even with a basic Tie), so long as they have regular personal interaction. This one feels like an especially compelling application of the Charisma idea, the \u201csee me, know me, feel me\u201d thing. The fact that it\u2019s a two-way connection inherently conveys a fascinating sense that a Lunar can\u2019t open their heart to another without needing to expose a bit of vulnerability, but what I find most fascinating about this is the idea of using it on an enemy; the idea of a Lunar cultivating and strengthening a rivalry with a powerful Dynast, and then being able to divine information about their status and plans in dreams, at the cost of needing to deal with similar information being conveyed back. God, the implications of that\u2026 Dynasts who are aware of the connection, but keeping it under wraps for fear of being viewed as compromised, Dynasts who know how it might be broken but just can\u2019t help but find the intelligence provided too valuable to pass up\u2026 oh dang, you could do something like the Rey-Kylo visions from The Last Jedi with this (presuming a later Charm doesn\u2019t make it full-blown), and that stuff was when that movie really started to pop for me. This is a good one. <br /> <br /> Hmm, maybe I jumped the gun before and Herd-Reinforcement Stance was what was previewed\u2026 yeesss, that was the one, the idea of being a Lunar on the outside who is able to act on members of a culture through a provisional Principle of one of their customs. That idea that an external perspective lets one get through to a person via the patterns of their society, even if they wouldn\u2019t care strongly in everyday life. I think it can have a surprising amount of variation to help or hinder members of a group.<br /> <br /> Okay, not much left now. Lion\u2019s Voice Command finally gives something Totemic\u2026 did I see this before\u2026 anyway, fairly basic function, become loud enough to hear over long distances, cheaper if you\u2019re in the shape of an animal with Legendary Size, can be taken with Strength for spirit shapes that can intimidate. I like how it emphasizes the fact that it\u2019s a form of bellowing with the idea that the only influence that can come across being inspire and threaten; you\u2019re not making nuanced appeals to fulfil complex instructions while your voice is ringing in a person\u2019s ears.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Psyche seems to be coming earlier for Charisma with Moonstruck Reverie Trick. Getting a little neatly transgressive there, like a time-release Cupid\u2019s Arrow (albeit not in a manner I would expect for a Chosen of Serenity). Sure, that a Lunar has a capacity to grant themselves virtually any trait that they would instil an attraction towards in another\u2019s dreams, but there are surely many benign and malevolent applications to letting such a platonic or amorous love at first sight form for a particular person or random stranger. I also like how, while the Psyche effect creates the inciting incident and lets the resulting Tie skip to Major, it conveys no other obligations or endurance, so the affected character is free to act on it as they please and it can erode naturally if the relationship proves incompatible. Maybe it\u2019s the romantic in me, but it gives me the image of a situation in which a person learns that their infatuation started with a bit of witchcraft employed by a Lunar, but the person affirms that their wicked magic is not the reason why the relationship could blossom and endure.<br /> <br /> Going back a few steps to return to the standby of Lunars generating fear; from the way that it not only enhances a threat or instil action, but denies the protection of Intimacies of courage or fearlessness, I like how Silver Thunder Roar\u2019s basic enhancement still conveys a certain texture of striking on an instinctual level that the rational consciousness can\u2019t fully deal with. Then it\u2019s Snarling Outburst Rebuke to let a Lunar boost their own influence complementary to how another resists it, and I\u2019m seeing another trend in which Lunars can draw strength from a kind of mirroring of an opposing character.<br /> <br /> Another Psyche Charm for the attractively named Endless Nightmare Hunt, which has another multitude of effects; increase the grip that an existing Tie of fear has on a character\u2019s Resolve (that they don\u2019t need to see the Lunar bringing in another fun instance of the \u201cnameless fear\u201d element), making instil rolls to strengthen that Tie while observing the character sleep, and afflicting them with nightmares to deny Willpower regain. It\u2019s curious that it\u2019s an Indefinite Charm, but given how the different effects likely have to take place on different stages, I\u2019m guessing that it\u2019s intended for the dedicated stalker of a Lunar, marking an individual as prey to follow and harass and weaken over an extended period. It\u2019s good then to provide the victim with a process for fully shaking it off, and not too much of an expensive one.<br /> <br /> After something heavy like that, it\u2019s nice to see a return to something a bit more pleasant in Songbird\u2019s Eternal Refrain\u2026 although that\u2019s mostly just an impression given by the first line. The actual effect of resetting emotional influence rolls to instil or persuade, and weakening the response, can just as readily be applied to get another shot at somebody who managed to shake off your attempts to hurt them through it. I think the idea of getting a Willpower refund from a shape that a target has an emotional Defining Tie towards might be the most\u2026 marginal Protean bonus yet. By that I don\u2019t mean it\u2019s not fitting, or not valid or useful, just that it\u2019s a nice side bonus rather than something that can function in the core of the power.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s interesting that Charisma is getting more Psyche than Appearance, I guess it constitutes a more assertive Attribute. Anyway, Unceasing Hunger Affliction, what could this possibly entail? Heh, I like that image of a Lunar\u2019s eyes flashing with ghostly fire\u2026 so in the base form, an inspire roll to inflict a basic Obsession towards some good or service, that can fade after a few days if the victim doesn\u2019t fail a test against it; not as devastating as the Appearance Charm to inflict Obsession, but it is after all only Essence 2, and can probably be effectively inconveniencing under the right circumstances. It picks up a bit more with an Essence 3 repurchase, letting the original target turn it from an obsession into a social craze; it might only transmit from the first, but point it at the right strategic factor and it can effectively spread far. I\u2019m imagining the devastation a Lunar might cause from things like spreading a desire for some limited resource; a bit of rioting over shortages, a bit of market speculation that turns into a bubble. Immaculate monks are meant to serve as cultural enforcers, I can imagine that more than a few see sudden surges in popularity for a given thing as a warning sign of Anathema activity.<br /> <br /> Of course, even at the individual level\u2026 make a prince obsessed with a market you have cornered, and then leverage it against them.<br /> <br /> Finally for Essence 2 there\u2019s Argent Revelry Festival. In contrast to a lot of the other Charms for a society at large, this one is for when the Lunar is right in the thick of things, an active participant; by leading or taking part in a customary event, all other participants can be inspired with pride in their society or culture, and given a temporary pool of dice for social or mental pools in actions in service to that society. I\u2019m particularly fond of this Protean effect, and its specification of an animal shape; I\u2019m seeing Coyote from Gunnerkrigg Court leaping and laughing about in the revelry, for the sake of the Lunar potentially maximizing the bonus dice that they provide for their fellows and followers.<br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s good stuff so far. My conception of Lunar social activity and governance is filling out a bit, although not fundamentally overturned. So far, I think that Charisma Influence is a bit more focused than its preceding counterpart, but makes up for that with a bit more social variation, and it will be interesting to see any unexpected sub-categories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:54:23-08:00","id":1289233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289194#post1289194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't it largely the same if it's 9 chapters over 4 weeks in 4 chunks or in 10 chunks? It's the same content over 30ish days, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to keep up with the subjects as they come in fresh. I don't want to be left behind of surrounding discussion. I want to put out these reviews in a timely manner.<br /> <br /> I wrote close to 14,000 words in reviewing the first two chapter, spaced over four days. That's a bit tiring; a relief period before the next preview would be nice.<br /> <br /> Instead we got Charms immediately after. So I wrote close to eight thousand words reviewing the Appearance Charms in <u>one</u> day. That's kind of exhausting. Today I'm repeating that for Charisma. In the middle of that are shapeshifting rules I'll have to make a slot to look at.<br /> <br /> Then tomorrow, we'll get a chapter on dominions, followed shortly thereafter by several more Attributes.<br /> <br /> I liked the previews more when there was more breathing room between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-18-2019, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T11:09:14-08:00","id":1289236,"title":"","content":"Actually tomorrow we're getting traits and character creation. Shifting rules are a part of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T14:36:53-08:00","id":1289314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289233#post1289233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then tomorrow, we'll get a chapter on dominions</div> </div> </div> </div>Not this week! No reason to frontload all of the setting material for preview purposes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T15:07:43-08:00","id":1289323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289314#post1289314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not this week! No reason to frontload all of the setting material for preview purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, everything out of order.<br /> <br /> Whereabouts in the thread did I leave that rising existential scream?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T15:08:35-08:00","id":1289325,"title":"","content":"Okay, keep going through the latter Influence Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Essence 3 starts with Argent Glyph Enchantment, another Permanent enhancement Charm, this time for Shining Moon-Child Mark. It allows the connotations of the mark to be alternately or thoroughly supplemented with making it impossible to remove (my head immediately went to the diadem example, but its clarified to not work on objects), giving it a term or condition to prematurely end (probably almost entirely useful for when its being used to project an emotional connection that is hurtful to the marked person), more specific information about the intentions or nature of the marked person, and making the power of the mark only recognizable to specific cultures. I\u2019m remembering a thought I had in the past about the prior Charm being able to serve as the Lunar process for designating messengers and go betweens, and I think it\u2019s useful to have a means of elaborating on that.<br /> <br /> Hmm, more social enforcement stuff in Taboo-Enforcing Beast\u2026 right, so it\u2019s a persuade action that doesn\u2019t need to target an Intimacy, can be used reflexively and is used to dissuade somebody from acting in a manner contrary to a culture that the Lunar deeply values, but is in in all other respects identical to a normal one. It can be used carefully to force such a Decision Point if used to enforce a society governed by the Solar Mate, and the Protean effects has the interesting inclusion of a socially important animal as well as a position of authority. Not much else to say about this specifically, but thus far I\u2019ve liked the way that this line is being realised throughout Charisma.<br /> <br /> An anima cost for Captivating Siren Voice, eh? Why, that\u2019s a very strange idea of a power to keep people\u2019s attention fixed on a performer, compelling them to press as closely in as possible; want to be careful with that, lest anybody be crushed or trampled. I\u2019m guessing that the Defining Intimacy it can be exploited as goes beyond just the compulsion it creates to approach, although I imagine that there aren\u2019t a huge range of actions that can be leveraged from fascination with a performing Lunar. Heh, it\u2019s got to make for quite a scene when a person compelled to approach or follow the Lunar is actively trying to attack (at least until upgraded by repurchase at Essence 4). Huh, wasn\u2019t expecting the Totemic animal to be a small prey animal\u2026 between that and letting it be Appearance\u2026 could it be following the logic of something magnetically adorable?<br /> <br /> Pity that it excludes actual kitties, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, I\u2019m now struck with a point from before about how expansive a single Attribute can be, with how Totemic Charms can allow the right Lunar to push investment in one Attribute into even more spaces.<br /> <br /> Culture-Hero Empowerment\u2026 at this point I can hardly tell what I have and haven\u2019t seen previewed. Just focus on the idea that it\u2019s new\u2026 from the name, and long formed idea about Lunars having a particular culture hero association, my first thought would have been for it referring to the Lunar, but no this is about elevating somebody else to that position. What do they get\u2026 ah, still following the customs enforcement subject, empowering somebody around being a custodian of something specific. Others from the society recognise that in them, their Resolve is strengthened against attempts to influence them against their charge, they\u2019re better at ferreting out transgression and get people to seek amends when they do, and the Charm can be combined without cost with a Moon-Child Mark. Having an especially dutiful servant who endures through great struggle can feed back to a Lunar patron to the point of relieving their Limit, and a Solar mate governing the society in question can share those benefits.<br /> <br /> I remember now, a sense that this side of Lunar Charisma, of enforcing societies from within, gives me a certain impression of their sacred guardian beast quality.<br /> <br /> Huh, at this point, Eagle-Among-Sparrows Attitude is surprising in its simplicity. So it\u2019s just\u2026 influence made to align with the Lunar\u2019s cares or attachments, and costs some more Willpower to resist unless done so with an Intimacy at least as strong as what is driving the Lunar. I imagine that it ultimately has power disproportionate with the number of words it requires. But then there\u2019s Goddess Crowned by Horns, doing as much as it can to provide an exceptionally difficult and draining to resist influence roll aligned with something Major or Defining once per story; I\u2019m not entirely clear on the reset condition, but going by the assumption of it being used uncommonly this does feel like a particularly good thing to deploy strategically. It goes to my thoughts on Charisma being less diverse but more direct.<br /> <br /> Lion\u2019s Roar Rebuke now comes along to defy my prior assessment with a shouting attack Charm. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s the deadliest decisive attack created by a Charm, but a ranged, unarmed attack to inflict knockback is probably nothing to sneeze at. It\u2019s probably freaky to see in action, at least.<br /> <br /> Rolling back again for another emotion, Scathing Lunar Condemnation gives a non-Charm bonus based on the strength of a hateful Tie to threaten or inspire fear. Thousand Throat Howl follows that with the stark image of a Lunar\u2019s anima erupting from their throat with the scream of their heart\u2019s blood library, and the straightforward and extreme effect of making everybody but allies that hears it flee or seek safety without any reservation, to the point that they actually get a bit of bonus to do so. Also penalizes Resolve (I\u2019m guessing against the original threaten rolls) depending on comparative Willpower (with a better choice by Protean when in an animal shape that targets are scared of, or just plain enormous). I just like the elegance of this, the terrible simplicity.<br /> <br /> The revolutionary stuff gets furthered with Shattered Yoke Fury, going beyond inspiring momentary anger and into helping others form enraged Ties in the moment to apply against people trying to influence them, and then act on their new rage.<br /> <br /> Okay, so, in the run up to the game, some writers talked about how well-suited Lunars were to revolutionary stuff, and I had reservations. I\u2019m really glad to see how these things are ultimately realised; not in the sense of Lunars being Essentially champions of the downtrodden or personifying revolution (at least not specifically, directly), but rather in Lunar elements of powerful, fierce emotion, of transgression, of being anarchic, disruptive or simply external (even playfully tricky) elements, and a bit of encouragement for others, all blending together for powers that can readily be applied to those purposes. I\u2019m very much happy to be sold on this facet of them.<br /> <br /> And with that, it\u2019s into Essence 4. God-Beast Exemplar Spirit: enhances Herd-Strengthening Invocation with a hefty surcharge that allows it to cause those who have a Defining Tie (not a positive one) to the Lunar, causing their attachment to the custom to become a Defining Principle, that\u2026 jeez, becomes hard to erode and makes contrary influence unacceptable! And they need to spend a hefty amount of Willpower just to become capable of eroding the Intimacy. See, what I like about this is that it balances the capacity to create such a powerful Intimacy so quickly with the need to cultivate strong feelings about oneself, and, well\u2026 more than a few Lunars might decide it\u2019s easier to become hated than loved for the sake of this. The ogre who acts the bastard to make others look good. Yes, picture the Lunar who makes themselves despised, to act contrary to a value they want to reinforce, such that society leans into it just from viewing the hated Lunar as its antithesis. Fascinating.<br /> <br /> Heart-Affirming Tribute allows the Lunar to reward their chosen culture heroes\u2026 oh, actually no, it doesn\u2019t specify that, it can work for anybody that has overcome difficulty or danger for the sake of a Major or higher Intimacy, and creates a talisman imbued with the power of an Eclipse-Ok Charm. For most mortals, that\u2019s still going to be fairly weak, although more than they\u2019d have otherwise (but if it can still work for Exalted\u2026). It\u2019s as hard as an Artifact but its power can\u2019t transfer, unless the Lunar wills it so for another valid recipient. Its an indefinite Charm, so the Lunar needs to commit motes to maintain the power, although they have an easier time restoring the Charm if they allow it to lapse; alternatively, it\u2019s not necessary to pay the mote cost if it\u2019s used for one\u2019s culture hero, and at Essence 5 a mere two experience points can make it permanent. Furthermore, 10 gold craft points can be used in place of the original Willpower cost, and 10 white points in place of the XP to make one permanent. For some reason, this one puts me in mind of a Lunar in the role of benevolent fairy godmother; they see some young heiress defy family and tradition to escape the castle and abscond with her dearest love, the prince of the neighbouring kingdom (also in hopes that their eventual marriage will allow them to unite their kingdom and make war on their wicked neighbouring state), and rewards her with a rock or tooth or something to let her walk on mist or turn into a bird or something.<br /> <br /> And now for Essence 5. My expectations are high.<br /> <br /> Argent Anglerfish Lure, a particularly threatening name, and a Psyche Charm to boot. Adds a hefty mote and anima surcharge to Captivating Siren Voice, allowing it to increase the Willpower cost to resist and causing victims to pursue the Lunar heedless of any surrounding dangers, and penalised against defending themselves from such. Is Totemic in the same manner as the prerequisite. Yeesh, this one makes for an especially unnerving alternative to all of the fear Charms. It\u2019s like a follow the white rabbit kind of thing\u2026 especially if you literally go into the damn Wyld.<br /> <br /> And finally there\u2019s Divine Monster Judgment, to fully embody the sacred guardian beast (or terrifying taboo beast). Damn thing can last for the length of a story, although it can\u2019t be used sans a Solar mate. Dedicating oneself to a custom of the society that the Lunar is strongly attached to, and that the mate rules, they get greatly enhanced bonuses to Resolve from relevant Ties (including to the Solar), automatically succeeds to read the intentions of transgressors if their Willpower is lower than the Lunar\u2019s Essence, has enhanced persuade or threaten rolls against transgressors, can weaken the Join Battle of transgressors that try to fight <i>and</i> gets the opportunity to make a decisive attack that doesn\u2019t reset to base, aaaaaand gets one opportunity, upon beating a strong transgressor, to make a roll from which they can reap Willpower and shed Limit. I\u2019m not quite sure about the limited use; if it lasts for a story but can only be used once per story, is that in the event that the character drops to commitment? In any case, it\u2019s an impressive and fearsome Charm, something that seems very well suited to stories focused on a society\u2019s internal issues, and has interesting implications for why a Lunar might be motivated to place a Solar (nominally) in charge of something that the Lunar has been invested in.<br /> <br /> I mean jeez, imagine playing a fresh Solar who has to deal with a mate that wants to shanghai them into this. \u201cJust look pretty and let me handle everything.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the Influence Charms. I\u2019d say they\u2019re hefty enough to not require another category besides warfare. They\u2019re a good show, in all, effectively more flavourful than just being good Charisma (although all of the elements of forging connections to the Lunar\u2019s values and unveiling their inner self actually present that, and make it feel meaningfully different from Ability Charms), nicely distinct from Appearance, while still not overturning any major assumptions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Warfare won\u2019t take me long to gnaw through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T16:39:13-08:00","id":1289349,"title":"","content":"Divine Monster Judgement says &quot;a custom of a culture that she has a positive Major or Defining Tie towards, <b>or</b> that her Solar mate rules.&quot; not and. It works fine without a solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T19:46:02-08:00","id":1289385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289349#post1289349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Divine Monster Judgement says &amp;quot;a custom of a culture that she has a positive Major or Defining Tie towards, <b>or</b> that her Solar mate rules.&amp;quot; not and. It works fine without a solar.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"HTTPS://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/adventutetimewithfinnandjake/images/2/25/S2e24_the_lich_shushing_finn.png/revision/latest?cb=20120506135823\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T19:48:06-08:00","id":1289386,"title":"","content":"All right, almost finished the second Attribute.<br /> <br /> <br /> Gets right to the point with a name like Pack Leader Attitude; adds bonus dice to a Charisma command action (and with sufficient Initiative, reroll 1s) to allow one to adopt the attitude what is of a leader of a pack. Is Totemic in the manner of the Appearance War Charms, which I\u2019m sure most of these will be. Then there\u2019s Fearless Beast-Warrior Exhortation, doubling 9s on rally actions and adding the group\u2019s Might in additional dice; I guess that represents a kind of appeal to the strength lent by supernatural power. Followed by Vengeful Beast Triumph, to not only reflexively roll to rally a battle group that is routing or has taken damage to Magnitude (pop pop), but sap some Initiative from the enemy that did the damage, that the Lunar actually gets to keep for once. I like the picture for that of an unexpected reversal that gives an enemy pause and bolsters the Lunar\u2019s confidence.<br /> <br /> Lead the Pride takes things along a different direction starting with adding a non-Charm success to an order action, and then being able to roll non-Charm dice equivalent to 10s on the original roll, before a new tree starts with Unified Pack Tactic, which allows a Lunar to employ some of that positive reinforcement quality to start a fight by transferring some of their Initiative to a lower ranked ally, only needing to actually experience half of the loss if they win the fight order anyway (a little bit of good-natured cheating, I think). This is also the first one that is not Totemic.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I\u2019ve not often given much thought to Wits, but I\u2019ll be interested in seeing what that might do with Join Battle here (assuming that\u2019s the correct Attribute). Mind, I\u2019ll have to wait until the very end to see it.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s funny to have to remind myself that some of these Charms are growing out of crossovers between sub-categories, like in Rampage-Unleashing Provocation. With that, the Lunar is able to employ positive or negative reinforcement on an ally who must be strangely willing, but also assert their (unmodified) Resolve against the influence, in order to be whipped into a battle frenzy that steels them against fear and enhances Strength, but makes them incapable of retreat or surrender unless they spend Willpower to end the experience. Relentless Lunar Fury is a Charm that still exists, and I\u2019m curious about how it must function given that an advantage of this Charm is triggering it immediately (unless the benefit of this stacks with that, and it\u2019s simply cutting straight to the heart of matters); other Exalted like Solars can trigger their own battle fury powers from it.<br /> <br /> Into Essence 2 with Lessons of the Winter Wolf, through which a Lunar can briefly train a battle group to have bonuses against fear and ignore some of the effects of deprivation and fatigue, but only fleetingly, lasting for a single battle or a week if unused. Lunars whose spirit shapes have a Berserker Merit can learn the Charm with Stamina, and its benefits can also be blended into (and made longer lasting within) the following Charm, Wolf-Pack Training Technique. That lets a Lunar spend a month training a group to give it slightly improved Drill, Willpower, Join Battle, attack and Parry. I\u2019d want to put these side by side with the Solar training Charms, but my cursory assessment suggests that Lunars might be better at bestowing a force with fearlessness that provides it with raw power, but not quite as much discipline and specialized battle tactics. Still, those might just be the province of Intelligence, which is fine; as I\u2019ve said, I love the idea of distributing fields of competence around Attributes like this.<br /> <br /> Now then, Crimson Fang Mantle to cover attacking a foe that has been rendered vulnerable, doubling 9s for command roles to attack an enemy with lower Initiative (with the commanded battle group\u2019s Might counting towards its rank), a nicely flavoured kind of battle tactic. It\u2019s back to Strength Totem Charms again. Then there\u2019s Battle Anthem of the Lunar Exalted, to inspire fury in their allied armies with a fight song that enhances their attack and damage, strengthens the experience of enraged Intimacies that matter to the fight, and bolsters them against rout, although the Lunar maintaining the song can\u2019t do anything else that isn\u2019t reflexive (which isn\u2019t as much of an inhibition as one might think to a Lunar, I believe).<br /> <br /> Into Essence 3 with Starving Beast Bloodlust, allowing a Lunar to provide further inspiration for a group that has experienced some of their Winter Wolf training, letting them benefit from perfect morale, increased Resolve against fear or influence to stop fighting, and the Lunar will even get bonuses to their commands as the battle group might wear away in a fight.<br /> <br /> Raiton\u2019s Banquet Assault allows calling for an attack that can be decisive in the battle, letting the successes of their order be added as dice to both attack and damage rolls; it can only be used once per scene, but the reset condition of their allies incapacitating an enemy or causing an enemy army to start breaking down is not too onerous.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Wild Fury Awakening is the first of these to be Protean, and\u2026 ahh, it\u2019s building off of animal summoning Charms. Simply put, call together lots of animals (of a type you can turn into), to arrive in 20 minutes or less; the number you get depends on how big and dangerous what you\u2019re calling is, with the stronger ones in smaller numbers, and a mere recommendation that the environment has an impact on how many are called (probably still within reason). If you call pack hunters, they even get very good Drill. The animals can hence be commanded, though on their own they\u2019ll only attack foes. Oh hey, they technically don\u2019t even need to be called for a fight, although commanding them for something else requires a regular influence. Still, it\u2019s nice to know that a Lunar can call in a few dozen squirrels or whatever, if they should ever need them. Actually being in the shape of the animal they\u2019re calling upon allows them to act as a more powerful commander. And hell, even for a weaker animal, between their Drill and the extra dice provided from a Lunar\u2019s commands, they might still be a bit formidable; might be that flock of pigeons can do a bit more damage to your flying machines than just blocking up your windscreen. Heh, they thought an army of pigeons was tonally dissonant at the end of Hunchback of Notre Dame?<br /> <br /> Shit, I\u2019m really attached to this now\u2026 yeah, screw tyrant lizards, go into battle guiding a flock of pigeons. They won\u2019t be so weak when you\u2019re telling them to go for the jugular, and they can fly and all. You also get to laugh when your enemies initially think it\u2019s silly, until they\u2019re left writhing with their eyes pecked out.<br /> <br /> Them or bats. \u201cWhen you\u2019re a bat, you\u2019re a bat all the way, from your first starting stat \u2018til the turn you decay.\u201d<br /> <br /> Finally, there\u2019s Invincible Beast-Warrior Empowerment, since Charisma actually gets an Essence 4 war Charm. My, this is formidable; convert all of the dice bonuses from Size, Might, Drill and <i>command</i> actions directly into successes! To numerous battle groups within a certain range at the same time? And ones commanded directly get hefty bonuses to morale (or extra Might if their morale is perfect). Sure, the Lunar needs to keep paying Initiative each turn to keep it going and it\u2019s only once per scene, but damn, use the Excellency and other Charms to put enough dice into your difficulty 1 command action and let a battle group build directly on those successes, they probably won\u2019t need to last very long. Your pigeon armies will certainly be thankful for the addition.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, the Charisma war Charms are suitably impressive. Not quite as personal as the Influence Charms, but you\u2019re not here for friendship, you\u2019re trying to accomplish an objective. In all seriousness, I both like it being more directly military than Appearance, and still having room for some unique weirdness with the likes of calling animals and making battle music.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aaaaand Charisma isn\u2019t done. I thought it was only two categories, it instead has the much awaited Territory Charms. Heh, I had caught a few references, but I assumed people were just speaking in anticipation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dare I fit in one more category?<br /> <br /> <br /> Eh, it\u2019s not that long, I might as well polish it off here, and I didn\u2019t need to write too much for Warfare (and I\u2019m pretty sure about half of that was brought upon myself by rambling on about pigeons).<br /> <br /> <br /> So, what are the beginnings of what a Lunar can do with Territory?<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm, a little nod to the very old notion of giving Lunars the Merged Keyword to allow greater accessibility for a smaller number of Attributes\u2026 so Boundary-Marking Meditation can alternately be a Wits Charm. The mote cost is hefty, but it\u2019s Instant and Essence 1, so I can hardly see cause to complain. So a Lunar can claim an area of up to their Essence times ten square miles (for a starting Lunar, that\u2019s still about a mid-sized town) as their territory, so long as they \u201cfully master\u201d it, defined as having travelled most of it, been at least accepted by any resident human communities, and have the consent or submission of any other supernatural beings; I like the story driven elements behind this, although I do want to closely compare it to past forms when I get the chance. Once that control is secure (with mastery, apparently the Charm merely requires staking the claim, which is established immediately), the player designates three qualities fitting the nature of the territory, after which actions supported by those qualities get the benefit of a specialty, and actions opposed by it a minor penalty. The ruling Lunar never experiences the penalty, and can withdraw benefits or penalties to others they perceive as they wish. Should the nature of the area change, the player can reassign qualities, and Lunars can hold a fairly decent, but limited, number of territories simultaneously. The benefits are simple, but still flavourful, and it is after all just the first step.<br /> <br /> It's followed by the specifically Charisma Charms Moon-and-Earth Blessing, in which a Lunar spends the duration of a night wandering an area (either fairly small or the full size of a claimed territory) placing marks to imbue its landscape with Essence, and increasing the general hospitability of the place; foraging, sheltering, navigation and surviving hazards (even in a barren climate) all benefit from bonus successes, and there are nifty cosmetic features, such as night-blooming flowers, will-o\u2019-the-wisps or odd flocks of owls. While an Instant Charm, it only lasts around a year for normal spots, but endures for the lifespan of a Lunar territory. I think this one lends itself well to what a Lunar might do for guerrillas and communities that flock to their banner, and I like the imagery of it.<br /> <br /> Going straight to Essence 3 (and with Creation-Spanning Passion as a prerequisite) gives Dream-Shrouded Wilderness, through which an area can be imbued with an influence action that will play itself out in the dreams of sleeping residents; while it only affects a given person the first time they sleep, the effect can last to target new visitors as long as the Lunar keeps the motes committed, and visits occasionally. It can also be imbued with Moonstruck Reverie Trick (the cupid Charm) to also give sleepers a capacity to fall in love per the Lunar\u2019s specifications. There are a few interesting implications and applications to this; strategically claim a territory that people are intended to come to later to widely and covertly influence them, have a distinct means with communicating with subjects or neighbours, make your influence felt without ever needing to make personal appearances, and (more skeevily) micromanage a community\u2019s love life a bit. Really, just add a bit to the mythos of an area, associated with a Lunar or otherwise; don\u2019t go into the Whispering Woods, people have been known to come back out of it changed. <br /> <br /> King-of-Beasts Sovereignty then goes in a direction informed by Charisma themes of animal communication and social reinforcement, by broadly targeting local animals of a particular species in an area enchanted with the Moon Blessing to create an enduring tie of loyalty to mortal inhabitants (strongest in a Lunar territory), that plays itself out as voluntary action to protect, work for and generally beneficially live alongside humans that treat them appropriately. It can only last a story, but well-treated animals might stick around voluntarily. I get a nice image from this of something of a more Arcadian image for a Lunar homeland; it reminds me of the Smurfs, for some reason. In any case, it\u2019s very pleasant.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m happy about the callback in Songline Legend Runes, a Charm building off of the one for placing a characteristic mark on people. The Charm is modelled as a permanent enhancement with surcharge, but I wonder if it can be applied retroactively, or if the Lunar would have to relinquish and reclaim the territory. Mind, there\u2019s no reference to it growing with the Lunar\u2019s Essence\u2026 for important ones, it\u2019s probably good to relinquish and reclaim it. With this, that can include adding special markers that give it the quality of a Moon Mark, both projecting the emotional context and adding as another source of minor benefits. Mortal inhabitants get to proactively mark themselves in like manner with the Lunar\u2019s consent, and native spirits are fully susceptible to either effect unless they\u2019re fully opposed to the Lunar. Not much else to say about this one, it\u2019s just a nice further characterisation to territories (although the visual element is making them more interesting to me than they have been in the past).<br /> <br /> Ah, something nice and ominous with Omnipresent Monster\u2019s Lair, a Psyche Charm. While within a territory, a Lunar can enhance Endless Nightmare Hunt to apply its effects to any applicable characters throughout the area (even if they enter after it\u2019s been initiated), without needing to be personally present for them. They\u2019re freed if they depart, and the Lunar has to stay, but considering how transgressive that Charm was, this feels like a very effective way to make a Lunar\u2019s domain a distinctly threatening and unwelcoming place, with minimal effort on the part of the Lunar. Heh, it reminds me of something I said recently, about the idea of a Lunar going to ground in an area that enemies would be cautious or foolish about following them into.<br /> <br /> Conversely (and at Essence 4), Nature\u2019s Seductive Lure allows for a rather hefty surcharge to the Siren call to designate a feature of the territory (glowing with uncanny light) as the thing that will draw people\u2019s attention. It can only last for a few hours, but otherwise requires no effort on the Lunars part, which might free them up for other activities. I\u2019m picturing rummaging through an army\u2019s camp while they\u2019re all off beguiled by a very pretty rock surrounded by talking trees.<br /> <br /> Finally, there\u2019s the Essence 5 Charm Living World Embodiment, for the blue-feathered, red-breasted Lunar who wants to play Fisher King. Oh, it\u2019s a Permanent Charm, that\u2019s very nifty. So the Lunar\u2019s territories all get health tracks, and while within one a Lunar gets the option to shunt up to half of any damage applied to themselves (or the worse detriments of disease) to the territory, which will manifest itself as the despoiling of the land and native flora and fauna (maybe the occasional dramatic surge of red in bodies of water), making Survival actions there more difficult, and diminishing the quality of its natural resources for Craft. It can heal over time, more rapidly if it was Moon Blessed, or if the Lunar forgoes some of the healing of their body. On top of that, there is the option to treat such Lunar provided healing as a means of averting things like curses or disease in the area, as well as letting it enhance the Moon Blessing in an otherwise undamaged territory to greatly increase the local fertility, bringing it to unnatural heights. Setting aside the strategic values of this Charm and the ways in which it can enhance the quality of a territory, I just like the setpieces that it can lend itself to; a Wyld Hunt in battle with an old and mighty Lunar in the heart of their dominion, the Lunar enduring terrible damage as the landscape around them withers and cracks, until everything around is finally rendered utterly barren before the Lunar is finally overwhelmed and succumbs.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the end of Charisma. I\u2019d say the Territory Charms did a lot to help bring it up to the level of how impressive Appearance was.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll read about shapeshifting stuff when it\u2019s in the Traits chapter preview tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T20:08:38-08:00","id":1289393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, there\u2019s the Essence 5 Charm Living World Embodiment, for the blue-feathered, red-breasted Lunar who wants to play Fisher King. Oh, it\u2019s a Permanent Charm, that\u2019s very nifty. So the Lunar\u2019s territories all get health tracks, and while within one a Lunar gets the option to shunt up to half of any damage applied to themselves (or the worse detriments of disease) to the territory, which will manifest itself as the despoiling of the land and native flora and fauna (maybe the occasional dramatic surge of red in bodies of water), making Survival actions there more difficult, and diminishing the quality of its natural resources for Craft. It can heal over time, more rapidly if it was Moon Blessed, or if the Lunar forgoes some of the healing of their body. On top of that, there is the option to treat such Lunar provided healing as a means of averting things like curses or disease in the area, as well as letting it enhance the Moon Blessing in an otherwise undamaged territory to greatly increase the local fertility, bringing it to unnatural heights. Setting aside the strategic values of this Charm and the ways in which it can enhance the quality of a territory, I just like the setpieces that it can lend itself to; a Wyld Hunt in battle with an old and mighty Lunar in the heart of their dominion, the Lunar enduring terrible damage as the landscape around them withers and cracks, until everything around is finally rendered utterly barren before the Lunar is finally overwhelmed and succumbs. </div> </div> </div>Fun alternative, beat your enemy to a place they want in time to claim it then watch the looks on their faces when they realize they can no longer hurt you without wrecking it themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T21:05:29-08:00","id":1289407,"title":"","content":"Oh snap, I can write on my browser at the moment!<br /> <br /> Anyway, a sufficiently canny observer might realize that the Lunar can lose that effect if they should be forced out of the boundaries of the territory.<br /> <br /> With Appearance and Charisma side by side, I see some very interesting characterizing trends for them that really set them apart from one another, and from a lot of comparable Ability Charms.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, Appearance is all superficial. It's very heavily focused on raw, primal emotions, on controlling the surface level perception of you and projecting that forcefully outwards. Even when the Charms aren't actively about subterfuge, the underlying Lunar remains obscured beneath them. A lot of it might even be viewed as shaping one's image into a kind of shield or intermediary, letting people perceive and interact with that while holding them at a distance.<br /> <br /> Charisma has more nuances, and lets you burrow yourself a bit more deeply into places, but is counterbalanced by needing to put more of yourself out there, and thus leaving some more of yourself exposed. So many of the Charms are based on empowering things along the lines of what you care about, but the consequence is that it requires you to care about things, and the right observer will have better avenues for figuring out what those things are. The Charms for interacting with societies in particular stand out there, with the degree to which you need to be invested, need to interact, even if it's making yourself look bad for the sake of cultivating an improvement.<br /> <br /> I'd say that's why it has these Territory Charms; in simple terms, it's driven a lot by home being where the heart is.<br /> <br /> (My giving more words to Charisma is largely because it's fresher in my mind)<br /> <br /> Going from that, I'm guessing that a major line of Manipulation will be about getting ahold of the Intimacies of other people, of drawing power from them, harnessing them to the Lunar's ends, twisting them against the people that hold them. If the heights of Appearance can burn an image of yourself into a person's soul where it torments them, and the heights of Charisma can let you fiercely reprimand people who infringe upon your cares, I would speculate that high level Manipulation Charms can curse a person so that the objects of their own dedication or adoration destroy them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T00:44:32-08:00","id":1289443,"title":"","content":"That sounds like reasonable conjecture about Manipulation to me.<br /> <br /> Also, the reason I was curious about your reaction to some Charisma charms was that post you quoted yourself making. Appearance does seem to need to be Present to be Effective (mostly), but Charisma has a number of &quot;delegation&quot; tools, like Culture-Hero Empowerment and the Territory charms, that let a Lunar exert their will over a group without their direct presence and may well heavily influence the lives of people they will never know.<br /> <br /> You make a good point about Charisma requiring that you put yourself out there though. Even if you can delegate everything, it's still presumably important to you and can thus be held hostage or attacked to draw you out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T06:00:56-08:00","id":1289483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289443#post1289443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Appearance does seem to need to be Present to be Effective (mostly), but Charisma has a number of &amp;quot;delegation&amp;quot; tools, like Culture-Hero Empowerment and the Territory charms, that let a Lunar exert their will over a group without their direct presence and may well heavily influence the lives of people they will never know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that even those are very personal in scope; the Territory Charms that don't require your presence at the time still being more broadly emotional, and in terms of what they're appointed to do and how, the culture heroes are kind of just substituting your direct presence for the presence of another impressive figure.<br /> <br /> As for the contrast between Appearance and Charisma, what really gets them going is how they're unified in the person of the Changing Moon Caste Lunar.<br /> <br /> Just going by those two, I'm seeing a character like a fortress, able to put up layers of walls around their personality, but opening them up at will enough to project their true values out upon people, but closing them again in the face of observers, who looking too closely just get a blast of that raw emotion.<br /> <br /> The idea makes that Caste more compelling to me than it has ever been. For one thing, it effectively feels like it fulfils the old promise of their vaunted social mastery. In some respects, it makes them feel stronger in that arena to me than the Zenith and Eclipse Castes. At least in terms of a degree of focused dedication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:42:32-08:00","id":1289564,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I have an opportunity to post normally here... possibly throughout the rest of the book...<br /> <br /> I've gotten kind of attached to my current procedure. I think I'll keep it going for the majority of the book... but can make a single, ritualistic concession, with the light first half of the current preview.<br /> <br /> Now...<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Okay, so releasing these chapters ahead of the Dominions one isn\u2019t how I\u2019d have done it, but it is done, and I may as well capitalise upon it. After having had to power through entire Attributes over the last couple of days, going through both of these would actually be fairly relaxed, and if I can get it done quickly I can actually give myself a break in which to play more Xenoblade.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(I didn\u2019t get a chance to actually play it, given how much I had to write; half of it was just spending 1500 words describing battling a herd of dinosaur cows. Also having lunch and playing N64 with my brother.)</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Just going past the nice art of a person being haunted by terrifying Lunar apparitions\u2026</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">So, chapter four, Character Creation. Fairly standard start, concept and Caste (and Silver Pact affiliation, if any), spirit shape (referencing again that it can be an animal with personal or cultural significance), the Tell (get into that more when it\u2019s described in detail). Already knew about the arrangement for Caste and Favoured Attributes and love the variations it can provide, and checking\u2026 yes, Lunars get one dot more per category each than Solars do. I\u2019m kind of interested in what the groupings mean for the slightly different arrangement of traits to character type; like, you could be a Full Moon Caste who Favours Appearance, make social your primary category, and then start with fours in all three of those Attributes. It certainly plays into my past thoughts that Lunars need less investment to access a greater variety of their powers.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Abilities are simpler, of course, not even having a Favoured category now (no mandatory Survival now), although they still get a generous quantity to distribute. They actually get as much as Solars\u2026 still have the limit to three without bonus points, but not being Ability Exalted makes that less of a concern. Come to think of it, character creation might be more generous to Lunars than Solars and Terrestrials, because they\u2019ve got a smaller number of important things to distribute dots between, and don\u2019t need to dip into bonus points to maximize those traits. Between that and the range of Essence 1 Charms\u2026 I guess it goes some way to making up for having no equivalent to Supernal Ability.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Merits are a lot simpler, just straight up get 10 dots. There\u2019s the sidebar describing the basics of the Solar Bond here, but it seems to me that this would be the ideal spot to describe how it can function as an Ally. And fifteen starting Charms; no more than usual, but a Lunar will have a good range to select from.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A few suggestions for starting Intimacies, including something that might express their personal rage, choose a Limit trigger (very interested in seeing what their Great Curse is like). And 15 Bonus Points, for\u2026 I\u2019m not quite sure how to compare the costs of these\u2026 Solars measure them according to whether they\u2019re primary, secondary or tertiary (with the first two being\u2026 more expensive, for some reason), while Lunars do flat costs by whether or not it\u2019s Caste or Favoured, with those being fairly cheap. One thing I can see for that is being able to bring the secondary category filled with Caste Attributes up to par with a primary one with one of the Favoured\u2026 and the other Favoured Attribute in tertiary\u2026 interesting. While it also includes the unique capacity to spend some points on latent abilities for animal forms, which seems reasonably priced.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">An interesting little sidebar describing how a starting mortal template might be modified by Exalting in play. Aaaand the finishing touches, establishing that the default for Lunars is also starting as somebody very new with Essence 1. Given their setting place, I do think that there can be a lot more traction for the more developed character creation rules, even if there\u2019s something attractive in the idea of playing somebody who experiences introduction to the Silver Pact\u2019s customs in play.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Summaries are fairly boilerplate, but I\u2019ve always liked reading their basic descriptions of Caste and Aspect\u2026 they\u2019re a bit more focused on describing roles than I\u2019d like, and I wish the other two had followed the Full Moon lead of describing in terms of what they use to overcome enemies and obstacles. Still, the roles and traits encompasses within each Caste are fairly broad and numerous, and the No Moon description sounds better than usual; to be honest, I\u2019ve often found \u201cshaman\u201d to not be entirely fitting.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">All right, show me these Traits!</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Really interested in the new Merits\u2026 so Heart\u2019s Blood goes up to three dots, and I think it\u2019s clever to designate it in references to the Familiar Merit. I think that two dots gives the most bang for your buck, although I might just be underestimating the value of another two or three high-value animals. In any case, I think the Merit is fairly generous with starting animal shapes, and you have no damn excuse not to include at least one bird! Also, given some ambiguities in the past, I like the option to add another dot on to increase the range of environments the animals can come from.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Skipping ahead a bit\u2026 I do think it would be nice to follow Second Editions lead and provide a sidebar of examples per environment, but I suppose word count is also at a premium. {thinks a bit} Also there\u2019s going to be a chapter later on heavily dedicated to animal write-ups, a sidebar might be redundant.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Good, a Merit to designate acquired human shapes. I know that in the last Edition, Lunars didn\u2019t start out with that power, but it was still kind of an oversight to not have anything clarifying what one might start off with when it could just be taken as a starting power. In any case, I think Stolen Faces might be even more generous than Heart\u2019s Blood, although that\u2019s probably balanced a bit by a lot of human shapes not being as useful as animal shapes. Yeah, take it at three dots, start off with ten insignificant faces to hide behind and one important figure\u2026 just checking back in character creation\u2026 oh wait, that\u2019s about your Intimacies, not another character\u2019s to the player\u2026 I guess it\u2019s implicit that an important shape carries some Intimacies that at least a few Protean Charms can capitalise upon.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ah, right, this is where it describes how Solar mate can be a five-dot Ally, fair enough. Description of Backing for the Silver Pact, the cost for Command over a beastfolk army, having a shahan-ya as a Mentor (I think it\u2019s interesting to suggest having them free if it\u2019s for a whole circle). And how to have their special magic children as Retainers.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ahahaha, I had not considered that the Traits chapter might be extended significantly by Supernatural Merits. I can probably bomb through most of these, don\u2019t need to describe every single one in detail.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hmm, why doesn\u2019t a snake tongue as a sensory organ stand out to me more\u2026 it makes absolute sense, and feels as though it was around before, but I can\u2019t remember it offhand. Anyway, like the description of precise sense of smell.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I like the feel of the Burrower Merit\u2026 ah, now Centaur is something that I was thinking about as I went to sleep. There\u2019s been some discussion of the idea of that being the model for a war form/hybrid body in the past, and I argued against it on a basis that I found it kind of silly. But then Hybrid Body Transformation came along with its image of making the form more diverse, and it was thinking about that which led me back to the subject of centaurs, in a mindset of \u201cyou know what, that actually seems perfectly valid to me now\u201d. Then I started thinking about those stolen Greek carvings that I saw once in the British Museum; amazingly designed, entirely in the wrong place. Anyway, how does this work\u2026 ah, the character is able to treat themselves as riding a mount, which given the more intricate rules for that now seems like a pretty good benefit.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Constricting body is neat\u2026 I like the variety of horrible additions that can be made to a natural poison. Hang on, let me bring up the core\u2019s Merits\u2026 none of the stuff related to extra limbs describes in terms of being to hold a greater number of things, but that should totally work, right? Although\u2026 you can have Entangling Limbs, how do they compare to Extra Limbs\u2026 the former can flurry while doing a grapple, the latter can reduce some of the penalty for flurrying, I\u2019d say they\u2019re different enough. The point is, you have a few ways to model cool hair tentacles\u2026 I\u2019ve been catching up on my She-Ra lately.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Fins seem to be especially useful, if the value is high enough; who could turn down extra dice in aquatic movement rolls? Heh, I like the idea of having something like a big impressive crest making it easier to instil Ties to yourself in people. Heh, I love the notion of having the Guile bonus for an inscrutable face is lost against people that become familiar enough with you.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hah, octopus smoke bomb. Oh, I like harnessing the distract gambit to give Lure a function, very nice for the trickster role. Natural Shield seems like it would lend itself to some really good stunts.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hmm, if Prehensile Tongue/Trunk is its own Merit, I wonder if the prior assessment of extra limbs was in error\u2026 I mean, if it was treated primarily as a cosmetic character trait to inform how they move, carry and hold things, while still not being strong enough to effectively strike or hold something heavy (so no extra limb while using a two-handed weapon), but my instinct is still telling me that on their own they\u2019re rather flimsy. Eh, I\u2019ll work it out later.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I don\u2019t remember what a Serpentine body used to do, but think the idea of slithering as a way of easily moving while prone is clever.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hmm, given the stuff that can be done with Spinnerets, I wonder if it might not ought to be higher value. Aaaand a few more, and it finishes off with Vibration Sense.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Yes, I quite like a lot of these Merits. I think they\u2019re flavourful, just useful enough mechanically, and create a lot of options for putting together your hybrid form in a manner that makes it effectively potent and capable.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hmmmm\u2026 I\u2019m going to put a divider here and take a little break. It seems like an appropriate place before getting into the deeper Lunar stuff, and I\u2019m making decent time.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ah, right, fonts... screw it, it plays into the demarcation.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-19-2019, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:13:37-08:00","id":1289592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Come to think of it, character creation might be more generous to Lunars than Solars and Terrestrials, because they\u2019ve got a smaller number of important things to distribute dots between,</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I don't think it is.<br /> <br /> Lunars get slightly more dots, and have less important things to distrubute dots between.<br /> <br /> But the freebie costs are much worse for them.<br /> <br /> A Solar can use their freebie points to get 89xp's worth of dots. A Dawn can start with Join Battle 11, Parry 7, 11 dice to attack with Decisives, resist poison 11, Per+Awareness 8, natural Soak of 5, Dex+Athletics 10, Dex+Ride 10, and Resolve 5 (6 against something).<br /> <br /> A Lunar can, at most, use their freebie points to get 56xp's worth of stuff. That may not be exactly right, but it's something like that.<br /> And they probably won't have any pools at 11. If they do, it'll be 1 at most (unless you min-max to do so, but it'll screw you, and it's better not to min-max like that).<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall, I'd say Solars have the best, then Lunars, then Dragonblood, then Mortals.<br /> <br /> A note: Dragonblood character gen is technically the best one. More Merits, Essence 2. But obviously it's the weakest because your 15 charms are much weaker.<br /> <br /> A second, more important note: My above comments about Lunar character gen are in no way criticisms. I am quite happy with Lunar character generation. I used to irritate my players by trying all kinds of complicated tweaks to the character generation system. If I run Exalted again, I don't intend to do anything to Lunar character generation, it's fine as-is.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-19-2019, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:41:23-08:00","id":1289632,"title":"","content":"Oh dear sweet mother of God do I not care about XP costs and the supposed value they place on traits. At all. My eyes are clouding up at the prospect of reading about them in my thread, not least because of the <i>endless <b>draining</b></i> arguments they constitute the prospect of inviting in. Any second now there's going to be a line about how all Charms should have power of equal value because they all cost the same XP and aaaarrgrhhaaarrrghhrarahghah<br /> <br /> Hey, anybody who sees the post above and feels an impulse to start talking about the whole BP/XP thing? Please be so considerate as to take that shit elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Like, I feel some contrary arguments, but I do deeply <b>loathe</b> this subject, and what it does to discussions, that I don't want it anywhere near my thread even from my perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:52:35-08:00","id":1289638,"title":"","content":"Okay, do you want me to delete that post? Or at least edit it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-19-2019, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:58:00-08:00","id":1289642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289638#post1289638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, do you want me to delete that post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nono, that's fine. I've expressed myself, and just want to move forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:00:11-08:00","id":1289643,"title":"","content":"Now, let\u2019s catch up by taking in the traits of the Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> With the Castes, this is going to be an occasion where I do something a bit different and consider a previous text in making my assessment. I won\u2019t necessarily compare anything, just any differences that stand out to me (especially if they seem to convey different messages about the Caste).<br /> <br /> Something I like about the imagery used in describing the Full Moon Caste is the sense of complement it gives to the Dawn Caste, and how it also roots them in a different context; that idea that the night can give dark creatures no respite from light. I get why the Second Edition one focused on Wyld imagery, but even considering the stronger focus on the Wyld, in retrospect I find it a bit too rooted in lore minutia to be very evocative. Similar goes for describing them expressing their fury in a variety of combative shapes.<br /> <br /> Given that the onus is on the Lunars for remaking their Castes, I like a section examining the motivation underlying a given Caste\u2019s function. Like here, the idea that the Full Moon Caste was devised with a very deliberate intention to wage war (as well as surviving the assault of enemies). And I think it\u2019s helpful to provide a description of the kinds of people that might wind up in the Caste, not just for the sufficient diversity but the significance of the fact that Caste is chosen by the Exalt (or at least determined after the fact of becoming a Lunar); what\u2019s particularly interesting is the crossover that the non-directly physical might have with other Castes, but who end up here for aspiration towards its combative ideal.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think that this Caste description is more succinct in the past; less fluff, less focus on irrelevant history, more about what they are.<br /> <br /> Spirit shapes are about the same in focus, although a greater number of suggestions is given here (including reference to animals of more symbolic value).<br /> <br /> What I like about the changed approach to describing anima banners is covered across the books in general, and the colour of the Full Moon anima has not changed here. What is different is the range of possibilities for a Lunar iconic display; they\u2019re no longer being confined to an image (even abstract) of their spirit shape; it can be anything from a monstrous form of that animal, to a different kind of martial image like a weapon or war banner, or stranger things yet, with me finding the idea of numerous radiating limbs particularly intriguing. I\u2019ll have to wait a bit to get the specifics of the powers, of course.<br /> <br /> Associations are all the same, as are most of the sobriquets (although Burning Moon has changed to Indominable Moon), and concepts are a bit broader than they would have been, but all about what one would expect.<br /> <br /> Nothing much to say about the sidebar describing the Immaculate perspective, it\u2019s just perfectly serviceable. However\u2026 I have to admit, I kind of like the Second Edition Caste quote a bit better. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Second Edition description of the Changing Moon is actually pretty fine, so I find this one to be more of an expansion on that base; primarily, it incorporates the image of denied revelation, which I find particularly resonant with my observations of the Appearance Charms and how they inform my renewed sense of the Caste. Similar goes with the descriptions of the various ways in which they might apply their powers, lending itself to the sense of how formidable they are, the level of insinuation they can achieve.<br /> <br /> No time is wasted on alluding to lost Castes (which in this instance arguably describes all of them from the First Age), which also helps with their image; don\u2019t describe them as a stop gap measure, a salvage, talk about them as a deliberate and intended design to meet with the challenges they were up against, a Caste to work its way into the systems of the usurpers and tear them apart from within. It may just be having seen two-thirds of their Attributes right up front, but I\u2019ve got to say, Changing Moon has gone from a Caste I was rather indifferent to into one that is occupying a huge amount of my attention and intrigue\u2026 which has to be the single most apropos reading of Exalted I\u2019ve yet had {laughter}<br /> <br /> Huh, reading the description of the people who might select the Caste, I\u2019m seeing another facet to the Full Moon description, and the premise of Attribute Charms in general: the part about people drawn to the allure of the divine trickster is having me think that some Lunars were people who weren\u2019t really good at a given field in the way that mortals would need to be, and upon being bestowed with the power of Luna, embrace the capacity to forego such formal skill in favour of the prowess of raw expression. I\u2019m seeing a courtier who was beautiful, but never very good at the game, embracing the Caste to be able to shape that beauty into a tool to make people project the idea of such skill onto them. Or maybe somebody like a soldier, who always wanted fame and luxury but lacked the skills and ultimately ended up as a basic recruit, and unexpectedly takes this Caste in order to have a more suitable means of pursuing those dormant ambitions. Fascinating.<br /> <br /> Given all of the mimicry Totems, I like how the suggested spirit shapes include animals known for deception. Preference among the suggested iconic displays is a toss up between rainbow fire and whirling silver masks. I actually think the previous sobriquet of Silver Mirrors would be fitting here, but I think the change in Immaculate title from the more generic Trickster to the more specific Face-Stealer is good, not least because it touches on what would be most terrifying and objectionable about them. Actually, I\u2019m not sure if I noticed this before, but one thing I\u2019ll give this and the prior sidebar is the little note on what precisely the Dragon Blooded present as the skill that qualifies people to protect them from these Anthema.<br /> <br /> And for the quote, we go from the Second Edition one in which somebody talks about having hunted lots of animals and people (the fuck?), to what I am 90% convinced is intended to be a callback to that old Exalted meme/sig in which somebody tells Chejop that they didn\u2019t stop a Lunar from coming in, because the Lunar killed that person and stole their face. In any event, delightfully creepy; I\u2019m really falling in love with this Caste.<br /> <br /> I do like that little note for the No Moon of the idea of Luna\u2019s light being shone in unknown places during the new moon phase, but I\u2019ve got to admit, I have a slight preference for the idea in the Second Edition write-up of it constituting a time where Luna is free for deep contemplation. Just to give things fair shakes. Still, the rest of that write-up, the stuff about the Exalted, it was too focused on the background, on sorcery and the idea that the main contribution to the Pact was providing the tattoos. No, the description of No Moon activities of travel, insight, and especially of functioning as mysterious advisors and speaking to gods with the voices of their priests, those are much more vivid.<br /> <br /> Same goes with the description of the background; the recognition that they lacked the means or the power to rebuild the old world, so instead they\u2019d focus on plumbing the ruined depths for new wisdom. The description of those who take the Caste is solid, but nothing more to say on it. I think there\u2019s good stuff in the spirit shape description, how the No Moons in general are more inclined to the symbolic (that idea of deep sea creatures is particularly good), but I\u2019m gonna have to give it to Second Edition then, covering all of those in addition to the idea of creatures sacred to Luna (white and black cats) and constructive types such as beavers or spiders.<br /> <br /> For the description of iconic animas, few things can beat a cloud of creepy eyes to me. And the final quote about matches the previous one; they both focus on the significance of knowledge, with a hint of playful confidence.<br /> <br /> Finally there\u2019s the Casteless. I\u2019ve never been entirely sold on this for anything besides a description of how Lunars function before being tattoed, or those who are kept apart from the Silver Pact, but I am finding this description kind of compelling. That focus on how the other Castes, their phases, are still aspects of the same moon, on those Lunars who still want time to determine who they are, and any that are simply unmoved by the roles and nature of the three Castes. Plus the sense that they might have an easier time diversifying. I\u2019m interested to see the description of how their anima powers work. Everything else is simply fine, though I\u2019m fond of how the greater scope of icons introduces the idea that their manifestation might change if a Caste is adopted.<br /> <br /> The basic nature of the anima banner is all fairly boilerplate, so let\u2019s see the powers.<br /> <br /> So, Full Moon gets to add hefty non-Charm dice to movement and feats of strength, plus enhanced soak, add half their highest physical Attribute to Resolve against fear and threats, and\u2026 ooh, have a daily option to follow a successful decisive attack by rerolling Join Battle with the addition of a physical Attribute; that seems like it might be particularly strong. Yes, I\u2019d say these are some nice overlays for Full Moon activities. <br /> <br /> What of my beloved Changing Moons? They can intrinsically lend a basic hypnotic quality to their speech in the form of some extra non-Charm dice to an influence roll, that a listener needs to spend Willpower to ignore or interrupt, they can get some improvements to their Guile, Stealth and disguises, and\u2026 I guess daily powers are a thing for each of them\u2026 ahh, here\u2019s the good stuff, they get an opportunity to make a person\u2019s negative Ties against them irrelevant in an interaction. Nice. Sure, they don\u2019t have an intrinsic power to look like people, but that was always weird with general shapeshifting anyway. This focus is more fitting.<br /> <br /> People were always critical of the No Moon anima, so what has been revised for it\u2026 the shadowy qualities of their anima can penalise rolls dependent on being able to see them, have an innate sense to detect supernatural hot spots, and their daily power\u2026 ah, they have something to let them convert their anima into a possibly hefty amount of sorcerous motes, but as an alternative for the non-sorcerers, they can have a free Excellency for a mental roll. That all seems fair.<br /> <br /> And then the Casteless\u2026 right, so they literally have a slightly easier time shapeshifting, which is an interesting little bit of lore about the nature of Lunar Essence, and\u2026 ah, I was worried that before it was saying that the Casteless fully shifted between Caste anima powers with each phase, which seemed to me a bit too much of a concession even if it was temporary, but no, they not only just get the daily power powers, each use expends it for the duration of the Lunar phase, and requires cycling through the others to get back\u2026. Something sounds wrong, check again\u2026 no, their anima power is not tied to the moon phase, they can use any of them any time, so long as they\u2019ve been reset with the other two. That is also fair, and rather interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, good stuff in the Caste write-ups. I\u2019m going to take another little break, have dinner, and then finish off what I presume is just the shapeshifting, Great Curse and Lunar XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:01:38-08:00","id":1289646,"title":"","content":"Sure, no worries.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja'd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:14:31-08:00","id":1289651,"title":"","content":"There's also other bits and bobs too, but they're small.<br /> <br /> I'm interested to see what you think of the Sacred Hunt and Moonsilver Tattoos sections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:18:05-08:00","id":1289772,"title":"","content":"Okay, finish it off with the iconic power of our Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A part of fluff establishing the principle and why the foundation is in the sacred hunt, and the describing the basic mechanical premise; a miscellaneous action costing a commitment of four motes. I\u2019ve gone a bit back and forth on whether or not I like shapeshifting requiring a commitment, but in the end I have to suppose that it comes down on the side of a mechanical and balance necessity, over image matters of a Lunar being able to maintain an alternative shape indefinitely without effort. Then there\u2019s a sidebar both establishing the limits of that shapeshifting, and clarifying to the best extent possible on what does not qualify as a mundane animal for the purpose of it (particularly in light of the larger range of Creation\u2019s fauna). This one I\u2019m all for, from the sense in the past about the original shapeshifting becoming diffuse and obscure under increasingly elaborate forms.<br /> <br /> So, what are the specifics of an animal shape\u2026 Essence, Willpower, Initiative, health, Attributes, Abilities, Resolve and Guile stay the same (the As in there surprise me a bit, but let\u2019s see what else there is). Can\u2019t use mutation Merits that aren\u2019t coming from Charms and the Tell (so I guess that resolves my question of the upper limits of its appearance). Right, so the Lunar\u2019s Attribute and Ability stays the same, but they can use actions the animal could do with its pool if its better, which counts towards the dice cap (so you\u2019re not getting the full scope out of that tyrant lizard by default). The Lunar still gets to use their own stats for other actions, possibly penalized if they end up unsuited to the shape in question. When it comes to attacks in particular, the Lunar can get much more benefit out of the increased damage rolls, including being able to put their full Strength Excellency on it, and even for a form where the Lunar\u2019s natural attack pool is better, the animal\u2019s weapon provides a slight accuracy bonus. They\u2019re also not limited in performing feats of strength, but that comes with a cost of being limited to their form\u2019s strength (presumably barring appropriate Charms).<br /> <br /> What else\u2026 using the animal\u2019s Evasion and Parry counts as Charm dice, but their soak and Hardness don\u2019t, and they can also get the use of special abilities and Merits (which also count towards the cap). In anticipation of this one, I went back over some of the dinosaurs, and some of those have some really good armour. A Lunar in the form of, say, an ankylosaur is somebody that a less powerful opponent such as a Terrestrial will be hard pressed to inflict damage on at all.<br /> <br /> The Lunars can train themselves to use the mundane latent abilities of their animal forms, with the particularly good benefit of letting such a development apply to all forms capable of it; teach your hawk shape to peck out the eyes, and you won\u2019t need additional training to do it while you\u2019re a pigeon. And last of all their language skills become sharply limited in an obvious manner.<br /> <br /> All of that under the caveat that becoming capable of Legendary or Miniscule Size requires the appropriate Charms. If I\u2019m reading correctly, a Lunar who performs the sacred hunt on animals with those sizes without the appropriate Charms still acquires the forms, just can\u2019t transform into them yet. I\u2019m unsure how to read the point about having them as spirit shapes; I guess it\u2019s something like that shape still informing your hybrid body and Totemic powers, but you may not be able to become them. I already know for a fact that it\u2019s not a matter of turning into a miniature tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> Ah, I had wondered if mutated animals would count as magical for shape acquisition purposes. So the answer is no, but to prevent them from becoming an easy source of Supernatural Merits, the value of those Merits is added to the cost of turning into them. Makes sense, and possibly resolves some questions about beings created by sorcery.<br /> <br /> Hmm, here at the end of the animal stuff, I wonder about the spirit shape\u2026 no exception is made for it, and this would be the place, so I guess it\u2019s like any other animal shape. That might be necessary under these circumstances, although I must admit to missing the concept of \u201ctrue forms\u201d.<br /> <br /> Now, for human shapes, even if you don\u2019t get their knowledge and memories, I\u2019m inclined to view the matter of copying their \u201csemblance\u201d as meaning that you not only get their appearance, but a few nuances such as their gait, how they carry themselves and the way that they talk; enough to keep the form from having severe intrinsic shortcomings as a disguise. I\u2019m thinking things like having to go out of your way to not have a limp, even if you don\u2019t feel any actual limited mobility or discomfort. I think this doesn\u2019t contradict the sidebar about Guile; if actions like that are needed to recognise differences, they can hardly be obvious. Other than that, yeah, not getting the shape\u2019s stats seems sensible all around.<br /> <br /> And how about how all of this is acquired, in the sacred hunt? I\u2019ll admit, with the descriptions of some of the alternative hunt Charms, I was expecting something a bit more intricate, but under the circumstances I guess that a \u201csacred hunt\u201d acquired through physical intimacy just amounts to declaring your intention to take the person\u2019s shape before you do your thing with them. I have mixed feelings; I did like some of the connotations of something with a bit of a deeper intricacy and ritual to it, but must admit that acquiring new forms is such a big deal for playing Lunars that such might create a sense of tedium, and it\u2019s not strictly out of character for Lunars. Still, that it allows for indirect killing resolves a question I had in response to a point from somebody else: they said that having an animal\u2019s shape connotes already being more powerful than it, but here I can see just shooting a tyrant lizard with an arrow tipped in nasty poison and following it until it dies, if you want more combat prowess than you\u2019re natively capable of.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea that hunting people for their shapes is intense enough to cause a Tie to form.<br /> <br /> Bit of Storyteller advice to skip hunts that aren\u2019t really necessary on stage, and a neat point that Lunars don\u2019t need fancy powers to acquire the entirety of their libraries if they\u2019re subjected to a deadly sacred hunt (with the same rule applying for any other transforming human targeted).<br /> <br /> I think the rules cover all of the bases, but one thing I miss a little bit is any description of the appearance and experience of the changing form. Sure, even with such a thing people are likely to picture it however they want, and there\u2019s probably never going to be a description that isn\u2019t unsatisfying (if not silly) to someone, but I do think it could be a decent place to add a bit more characterisation to Lunar magic.<br /> <br /> Next is the Tell, and after the amount of build up I\u2019ve been getting from other references I\u2019m particularly interested to see how this functions.<br /> <br /> Okay, basic idea is still the same, a feature that is characteristic to a Lunar and remains consistent across shapes; unlike the prior Edition, it doesn\u2019t need to be specifically based on the spirit shape, or even overtly supernatural. I\u2019ve always been a bit unclear on if that applies to other human forms, but when the capacity to gain such is now innate and it straight up says that the Tell appears in any form, I guess there\u2019s no question. I\u2019ll admit that, personally, something about that has never fully sat right with me; it\u2019s not an objection to the Tell in principle, just the sense that the stolen human form feels indelibly marred if it\u2019s obligated to carry something like your iconic face scar. Maybe I\u2019d be better off just looking at the concealment rules more in terms of the Tell actually being obscured upon an insufficient observer, rather than present but unnoticed.<br /> <br /> Okay, rules about seeing through it, something that the last Edition at least made very convoluted. It appears that the innate concealment of the Tell applies even in the original human form, so it\u2019s just a flat difficulty of 7 for a character to roll Perception + Awareness to perceive it; I\u2019m guessing that in the case of a Lunar\u2019s core identity, there are features in which it\u2019s less about literally seeing the feature, and more about realizing that it\u2019s the one marked across their forms. For a person who\u2019s detected the Tell before, they get three bonus successes to start, making the roll a lot more manageable (I\u2019d say in a lot of cases that\u2019s for people who have seen the Lunar when their anima was glowing), and it counts as a disguise for magic to help see through such. A person who succeeds can see the Tell, and make the connection to another form that they\u2019ve seen the Tell in; if they fail, they don\u2019t get to try again until the Lunar changes shape. An observer can gain some bonus dice if the Lunar is acting distinctly out of character, and even more if a read intentions or profile action has discerned more subtle discrepancies. The observation roll might be penalised, but the Tell can only be truly undetectable with the Subtle Silver Declaration Charm, and Tells as physical animal features can be modelled with the right Merits, in which case they become more apparent (presumably just in the true form), but still require this rigamarole to perceive and connect them in other forms; I presume you\u2019re not obligated to take a mutation if you want your Tell to be claws or horns or something, it just leaves such a feature purely cosmetic, with no mechanical benefit.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a bit wordy, but I think that the basic concept is straightforward enough, and it covers all of the bases.<br /> <br /> Okay, a few points to round out shapeshifting\u2026 almost all equipment vanishes to Elsewhere when in an animal form, but moonsilver armour (and some weapons) can innately reshape itself appropriately, Martial Arts are completely incompatible with any animal shapes, good good, it doesn\u2019t provide any healing and crippling injuries carry across all forms\u2026 ahh, concerns with size, this is of interest to me. The basic rule is that, if within a space that wouldn\u2019t accommodate the shape turned into, the shapeshifting action needs to be flurried with an appropriate demolition feat to break those confines; if it fails or can\u2019t be done, then the Lunar will simply not change. Changing shape while inside another character into something that would tear them apart from within is stated to simply not function, not any other kind of shapeshifting that would innately cause damage. That\u2019s never been a premise I especially liked, so I\u2019m ready to take it at face value. Honestly, I\u2019m kind of good to not even bother contriving an explanation for it; suspension of disbelief will serve for me. There\u2019s a final sidebar to basically remind that the rules can\u2019t cover every eventuality, and not all combinations may work for all people, so adjust for taste.<br /> <br /> The rules for the Solar Bond are next, but I saw them ages ago. I don\u2019t have much else to say on it, beyond reiterating that I like the manner in which it is mutable.<br /> <br /> Now, the Moonsilver Tattoos, something else I\u2019ve been interested in the specifics of. We get a basic description of their value in fixing the Castes, as well as a clear description of the experience and implications of that for a Casteless character. There\u2019s an explanation of how diverse the tattoos are capable of being, fulfilling basically any aesthetic preferences, and how in addition to fixing Caste they provide complete immunity to the Wyld, and magic that would alter their shape without their consent. A one mote commitment allows the tattoos to be concealed indefinitely so long as the Lunar\u2019s anima isn\u2019t glowing.<br /> <br /> But the most interesting departure from prior Editions is how the tattoos explicitly aren\u2019t an Artifact. On the one hand, that means they can possess no other powers as they could in the past, and would have particularly big implications with Evocations. On the other, the whole attitude to applying them has been overhauled; where before, it was somewhat proprietary (including the use of a Charm), here it\u2019s rendered as virtually trivial, with the idea being that so long as a Lunar has the materials and knowledge (with a note on how most Silver Pact members teach the process freely), it almost takes care of itself. Even making a dice roll for it is recommended to be exclusive to high-pressure situations.<br /> <br /> I actually think this is really cool for a number of reasons. The basic one is that it frees players and characters to treat the matter with as much or as little ceremony as desired; it can be a big deal where a carefully considered initiate goes before a council and makes a big thing of declaring their intended Caste, and then a respected shahan-ya steps forward to reverently apply the tattoos while reciting some narrative about Luna\u2026 or can be done in the field by a young Lunar who learned it a week ago to help get the fellow they\u2019ve discovered right into the thick of things (the latter is a scenario I find especially compelling). Not to mention the freedom to not be reliant on the Pact for tattooing. The wording does at least limit it to requiring another to perform it for you, but I prefer that as well, given the intimacy I ascribe to fixing a Caste. Overall, it\u2019s very interesting to me.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I never got around to saying it in the Silver Pact chapter, but I also love how the Pact as a whole isn\u2019t described as having standardised ceremony or procedure, meaning that anything from interactions between individual Lunars to the format of councils can be just played by ear. I like the notion that approaching one shahan-ya might be something that requires very intricate and precise displays of etiquette and ceremony, and approaching another might be as simple as walking up to their door and shouting for their attention, and that the standards of the Pact as a whole mean that the one who prefers the former can\u2019t be too pissy if approached by somebody in the manner of the latter.)<br /> <br /> Okay, what can Lunar XP tell me about character and Caste? \u2026Ehh, for the most part, for the three Castes, not much that wouldn\u2019t be apparent just from reading their descriptions; the advantage of them being so broad and down-to-earth, I suppose. Though I do like the trickster element for a Changing Moon role bonus of solving a problem that they created for themselves, that\u2019s very Loki, and I\u2019m liking the premise that the No Moons are the ones who actually foster communication between people. The Casteless one actually takes the prize here: the idea of role bonus for an achievement that lets them recognise something about themselves is good enough, but what I find especially interesting is the idea of XP for such accomplishments in basically\u2026 being a Lunar. The most basic essence found in being a face stealing shapeshifter. It\u2019s actually a rather compelling bit of additional characterisation to being Casteless. And yeah, also getting such from effectively protecting some system they\u2019ve invested themselves in is also neat.<br /> <br /> Training times and raising Essence fairly standard\u2026 all right, bring it home with the shiny new Lunar Great Curse!<br /> <br /> Errrbpaprrr\u2026 riiigght, so where for a Solar it\u2019s a case of things conflicting within them or contrary to their most dearly held values or illustrations of the limits of their power break into them and compel them to extreme and dramatic displays of action, either to express their frustrations or try and redress their grievances, for Lunars it\u2019s stress and strain causing the Curse to appeal to their innate monstrosity, and trying to tip their natural balance in favour of that. A lot of the basic functions of how that reaps Limit are the same as for Solars, with action contrary to Major and Defining Intimacies calling for rolls and a Limit Trigger, and the samples and standards of the Trigger are very similar to Solar ones, although I have a bias to impress upon them a more emotional context (especially provocation of their inner rage)\u2026 actually, scratch that, I do see something innate to the text in which the subject of the difficulties is always focused on the Lunar (and occasionally their Circle).. yes, a lot of Solar triggers are about their response to things happening around them, things happening to others or by others that the Solar can\u2019t stop, but for the Lunar it\u2019s all about what has happened to them, what is hurting or hindering or constraining them. In essence, I could collectively characterise it as a chain that a Lunar is still struggling to be free from.<br /> <br /> The result of it reaching a breaking point is not a Virtue Flaw, a perversion of heroic character, but a Monstrous Urge, a compulsion to act in a manner forsaking human reason or sensibility. The basic mechanics function the same, but the resulting activity\u2026 let\u2019s see, the examples are furiously acquiring and hoarding something of material value, going about obnoxiously proclaiming and proving their own perceived superiority, having an extreme violent response to anything posing the slightest impediment or inconvenience, sowing chaos and disrupting stability for its own sake, becoming an uncompromising avenging beast, fixating on a specific target to stalk and harass from a distance, conducting all of their business in a manner intended to maximize terror for everybody involved and witnessing\u2026 aw jeez, designating a category of living being to obsessively hunt, slay and devour (which can include humans), and obsessing over being worshipped and beloved and engaging in grandiose displays to draw that attention.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I find this to be sufficiently distinct from the Solar Curse as to be interesting, and really round out the characterization of Lunars and how they\u2019re perceived by others.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s interesting to me is that, in my eyes, a Virtue Flaw is something that could be perceived by the right person as the Solar still conducting themselves heroically, even if the manner becomes extreme. I feel that it can often be harder to separate from the Solar\u2019s general behaviours and ambitions, and even if it gets to the point where an observer (like a Sidereal) is recognising that something has gone terribly wrong, it might conceal itself in the image of a Solar that has become too unreserved and unrestrained in the exercise of their power.<br /> <br /> For me, Monstrous Urge looks like it would generally be less covert. That it can often seem a lot more like a very extreme shift in behaviour, into an activity that is monstrous in its priorities, something that many could view and see the Lunar not acting normally. Where it most closely aligns to how a more lucid Lunar might act, it unfortunately aligns with some of the worst things that their powers can achieve, or activities it might guide them towards, meaning it\u2019s also a Curse that illustrates and emphasizes the most disturbing things about the Lunar ethos. We\u2019re told that in the functional Lunar, humanity and monstrosity are in balance and can be freely shifted, but a person who has seen what they become when their wrath or frustration boils over, it probably seems more like the monstrosity is something lurking beneath the Lunar\u2019s surface, and enough provocation can let it loose. In my view, Monstrous Urges might be consistently scarier than Virtue Flaws.<br /> <br /> It could be seen as going some ways towards why the Sidereals didn\u2019t trust the Lunars with the Usurpation, even if they couldn\u2019t be the highest priority in sealing away. That in the eyes of Sidereals, Solars can eventually be corrupted by the extent of their power, and the things they can do with that corruption are strong enough to be intolerable, they would see the innate mercurial nature of Lunar power as something that ultimately can\u2019t be predicted or controlled, even in a more isolated circumstance.<br /> <br /> The thing I\u2019d find most unnerving in that scenario is the possibility that some Lunars are also under that delusion. Something about what Lunar Exaltation represents, the innately liberating quality of it, the degree to which it is concerned with matters of identity, makes the Great Curse tainting that with an idea that they\u2019re innately unbalanced, that their liberation exposes a horror, feel like a greater crime by the Primordials than the other Curses.<br /> <br /> I mean jeez, that power gave Leviathan a body that properly expresses his identity. It\u2019s got to kind of suck if he\u2019s also under the impression that it\u2019s a power that means getting too frustrated can cause him to fly off the handle and go around obsessively eating people.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, Traits chapter ended on a high (if somewhat sombre) note. Hopefully I\u2019ll get a decent break before more Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T05:11:19-08:00","id":1289870,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, Monstrous Urge is something that looks like the Lunar knows is stemming from the Jungian Shadow; the more Limit she accrues, the more she can feel the beast surging. So it's not something they can get addicted to. So they're actually a little saner on average than Solars when normal, which is an interesting liminal quality that really fits them; the very fact their Great Curse makes them monsters makes them more human at other times.<br /> <br /> Although, Seven Devil Clever's most frequent Urge is Avaricious Hoard-Beast Craving. Why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OKH6PN4nG18\" data-code=\"OKH6PN4nG18\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/OKH6PN4nG18/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:49:05-08:00","id":1289977,"title":"","content":"My sense of the Great Curse cooled down a bit a few hours after my initial reading.<br /> <br /> Mostly just drawing from the sense of Lunars in the Silver Pact chapter; they don't really seem widely afraid of themselves as unstable monsters playing at humanity. I can now imagine that such an attitude is only liable to crop up with Lunars who have had an especially traumatic experience of a Monstrous Urge. I would suspect that most other Lunars just accept the possibility as a part of themselves, that they need to manage as best they can, and otherwise not get hung up on.<br /> <br /> If they can recognise some of the patterns, it might help to surround oneself with people whose presence would help cool them down. Asking somebody to be in that position is distinctly unfair, and liable to be exhausting, but it might still be how some Lunars try to cope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:04:16-08:00","id":1289985,"title":"","content":"The more I think about the Casteless, the more I'm fascinated by the implications of things like their reduced shapeshifting costs and their role XP bonuses, and what those might say about an original, pure nature of Lunars.<br /> <br /> I've had a notion for a while that they had no Castes when fighting in the Primordial War, and between this and the matter of Bonding to Solars explicitly only happening after the war, I went to sleep forming this whole elaborate backstory for the Lunars (as well as a clearer image of what First Age Castes could be).<br /> <br /> The significance of that being it making me think of the idea for a heterodox Casteless shahan-ya, who accepts the Castes for the purposes of making war against the Realm, but advocates that in the aftermath the Lunars should allow knowledge of Caste fixing to die out, and embrace Castelessness as a true liberation and experiencing the pure, essential nature of being a Lunar; not of attaching themselves to a role, but living life as a constant journey of self-discovery and mutable form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:09:01-08:00","id":1289989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289985#post1289985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had a notion for a while that they had no Castes when fighting in the Primordial War</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I kind of like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:11:57-08:00","id":1289990,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea. What do you suppose the casteless's third anima power should do in the absence of any other castes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:18:38-08:00","id":1289991,"title":"","content":"For ease, it could just be the same; maybe they built on that for the Castes.<br /> <br /> But exact mechanics aren't really important for something that existed 6500-ish years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:35:15-08:00","id":1290001,"title":"","content":"My image of the Primordial War has increasingly shifted away from the conception that was more explicit in Second (and kind of implicit in First) as a widespread, dedicated, organised system managed by the gods, than... kind of like the parts of the Silmarillion after the Battle of Sudden Flame. So you've got somebody like Solar Tuor being prompted by Sidereal Ulmo to journey to the hidden Dragon Blooded refuge of Gondolin and rise to great renown among their ranks, except maybe this time you convince them to go off and make direct war against something significant to the Primordials, and are at the front of their efforts.<br /> <br /> Like, I already formed a conception a few years ago of the different Exalted types emerging independently (if around the same time), and for the most part getting together and organising to do battle against the Primordials was something that they had to manage on their own. The Sidereals were the main connective tissue; the ones more consistently in communion with the gods, and dedicated to pulling a lot of strings to bring lots of Exalted together and pointing them at things that could strategically or literally hurt Primordials. And you'd get stuff like Solar Samson being enslaved for years by a group of Lintha, before finally getting the right opportunity to bring the house down upon them, except maybe this time Samson lives.<br /> <br /> The point is, in that model, the Lunars now have a place in which, for the most part, they're off doing their own thing, and the unions of Solars and Dragon Blooded are often content to give them a bit of a wide berth. In a lot of cases, it results in Lunars who functionally serve as a vanguard of Exalted assaults, often throwing themselves with gleeful wild abandon against Primordial forces or insinuating themselves into their secrets and societies in order to sew discord. Within that picture, no Castes felt like a good fit; that Luna's gift was a powerful liberation, to set themselves against the fetters of the enemies of the gods, and joyously tearing them apart.<br /> <br /> It also helps put the origin of the Silver Pact into context for me; that their initial conception of the world governed by the Exalted was utter freedom, against which a Solar proclaiming authority provoked extreme rage and drew so many of them magnetically just on principle. And in that concentration, they got to experience two things; a much much wider experience of one another (not to say they never associated in the war, just not on that scale), and a stronger firsthand look at how impressive the Solars were, experiencing a kind of opposition that the demons and monsters had never offered them.<br /> <br /> It cooled down their moods, and both sides realised that there was an opportunity to make concord. So they drew on the examples of their respective patrons, and engaged in a union of Chosen of Sun and Moon; three hundred Lawgivers to three hundred shapeshifters, with the remaining one hundred standing in witness. The Lunars vowed to serve, protect, teach and test the world that the Solars would create, the Solars vowed honour and fidelity to the Lunars, who would ever be the first in their counsels. And in the consecration of that union, the Lunars gained the capacity to form Castes, to engage in the roles they pledged to the Realm; guardian, courtier, priest, trickster and loremaster. It constituted giving up some freedoms*; their forms became a little bit more immutable, the powers of their animas would not shift and transition, the affirmation of self-discovery replaced with that of fulfilling their chosen duties. But it also gave them stability, a place in the world, and considerable power.<br /> <br /> Then the Usurpation happened, and a lot of the foundation of that stability cracked. Fortunately, the lessons of the First Age prevented the Lunars from merely returning to the anarchy of their progenitors; they forged new, simpler, more raw Castes to protect themselves and what they valued in a world of new enemies, and make unrelenting war upon them.<br /> <br /> * I'm picturing First Age Castes as a bit more rigid than Second Age ones, with something like lesser choice in key Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:00:13-08:00","id":1290068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289991#post1289991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But exact mechanics aren't really important for something that existed 6500-ish years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, to my mind, what value is in my notion would primarily come from mythology Lunars can tell each other, some speculation on anything like a supposed Lunar core nature, and any politics that might arise therein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:31:44-08:00","id":1290083,"title":"","content":"I suppose the primary political effect would be to have a small number of Lunars who believe that being Casteless is the &quot;true&quot; form of Lunars. (Though I can't see Lunars overall being very fussed about what the &quot;right&quot; form to be in is.)<br /> <br /> Which... is the same as 2nd ed presented Casteless, but at least this time there's some sense to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, 6500 years later... Lunars probably have a number of myths about their origins. I mean, not utterly different (6500 years isn't that many generations for someone like -That-Remembers), but still.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T15:10:35-08:00","id":1290113,"title":"","content":"You think that some First Age Lunars who just didn't care to be involved with the Pact or its war, like Lilith, decided to remain Casteless after the Lunars broke their Castes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T16:53:59-08:00","id":1290141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290083#post1290083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the primary political effect would be to have a small number of Lunars who believe that being Casteless is the &quot;true&quot; form of Lunars. (Though I can't see Lunars overall being very fussed about what the &quot;right&quot; form to be in is.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like the Casteless shahan-ya I imagined up there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, 6500 years later... Lunars probably have a number of myths about their origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my mind, a lot of myths for the sake of personal history and spiritual exploration have largely fallen to the wayside, and a lot of the Silver Pact tends to share minor variations on something focused primarily on establishing the background to their outrage.<br /> <br /> That is, the origin is never really relayed in isolation, it's just the first couple of paragraphs of a cycle based around establishing what the significance of the Realm was to them, why its loss hurts them so (and the fact that they were turned out and hunted down), and some legacy for the attitude underlying their current Castes.<br /> <br /> A few scholars (especially students of First Age Lunars) might retain the memory of some older narratives, which can often be rather esoteric, but there's not often much call for them, and many second generation Lunars in particular view them as distinctly old-fashioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, not utterly different (6500 years isn't that many generations for someone like -That-Remembers), but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though even throughout the First Age, it was uncommon for Solar or Lunar Exalted to live up to a thousand years, and that by the Time of Tumult the majority of Lunar Essences have been reincarnated dozens of times.<br /> <br /> {does the maths}<br /> <br /> Hmm, average lifespan of 300 years amounts to 22 incarnations since the start of the First Age? That's actually still not too many compared to several millenia. Only way to make the turnover feel really enormous is to skew the averages quite a fair bit.<br /> <br /> There are probably some ways to bend it a bit to serve, but right now it does actually seem to lean more in the direction of most Lunars having enough past lives that being able to recite a list of each one with a handy summary would not be too hard a task.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:10:43-08:00","id":1290382,"title":"","content":"Now, for my own read on the first snippet of Charm preview:<br /> <br /> Nest-Raiding Slyness: Dexterity\u2019s Heart\u2019s Blood Charm, through which a shape of person (or animal, for once) can be acquired be getting into a target\u2019s home while present, not getting caught, but also doing something that makes it clear they were there in a way hurtful or outrageous to the prey. I like this in basic principle for giving Lunars an element of transgression, for it being another representation of a trickster archetype, and for what it implies about Dexterity Charms in general, the likelihood that they will be more than just the physical.<br /> <br /> Twisting Penumbra Veil: But for the benefit of the physical, there\u2019s this power to perform the unique action of clashing an attack with a Stealth roll, to not only stop it but immediately move into concealment. I like a few things for this one; taking advantage of the Attribute quality for pulling application of an Ability into an unusual circumstance, and being another instance where it feels like an animalistic and mystical quality are being represented at the same time, neither more prominent than the other. That and feeling as though this could be the crux of a fighting style, pointing Full Moons in general towards something more diverse than the stereotypical direct rampager.<br /> <br /> Living Hive Transformation: Still, for something more directly animalistic (even if remaining rather witchy and creepy), I don\u2019t think you can beat having the Lunar\u2019s body writhe with miniature bestial transformations. I feel as though this one might satisfy people who want something more protean in Lunars, without diffusing their whole characteristics. And mechanically\u2026 hmm, commit 3 motes for a scene to make small, but penetrating, decisive counterattacks any time somebody at close range hits you, especially when they\u2019re trying to grapple. What I like in this is a sense of Lunar fighting including a persistent denial of options to an enemy, or at least punishing them for trying to power through anyway. Plus girding Deadly Beastman Transformation a bit with the idea that it can pull some other Simple Charms along with it.<br /> <br /> Raiton\u2019s Dark Auspice: Intelligence Charm to give a bit of that world walker attitude, which I know people often felt was lacking in the direction of the Underworld. I think it\u2019s another good instance of a multi-faceted Lunar Charm, and I absolutely love the complete weirdness to a ghost of somebody whose shape the Lunar has feeling a (virtual) Major Tie of friendship for them; you don\u2019t get a Protean benefit for it, but imagine using a Charm on a ghost while actually being in their form?<br /> <br /> Insidious Lunar Transformation: Do a bit of that Circe thing, feeding a person some blood to forcefully transform people into animals. Or animals into other animals, technically. Perhaps permanently for a strong Lunar against a weak-willed target. I wonder what the shelf life is on the blood after it\u2019s been shed (considering the idea of tricking consumption), and implications that might have for setting up several people at once. Still, even for one, I\u2019m imagining a Dynast being summoned to their mother\u2019s home, and being greeted by her seated in her stately chair in the shape of an oclot or something, one of the attendants explaining that she seems to have been cursed by a Lunar. Still, it also has a number of viable applications besides impeding or weakening a person; helping allies or charges out of tight spots, for instance. Overall, a nice Charm.<br /> <br /> And last of all,<br /> <br /> God-Skinning Hunter Art: Something to incorporate a bit of rough Lunar imagery into the act of crafting Artifacts, reaping gold points from the Essence of a supernatural being towards the process of crafting something including their remains, as well as getting the opportunity to immediately awaken some Evocations, either for oneself, somebody who helped in the killing, or one\u2019s Mate. I like this for the hunter and skinner imagery, and adding a distinct and powerful Lunar take on the crafting system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:34:26-08:00","id":1290448,"title":"","content":"I love Raiton's Dark Auspice.<br /> <br /> It's just so... straightforward. No motes or willpower required. Just a small bonus that doesn't require activation.<br /> I assume there are equivalents for other kinds of spirits, I hope they're also permanent.<br /> <br /> I also like to see that, unlike previous editions, No Moons as Shamans is properly supported. In 2nd ed, while you got some stuff about the Wyld, there was no social stuff. Social stuff was for Changing Moons. But this edition happily hands you Social benefits against spirits despite being the Mental Primary Caste, because the point is not that you're the clever-clogs Caste, it's that you're the Nightwitches, the shamans who deal with gods, ghosts and demons. (Not to mention charms that indirectly help you socially against spirits, by telling you stuff about them that will help you know what they want.)<br /> I noticed there were several Lunar XP conditions for No Moons that were actually social-based (with a small &quot;s&quot;), but specifically about spirits. Making peace between spirits and human communities, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> I like God-Skinning Hunter Art as an expression of how Lunar craft is, well, Lunar, as opposed to just giving bonuses to crafting artefacts of Moonsilver like a Solar would.<br /> I hope there are other charms that entail incorporating furs, hides, fangs, etc, though I guess there's a limit to that as charms need to not be too similar.<br /> <br /> As both my current and retired Lunar PCs favour Intelligence, I'm intrigued to see the Intelligence charms. They were very limited in 2nd ed (you mostly took it for Sorcery), and now they presumably have mostly lost mental defence to Wits (which is what Resolve is based on). So I'm expecting to see plenty of cool, new stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-21-2019, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T03:21:44-08:00","id":1290705,"title":"","content":"Nest Raiding Slyness looks to be such a fun form acquisition charm. So sneaky; so cheeky! There is plenty of dramatic, or comedic, potential to play out with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T05:39:29-08:00","id":1290726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290705#post1290705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nest Raiding Slyness looks to be such a fun form acquisition charm. So sneaky; so cheeky! There is plenty of dramatic, or comedic, potential to play out with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also seems like something Raksi has as her favorite way to pass the time when someone warrants a <i>special </i>hell.<br /> <br /> In the most beautiful writing any mortal has ever seen, with silver flourishes: &quot;I can see your house from here! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:10:51-08:00","id":1290886,"title":"","content":"I have been cut off from the Internet all gorram day because of a mix-up with the bills!<br /> <br /> I don't want anybody thinking that I've been daunted by the matter of going through these Charms! If things had been working properly, I would have launched right into them.<br /> <br /> As it is, it's too late for me to do more than the Essence 1 and 2 Dexterity Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T14:46:04-08:00","id":1290906,"title":"","content":"No worries man, do it at a pace that works for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T15:01:29-08:00","id":1290912,"title":"","content":"Okay, looking forward to seeing the Dexterity Charms on a few fronts; getting a better sense of the Full Moon, some more direct Lunar combat power, and any more twisty weird stuff.<br /> <br /> Skipping straight over the already seen Heart\u2019s Blood Charm and\u2026 oh right, Emerald Grasshopped Form also qualifies under that header, that makes sense. I actually think the idea of needing really high Dexterity to do that lends itself to a fun image of needing to be really flexible to compress your flesh and Essence into something Miniscule. I think the high cost both lends characterisation and a bit of balance, while effectively offset by waiving it for going between forms directly. And yeah, makes sense to make it Totemic for characters with a Miniscule spirit shape.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a follow-up with Tyrant Mouse Dominion, allowing the reduction of any other shape (explicitly including human ones) to Miniscule size, being able to take moonsilver Artifacts down with you. Becoming a shrunk down human isn\u2019t really for me, but I know there are other people that value it and can\u2019t begrudge it to them. Mind, some of the descriptions of the limitations (I\u2019m presuming this is generally how the Merit works) alleviate a couple of concerns, particularly with the limits of dmage.<br /> <br /> Okay, Offensive Charms. Start with Finding the Needle\u2019s Eye, a somewhat basic enhancement attack that still lends some flavour with the combination of rerolling dice and ignoring defensive bonuses. This one is actually of interest to me particularly, because it might provide a model for how a moonsilver powerbow based on flexibility in its limbs works, a thing I\u2019ve tried to figure out in the past. Anyway, being in the form of an appropriately flexible animal provides a bit of extra Defence mitigation.<br /> <br /> Coyote-and-Badger Tactic feels to me like another thing effectively melding animal imagery, Lunar deftness and denial of enemy advantage in its use of distract gambits to remove enemy Initiative, and I get a particularly strong sense of the Protean benefit coming through in assuming a shape that is more inherently suited to the Charm\u2019s function, the idea of making yourself something that can act that way better.<br /> <br /> I like how Weapon-Snatching Coils describes its effect (for three guesses what) in terms of either being uncannily twisty or actually springing tendrils, just to encourage either approach to a player\u2019s tastes. I particularly like the Protean image of being something able to grasp and fling away a weapon with a tail, although for some reason my mind keeps fixating on an iguana. Striking Mospid Method has less to show in the basic description of rerolling dice for an attack roll, but that\u2019s all right, and even a bit desirable; some stuff just needs to be good Dexterity.<br /> <br /> Foe-Driving Attack is similar, although it has a bit of personality in the idea of pressing on an onslaught, a bit of characteristic fury. And then starting up again with Many-Armed Warrior Panoply\u2026 hmm, they finally did come back with something to let attunement for multiple Artifact weapons be reduced. I wonder if this is something that might fit for Solars, or if it gets its leeway from the whole cross-weapons thing of an Attribute Charm. I\u2019ll want to think more about this one, although I\u2019ve no problem with it for itself.<br /> <br /> Needle Quill Technique conveys an image I\u2019ve always liked to associate with Lunars, converting a body part into effective ammunition. If there was going to ever be a realisation of bombardier beetle imagery in a Lunar Charm, I think that being able to use caustic secretions as Flame weapon ammunition from Bombardier Spittle Alchemy is fitting and reasonable.<br /> <br /> Hmm, what kind of nasty thing might Stinging Ichneumon Scourge do\u2026 huh, not as bad as I was thinking, just letting the self-made projectiles to burrow or chase an enemy to keep the onslaught penalty on them for a few rounds\u2026 ahh, a decisive attack is the one most distinctly conveying the idea of it embedding, thus allowing it to last longer. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> Right, there\u2019s Sinuous Striking Grace to model heightened instinct and awareness in being able to add Dexterity or Wits to determine Initiative order, and get a little attack bonus if you\u2019re going for somebody who hasn\u2019t acted yet, a nice predatory aspect to it.<br /> <br /> Hmm, probably going to be a few Dexterity Charms that provide basic necessary functions\u2026 what am I saying, it\u2019s still only Essence 1, plenty of room to grow.<br /> <br /> Okay, bomb through them a bit\u2026 Cunning Beast-Warrior Reflexes provides improvements to flurrying a physical action with something, Wasp Sting Blur\u2026 shuts me right up with an attack that gets bonus dice and a reasonable possibility of making a follow up decisive attack that calculates damage by the target\u2019s onslaught and ignores Hardness, that sounds pretty nifty.<br /> <br /> Aaaand into Essence 2 already. Maybe I\u2019ll come out with more than I planned.<br /> <br /> Consumptive Worm Hungers is a fulfilling my expectations of an upgrade to the Ichneumon Charm, modelling an even more aggressive persistent attack by other repeatedly draining Initiative based on the Lunar\u2019s original damage roll, or repeatedly rolling a Hardness-ignoring damage die. I like the extended hunter element of this, even if the gambit to remove an embedded quill isn\u2019t very difficult and so any unmolested person or animal could probably manage it. Still, keep the pressure on, and it might wear down an enemy or victim something nasty. If nothing else, it might increase the perceived necessity to direct attention and Initiative at the quill.<br /> <br /> Twin Fangs Strike\u2026 I recognise the name, so I\u2019m really compelled to compare effects\u2026 hmm, closest thing before seems to have been Twin-Fang Technique, in which you got to attack with two weapons in a row. I think this pack hunter thing in which the beneficiary of a distract gambit gets to make their attack immediately. It synergizes with Deadly Wolf-Pack Onslaught, which <b>really</b> builds on the image with being able to make one distraction that can benefit multiple allies, as well as its per-scene reset of making a decisive attack on somebody under heavy onslaught, and probably something particularly strong in the Protean effect to provide Initiative to allies who are crashed.<br /> <br /> Go back to something more straightforward with Hunter\u2019s Eye Precision to let a ranged attack be aimed reflexively (which is obviously Totemic with Perception, for when your spirit shape is known for keen eyesight). Birds-Fall-From-Flock Targeting does something a bit more interesting in permanently endowing a Lunar with the capacity to aim at multiple nearby people at once, allowing flexibility in who they opt to shoot, while I find the surcharge it allows to attacks in which you roll first and then choose who you\u2019re actually going for, with the particularly nice idea of forcing a bunch of potential targets to defend themselves before knowing whether the blow will land on them or not. I like that element of unpredictability and trickery there.<br /> <br /> All right, full version of Octopus-and-Spider Barrage. I think it\u2019s ultimately stronger than the QC one, an across the board multi-attack, can be done with any Ability per attack, reflexively change weapons, and with up to a number of attacks one higher than the character\u2019s Essence, to a total of five. Initiative is still divided, but unlike a lot of similar attacks it doesn\u2019t ignore Hardness; considering the potential size and the flexibility, I\u2019d say that\u2019s a fair cop. Oh, actually, it also lets a chosen number of those attacks by levelled on the one opponent, and the Protean effect lets successful attacks add dice to the following ones\u2026 yeah, I\u2019d say this one can be pretty strong if used under the right circumstances. I like how this one gets the root concept of the original idea, while also not tying it directly to using each limb (either obligating a human form to use their feet or making an actual octopus or spider overpowered).<br /> <br /> Aaaand last Charm for the time-being, Unerring Fang Technique. Full Excellencies on withering attacks get to add a non-Charm success, and extra dice for every ten they roll. That\u2019s just gravy.<br /> <br /> Yes, I think these are off to a good start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T20:22:45-08:00","id":1290982,"title":"","content":"Ehhh, screw it. I can finish off the Offence Dexterity Charms.<br /> <br /> Okay, Essence 3 starting with Agitation-of-the-Swarm Technique.<br /> <br /> I remember, ages ago, at one of the earliest times of postulating on Lunar Third Edition Charms once a baseline was established with Solars, I speculated that in comparison to Solar Charms that entailed more complex processes, Lunar Charms might be uniformly more direct and singular. It\u2019s been interesting to see ways in which that was ultimately off the mark, with how many have gone for effects layered on top of each other. In this case, a sufficiently effective decisive attack can forgo a bit of damage (a limitation that can eventually be overcome) in exchange for instantly disarming or unhorsing the target. When I look at this one, even though it\u2019s not in the description, I get the impression of Lunars at least looking like they move in ways that are really weird, if it\u2019s not outright stunted to include some manifestation of a bodily transformation to push the additional effect along.<br /> <br /> Toothless Pride Tactic\u2026 I actually feel as though Lunars are consistently engaging an element of having advantages to mitigate being outnumbered, if not actually being better there, so I\u2019ll also eat crow on the at least one occasion where Third Edition White Reaper Style had no direct resonance with them. The image here, of a disarm gambit that can be applied against multiple people, including at range and against whole battle groups\u2026 quite apart from the tactical value, just picturing scenarios in which it would be used\u2026 a Lunar surrounded by a gang of toughs trying to intimidate her, only for her to blur briefly and they all find themselves disarmed. Or an army that is trying to cross a bridge that an obstinate cloaked figure is sitting in the middle of, and when the general makes a threat a silver blur seems to shoot through the middle of the nearest formation and it takes troops a few seconds to register that their spears are missing, and the general decides maybe it would be better to seek a different bridge. It\u2019s delightful.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s Deadly Raptor\u2019s Flight for the Lunar that wants to be moving at full pelt and have their aim remain fixated on a chosen target. And then Thousand Claw Affliction, providing the uncommon multi-withering attack; it may limit how much Initiative can be gained from any one foe (although with enough of them that might end up still getting more than would be common), and considering that this also allows different Abilities and weapons, seems well suited to fighting in concert with good allies. The Protean effect to up the limit of Initiative that can be gained per attack really awakens the cheesemonger within me, and he wants to find a colony of mutated six-armed apes so that those attacks can still be made with bow and sword.<br /> <br /> Running Through the Herd allows the multi-attack Charms to shift the Lunar by a range band after every successful attack, which doesn\u2019t need to count as their movement action if in the appropriate shape. Supreme Predator Alacrity is interesting as a scene-long Charm without a cost, just requiring the Lunar to win Join Battle, and thus providing a mote discount to a variety of lock-on and improved accuracy attack Charms against everybody lower in the Initiative order. I like this one for conveying a sense of a rising fighting spirit that has a predatory edge; a sense that a Lunar is a bit more tensed up at detecting weakness, sluggishness or hesitation in foes.<br /> <br /> And then Lightning Stroke Attack, for the Lunar who wants to be sure that they\u2019re getting the best result from a hit, allowing them to make a decisive attack roll twice and get the better offer, and only pay for Charms enhancing both of the attacks once. I\u2019d almost wonder if this should have a limit per scene, but I suppose that requiring high Initiative gives opponents latitude to prevent it at all.<br /> <br /> Now into the Essence 4 Charms. Heart-Piercing Instinct continues that theme of the Lunar invigorated by sensing weakness, giving them a scene-long capacity to add dice for aiming (or convert them directly into non-Charm successes) when attacking an enemy within reasonable range that is crashed or starting to get badly wounded. Twisting Moonsilver Stroke reverses the order of and broadens its prerequisite, allowing a successful gambit of any type besides grappling to be followed immediately by a normal attack on the victim. For this I just like the image of snatching away a person\u2019s weapon just to cut them down with it, although it can also pair nicely with some custom gambits to mess with people in other ways.<br /> <br /> Finally for those there\u2019s Unhesitant Scorpion Lash, in which a Lunar using the multi-withering attack can either reflexively press a decisive attack on somebody that has been crashed, or use Octopus-and-Spider Barrage to get at as many crashed enemies as the normal limits will allow, with a Lunar in the correct form getting back some Willpower if one of the targets is taken out. I\u2019m really liking how the new combat system is really lending itself to a tree growing out of Octopus-and-Spider Barrage; sure, it was always an iconic Lunar Charm, but I feel that all of this is giving it a deeper characterisation than just \u201cextra limbs is the Lunar answer to flurrying attacks\u201d. Especially fun since the Charm often had the unfortunate distinction of being highly valued due to poor wording encouraging a desire to pack on as many limbs as possible to make some really ridiculous flurries.<br /> <br /> Okay, what terrors await at Essence 5?<br /> <br /> Greatest Huntress Mastery; in the highest expression of going for the jugular of a downed foe, the Lunar can spend motes and anima levels to target a crashed enemy over whom the Lunar has more than twenty Initiative with an unblockable, undodgeable decisive attack. Can only be used once per scene, and the reset condition is a very hefty requirement to gain at least 20 Initiative from one attack, that crashes an enemy, who was also above the Lunar in the Initiative order. I\u2019m a little bit uncertain about this one; I\u2019d want to compare it to any Solar Charms to make an attack nigh-unavoidable, and wonder if that reset condition is even possible. That said, I do like the imagery, of the anima trailing from the attack to form after-images that converge on the victim; it\u2019s got elements of a cool ki attack, evoking a predatory spirit, as well as having plasticity from several methods that a Lunar can attack through.<br /> <br /> My final assessment of the Lunar Dexterity Offence Charms is that it\u2019s really enjoyable how a number of Lunar qualities, predatory, flexible, even playful and tricky, effectively come through in a lot of powers, without needing to incorporate any more body transformation than desirable. I find them to have effectively fulfilled the promise of making a Lunar swordswoman feel appropriately powerful even if of the type to not want to heavily transform their body in battle.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it\u2026 actually combining these with the likes of White Reaper and Single Point Shining into the Void\u2026<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T22:37:59-08:00","id":1291014,"title":"","content":"You know, I like how Needle Quill Technique is ultimately made to feel like more than just a Lunar-skinned Charm to generate ammo by virtue of the following tree of Charms that all build off the idea that throwing a little piece of yourself at an enemy lets it continue to harass or assault them. Those follow up Charms would be just fine as things a Lunar could do with ammunition in general, but it means something a little bit more when it's specific to the bits that a Lunar shed to attack with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:20:30-08:00","id":1291039,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or is anyone else getting TAW flashbacks reading these charms? In a good way, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:31:33-08:00","id":1291064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1291039#post1291039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or is anyone else getting TAW flashbacks reading these charms? In a good way, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the best ways without the &quot;Let's make them Silver Infernals&quot; baggage. Like... The Charms evoke an otherworldly terrifying air of the Lunars... They're definitely Argent... And well, getting to the Int charms will tell how Witchy they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T07:53:03-08:00","id":1291131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1291039#post1291039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or is anyone else getting TAW flashbacks reading these charms? In a good way, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never read those Charms, makes no odds to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:12:42-08:00","id":1291151,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the Defence Charms will be about as long as the Offence ones, so I\u2019ll handle them at the same pace, and then see about going through what\u2019s left to the end.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, start with Agile Beast Defense, something that supplements the basic element of giving Initiative for successfully defending against an attack with some more of the predatory imagery in getting extra Defence against somebody at lower Initiative or who rolled 1s. The Protean benefit of being a small creature allowing the Charm to be declared after you already know how well the attack will go seems particularly good, if effectively offset by how being so small means that you\u2019re primarily oriented at defence. Bending Before the Storm is similar, being able to alternately subtract half of the penalties to Defence, or all of them against those lower-Initiative attackers. And then Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance incorporates a bit more of their imagery to create a scene-long effect in which they can reflexively make defend other actions for allies in close range, and treat anybody attacking a ward as having lower Initiative for the purpose of preceding Charms. Ah, the Charm only works for defending a designated person, and ends if somebody else is defended, that makes sense, keeps a whole circle from clustering around the Lunar.<br /> <br /> Golden Tiger Stance brings in a picture of Lunars mirroring the movements of an attacker, modelled with them getting +1 to Defence and no onslaught penalties to failed attacks for a turn, and lets Bending Before the Storm cause successful defences to also drain some Initiative from the attacker. Coiled Serpent Strike is fairly basic as an introductory counterattack Charm, although it has an Essence 2 repurchase to let it counter multiple attacks on the same tick and putting off resetting Initiative until the end, to get in that advantage when outnumbered.<br /> <br /> Into Essence 2 with Ever-Evolving Defense, which emerges from the universal Charm Quicksilver Second Face, enhancing that rapid shapeshifting as a defence by letting its successful use acquire extra Initiative, and a repurchase at higher Dexterity allows a surcharge to be paid to let the Charm be used against an already rolled attack, on the condition that the Lunar assume a shape that has not been used in the scene (with another Charm letting that surcharge be waived). I like using some of these Dexterity Charms to enhance that defensive application of rapid shapeshifting, to help that image retain a significant place in their defensive suite.<br /> <br /> Fleet Gazelle Exercise rests on an image of Lunars being supremely elusive prey (and maybe a bit of revelry in outpacing pursuers) with a scene-long bonus to Evasion and getting Initiative after every round in which attacks failed to hit them. Followed by the image of evasion to twist an attacker into overextending themselves, being used after dodging a decisive attack to make an attacker lose Initiative for every 1 on their roll (also 2s, if in a Tiny or smaller shape), up to the Lunar\u2019s Essence. I might think it\u2019s not fully in the spirit of Lunar Charms to specify a defence, but between the usefulness of the effects and the image that they\u2019re drawing upon, tying it to Evasion is appropriate.<br /> <br /> Foe-Baiting Sidestep keeps going, letting the Lunar who has successfully dodged a close-range both move away by a range band, and drag their attacker along with them. I can\u2019t fully recall, but I think this is fairly distinct from a lot of Dodge Charms to move after evading, and I imagine it\u2019s intended for things like pulling an attacker away from the benefit of their allies, or into better range of the Lunar\u2019s own. That and the suggested application of pulling them directly into harm\u2019s way, even if the person gets the opportunity to recover. Or heck, since it doesn\u2019t use up the enemy\u2019s move action, it might just force them to waste it to get back into a previously advantageous position, rather than advancing or retreating as they might have intended.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, having already seen Flowing Body Evasion, it\u2019s interesting to actually see all of these Charms that a Lunar might use on somebody even when their attack was actually successful.<br /> Ah, but Parry gets a bit of love as well, starting with Gleaming Crescent Block, by which such a guard can cause 1s to be subtracted from attack successes, and which gets to combine with Coiled Serpent Strike by letting that loss be added as dice for the counterattack\u2019s damage roll. To just skip a little for the sake of keeping that theme going, I\u2019ll observe Vigilant Mastiff Technique, which grants +1 to a Parry for protecting somebody with defend other, and forces anybody who wins to direct the attack at the Lunar, which can function against even unblockable attacks if the Lunar knows the Charm Heron Sheds Rain (coming up a bit later).<br /> <br /> Finally, there\u2019s Sensing the Deadly Flow, by which heightened battle instincts are represented in suffering no defensive penalties from wounds, onslaught or grapples, as well as waiving the Initiative cost and Perilous keyword of Golden Tiger Stance, and discounting the cost of Bending Before the Storm.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the defence might lend itself a bit less to vivid imagery than proactive attack does, but that what is managed here so far makes a good show of it, particularly anything that lets Lunars cheat a little with being selective for defence against attacks already known to work, and the number of things that can be done to an attacker who failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T14:26:43-08:00","id":1291256,"title":"","content":"Okay, upper ends of Dexterity defensive power.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cunning Prey Reversal has fun imagery to the name, of building on its prior to show that prey and predator are not a dichotomy in Lunars, by way of giving them bonus Evasion against a decisive attack, and lets them get the lost Initiative from when the attacker misses, with Protean to go in for the \u201conly use it when you know it\u2019ll work\u201d thing. Snarling Watchdog Retribution, that was in Glories I think, furthering the protectiveness element by letting a Lunar with ten or more Initiative make a decisive counterattack against somebody going for their ward, which is made especially potent by being able to <i>add</i> the ward\u2019s Initiative to the roll to determine damage, without the ward even needing to reset Initiative.<br /> <br /> I see that Flowing Body Evasion has been slightly modified from the preview, where adding it to a base defence had the potential to be a costly waste if the attack actually failed, so I think it\u2019s beneficial to have the basic form give you <i>something</i> in added Evasion, before it gets into the Willpower surcharge to subtract Evasion from the damage of successful attacks.<br /> <br /> Okay, Heron Sheds Rain was mentioned before, what do\u2026 ohh, they\u2019re getting their high power parry up front as well. So on the base of it, Parry can be applied against unblockable attacks, and a surcharge lets the character roll their Initiative and add successes to Parry as a non-Charm bonus, which sounds like it has the potential to make some especially strong blocks, necessarily offset by the reset of Initiative (which is held off until after some necessary counterattacks are made). I feel as though, on the face of it, the actual defensive power behind this parry might be stronger than Heavenly Guardian Defence, although that Charm has it beat in being less overtly costly (although it might hurt for stopping a bigger attack), and only being available once per scene barring the rather heavy reset condition of getting at least 20 Initiative in one go.<br /> <br /> Heh, and speaking of being predator and prey simultaneously, Shadow-Chased Silver Defense represents the image of a Lunar somehow moving to escape and intercept simultaneously, allowing them to Parry and Evade at the same time, not only adding the values together, but letting Charms specific to either form of Defence co-exis\u2026 hahaha, oh that\u2019s delightful, to have said \u201cit\u2019s slightly contrary but necessary to specify Charms to defence type\u201d and then ultimately have them reconnect at a point of \u201cLunars can do both at once\u201d. Wonderful. Sure it makes sense that it doesn\u2019t fully work if faced with an attack that one of the defences can\u2019t be applied against, and it can only be used once per scene, but it\u2019s fairly cheap and the reset condition of defending from three decisive attacks is fairly accommodating. This is a good one.<br /> <br /> Ah, and this line stops with an Essence 4 Charm, Becoming Water\u2019s Envy, in which the Lunar gets a particularly weird and mystical form of defence by way of responding to an attack that successfully beat Evasion by rolling current Willpower + Evasion, to establish a threshold that the damage roll needs to beat to be able to apply itself at all (with failure qualifying as a dodge). I think the wording on the last line needs to be a little bit clearer, but I take it to mean that an attack dealing damage lower than the established threshold but enough to fill the Lunar\u2019s health track will not be stopped by the Charm; I can see that both as a necessary balancing concern, and something to go with the imagery of the Charm as constituting a battle of wills. Either way, it can only be used once per day, barring the reset condition of effectively dodging every attack in a fight, which I\u2019d say is challenging, but conceivable.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, Defence ultimately came across fairly well, being all sinewy and tricky and powerful. Dexterity has made a good case for Lunars in combat, once again doing the good job of letting one Attribute effectively carry a lot of the pressure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T20:28:49-08:00","id":1291413,"title":"","content":"See if I can\u2019t finish off the Dexterity Charms.<br /> <br /> Looking back on the Second Edition write-up, I recall how the ones for moving around were the Dexterity Charms that I found\u2026 interesting at all (I\u2019d kind of forgotten how weakly written Dexterity overall felt to me). So I\u2019m looking forward to seeing what might be done with that angle in this set up.<br /> <br /> <br /> But, got to start small, with Graceful Crane Stance, which functions identically to the Solar Charm of the same name as usual. It then gets to immediately leap into something weird, with Cat-Footed Grace described as having the image of a Lunar regaining footing by shifting one\u2019s form directly upright, mechanically represented with a reflexive rise from prone action that can be made off turn, doesn\u2019t count as movement, and can reroll 1s. And then Wind-Dancing Method, allowing for controlling one\u2019s descent to be able to do things like slow down falling (increasing the time and reducing the damage from a fall), and being able to horizontally cross a range band without it counting as a movement action; this one is described as alternately making one\u2019s body lighter or growing the kinds of membranes that flying squirrels and the like have. It makes me wonder if a few of the mobility Charms might entail some more overt transformation.<br /> <br /> Instinct-Driven Beast Movement allows brief bursts of high speed as an automatic success to a movement action or appropriate extended action, and getting some extra Initiative if it supplements a successful opposed action in combat, with a Protean effect of a speedy animal getting to take that Initiative reward away from an opposing character. And Spider-Climbing Attitude simply allows one to cling to and move around on walls and ceilings and the like (with Lunars that have spirit shapes that can do likewise being able to learn it with Wits), although it requires continuously putting in motes across turns. I\u2019m wondering if a later Charm might relieve some of that burden.<br /> <br /> Heh, Wounded Beast Flight: \u201cI\u2019m not running away Finn, this is all part of my plan!\u201d For Lunars to harness the motive of their injuries to make it easier to move out of a fight, ignoring wound penalties for disengage and withdraw rolls, and not needing to lose Initiative when disengaging under sufficiently bad wounds. In all seriousness, I like the way the first line characterizes this all in terms of rage, the idea that it can motivate in directions besides furiously fixating on an offender.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been waiting on a reminder of the previewed Swift Killer Style, by which a Lunar can adopt the image of a speedster fighter or hit and run attacker, getting to reflexively move a range band away in whatever direction they want (allowing flexibility in follow up tactics) when they close in on and hit an opponent, with flying or aquatic forms being able to rise fairly or descend fairly long distances, in return for paying a bit of extra Willpower. I was already interested in seeing this the first time, a more direct combative Charm in the midst of a lot of previews focused on the personal, transformative or mystical elements, and think it pairs especially well with a number of the actual combat Charms (those being why I wanted to see it again, now that there\u2019s context).<br /> <br /> Shifting Octopus Trick is a root Charm to let a Lunar\u2019s body become flexible or gelatinous to make keeping a hold on a Lunar more difficult, enhancing actions to escape bonds, with the benefit of doubling 9s and starting with their Essence in successes against ropes, chains or manacles that are magical, making escape from the mundane a guarantee regardless of rolls result, with failure just making it awkward enough to entail some dramatic complication (an element that I\u2019d honestly like to have seen in some Solar Charms), and being able to double 9s to escape a grapple, with animal shapes that can contort being able to double 8s instead. The dramatically interesting failure thing is a nice way to handle a power like this, and I feel that being so low down might create an interesting basic assumption about how Lunars need to be handled.<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Armor Approach describes itself as involving a Lunar\u2019s flesh flowing into or out of armour, and while that might often be pictured as entailing actual fluidification, the image it most recalls to me is an event from Fullmetal Alchemist; namely, when Alphonse Elric is accosted by a bunch of human chimerae (in that setting, hybrid beings created through alchemy), they effectively take him captive by one of them with snake features sliding head first into his neck hole, adjusting herself within through contortion, and getting her limbs inside of his and bracing them up. I don\u2019t know, it always stuck with me because of how the artwork effectively made it look very sinuous, and kind of weird and violating for Al to experience, so it\u2019s where my mind is going with this; I think it would still constitute a sufficiently weird and unique way for a Lunar to get into a suit of armour. Anyway, in addition to letting one don armour with time reduced from minutes to turns, they can briefly remove the mobility penalties of armour (which puts me in mind of the old moonsilver attunement bonus, which I was always fond of), and at Essence 2 can purchase it again to be able to provide that assistance to putting armour on another person or animal (that being something where I <i>would</i> see more fluidity), and able to relieve a mount\u2019s strain under armour as well.<br /> <br /> Essence 2 starts with Predator Grace Technique, a short but sweet Charm in which a Lunar benefits from rushing a wounded enemy by adding their penalty as non-Charm dice to the action, which in addition to the described image of going for the weak first, I take as Lunars being able to excite themselves with the sight or scent of a weakened enemy. Ferocious Hound Pursuit is taking the same cue as a bunch of previous Charms directed at lower-Initiative enemies, this one letting them replace the usual effect of a successful rush with instantly advancing a range band towards the target, which doesn\u2019t count as a move action. And it all comes to Silver Jaguar Pounce, in which a Lunar can immediately advance a range band closer to an enemy that was just crashed or had wound penalties increase, and getting their Essence as bonus damage dice if a decisive attack is made no later than the Lunar\u2019s next turn.<br /> <br /> Yeah, a lot of this is the kind of stuff I like in the Second Edition Charms, the image of honing in on prey or a designated rival. A lot of this is probably ultimately more balanced than it was before, if only because some of the powers get to be spread out across a larger number of Charms.<br /> <br /> Shifting Many-Legged Stride gets back into some of the weird with the description of a Lunar\u2019s legs continuously changing to adapt to the landscape, although it\u2019s fairly low-key and unintrusive (by which I mean it can be adjusted to taste); anyway, a movement action gets to ignore penalties from terrain, and the concept of adapting to impeded movement gets extended to gambits such as grapples of unhorsing (I\u2019m getting the picture of a Lunar\u2019s feet becoming hooked and flattened to grip to a horse\u2019s underbelly, which must take the animal some getting used to), adding the Lunar\u2019s Essence to the difficulties. In a fast animal form, crossing such terrain also lets one get some extra dice for the move action, and a little more to the difficulty of the gambits.<br /> <br /> For even more definitely not running away, there\u2019s Bounding Hare Evasion, for a disengaged Lunar to get an extra range band away from an enemy (in lieu of being allowed to move again if pursued), although the spirit of it prevents its use on the same turn that the Lunar attacked somebody. And for the occasions where a Lunar can\u2019t not run away far or fast enough, there is the Cornered Rat Frenzy; usable when a character has Initiative 10+, they start by adding Essence in non-Charm dice to disengage rolls, and if it still fails then a reflexive decisive attack can be levelled upon the opponent who beat the roll (although they lose the Initiative from the failure before getting to make the attack), with 10s on the disengage roll added to the attack as non-Charm dice, and incapacitating the confining enemy then allows the disengage action to have succeeded. The Charm doesn\u2019t count as an attack for the prior one\u2019s purposes, and a Lunar who knows one of the multi-attack Charms from before can pay Willpower to be allowed to make an attack against any enemies that beat the disengage roll.<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Guardian Defense folds back to one of the Defensive Charms, acting as an enhancement to Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance to allow defend other actions to extend to short range, as well as having the option to spend Initiative to instantly cross a range band when a ward is attacked, if doing so would bring them in range to defend other, which doesn\u2019t use up the move action. It also finally inclines one of those Charms to the Solar Mate, allowing spent Initiative to be recouped if the Lunar\u2019s defence succeeds, or they take the hit for the Lunar. There\u2019s a Protean effect to let flying forms ascend after moving to protect an ally, but I feel a little bit shaky on the application of that. That might just be because it\u2019s getting late, and my attention is starting waver a little.<br /> <br /> And Mobility Charms come to an end at Essence 3 with Relentless Cheetah Pace, with which predatory instinct allow a rush action to be made against an enemy at medium range, spending the next two turns automatically crossing the intervening range bands in addition to any normal movement, with the bonus of combining with Ferocious Hound Pursuit to cross the distance instantaneously, which has to be a rather terrifying final sight for many people to have experienced. Probably a lot of people being told they\u2019re going to be broken like a Kit-Kat bar.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I think the Movement Charms effectively capture a lot of the imagery that I found compelling in the past, and then expand upon it. They also synergize very nicely with some of the prior Offence and Defence Charms, helping to both characterize Dexterity and extend its capability. My initial impulse was to be a bit off about it being largely combat oriented, and having less for general improvements to raw speed output, but\u2026 my first following thought was to not really care, since it didn\u2019t feel strictly necessary for that to be an area of expertise, that was immediately followed by the idea that a lot of Charms like that may end up with Strength and/or Stamina instead. Which I would actually be all for, both on grounds of those feeling appropriate to outputs of raw power or endurance compared to Dexterity having a focus on more precise movements, and to continue that element of certain competencies being distributed across Attributes.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's getting late and there\u2019s some more of Dexterity than I was expecting, so I\u2019m going to leave those until tomorrow, and then get a start on Intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T12:26:50-08:00","id":1291576,"title":"","content":"Ah jeez, I have not managed my time today effectively at all. Woke up earlier than I have in days, and then putz around taking ages to write one of the shortest sections of commentary I have yet. I'm gonna be paying for it tomorrow when I'm trying to power through Intelligence.<br /> <br /> Heh, I wonder if Dexterity getting more subcategories than the prior Attributes might contribute to its unfortunate godstat reputation. Anyway, I\u2019d like to see how its flexibility provides an alternative approach to Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> Starts with Night Stalker Approach, which being an Instant Charm, entails adding some motes to the cost of Charms that enhance things like Larceny, Stealth, and anything done while in concealment to let them be mute, with small spirit shapes getting to take it as Manipulation. Seems fair, both as an Essence 1 Charm, and to generally not let Lunars readily keep hidden while employing their powers. Skulking Rat Spirit lets a Lunar reroll 1s (and 2s when in a small animal shape) on rolls for Stealth, concealing evidence and covering tracks, to represent an image of being able to depart without leaving a trace. And Unseen Predator Menace starts bringing in the scary stuff, with Stealth rolls being unpenalized by concealment in combat and sapping Initiative from enemies that fail to beat the rolls, which the Lunar can get a chance to steal if they\u2019re in the shape of an ambush predator.<br /> <br /> Snake-Finger Style (another great name) is used to double 9s on a variety of larcenous actions dependent on nimble hands, and prevents any drawbacks from lacking proper equipment. And we\u2019re already in Essence 2 with Midnight Phantom Movement, a name that puts me in particular in mind of sign-offs that would be attached to threatening messages in the Irish Land Wars; the actual effects enhances Lunar Stealth rolls to maintain concealment, and prevents them from being penalised for crossing terrain in which such concealment would be especially tricky, with ambush hunter animals shapes also getting an enhancement to when they rush an enemy from out of that concealment. I\u2019ve got to say, it\u2019s nice to be seeing these Charms after, shortly before doing so, having been thinking about the tiger specifically in terms of different values it might have as a shape.<br /> <br /> But, like the other Dexterity Charms, there\u2019s another facet to the Lunar ethos, found in Elusive Prey Approach, allowing a Lunar to follow a successful dodge by reflexively rolling to enter concealment, albeit without removing the associated penalties on its own. And it returns to the larcenous character with Thieving Magpie Prana, conferring a potentially heavy bonus of non-Charm dice to rolls for pickpocketing or general theft for when the Lunar is currently unobserved, with the added benefit of putting a timer on how long defeated potential observers have before they\u2019re able to notice the object missing.<br /> <br /> Flashing Steel Reversal is one of these growing out of some of those combat Charms, to improve what Lunars can do with disarming; when attempted on lower-Initiative enemies, they get the unusual ability to add an Ability (Larceny of course) to the attack and Initiative rolls, and with a free hand and close range get the option of reflexively readying the removed weapon for themselves, although it takes Essence 3 to be able to overwrite the commitment for Artifact weapons, and the Lunar is otherwise stuck wielding it with its awkward weight. Rather than itself, I\u2019m suddenly thinking something about the old Charm clouds, which I might elaborate on later.<br /> <br /> Night\u2019s Swift Fang is a scene-long enhancement that lets a Lunar who is hidden from all enemies at the start of a round to get a bit of extra Initiative, and take their turn first, being able to make an unexpected attack with a free Excellency if their Initiative was already high enough to go first. It can only be used once per scene, with no reset condition, but an appropriate animal shape improves the extra Essence acquired.<br /> <br /> For Essence 3, they get Argent Whisper Cunning to flurry Stealth actions with anything besides attacks or other things that break concealment, unless they make a repurchase allowing a Willpower surcharge to let the Stealth flurry with a decisive attack, with a successful attack obligating them to use up their movement action to move into a new concealment area and attempt Stealth. If in an ambush predator shape, the flurries don\u2019t even need to take penalties.<br /> <br /> These stealthy attack Charms are fine, just not much more to say on them.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see\u2026 Shadow Talon Execution, can make a regular decisive ambush attack but get to add extra successes to the attack roll (animal shape gets double 9s on the attack roll, potentially maximizing the damage) that sounds decent. Silent Swooping Owl, makes the Lunar and their use of tools completely silent for a round. Twisting Penumbra Veil\u2026 ah yes, this was previewed. It\u2019s a shame, it\u2019s the more interesting of these Charms with its clashing an attack with Stealth, but I\u2019ve already talked about that. Although I will say that, in context, that kind of power to return to concealment feels a lot more important.<br /> <br /> And then it gets to end with an Essence 4 Charm, Cryptic Unknown Beast. Ahaha, that idea of forcing characters to reroll their successes on Awareness rolls against Stealth in order to convey the idea of being momentarily visible before vanishing to mess with people is great. It\u2019s once per scene, but is reset by the process of the whole preceding style by incapacitating an enemy with an unexpected attack and then effectively concealing oneself from enemies, even being able to roll Join Battle again if the saved Stealth roll conceals from everybody, with the right shape.<br /> <br /> <br /> Subterfuge does a few nice things. It rounds out Dexterity\u2019s characteristic theme, feels like it encompasses a comprehensive stealthy fighting style in its own right, and contrasts effectively with the kind of subterfuge that Appearance can provide.<br /> <br /> But Dexterity is not done yet. I\u2019ve got some other business to attend to, but when I\u2019m ready I\u2019ll try and zoom through the Swarm Charms to finish it off. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T21:14:29-08:00","id":1291713,"title":"","content":"I have come back from seeing Alita Battle Angel, and feel as though I have seen the face of my new Lunar patron. Time to chase that feeling into the Dexterity Charms that in no way resemble a single thing she does in that film.<br /> <br /> Okay, finishing off Dexterity a bit with the Swarm Charms, looking like an elaborate extension of what previously only functioned as a couple of Knacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> It gets right into things from Essence 1 with Cunning Anglerfish Decoy, allowing one to pull off the Sun Wukong trick of snipping off a piece to form a personal duplicate. It\u2019s necessarily limited, not having a capacity to act independently, can\u2019t perform proper actions at all, doesn\u2019t withstand more than one successful hit, and unable to move very far from the Lunar, although its defensive capabilities can be decent, and depending on the original Lunar it might be surprisingly good at not being sussed out. My initial thought on the ability to hold conversation is that results might be limited with the Lunar\u2019s bound range, but on further though, quite apart from medium being a decent range, I\u2019d say the option for the Lunar to be following or ranging ahead in an alternate form can help preserve the ruse. I also think that it\u2019s clever to model forming a duplicate with witnesses, and banking on enemies thinking that they\u2019re the real one, with a Stealth action to become concealed even in plain sight. And I find the number of duplicates to maintain at once, and costs of producing them, to be quite generous.<br /> <br /> Still\u2026 considering the premise, maximum Dexterity doesn\u2019t not make sense, but creates a bit of a flat curve. At least as far as enhancements to human duplicates go.<br /> <br /> Oh hey, and to let more people in on the fun, it\u2019s actually a Totemic Charm for <i>two</i> Attributes, with small creature totems having the option of Manipulation or Wits. So under the right circumstances, any of the Castes can get in on the fun.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I\u2019d actually been thinking before that the picture of the Lunar breathing out a swarm was for one of these Charms rather than Intelligence (which actually makes me even more excited to read that one). Thousandfold Wasp Dance is fairly straightforward in function, produce the creatures as an environmental hazard with some of the qualities of a battle group, that can partly move by the Lunar\u2019s will. Definitely think it makes more sense for dispersal to utilise a gambit with something like fire, rather than the idea of swatting down the whole swarm in bunches.<br /> <br /> Oh, that one was Essence 2, and used the prior as prereq? Mildly curious choice.<br /> <br /> Essence 3 is also following directly from Cunning Anglerfish, for good old And-and-Starfish Trick. It functions as an enhancement to its prerequisite, allowing a not too expensive surcharge to be paid to give the initial duplicate something like true independent life. {rereads} Ah, CAL is able to duplicate animal shapes, the Lunar just has to be in them at the time. As for what independence entails, the duplicate can think for itself as make choices about actions, if human gets copies of everything inherent to the mind and body, as well as the Tell, and an unencroachable Tie of loyalty to the original. It\u2019s still limited to the Lunar\u2019s proximity, but measured now in miles. Equipment gains functional duplicates (although Artifacts are just replicated cosmetically), but possesses no supernatural powers. Mundane observation of personality can\u2019t distinguish the copy from the original, and if the Lunar wants to internalise what the replica experienced while it was separate, it\u2019s necessary to end the Charm while touching them for absorption, otherwise everything is lost. This one also gets to be used repeatedly, but loses the generous discount.<br /> <br /> This would be something where I\u2019m starting to buy it being Totemic for small animals a bit less, even if I can suppose some logic of having mass to spare.<br /> <br /> An alternative path for CAL that incorporates one of the counterattack Charms is in Living Hive Transformation\u2026 which I already saw and commented upon. Neat form of area denial and punishing attackers, fun creepy image, putting it amongst the Swarm Charms actually helps to settle it in a bit more amidst all of the other Dexterity Charms that are less overt.<br /> <br /> Essence 4 provides Hungry All-Consuming Cloud, enhancing the duplicate Charms further, and\u2026 hoo boy this is a long one. Okay, work through it, errr, ah, Lunar becoming a swarm; alternative way to activate Emerald Grasshopper, that sounds reasonable. In place of the usual effects of Miniscule Size, the Lunar is stuck with\u2026 oh wait, there\u2019s good stuff too; it goes extra health levels for the more diffuse form, gets a swarming attack with decent stats and a whole bunch of flexible tags (including the Flexible tag), which can hit multiple enemies at once in the typical manner, and is incompatible with Simple Charms. There are a few enhancements to grappling (which does give a certain impression of these still being super strong vermin)\u2026 oh, it\u2019s actually basically all good stuff; the Lunar can\u2019t Parry, but Evasion goes up, minimum withering damage is halved, and decisive attacks are slightly weakened, although the benefits can\u2019t apply to things like fire, large projectiles, multi-attack or area-of-effect powers, and whatever else might strike a large portion or otherwise mess up a swarm. Grapples become impossible barring a power that could grasp or scoop up a swarm, and anything human size or smaller has difficulty getting away. I\u2019d say that this effectively makes a Lunar becoming a cloud of little devils seem like something impressive and powerful, after the previous Charm took up the space of modelling it as an environmental hazard. I think a fight involving two Lunars doing this in opposition would be neat.<br /> <br /> Oh, aaand Essence 5 provides Locust-and-Starling Legion, allowing a Lunar to branch out as a whole battle group (for all intents and purposes, one fixed at Size 3), albeit one with some limits: can\u2019t have Drill or Might, Initiative works in the normal manner, has to divide between withering and decisive attacks, and can\u2019t be targeted with command actions or similar Charms. Also can\u2019t combine area attacks with Simple Charms. Magnitude (pop pop) still confers a noteworthy benefit of being separate from the Lunar\u2019s main health track, as attacks disperse copies rather than hit the true self (which going by the Charm\u2019s mechanics, I guess is effectively non-existent while spread out as about a hundred creatures), and filling the track to reduce Size creates a risk of the Charm ending prematurely in lieu of rout, with such a sudden collapse causing the Lunar to take a level of damage. It can only be used once per scene. I know that Vance went back and forth on letting Lunars become battle groups, but I\u2019d say this came upon an effective compromise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So that\u2019s the Swarm Charms, a nice consolidation of what were some previously distributed and slightly meandering effects, and rounding out Dexterity with some very overt transformation shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:12:48-08:00","id":1291980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1291014#post1291014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I like how Needle Quill Technique is ultimately made to feel like more than just a Lunar-skinned Charm to generate ammo by virtue of the following tree of Charms that all build off the idea that throwing a little piece of yourself at an enemy lets it continue to harass or assault them. Those follow up Charms would be just fine as things a Lunar could do with ammunition in general, but it means something a little bit more when it's specific to the bits that a Lunar shed to attack with.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a neat subplot in Kelly McCullough's WebMage series where Tyr's hand shows up as a supporting character and meets Tyr and is <i>thoroughly pissed</i> that Tyr never came back for him.<br /> <br /> Honestly, seemed kinda unfair, but reading your thing made me wonder if these detached bits of yourself could not only take on a life of their own, but their own sapience as well, and the open question of how much agreement there'd be between the original Lunar and their lost progeny after a hundred years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:12:59-08:00","id":1291981,"title":"","content":"Okay, messed up a lot of stuff with my time, so\u2026 going to be a little bit of a strain to fit this in.<br /> <br /> <br /> So Intelligence. It\u2019ll be interesting to see where this one can go, considering that its purely cerebral quality has been a frequent source of consternation in assessing the Lunars in the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Heart\u2019s Blood Charm is Blood Geas Binding, allowing for shapes to be taken in payment from people that break oaths sanctified by the Lunar. I think it\u2019s interesting how this one could be taken to a few places, such as the shape being employed for retribution, or possibly even the people bound by oath knowing the consequences and being incentivized by them. It makes me wonder if knowing that a Lunar can look like you is a scarier prospect than the curse of an Eclipse Caste.<br /> <br /> And it makes sense that Memory-Drinking Meditation is part of this category. I\u2019ve already talked at length about the implications of that one, but see that this more finished version has an upgrade at Essence 3 allowing for a slightly larger mote commitment to acquire the entirety of a person\u2019s memories in one go, although it seems at least one Tie still needs to be acquired. I think it\u2019s good for the experience to be kept grounded in experiencing the memory as the original person did, find the idea of using the other Charm to go diving through an entirely new set of impersonal experiences to make an intriguing image, and think there\u2019s something neat and unique in the idea of teaching yourself a skill by consulting adopted memories of having already learned it.<br /> <br /> Stolen Voice Echo helps the Essence 2 Lunar maintain the viability of their disguises by being able to use the Memory-Drinking Charm (at higher cost) to acquire a target\u2019s languages in addition to memories, which can ultimately serve as a means for a Lunar to retain that language permanently. I like this better to the last Edition\u2019s method of language acquisition, which was more straightforward and dull. Huh, Intelligence sure gets a lot for Heart\u2019s Blood\u2026 ahh, Lessons in the Blood extends the prior element to a more mystical side, as the Lunar is able to steal a target\u2019s knowledge of a spell, Martial Arts Charm, or some of the thaumaturgy they knew. What I like about that one is how it synergizes with Charms to acquire shapes without killing, such that it might imply even a somewhat voluntary exchange for the sake of expediting instruction.<br /> <br /> And a sidebar addressing the subject of experience debt, which functions the same here as in the prior Edition.<br /> <br /> Okay, Knowledge Charms, just going to skip ahead a little\u2026 not that many, I can cover all of them before posting this.<br /> <br /> Starts with Inevitable Genius Insight, taking a syncretic approach to Lunar mental capability by letting them add part of\u2026 just about anything with its own knowledge base to a Lore roll, as well as treating their specialties as a basis for being able to use something as a Lore field. If there was going to be any Attribute that said \u201cit really helps to have some Abilities to go with this\u201d, I guess that Intelligence would be up near the top. At least at this early point.<br /> <br /> Wayfaring Sage Meditation is similar, but in a more instinctual or holistic direction, as the Lunar is permanently enhanced to be able to treat profound personal experiences or achievements as a basis for Lore fields, which also feels like a very good characterizing element, a picture of how an Intelligence Lunar might live their life (which has some use for a concept I\u2019ve had in the past). Also lets that experience provide specialties to other Abilities for dirt cheap.<br /> <br /> But Dreaming Wisdom Revelation takes things into the more strange and mystical by providing the starts of a Lunar divination. The Lunar gets to perform some appropriate divinatory ritual, make a dice roll, and bank the successes as points representing foresight that can be used for a variety of things based on the image of having seen something cunning or gotten a direct channel to some source of knowledge; stuff like getting more fact introduction, contributions to spells or craft projects, improves some information based activities, get to use a few Charms retroactively for the image of knowing ahead that you\u2019d need something, or make fact checking automatically successful. I know it\u2019s early, but I think this is a good place to start with clarifying or consolidating some ideas from prior Editions with regards to Lunar divination or encoding universal knowledge, that kind of just floated around vaguely, never quite being fully realised. I think it\u2019s good for something like this to be limited to once a story, and like the reset condition being acquiring the lore field from the prior Charm, both for giving that more impact and adding to the incentivized activity.<br /> <br /> Tale-Spinning Mastery pulls in an element hinted elsewhere that I\u2019m interested in seeing realised, Intelligence as the Attribute of the teacher and storyteller. I do actually think that it\u2019s good to put this element here rather than in the social Attributes, for a few reasons; those are already focused on their own thing, it helps realise some of the foundational concepts of the No Moon Caste, and it lets Intelligence have something to not keep it too internally focused. I also think it can be a useful way of characterizing the Lunar take on the Attribute as more than just something clinical, and if it\u2019s fudging the lines a bit\u2026 Lunars need it, and Intelligence Charms need it, so I won\u2019t keep score if you won\u2019t. As for the effect, it\u2019s a distinct way of providing a listening character with Ability dots, especially if the Lunar tells about something that happened in the game (or\u2026 just learned a story in play) or using a fact that they introduced. Whatever the level, it greatly reduces training time to model the character developing skill in that unique manner, and balances the subject of experience debt not being tracked for NPCs by limiting the use on them per story. The base Charm can only teach one at a time, but purchase at later power can widen the instructed audience.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, Night\u2019s Mercy Panacea\u2026 I think this was previewed before, but the wording seems a bit different\u2026 the mechanical element of getting non-Charm dice for using a treatment based on an introduced fact seems new, and I\u2019m sure that before it referred to the treatment based on exuding something from the Lunar\u2019s body\u2026 maybe I\u2019m mixing it up with something else. If not, it\u2019s a small change, but I\u2019d have some thoughts\u2026 perhaps I\u2019ll go over them later. As for the Charm, the basic effect is fairly straightforward, but I think the Lore element colours it a bit towards this Attribute\u2019s character.<br /> <br /> Plague-Swallowing Kiss gets something more overtly them, with being able to cure a person outright by absorbing the malady directly into their own body, which I\u2019d say is both flavourful and can have some further applications based on additional Lunar powers. I particularly like the Totemic option based on a spirit shape of a carrion feeder.<br /> <br /> Moonlit Cauldron Apothecary is extending some of the prior significance of the Lore side with allowing one to introduce a fact about the existence of some rare herb or mineral that can be used to roll to cure a familiar poison or disease instantly (which I think also gives a certain attunement to the natural world quality, but not a very heavy one), although it still needs to handle the subject with the normal rules. My first impulse is that, even if this is appropriately flavourful, it\u2019s a much more roundabout way of getting at something that\u2019s very straightforward for Solars. My second impulse is \u201cit\u2019s an Essence 1 Charm, you prig, give them a chance\u201d. There are some thoughts, but I\u2019ll wait until the picture is more complete. Speaking of, there\u2019s a reference to interaction with another Charm, but I\u2019ll wait until I see what that does.<br /> <br /> Oh, maybe that Charm I saw previewed was this one that it\u2019s saying can be used to directly synthesize one\u2019s discovered medicine.<br /> <br /> Okay, moving on. Bone-Mending Technique: administer a treatment that can greatly increase a character\u2019s rate of healing at rest. Like, assuming somebody with a minimum of Medicine of 1, their patient is healing nine times faster. Even more if they incorporate something from an introduced fact. Sounds useful. And Flesh-Sculpting Art makes a return; I think there are some neat ways of systemizing the way that flesh is rendered malleable here, rerolling 1s for surgical rolls, don\u2019t get penalties for no tools, able to do hours of work in minutes, and the surgery itself never causes injury. On top of all that, the stuff with being able to alter faces or add little body pouches is just gravy.<br /> <br /> For Essence 2, Moon-Kept Mysteries\u2026 okay, I\u2019m seeing it now, using some of these avenues for Lore checks to represent all of that long talked about stuff of No Moons extracting hidden wisdom. The mechanical effect of double 9s for a Lore or recollection roll and getting Willpower from a big success is simple, but it\u2019s building up the image.<br /> <br /> Ah, Counting the Elephant\u2019s Wrinkles, that\u2019s the good stuff. Gets to reroll dice on rolls to introduce facts or other things including mental Attributes related to a recalled memory\u2026 I\u2019m liking the image of somebody pulling up a key fact about warfare to help bring their command roll up. It can also be a basis for enhancing Resolve against effects that would alter memory. Have to wait until Essence 3 to get it in a form that allows one to experience a memory again at length and in detail, though, which also gives a once-per-story option to use it to negate memory-altering powers when attention is drawn to them; I\u2019m liking those together for the image of diving into one\u2019s memory and manually correcting the out of place elements. I think this is a bit narrower than some prior Editions have made it, but it benefits from being systemized.<br /> <br /> Huh, into Essence 3 already. Burning Moonfire Mind, that\u2019s another good name. A Lunar gets to make an Intelligence roll with a couple of options for Abilities (including Integrity, interestingly), and turn the successes into motes that can be held for a scene to be spent on later mental Charms to enhance a variety of cerebral actions, or put into sorcery. This feels like a Charm that can only be fully appreciated with some good experience with managing mote pools in play, and the value of some useful things not taking a knock out of it. It would probably feel more overt to me if it was phrased as a discount, but this way it gets to be more overt in building up a spell.<br /> <br /> Okay, what does Midnight Soul Reprieve do\u2026 ah, a kind of medicinal action crossed with a bit of the storytelling to help treat mental illness. And it manages that with\u2026 right, so in the short term, a character has some of the symptoms relieved, and in the long term (upon success with a somewhat lengthy extended action for treatment) downgrades its intensity to a minimum of Minor (except for Addicitions, which can be removed completely). Relieving the symptoms of a Minor level illness doesn\u2019t require dice action, just paying the Charm\u2019s cost. It can also help fight off Psyche effects or other powers to alter the mind, with a successful roll reducing the Willpower needed to resist them. I overall appreciate this for the same reasons that I did the similar Terrestrial Charm, and would be interested in seeing how those compare.<br /> <br /> Oh, and it\u2019s finally an Intelligence Charm with a Protean effect, giving the dice rolls double 9s if in a shape the patient has a strong Tie to; apart from the human side, you can make for an effective therapy animal.<br /> <br /> Right, Starfish-and-Salamander Meditation was mentioned before, what does it do? Right, this is for treating crippling effects and other disfigurements or congenital shortcomings. Takes the form of a lengthy extended action, although its interval can be shortened\u2026 no, the roll interval can\u2019t be shortened, just the amount of time the Lunar needs to spend working on the patient per interval, with Flesh-Sculpting Art. And Moonlit Cauldron Apothecary\u2026 oh, it partially bypasses the usual extended action rules and lets all of the successes on an interval roll count towards the goal. This is kind of one where a comparison to a Solar Charm feels very straightforward and ends up with a power that is less good (albeit in a slightly more elaborate way, mechanically, and one that still allows the Lunar to ultimately completely restore somebody). I don\u2019t really mind that; it probably has to end up somewhere, and it doesn\u2019t feel like a very big deal considering all of the gems surrounding it.<br /> <br /> Up to Essence 4, and What Lies in Darkness\u2026 models Lunars being able to deepen awareness and draw knowledge from altered states by making rolls to introduce facts without being limited by background. It can only be used once per story (albeit with a reset of the introduced fact greatly aiding the Lunar or somebody close), but I\u2019d say this is a good way of using that system to represent Lunars being able to know things beyond their normal ken.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Intelligence is off to a decent start, some nice effects and imagery in here.<br /> <br /> Tuesday has unfortunately caught up with me before I\u2019m done, and I got a very late start today. Maybe I could spend the next few hours pushing through the next twenty pages, but\u2026 I think I\u2019m better off, on several counts, of getting a nice earlier night in now, start up fresh and early in the morning, and see if I can\u2019t polish them off quickly before going straight into some Lunar Dominions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T16:36:56-08:00","id":1292009,"title":"","content":"Martial arts and sorcery tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T16:54:21-08:00","id":1292013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292009#post1292009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial arts and sorcery tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus Christ...<br /> <br /> I think we're far enough away from the last preview of setting material that getting the Dominions now would no longer qualify as front-loading. It seems to me that saying the chapters aren't being released in order because they don't want to front load setting material is kind of a contrary sentiment to releasing a couple of chapters full of mechanical stuff (including the intricacies of a couple dozen new Merits, and the shapeshifting and Tell rules), followed by Charms, followed by Martial Arts and Sorcery, and then what, more Charms? Or is this week replacing the Charms with the Dominions chapter?<br /> <br /> Right now, I'm feeling as though the alternative to not front loading setting stuff is to leave us so crushed under the weight of mechanical stuff that seeing text referring to something other than Charms will feel like manna from Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T17:31:16-08:00","id":1292026,"title":"","content":"I agree it would be nice to take a break from mechanics for a little bit.<br /> <br /> Going back to the review I really like how witchy/mythical the intellect charms are! They really caught my interest even if they don't have the raw poor of solar lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T21:38:05-08:00","id":1292067,"title":"","content":"Well, Lunars has basically three chapters of setting info and the rest of the book is mechanics and they already gave us two of them. At some point we were gonna have an &quot;all mechanics, all the time&quot; week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T21:55:47-08:00","id":1292069,"title":"","content":"Eh; Artifacts are technically mechanics, but they're not only divided by little character beats, they're a lot less intense than Exalted or Martial Arts Charms.<br /> <br /> You go Silver Pact/Charms/Traits/Charms/Dominions/Charms/MA &amp; S/Charms/Antagonists and animals/Charms...<br /> <br /> Hmm, too many weeks... so is the alternative to front loading setting stuff to just pack it in at start and stop? Because it's looking like we're getting Dominions, other characters and animals <i>and</i> Artifacts all packed together in the last week, in addition to the last few Attributes. That seems rather heavy.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe I should consider this schedule from the perspective of somebody who would just read the damn thing, rather than keep a running commentary on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T22:08:12-08:00","id":1292071,"title":"","content":"I think it runs through the 12th, so they might have Artifacts on the last day or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T22:25:24-08:00","id":1292076,"title":"","content":"I thought we would get Dominions and the MA/Sorcery chapter tomorrow. Could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T23:56:02-08:00","id":1292084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292069#post1292069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh; Artifacts are technically mechanics, but they're not only divided by little character beats, they're a lot less intense than Exalted or Martial Arts Charms.<br /> <br /> You go Silver Pact/Charms/Traits/Charms/Dominions/Charms/MA &amp; S/Charms/Antagonists and animals/Charms...<br /> <br /> Hmm, too many weeks... so is the alternative to front loading setting stuff to just pack it in at start and stop? Because it's looking like we're getting Dominions, other characters and animals <i>and</i> Artifacts all packed together in the last week, in addition to the last few Attributes. That seems rather heavy.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe I should consider this schedule from the perspective of somebody who would just read the damn thing, rather than keep a running commentary on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The KS runs from Feb 12th to March 14th, which gives us five Tuesdays (12th, 19th, 26th, 5th, 12th) and four Fridays (15th, 22nd, 1st, 8th). So that's five slots for the non-Charm stuff and four for Charms.<br /> <br /> So it goes Silver Pact/Charms/Traits/Charms/MA&amp;S/Charms/?/Charms/?, where the question marks are Chapters 3 (Dominions), 8 (Artifacts) and 9 (NPCs and animals). Now, there are more chapters remaining than question marks, so one week's going to see two chapters, probably 8 and 9.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T09:56:27-08:00","id":1292199,"title":"","content":"Ohhh I\u2019m a little messed up. I\u2019ll recalibrate eventually. Let\u2019s see what some nice Mysticism Charms might do for me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right, Crossroads Walker Entreaty. Basically like a somewhat weaker version of the Eclipse anima diplomatic power, with an additional quality of making hearing what they have to say mandatory, that the spirits and fae (which a sidebar provides definition for) can pay Willpower to be able to ignore the words and a bit more to initiate violence. But the Lunar also gets a bonus to their Resolve and Guile, and if they\u2019re in a shape that the beings have an important Tie towards then overcoming the Charm requires Decision Points instead of just Willpower. Seems like a good way to get a foot in, and I do like the notion that it sometimes ends in a paw or a hoof.<br /> <br /> Ardent Prayers Fulfilled, lets one make influence rolls to get a spirit or fae to act for the benefit of their worshippers, or that conveys a message from those worshippers, gets double 9s and the unique benefit of adding their Cult rating as non-Charm dice. I find the idea that the Cult can\u2019t be a source of Willpower to resist the influence to be particularly neat and insidious.<br /> <br /> And Devil-Pleasing Chiminage was seen in preview, but if there\u2019s anything new to it\u2026 the Essence 2 benefit of getting to treat the offering as a Defining Intimacy to appeal to sounds unfamiliar. In any case, this fact introducing is a neat way to present the idea of appealing to spirits with unusual offerings, and I particularly like the idea that it could convey an element of knowing a way in that even the spirit doesn\u2019t know yet.<br /> <br /> Raiton\u2019s Dark Auspice, already previewed as well, although I had missed that it was a permanent enhancement to interacting with ghosts at the time. And then there\u2019s Graveyard Hound Vigil, which upgrades Charms that work on spirits and fae to include physical undead beings excluding the Exalted; I do kind of wonder about that, since the general presentation of zombies is as something mindless, and I\u2019m not even sure of the circumstances in which they would have worshippers\u2026 what sounds more valuable is gaining the capacity to gain Willpower and shed Limit for upholding an important Intimacy through a variety of achievements related to the Underworld and the dead. If there aren\u2019t other Limit shedding Charms, I could get an interesting picture from this of characters being able to centre themselves against the pull of their Urges by standing on the liminal space between the living and dead worlds, so that would be a vivid way of pulling in that world walker element.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Penumbra Witch Mastery looks like a good example of one of those multi-faceted Charms; extra dice and 1 rerolling for sorcery and thaumaturgy rolls, introducing facts about or understanding a variety of supernatural beings and phenomena, and character insights into spirits and fae. I think the manner in which it is both broad and specific helps it feel more interesting than the usual dice enhancements, and it\u2019s still effectively working out the image of Lunars having unusual sources of knowledge.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Sharing Luna\u2019s Gifts, that sounds promising; has a health level cost and all. Yes, Charm for granting mutations (with an experience debt cost; I\u2019m going to assume that it treats the usually Innate/Story Merits as though they could be purchased for that purpose), that seems reasonable for Essence 1, and up to five dots is fairly generous. The capacity for the Lunar to target themselves with the Charm (not needing to spill their own blood to anoint themselves, which I would have found a neat image, but the picture of just harnessing their blood directly kind of matches it anyway) initially felt like it resolved a question for me; five dot Wings would be a particularly useful mutation, but they\u2019re beyond anything but Hybrid Body, which would both require a winged spirit shape and takes up most of that Charm\u2019s benefit. But the fact that the Charm bestows the mutations permanently\u2026 would it be possible to add the Merit for making those wings retractable on top of this once the experience debt has been paid off? Mind, that would mind up making those wings a bit more convenient than what those shapeshifting Charms could provide\u2026 I\u2019ll think about it.<br /> <br /> Ooh Swarming Locust Punishment looks like a neat kind of curse; enhance the Blood Geas Charm so that oathbreakers not only forfeit their shape, but become targeted by vermin in ways that cause things like pain and difficulty to getting through the wilderness, prevent them from effectively sleeping, and potentially induce an Obsession with eliminating the pests tormenting them. I do like how the Lunar has the power to deliberately revoke the curse before its natural duration of (Essence) weeks elapses or set a condition to end it; I, for one, would have a mind to often defaulting to a condition that stops it before it starts, in any case where the Lunar doesn\u2019t think that the broken oath warrants that kind of punishment.<br /> <br /> Okay, Essence 2, beginning with Argent Guardian Yantra. Converts a bit of the anima into a ward that can\u2019t be crossed at all by any spirit with lower Resolve than successes on a roll that the Lunar makes establishing it, unless their Essence exceeds the Lunar\u2019s (which still costs them some Willpower). I\u2019m not quite sure about the shape of the ward; the radial one is clear enough, but the line\u2026 the description about being bound against crossing it sounds like just projecting a section that can cover a particular path, but the description of the projection kind of sounds like it\u2019s extending from the Lunar\u2026 I think the description of that one could be a bit clearer. Still, it sounds like it can have its uses; an image that stands out to me is a Lunar that has worked their way into a court of devils to negotiate, and when they go south surrounds themselves with a barrier to hold attackers off for a moment before getting to turn into something highly mobile to make good an escape. Maybe instead cast some kind of useful spell.<br /> <br /> Keeper of Midnight\u2019s Gates provides a means of forcing spirits to materialize; even for the spirits that can resist that force, I\u2019d say that there can be a benefit to inducing them to spend Willpower. Ghost-Banishing Howl allows one to exorcize possessing spirits, only needing a roll to beat their Resolve; it can also be used to make an Argent Guardian Ward into a cage for spirits (which frankly sounds more useful), and it has what looks like the most useful Protean benefit to an Intelligence Charm yet, of allowing a shape the target is afraid of to strip Willpower equal to rolled successes from any spirits of lower Essence.<br /> <br /> And finally Cage of Horn and Sinew allows one to ape one of Jesus\u2019 less known feats, of forcing an exorcized spirit to inhabit the body of a nearby animal for months at a time. The process sounds particularly nasty for the spirit imprisoned; they\u2019re stuck with the animal\u2019s traits, can\u2019t use any powers, even their mental capacity is diminished to be in line with that natural to the creature\u2026 they nominally have control of the body, but can\u2019t even lead it deliberately into death to free themselves. And even when they do depart, it leaves a mark on the spirit as a Defining Intimacy related to the animal\u2019s nature and/or experiences while imprisoned (the animal gains a similar thing in response, possibly even becoming god-blooded, assuming the animal isn\u2019t immediately slain by the newly released spirit). It overall sounds like a rather fearsome thing that Lunars might do to unruly or offensive spirits. Ah jeez, and it gets even worse; if the Lunar has the Charm to permanently destroy the spirit, they get the option to imprison it for a whole year, during which the spirit is bound to a Defining Tie of gratitude for the Lunar\u2019s mercy. That one can even apply to spirits of higher Essence so\u2026 yeah, might be some horror stories among gods and demons of people pissing off the wrong Lunar and getting the enjoy a year spent as a trout or something.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Font of Dark Wisdoms\u2026 oh wait, I get it; my first read was that the Thaumaturgist Merit it bestowed was limited, but I can see how it\u2019s not just limited to those five dots of rituals, that\u2019s just the amount you get for free\u2026 which I think might ultimately amount to getting to pay the cost of all those rituals as a single package\u2026 yeah, even if Intelligence isn\u2019t Caste or Favoured, you\u2019re getting between 13 and 15 XP worth of rituals for a discount of 3-5 points. And you get to take the Charm repeatedly to get even more rituals at a premium, so it\u2019s still beneficial even if you get the Merit just from becoming a sorcerer. Actually, come to think of it\u2026 those five dots of rituals surely aren\u2019t including what you got for getting the Merit the first time\u2026 do you get a new ritual every time you take the Charm? Overall, this seems like a decent path into that form of minor magic.<br /> <br /> A Lunar initiated into sorcery can learn the Spell-Rending Talon, through which decisive attacks by a high Initiative Lunar can help to distort spells that are buffing up the sorcerer that the Lunar is attacking, with the particularly good looking benefit of not counting towards the terminus for that disruption.<br /> <br /> Ah, finally getting to this one at Essence 3: Beast-Soul Awakening Crucible. Create a zone (that has to be situated in a demesne or Wyld spot; hadn\u2019t expected that, but it seems reasonable) in which people who pass some appropriate trial acquire six dots worth of mutations modelled on the Lunar\u2019s spirit shape, a transformation meant to convert them into beastfolk, that they become capable of passing down to their children to propagate lineages. If the Lunar is a chimera, their zone can bestow mutations reflecting one animal or the other, depending on how the trial is passed. I wonder if the mutations are determined by the Lunar upon creating the crucible, or apply differently for every petitioner. I like how the Lunar not only doesn\u2019t fully control the nature of the trials, but that it\u2019s also meant to include the nature of the demesne or Wyld. And the consequences for failure sound sufficiently repelling as to give a lot of people pause, making for an effectively evocative setting and story element even apart from the considerations for not empowering whole armies of people. Ah, the duration had been a bit of a concern, but it\u2019s fine that it\u2019s just how long the motes need to be committed before becoming permanent. And apart from functioning as an avenue to take such zones down, I like how a Lunar being committed to preventing a manse from being built or the Wyld from being shaped could be readily misinterpreted as them caring about preserving nature or the Wyld. Finally, the number of grounds that can be maintained sounds rather generous, even before considering how territories don\u2019t count towards it.<br /> <br /> Okay, want to go through them a bit more quickly now when they don\u2019t stand out especially\u2026<br /> <br /> Crimson-and-Silver Rebirth: clean somebody in your blood to remove a mutation or shaping curse, although you only get one shot at it. But you do get to take away such things that you bestowed yourself without cost or roll\u2026 all right then, that resolves the Wings dilemma\u2026 possibly\u2026 do you still have to pay XP for a mutation after removing it from yourself? I might not be taking these in the spirit that they\u2019re intended. Heaven-Darkening Eclipse allows one to\u2026 wow, that\u2019s powerful, introduce facts about how to dispel the ongoing effects of spirit Charms (not for the Incarnae or Yozis or any theoretical Essence 10s) or sorcerous spells, allowing actual dispellation rather than mere distortion, although doing so gives the Lunar away to the one who cast it. And when repurchased at Essence 4, actually allows for Terrestrial workings to be destroyed entirely, and suppress higher ones for the length of some major task of the Lunar that the working would impede. This is a big one, and might speak a lot to the kinds of sabotage that Lunars have levelled throughout the Second Age.<br /> <br /> Ohoho, Unravelling the Tapestry looks like <i>fun</i>; the discordant element of Lunars allows them to determine loopholes even in the enduring prophecies of Sidereal and Solar Exalted. The opposition can\u2019t be casual, and can\u2019t mitigate the predicted effect entirely, but the Lunar, their Mate, anything they deeply care for and magically claimed territories will be protected by such success, and the Lunar also gets to be forewarned by prophecies that would target them or their cares to the extent that the Charm activates itself. I like the little example given and all. It\u2019s an impressive way of having Lunars interact with such events, fitting with their nature, and also puts a bit of their relationship with Sidereals into context.<br /> <br /> Already saw Insidious Lunar Transformation\u2026 but Endless Masquerade Affliction lets one do a similar (but longer lasting) effect of turning one person into another (one of the Lunar\u2019s shapes)\u2026 it\u2019s described as a curse (and surely would be, if you turned a prince into a peasant or the like), but can surely be beneficial to some people, like disguising one\u2019s agents or creating confusion about where and when certain people were and which ones might be Lunars. Selkie Mantle Enhancement extends from ILF to grant a person the capacity to change back and forth between human and animal (or human, if the Lunar also has EMA) at will, for as long as the Lunar commits motes for them (made cheaper if Lunar and beneficiary care strongly for one another).<br /> <br /> Spirit-Sealing Talisman allows exorcized spirits to instead be imprisoned within objects, from which they can <i>never</i> escape unless destroyed (made harder by their supernatural durability). The Lunar can commit motes for the talisman\u2019s wielder to be able to use an Eclipse Charm the spirit either has, or a custom one that fits their nature, as long as they have the appropriate Essence (although the Lunar can spend Willpower to let another use the Charm on the Lunar\u2019s behalf, of which the Lunar will always know), and while the power is lost if the commitment is dropped, the Lunar can freely recommit to acquire it again, while the spirit remains imprisoned. This one sounds both very useful <i>and</i> horrible.<br /> <br /> From Essence 4, Chains-of-Silver Geas provides yet another path for dealing with truculent spirits and fae; they just need to overcome the being (which seems to need to present a meaningful opposition) in some challenge, physical, spiritual (i.e. exorcism) or social, which then becomes irresistibly bound to perform an inconvenient or serious task, or even a life-defining one if the Lunar\u2019s Essence is equal or greater. It\u2019s even a very compelling binding, from which the being can only meaningfully deviate to attend to another threatened Major or greater Intimacy, or use them in Decision points to win short reprieves from pursuing the task. It can only made to last more than a year if it entails a task that the being could meaningfully conclude, but automatically prevents them from attempting to harm the binding Lunar in any capacity but self-defence. And it can only be used <i>against</i> a character once per story; you can\u2019t readily put multiple bindings on the same figure, but you can hand out geasa left and right to many. This one looks really good on a number of counts, such as mystical binding rooted in a specifically Lunar method, engaging the function of guardianship, giving a bit more substance to how often the fiction has referred to them as bending gods and Raksha to their will. Good stuff all round.<br /> <br /> Hmm, pretty sure that Doom Brought to Heel was previewed\u2026 yeah, I\u2019ve seen the power to evoke a cured poison or disease as a serving spirit before. Not much to say about it on its own, but some of its interactions with other Charms\u2026 hmm, not too sure about being able to remove a person\u2019s mental afflictions altogether in the course of turning them into spirits\u2026 oh, but the idea of converting a defeated Charm or spell directly into a weird kind of spirit directly contrary to the power it was born from is particularly interesting. In most respects, the power comes off very well.<br /> <br /> And last of the Mysticism Charms, Witch-Among-Swine Spite; that\u2019s a name with some real teeth on it. When a character the Lunar distinctly dislikes offers some kind of offence in their presence, it becomes possible to curse them into animal shape at range and without feeding blood. Most of the heavy lifting of this one is done by the prior Charm, but it adds on a nice bit of edge; to my eyes, more from the punishing offenders side than the doing it at range.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, Mysticism acquits itself well, lots of distinct curses and blessings and a particular character to how they interact with other supernatural entities, a little bit more stick than carrot.<br /> <br /> Crafting shouldn\u2019t take very long, and then I\u2019ll get a starting look at\u2026 some of the new stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:38:22-08:00","id":1292213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ardent Prayers Fulfilled, lets one make influence rolls to get a spirit or fae to act for the benefit of their worshippers, or that conveys a message from those worshippers, gets double 9s and the unique benefit of adding their Cult rating as non-Charm dice. I find the idea that the Cult can\u2019t be a source of Willpower to resist the influence to be particularly neat and insidious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really liked this charm for being directly shamanic; in the sense that it's really all about interceding between mortals and spirits. I'm not sure I'd use it a lot, but it's very characterful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I do kind of wonder about that, since the general presentation of zombies is as something mindless, and I\u2019m not even sure of the circumstances in which they would have worshippers</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not much use with Ardent Prayers Fulfilled, but I think it's very useful for Crossroads Walker Entreaty, because as long as you don't attack, zombies will have to spend 2wp to attack you.<br /> <br /> There's also the general persuade charms; while persuading a Zombie might be pretty difficult, because they're very stupid, I think you could roll (maybe with a penalty) to persuade them to do stuff like &quot;attack that guy&quot; or &quot;go away&quot;. Or maybe bargain, like &quot;No, don't attack that village. Wouldn't you prefer this tasty brain I'm holding? Look, doesn't it look good? Eh, eh?&quot;<br /> Same as you'd roll against a dog or horse or something.<br /> <br /> And there might be more intelligent zombies or revenants. In 2nd ed, there was a Celestial spell where you could make an intelligent zombie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, Sharing Luna\u2019s Gifts, that sounds promising; has a health level cost and all. Yes, Charm for granting mutations (with an experience debt cost; I\u2019m going to assume that it treats the usually Innate/Story Merits as though they could be purchased for that purpose), that seems reasonable for Essence 1, and up to five dots is fairly generous. The capacity for the Lunar to target themselves with the Charm (not needing to spill their own blood to anoint themselves, which I would have found a neat image, but the picture of just harnessing their blood directly kind of matches it anyway) initially felt like it resolved a question for me; five dot Wings would be a particularly useful mutation, but they\u2019re beyond anything but Hybrid Body, which would both require a winged spirit shape and takes up most of that Charm\u2019s benefit. But the fact that the Charm bestows the mutations permanently\u2026 would it be possible to add the Merit for making those wings retractable on top of this once the experience debt has been paid off? Mind, that would mind up making those wings a bit more convenient than what those shapeshifting Charms could provide\u2026 I\u2019ll think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can stack it, though obviously you have to pay XP, as it mentions Storyteller characters only being able to get it once a story. So Wings with one use, then Subtle and something else with a second use.<br /> <br /> I think Wings costs 22xp though, which is a ton.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And finally Cage of Horn and Sinew allows one to ape one of Jesus\u2019 less known feats, of forcing an exorcized spirit to inhabit the body of a nearby animal for months at a time. </div> </div> </div>People don't know about Jesus's low-key trolling?* Obviously seminary training needs to improve.<br /> <br /> *Which kind of works in Exalted, as the Realm also has Legions, though I'm not sure I can actually think of any societies with unclean-food taboos in Exalted, oddly. I think the Icewalkers don't eat their totem animal, but from respect rather than it being unclean, so wouldn't really want to put a spirit in one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Already saw Insidious Lunar Transformation\u2026 but Endless Masquerade Affliction lets one do a similar (but longer lasting) effect of turning one person into another (one of the Lunar\u2019s shapes)\u2026 it\u2019s described as a curse (and surely would be, if you turned a prince into a peasant or the like), but can surely be beneficial to some people, like disguising one\u2019s agents or creating confusion about where and when certain people were and which ones might be Lunars. </div> </div> </div>IIRC, our Changing Moon had great fun turning her husband into herself, then turning herself into him, and the two of them getting up to shenanigans as each other.<br /> (Though he didn't appreciate being a concubine as much as she did being a Prince)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:47:59-08:00","id":1292218,"title":"","content":"When I first read Flesh-Sculpting Art I was like &quot;Hey, we can't induce Mutations? What gives?&quot; And then I kept reading and found that the follow on charm, Sharing Luna's Gifts, was in the Mysticism section. Which... ok, I guess I agree with it, but it makes it a bit difficult to find things.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I hope they decide to publish official charm diagrams for Lunars or that we can get that as a stretch goal, because I think Lunars kind of needs a set of them. I get that wordcount is at a premium so they can't be in the book, but I'd buy a pdf of them for an additional dollar or so and I'd be much more interested in a set of those than I would charm cards.<br /> <br /> Have you found it difficult to find things at all? Or figure out how charms relate to each other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T11:08:52-08:00","id":1292223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292213#post1292213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There's also the general persuade charms; while persuading a Zombie might be pretty difficult, because they're very stupid, I think you could roll (maybe with a penalty) to persuade them to do stuff like &quot;attack that guy&quot; or &quot;go away&quot;. Or maybe bargain, like &quot;No, don't attack that village. Wouldn't you prefer this tasty brain I'm holding? Look, doesn't it look good? Eh, eh?&quot;</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Same as you'd roll against a dog or horse or something.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It makes sense, but feels somewhat unsatisfying.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think intelligent undead need to have more examples than just the power to make them to feel more present in the setting, and meaningful to interact with.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But maybe there are some things I've overlooked in the mini-releases.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think you can stack it, though obviously you have to pay XP, as it mentions Storyteller characters only being able to get it once a story. So Wings with one use, then Subtle and something else with a second use.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think Wings costs 22xp though, which is a ton.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I wonder if it would be unbalanced to be able to remove a mutation at will with the later Charm and duck out of the debt, but then there's the question of whether you lose the XP paid on something that you opted to remove from yourself.</span></span></span></div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292218#post1292218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I first read Flesh-Sculpting Art I was like &quot;Hey, we can't induce Mutations? What gives?&quot; And then I kept reading and found that the follow on charm, Sharing Luna's Gifts, was in the Mysticism section. Which... ok, I guess I agree with it, but it makes it a bit difficult to find things.</div> </div> </div> </div>This relates to something I was alluding to before; in a very superficial sense, I think it's similar to stuff that I always heard about the old Lunar Charm clouds, except where the deviations and crossovers are internal to each Attribute, rather than jumping around between several of them*.<br /> <br /> I think it's ultimately beneficial for major reasons around making clear that these subcategories are just soft distinctions, and the Charms are all ultimately of the same Attribute, and to emphasize the diversity of Lunar powers by showing that the trees are not strictly limited to each of those categories; if it makes sense for a Charm to develop in a direction that falls under a different one, then go for it.<br /> <br /> I think that categorizing them like this ultimately makes it easier to know what effects can be found where, and helps maintain the sense of thematic consistency, and that sometimes being far removed from a prerequisite is a reasonable exchange for that.<br /> <br /> * I recall a person who once said that they liked the Charm clouds, because he saw them as encouraging diversity in Attribute allocation, to which I responded that it really just made developing a character's powers really taxing. I think it's apparent now that they're a lot better off when specialization is encouraged, and diversity is much more strongly emphasized by giving all of the Attributes interesting things to do rather than making them mandatory.<br /> <br /> In a sense, I suppose I can imagine one way in which Grabowski's point about Appearance was kind of vaguely reasonable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T11:23:26-08:00","id":1292224,"title":"","content":"There's always Moon's Hidden Face for hiding stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T13:08:30-08:00","id":1292241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292223#post1292223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It makes sense, but feels somewhat unsatisfying.</span></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think intelligent undead need to have more examples than just the power to make them to feel more present in the setting, and meaningful to interact with.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But maybe there are some things I've overlooked in the mini-releases.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"> It interacts with all Charms that deal with spirits, including Argent Guardian Yantra and, presumably, the inevitable Spirit-Detecting Glance/Ghost-Eating Technique-alikes.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T13:15:17-08:00","id":1292244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292241#post1292241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It interacts with all Charms that deal with spirits, including Argent Guardian Yantra and, presumably, the inevitable Spirit-Detecting Glance/Ghost-Eating Technique-alikes.[/LEFT]</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant creatures, not other Charms!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T13:17:03-08:00","id":1292246,"title":"","content":"Okay, time to finish off Intelligence.<br /> <br /> <br /> You know, prior to looking at it, I had been thinking about the matter of Lunar relation to Abilities and what it might mean for a category to be focused on a singular one. Thus, Many-Phase Insight is a very good one to start with, as well as being an interesting concept in its own right; being able to generate craft points with success in tasks related to learning and knowing things concerned with one\u2019s Craft categories, or employing self-made tools for matters of medicine or navigation (as well as still giving the Attribute a nice hint of tattooing, with that being valid as an objective for points).<br /> <br /> Similar with Brilliance-Drinking Approach, that idea of harnessing inspiration from the blood of other crafters (possibly including the likes of beavers and spiders and such). Apart from the general picture of the nature of their power, I think it\u2019s interesting to consider the context in which things like this would be applied; Lunars in circumstances where they don\u2019t really have the resources or opportunities to keep up a continuous crafting practice, so you build towards important projects by means of survival and learning and hunting.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I knew there would still be sorcery, but\u2026 Demon-Drinking Fang, that was mentioned before and hasn\u2019t been seen yet\u2026 maybe crafting won\u2019t be very long. Faster!<br /> <br /> Protean Creator Discipline just covers a simplistic image of being a multi-faceted crafter by being able to double up on their Ability points for applying across numerous fields. And now that they\u2019ve got all of this build-up for working on things, Wonder-Weaving Art starts to provide their actual capacity to craft, although it\u2019s dependent on calling up the full scope of their Lunar intellect, with full Excellencies on craft rolls providing the additional benefit of double 9s, which at higher Essences can be improved to 8s or even 7s with craft point and Willpower surcharges.<br /> <br /> Pattern-Realizing Genius might turn out to be their closest equivalent to Craftsman Needs No Tools; rather, the craftsman definitely needs all of the tools, and raw materials, and the Lunar\u2019s supreme insight into how they fit together allows them to complete a project with great rapidity (the image of somebody assembling things with whirring hands is one I like, but didn\u2019t fully fit with Solar Charms, I think it works better here). Also nice to be able to get a little discount on the point cost for major projects.<br /> <br /> Beast-Slayer\u2019s Art\u2026 is not one of the previewed Charms, just an earlier version of the concept; using the parts of a slain animal (or similar spirit) in a major project provides additional silver points towards the endeavour; I think the limit of one animal per project and one project per animal is appropriate for keeping the Lunar from making everything out of a dozen voles or arming a battle group with the remains of a yeddim. For Essence 2, Endless Ingenuity Approach lets a character reap gold and silver points from upholding Intimacies with the use of knowledge and cunning, nice bit of expansion from prior concepts and characterisation there (and I think the per-story reset condition of fulfilling objectives with at least a major project is very fitting). And Implicit Design Epiphany is one where I like the description of reaping insight from their own inherent multiple possibilities, and the basic mechanical function of improving craft point rewards (particularly how it can apply to Charms to get them as well).<br /> <br /> Inchoate Wonder Realized is the first directly for making Artifacts\u2026 I had been wondering how they might realise that idea of Lunars working effectively in constrained and limited circumstances, and the idea of being able to skip ahead a bit when something is being made or repaired to keep it going for a short period seems like an interesting way of managing that. You\u2019re building the thing, you reach the limit of your means or patience, you just hold the rest together for a story with your Essence and go straight out with it. If you get the chance to finish it towards the end, great. If not, just keep it together for use and then put it aside until you can work on it again. Quenched in Legend can enhance that Charm towards furthering the Artifact\u2019s development by providing gold points to complete it as rewards for various feats achieved using it, and awakening Evocations out of it, with a particularly significant bonus at the Charm\u2019s end if an especially significant goal was accomplished using the device, so that\u2019s another one for Charms shaping interesting stories.<br /> <br /> Ever Mutable Prowess provides further help, as the Lunar can meditate to convert their craft points upwards. And Shifting Skin Raiment\u2026 wonder what a gold point cost might be good for\u2026 ahhh, they get to create clothing and jewellery from animal parts and imbue it with the power to bestow mutations. Not as powerful as true Artifacts, but don\u2019t have Essence costs or commitments, and at up to five points per item\u2026 maybe <i>this</i> would be the way to let a character give themselves functional wings. And for the Lunar who wants to share, treating the object as the basis for Moon-Marking somebody lets them invoke the transformation without cost. It is expensive, though, so probably only used sparingly.<br /> <br /> Silver Crucible Refinement helps towards the work by getting to spend craft points to add non-Charm dice to a roll, although I\u2019d say it really comes into its own at Essence 3 when those points also get to count towards the crafting cost. Introducing Essence 3, Ecstatic Inspiration Satori provides even better craft point rewards when Defining Intimacies are upheld through mental prowess. And Manifest Miracle Forging allows a Lunar to act more rapidly in just about any magical crafting project (plus general large-scale crafting) besides First Age Artifice, making them intervals shorter and discounting the gold point costs.<br /> <br /> God-Skinning Hunter Art was previewed, make Artifacts from powerful creatures. Hmm, Inexplicable Lunar Wonders\u2026 it\u2019s a curious kind of thing. Doesn\u2019t cost any Essence, and the player gets to defer stating what the intended function and character of the Artifact (or manse) is until it\u2019s actually completed\u2026 I was kind of anticipating it to be something that would allow one to hold that definition off until encountering a circumstance in which declaring what it was retroactively would be useful. I guess that the value of this is being able to work on a project without other characters (such as spying enemies) being able to tell what you\u2019re working towards, and not needing to designate something that will be cut off forever if the project fails. It\u2019s interesting, if nothing else.<br /> <br /> It skips straight over 4 and into ending on Essence 5 with Unbound Demiurge\u2019s Dream\u2026 wait, wasn\u2019t there a preview of a Charm to share Artifacts with one\u2019s Solar mate\u2026 was that in a different Attribute? Hmm\u2026 {checking} ahh, it\u2019s in Wits, it will literally be one of the last Charms. Okay, moving on, Lunar gets to spend white points to make a craft roll for a superior or legendary project not count towards the terminus (although in addition to the expense, the number of times it can be used on a project is\u2026 twice, really, for just about any playable Lunar). Fair enough it\u2019s powerful, if not quite as sexy as the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So I ultimately think that as much of Lunar crafting as is shown here strikes a nice balance between the particularly Lunar (emotions, multiple approaches, including animal parts, cunning) and some more general crafting enhancement (which still includes hints of their distinct nature). So what\u2019s left\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ahh, of course, warfare Charms. Back when I was thinking straight, I had anticipated these, because of course, it\u2019s one of the command Attributes. There clearly aren\u2019t many of them, so I\u2019ll come back in just a little bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T15:00:37-08:00","id":1292271,"title":"","content":"Come on, quickly, warfare.<br /> <br /> <br /> Predator\u2019s Deadly Cunning lets them finally get to do something with strategic maneuvers, starting off with the basic adding dice and rerolling 1s, with pack hunter Lunars getting to take it as a Stamina Charm. Argent Pack Formation adds a success and ignores penalties depending on the battle group\u2019s Might. Raiton Follows After adds non-Charm dice to Intelligence command rolls for every 10 initially rolled, as well as what is basically an Excellency when the order is to go for an enemy that is crashed. Silver General Foresight shakes it up a little with the image of employing the Attributes prophetic quality, by giving the attack rolls of a battle group following one of the Lunar\u2019s strategems a bonus success, and allowing command rolls to reroll 1s.<br /> <br /> Goes into Essence 2 with Dauntless Tactician\u2019s Reversal allows one to exchange Initiative for dice on an allied battle group\u2019s rout check, and provides a very brief bonus to Defence and soak for the group that successfully holds together. Triumph-Directing Insight allows a Lunar to transfer the bonus for crashing an enemy or reducing an enemy battle group\u2019s Size from the group that got the key attack in to another one in medium range, in addition to even more Initiative if the crashed enemy was a battle group. Silver Lion Supremacy allows a general to add non-Charm dice to Strategic Maneuver rolls based on the Might of allied battle groups (which plays into the value of beastfolk troops), with a stunt that directly incorporates their supernatural abilities into the Maneuver turning that bonus into successes instead. And Quicksilver Strategy Meditation models the image of their flexibility and unpredictability by letting a character roll to benefit two Strategic Maneuver rolls simultaneously, dividing successes between the two, and being able to active both at once with enough successes.<br /> <br /> Finally, for Essence 3, there\u2019s Sparks-to-Fireflies Reversal: Lunar gets to make a Strategic Maneuver roll, that an enemy is allowed the opportunity to make an opposing roll against (needing to pay Willpower if their armies aren\u2019t already in battle). If the Lunar wins, all enemy strategems are negated. Can only be done once per story, and reset by suffering a major combat setback that puts a Major or more Intimacy at risk.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Intelligence warfare Charms help round out their capability in that area, but does come across as the least invested and valuable branch of that, or at least not the most interesting one; generally utilitarian. Makes enough sense, that the others might be forms of warfare aligning more closely with the Lunar Essence, and it\u2019s good that they still don\u2019t end up being bad Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, all that\u2019s left is the brevity of sorcery.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, Terrestrial Circle Sorcery requires four Charms in any Mental Attributes to learn. Probably a bit of a non-problem for No Moons, and for the rest\u2026 I don\u2019t really mind the characterisation of sufficient investment into those mental enhancements being necessary as a substitute for proper occult knowledge. Cloaked in Moonfire\u2026 wow, being able to hold onto sorcerous motes while not shaping a spell just for having your anima glowing? That\u2019s really good. They might just make No Moons premier combat sorcerers yet.<br /> <br /> Essence 2 gives Shadow-Hands Invocation\u2026 they can flurry shaping sorcery with other actions? I mean, fair enough they can\u2019t be attacks, but still. Getting to make it last for a scene just by committing, what, four motes, six motes? Wow, good for them. The image of having your detached shadow going around shaping the sorcery is cool and all.<br /> <br /> Up to Essence 3 in order to initiate into Celestial Circle. It takes knowing five spells to learn, and honestly, I kind of feel that such a thing should be the case for Solars as well. I mean, I know it\u2019s unlikely to have the second circle without having learned any of the first beyond initiation (and its automatic spell), but the possibility still grates a little.<br /> <br /> And finally, an Essence 5 Charm in Cosmos-Rending Fury, for the real battle sorcerer. Winning Join Battle allows a Lunar to make a reflexive shape sorcery action with a free full Excellency; starting something with the wrong Lunar is just inviting a nasty spell to be blasted off at you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So Intelligence has done very well. Very effectively realises a lot of the fluff attached to the No Moons in this Edition, expands on some old ideas and very heavily fills in old gaps, overall gives Intelligence a lot of interesting and useful things to do in comparison to an Edition in which it\u2026 mostly just gave some craft and combat stuff, and not even a lot. Speaking personally, I\u2019m also very happy that it never went for anything like expanding brains. It did end up going to some very different places than some preliminary ideas I had in the past, but I\u2019m currently thinking those might ultimately be better suited to Wits, maybe Perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T17:02:43-08:00","id":1292296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292271#post1292271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Up to Essence 3 in order to initiate into Celestial Circle. It takes knowing five spells to learn, and honestly, I kind of feel that such a thing should be the case for Solars as well. I mean, I know it\u2019s unlikely to have the second circle without having learned any of the first beyond initiation (and its automatic spell), but the possibility still grates a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. That makes me wonder about revising Solar sorcery initiation to have comparable 'must have at least X spells' (maybe combination of 5 spells or Occult charms) for Celestial Circle, and a total of 10 or 15 for Solar- but then removing the 'no Supernal' restriction.<br /> <br /> I might pose that one a 'what breaks if' thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &quot;What breaks if I start the game letting a player summon Ligier&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T18:06:22-08:00","id":1292312,"title":"","content":"Creation, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T18:30:14-08:00","id":1292319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292296#post1292296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might pose that one a 'what breaks if' thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &quot;What breaks if I start the game letting a player summon Ligier&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything breaks, as such, but it might have issues with overshadowing the contributions of other players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T20:39:08-08:00","id":1292356,"title":"","content":"Hmm\u2026 okay, I can fit in one Martial Art before sleep.<br /> <br /> Centipede Style. Described as being all about speed in the form of rapid barrages of attacks and nimble footwork to get around enemies; even apart from the direct animal symbolism, I can see how this would be very complementary to a Dexterity focused Lunar. It\u2019s all intended to build to a point where the worm down enemy is grappled, to either hit an opened weak point or poison them. Said to be similar enough to Snake Style that in the East, schools have a tendency to either form rivalries with the other style, or syncretize with them. The weapons are fighting chains, hook swords, the newly introduced iron boots, seven-section staves and tiger claws, it can be used in light armour, and benefits from skill in Athletics and Dodge.<br /> <br /> For the Charms, first is Blurring Scurry Prana, which adds dice to a movement action, improves Evasion if that movement is successful, and if used to enhance a rush that succeeded to bring the martial artist into close range with an enemy, gives an extra die to follow up attacks. Motion of Myriad Legs gets into being able to launch a multi-attack really early on, no less than three of them, which can ignore Hardness (although they are limited to a single opponent). It\u2019s also limited in a distinct way by mandating a minimum of Initiative that must be dedicated to each attack, but in exchange gets the benefit of at least one attack connecting and hurting making an onslaught penalty last for an extra turn. Terrestrials get fewer attacks, and their divided Initiative is rounded down instead of up. I\u2019d overall say that this one\u2019s limitations make it reasonable for being such a low level.<br /> <br /> Chitinous Centipede Shell allows one to add the better of their Athletics or Dodge to soak, or use them as Hardness, which Mastery makes function for the length of a whole tick rather than against a single attack; I find it a neat picture of synthesizing the emphasis on speed with being able to ape the creature\u2019s armour.<br /> <br /> The Centipede Form conveys the neat image of moving with a kind of speed to create afterimages giving the impression of dozens of limbs, giving a persistent +1 to Evasion, and allowing decisive attacks against enemies with an onslaught penalty (nicely building from Myriad Legs effect if the stylist fights alone) to get double 10s on the damage roll, or reroll 1s on grapple control rolls, as well as being able to flurry an attack and movement without penalty. It can be reflexively activated when attacking or grappling an enemy with a more severe onslaught penalty. I\u2019d have to look back at prior Form Charms, but I vaguely feel as though those are often about setup, where this looks more about payoff, so I\u2019ll be interested in seeing where the later Charms go.<br /> <br /> Hundred-Leg Embrace (which curiously has a health level cost) allows greater control of a grapple, getting a non-Charm die for every 10 made on the control roll, and forcing an opponent to subtract their 1s from successes. Ah right, the health level cost is optional, made only if they oppose an attacker\u2019s control roll, to represent dislocating a grabbed limb and reposition to reflexively turn the grapple gambit back on the attacker, with bonus dice to attack and control roll based on their initial successes. I like the name for this, The Ninety-Nine More, and what it conveys about the Centipede approach to grappling; Terrestrials can\u2019t use it.<br /> <br /> Tenacious Centipede Technique\u2026 going to put a pin for the moment in that lore, and concentrate on it being used as the basis for an effect of ignoring penalties of injuries and fatigue equivalent to Athletics for rolls for attack, grapple controls, movement and Evasion, for the length of a tick. The Charm is not limited to characters that have taken injury (or worthless for those who have other powers to relieve penalties), as they\u2019ll instead get half their Athletics in extra dice for withering attacks and grapple controls; that feels to me like the kind of need that might have come up in playtesting. Terrestrials are limited by being unable to relieve penalties to their Evasion.<br /> <br /> And it finally brings the poison with Venom-Dripping Mandible, which just basically envenoms a decisive attack, although with the local benefit of being able to add an enemy\u2019s onslaught penalty at the time to its duration, or expend rounds of control while conveying it through a grapple to also extend it.<br /> <br /> Agony-of-One-Hundred-Hells Technique looks particularly nasty, a decisive attack that makes an enemy add onslaught penalty to wound penalty, although given the limit to -4, it feels as though this might be an attack more intended to open a fight than end one. Although, it also allows a poison to discharge multiple rounds of its duration in one go, the number depending on onslaught or wound penalty (or, if grappling, a much higher total for expensing control rounds), so perhaps it can serve both functions. Not often in the same fight, though, with the per-scene use that requires raising an onslaught penalty very high with decisive attack\u2026 unless that earlier Charm can, if used repeatedly, keep rolling the onslaught penalty to the next round over and over again to keep building it up? That might make sense with some of the other effects.<br /> <br /> And last is Numberless Blows Technique, which serves as a permanent enhancement to Motion of Myriad Legs, allowing a large mote surcharge and anima payment to be made for that Charm, both adding one to the number of attacks that it can make and adding half of one\u2019s Essence as damage dice to all of its attacks (which I think might greatly increase its capital as a multi-attack Charm). On top of that, two attacks successfully dealing damage makes the last of them unblockable, three makes it undodgeable as well, and four makes it function as an ambush. If the multi-attack takes the form of a grapple savaging, rounds of control can also be surrendered to add even more dice to the damage roll. Yeah, I\u2019m pretty sure that this is the nastiest Charm for multiple attacks in the whole game\u2026 possibly a little bit too good. Sure, the motes are costly, but it doesn\u2019t exactly rely upon something set up earlier in the style, I think the conditions for piling damage into each of the attacks are very generous, and you can even use it on more than one opponent in a scene. And jeez, Mastery allows Charms besides Excellencies to only be paid once to apply to all of the attacks? Sure the Solar is limited in what can be done with their own Charm, but anything they might fold in with other Martial Arts\u2026 even the Terrestrial limit of only being used on crashed enemies is fairly accommodating, given what the venom can do to an enemy\u2019s Initiative, and if they can\u2019t inflict ambushes (and still one less than others in how many attacks they get) they still have a shot on all the rest for some major attacks. I wouldn\u2019t characterize myself as somebody with deep insight into mechanics, but I wonder if there\u2019s something that I\u2019m missing behind this, and if it possibly might need a bit of tweaking.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any event, I think that Centipede presents itself well as a Martial Arts Style; it's got an evocative flavour that it consistently realises mechanically, there's good internal synergy, I'd say that it holds together effectively. And it is nice to keep having Martial Arts focused a bit more on stylized methods of hitting people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T23:08:49-08:00","id":1292388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292296#post1292296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. That makes me wonder about revising Solar sorcery initiation to have comparable 'must have at least X spells' (maybe combination of 5 spells or Occult charms) for Celestial Circle, and a total of 10 or 15 for Solar- but then removing the 'no Supernal' restriction.<br /> <br /> I might pose that one a 'what breaks if' thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &amp;quot;What breaks if I start the game letting a player summon Ligier&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Your party when the sorcerer fails the binding roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T23:37:36-08:00","id":1292391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292388#post1292388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your party when the sorcerer fails the binding roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that while Ligier's stats aren't printed, in prior editions he was in the same ballpark of power as the UCS, pretty much. You'd have to be in a really bad way to risk everything on a roll that you almost certainly don't even have good odds of making","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T03:40:09-08:00","id":1292429,"title":"","content":"Jeez, poor Ligier needs a good write-up to remind people what he's about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T03:57:12-08:00","id":1292436,"title":"","content":"I just want to say that, while I was pissy before, having actually seen a Martial Art again reminds me of how they're a lot easier to read than full Exalted cascades, because of the tighter focus and more obvious synergies. And I believe that there are fewer here than in What Fire Has Wrought?<br /> <br /> Compared to any Charms, good spells are a bit of a cakewalk, and new Celestial ones are actually rather exciting. This chapter shouldn't take very long.<br /> <br /> And then next up will be Manipulation Charms, which I am super excited to see.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I went looking back over the Universal Charms before to clarify some stuff about mutations, and seeing them in context of shapeshifting rules relieved some concerns. The cost of committing four motes for a shape had seemed a bit high to me, but when there's an Essence 3 Charm to commit three motes to be able to shift freely for a scene, it feels a lot more reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T07:51:42-08:00","id":1292483,"title":"","content":"Yeah, WFHW had 7 or 8 styles, Lunars only has 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T07:57:18-08:00","id":1292485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292429#post1292429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeez, poor Ligier needs a good write-up to remind people what he's about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, I'd love to see any third-circle at all, just to get a vague idea of their power level. Eric said he wrote one up (a new one of the Ebon Dragon), but I guess it's in the queue for monthly releases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:08:54-08:00","id":1292488,"title":"","content":"Okay, show me what Falcon Style\u2019s high-flying kung fu antics can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, actually uses the term \u201chigh-flying\u201d, that\u2019s cute. It\u2019s all leaping into people and working one\u2019s way to a high spot to launch down from, plus a bit of grappling to position them and knock them to the floor for that drop. Also described as being very showy, of a kind liable to draw a lot of people to watch the fights\u2026 hmm, suddenly want to rewatch Jet Li\u2019s Fearless. Probably popular with children; children are pure, they know who\u2019s the strongest. It\u2019s all about the arms and headbutts, accommodating cestus, boots, and the slightest concession with tiger claws and improvised weapons, although it gets to use light armour, and obviously benefits from having Athletics and Dodge.<br /> <br /> So first, that Falcon Takes Flight, allowing them to make grand leaping manoeuvres in the form of adding half their Martial Arts rating as successes to disengage, rush, and rise from prone actions when they\u2019re stunted to include jumping and flying motions, or else make reflexive move actions straight upwards away from an enemy following attack (I suppose that\u2019s something beneficial for when there\u2019s a tree branch or ceiling fixture or something to grab on to\u2026 or maybe it is just valid for getting to a balcony or hill top). Mastery allows either movement to higher elevations to let the successes not count towards the dice cap. This sounds like something that could be fairly useful even for just dipping into the style.<br /> <br /> They get to start actually attacking with Swift Talon Strike (which is another root Charm), letting an attack made following moving into close range with an enemy get an automatic success on attacks, that reroll 1s on the damage roll or to control a successful grapple, with 2s also given that bonus if the movement consisted of descending from a higher position. I\u2019m seeing now that the descriptions of flying aren\u2019t merely metaphorical, it just happens to be a style whose method can be readily complemented by a human that can actually fly. I\u2019m okay with that; I don\u2019t want Styles that could <i>only</i> be used by such a person, but something where it incidentally complements is fine, even desirable. Mastery is similar to the last one, success is non-Charm.<br /> <br /> Raptor\u2019s Fatal Descent allows decisive attacks at a lower enemy (one either knocked prone or at a point beneath the stylist) to add Athletics or Strength as extra successes to a damage roll, and drains Initiative for every 10 on that roll; it comes with the slight drawback of being left prone, but one doesn\u2019t get penalties for being so (and can\u2019t us the attack again until risen, although I would take that as a given). Dropping down usually counts as a movement action, but not for Mastery.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve got to say, not as a criticism but just an observation, for the way the style is described, it does seem to go straight into the aerial attacks. Mind, given the description as being showy, I guess I can see the idea of going for the more big ticket stuff early and then working in the tactical setups deeper in.<br /> <br /> So what does the Form Charm allow? Spreading out their arms to assume a nimble stance from which grapple control rolls get double 9s and Athletics added to rounds of control for the sake of throws and slams. They also get reflexive move actions without needing to roll for ascension, and falling damage gets halved, as well as improved Defence against anybody at a lower elevation who doesn\u2019t have Reaching attacks. Reflexive activation comes from succeeding with a high threshold over opponents in movement rolls and grapple controls. Does definitely feel like a good tactical crux for the surrounding attacks.<br /> <br /> Hmm hmm. Hmm.<br /> <br /> God help me, the entire time I\u2019m reading all of this I have this theme song stuck in my head:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UOoFqbdr-XY\" data-code=\"UOoFqbdr-XY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UOoFqbdr-XY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Tell me it\u2019s wrong!<br /> <br /> Okay, Grasping Raptor Claw allows one to make nasty grapples in which a restrain or drag action gets to be followed by a decisive savaging attack, throw or slam, both on the same turn. It costs Initiative, but that gets refunded if the opponent is rendered unconscious or dead. This feels like a good setup for those who can\u2019t fly, pulling an enemy into range of something that can be climbed and then immobilising them. Terrestrials are limited by needing to treat the two actions as a flurry, with appropriate penalties.<br /> <br /> Talons Greet Prey improves their defensive options a bit, giving bonus Defence against an attack at close range, and allowing a counterattack grapple if the assault fails, with 1s on the original attack added as non-Charm dice to the attack and control rolls. Can only be used once a scene, but gets reset by incapacitating a grappled enemy (especially helped by some of the prior Charms) and then getting to Initiative 12, but it also has the unique benefit of not having its limit used up at all if the grappled opponent is immediately thrown or slammed.<br /> <br /> Hero-Killing Death Dive, that\u2019s a rather threatening name for something in a Style with this character. Ohhh, it\u2019s for that cool Black Widow manoeuvre, with the head grapple and the pulling somebody down; those are always a treat to see people actually do. I need to look back at that martial arts blog\u2026 anyway grapple gambit gets double 9s on attack roll, and winning control immediately renders opponent prone and takes Initiative equal to any rolled numbers that provide double successes for the attack roll. Sounds very helpful for resetting Talons Greet Prey.<br /> <br /> Neck-Piercing Hook is a much flashier rendition of the idea, with its thing of grabbing them in the legs and then spinning while up in the air; that lets them have a longer ranged throw from a grapple, and on impact the opponent is forced to make an Athletics roll against a difficulty based on surrendered rounds of control, and if they fail they get to suffer a second damage roll; it\u2019s limited to dice equal to successes on the first one, but gets to ignore soak or Hardness. It\u2019s also a Charm that gets stronger at higher Essence, being able to increase the throwing range in exchange for halving the second damage roll. Terrestrials are limited in dice on the second damage roll, but not too severely.<br /> <br /> Raking Talon Kick has a nasty sounding strike, with the spinning from behind to catch an enemy in the face with both legs. The mechanics look a bit intricate\u2026 has to be used on an enemy that was thrown or slammed immediately before, letting it be a decisive attack that gets a damage bonus from the rounds of control used to make the preceding throw or slam. A proper stunt to use the environment to make the elaborate manoeuvre allows the kick to benefit from surprise attack rules, and Raptor\u2019s Final Descent can enhance it without that Charm\u2019s usual restrictions. Terrestrials don\u2019t get to add more bonus damage than half of their Initiative.<br /> <br /> And finally, Doom Plummets Down. Needs a grapple with at least five rounds of control to give up, and throwing an enemy into a hard surface, upon which a reflexive decisive attack is launched. Player gets to come up with their own format for a signature move, and stunt dice for describing it get added to the damage roll as well, and they get to make the initial throw decisive and let the reflexive attack go before Initiative is reset. It can be enhanced even further by using Raking Talon Kick\u2026 ah, that Charm and Raptor\u2019s Final Descent are normally Simple Charms, getting to combo them with these things is a big deal. And as a last normal benefit, they get to leap into range with an enemy thrown further with Neck-Piercing Hook reflexively, although it uses up the movement action. Mastery allows a successfully struck enemy to be reflexively rushed or disengaged with automatic success, without movement being used up, and Terrestrials can only use it on crashed enemies and don\u2019t get the option to use it with a withering throw.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not much to say in summary of Falcon Style, it\u2019s another fairly solid thing. Does seem like it would be a useful thing for dipping, in order to get some handy supplements to other Styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T13:00:01-08:00","id":1292579,"title":"","content":"All right, a solid foundation was built with more grounded Styles, now let\u2019s indulge in some esoteric weirdness with Laughing Monster.<br /> <br /> <br /> The implication that the actual Style as a whole was originated by Fair Folk, developed by their dream-stealing antics, is interesting. I have a lingering affection for the old descriptions of Fair Folk limitations with Martial Arts, but I can see how that might be contrary to the interests of making them a lot less arcane and convoluted. And hey, it lends itself to a background in which a Lunar discovered a Style by coaxing it from a raksha\u2019s remains.<br /> <br /> As for the Style, it\u2019s described as being all irritation confusion and humiliation to put enemies off balance. I like the description of the training methods, internalizing a bit of discord and lack of shame. I also enjoy the idea that it\u2019s primarily a style for people on the margins. It employs things like slaps and leg sweeps, wields the staff, war fan and whip, can\u2019t be used with armour, and while its footwork naturally employs Dodge, it\u2019s also distinct in benefiting from Abilities such as Presence and Socialize, and even a bit of Occult for the more unusual mystical elements.<br /> <br /> Begins with Furiously Stalling Destiny. Stylist gets bonus Evasion against an enemy, and the first attack made on the one who did it before the end of the stylist\u2019s next turn gets a die of post-soak withering damage, or die of regular decisive damage, while gambits get an automatic success to attack and Initiative rolls, all to represent the idea of somebody taking in violence directed at them and pointing it back at an opponent. Its bonuses can also be stacked repeatedly for the same opponent attacking repeatedly, a chain that breaks if the fighter goes for somebody else. Masters get that option familiar to Lunars to activate the Charm after an enemy attack has already been rolled, while Terrestrials are limited to their Essence in number of times the Charm can stack.<br /> <br /> Deeper-Into-Trouble Technique allow one to infuriate an enemy by enhancing a decisive damage roll with double 10s and the level of an enemy\u2019s negative Tie as bonus dice. The resulting fury means that the enemy can get Willpower if they immediately attack and successfully crash or incapacitate the stylist, and gives a decent penalty to attacks made on anybody else. That penalty actually lasts the whole scene, unless the infuriated opponent successfully hits the stylist, although having gone for somebody else first forfeits the Willpower bonus.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m getting a good feel for this Style; feels reminiscent of Black Claw, but with a very different emotional tenor.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Form Charm already. Laughing Monster Form allows one to assume an obscure and unpredictable stance, with a different take on being surrounded by illusory arms. Distract and disarm gambits are enhanced with dice equal to the stylist\u2019s Occult, and when an attacker from close range misses and loses Initiative, the fighter can make a decisive counterattack for dice equal to the lost Initiative that ignore Hardness, and don\u2019t reset Initiative. Or they can counter with distract and disarm gambits, that use Initiative as normal, but get bonus attack dice equal to lost Initiative. Terrestrials need to spend some of their own Initiative to make counterattacks, and the Form can be entered reflexively by either provoking somebody into battle against them with influence, or use dodging to make an enemy\u2019s Initiative drop below their own. While I imagine that there may be later Charms to help on the dodging front, there are definitely ways in which a Solar or Lunar\u2019s own Charms could help them harness the benefits of this Form.<br /> <br /> Inauspicious Moment for Attack allows enemy assaults to be clashed with a slightly enhanced distract gambit, which if successful counts as a dodge for the user, and creates an opening for a reflexive decisive attack for the beneficiary of the distraction. It can also capitalise on a later Charm, Unitary Being Forge, to allow the clash to be made with a decisive attack, with a special source of base damage and ignoring Hardness, which can also be enhanced by powers to improve distract gambits. Terrestrials have to treat the action as their attack for the round, meaning they can\u2019t use it if they\u2019ve already attacked.<br /> <br /> Using Subtle Hammer lets a stylist follow distract or disarm gambits with reflexive decisive attacks that ignore Hardness, rolling for their damage the extra successes on their gambit\u2019s roll, and getting back the Initiative spent on the gambit if the enemy is incapacitated. It can only be used once per scene, but has the straightforward reset condition of successfully clashing an enemy with the prior attack. Mastery allows the Form Charm\u2019s bonus dice for gambits to be added to the attack rolls of this Charm. There\u2019s a good image going, of wearing an enemy down with lots of small decisive attacks while continuously messing them up with distraction, disarming and enough annoyance to keep their attention focused on the stylist. Furiously Stalling Destiny probably helps a bit with continuously building the stylist\u2019s Initiative to help those attacks and gambit.<br /> <br /> Right, the style was described as having been employed to turn a Raksha court upon itself, and that\u2019s coming in with Thieves Fall Out. A decisive attack can be rolled against two enemies close to each other, Initiative divided evenly between them; if they both take a hit, the disrupting impacts cause them to stumble over one another whenever close by, meaning that for the rest of the scene they both lose Defence if they\u2019re in close range, as well as losing a bit of Initiative at the start of each of their turns, which go to the stylist. It can also be used to attack battle groups, enhancing the attack\u2019s damage dice, causing the group to have a persistent Defence penalty, and to lose a point of Magnitude (pop pop) at the start of each turn in lieu of the smaller scale drip, that the stylist won\u2019t get as Initiative.<br /> <br /> That starts getting worse with Friendship-Dissolving Venom, through which dodging an attacks allows it to be redirected against somebody else within its original range; the attack has all of the power directed at the stylist when it resolves against the new character, and if Initiative is lost for it being withering, the stylist gets that. The redirected attack can also get bonuses from Furiously Stalling Destiny. If the roll for the redirected attack is also greater than its victim\u2019s Resolve, they form a Minor Tie for the attacker to represent their outrage, with contrary positive Ties being suppressed for the scene. The stylist even gets to make a reflexive Presence or Socialize roll to persuade the newly angered character to act in a manner antagonistic towards the one who hit them. The Charm has a Willpower cost, that is waived if attacker and victim have already been affected by the prior Charm. Masters can further enhance the redirected attacks with supplemental Laughing Monster Charms, while Terrestrials only get to redirect attacks at non-trivial enemies when they\u2019re crashed.<br /> <br /> You know who this reminds me of? Heysha Black Asp. And, while I\u2019ve always been kind of dubious about almost everything about her schtick, I did like the way that the comic in Manual Lunars portrayed her fighting style. I like something that I feel would more effectively portray that than Lunar Hero Style really did.<br /> <br /> Right, that thing referred to before, Unitary Being Forge, errr\u2026 bit complicated. So the stylist hits an enemy who possesses a negative Tie of which the stylist is aware with a decisive attack, getting to reroll failed dice equal to the strength of the Intimacy. If the damage is at least the target\u2019s base Resolve, the Intimacy detaches and becomes embodied as a semi-tangible imp, a mental shaping power that appropriate magic can defend against. The imp remains by its originator\u2019s side constantly and indelibly, in manifest form for the length of a scene; during that, the victim can\u2019t benefit from the Tie, but still takes its drawbacks, and their base Guile is halved by the imp giving away their feelings. Once per round, the stylist can have the imp grant the lower of Intimacy strength or Essence as extra damage dice to decisive attacks against the victim, from any source. A gambit with a difficulty of just the Intimacy\u2019s strength can be made to destroy the imp, but the victim\u2019s Guile is the basis for its Defence, and its only vulnerable to magic that can hurt the dematerialized; magic to permanently slay spirits weakens the Intimacy by one step. This one is some carp dragon weirdness to me, and for a Martial Art that came from the Fair Folk that\u2019s a real boon.<br /> <br /> Shuffling the Pieces harnesses that power further, by allowing the stylist to take hold of the imp when close enough and wrapping it around their weapon, a state in which the creature can\u2019t enhance attacks against the victim, although the other effects remain, and while the imp is still vulnerable to destruction, the stylist is always considered to provide defend other. The benefit for having done this is that the imp can be imbued into a decisive attack, to allow the Intimacy\u2019s strength in damage dice to be rerolled, and if used on somebody besides the imp\u2019s originator, and attacks of damage at least the target\u2019s Resolve embed the imp in the mind, which causes the Intimacy to move from the prior character to the new one as a mental shaping effect. If the new Intimacy fundamentally opposes a strong existing one or is generally incompatible with their identity, they develop a Minor Derangement appropriate to the contradiction in their personality. Terrestrials can never fully transfer an Intimacy, only imbuing it in a new character as Minor, and weakening it by a step in the originator. I guess this is useful for spreading promoted bad Intimacies around, to create further group discord.<br /> <br /> And finally, the thus far uncommon Essence 4 Martial Arts Charm, called Dancing Wind-Monster Transformation. A seven mote, one Willpower surcharge can be added to Laughing Monster Form, allowing the user to diffuse themselves as an immaterial body in the form of an inchoate cloud of mocking madness. Allies within short range will gain the benefits of Laughing Monster Form, and their attacks and dodges can benefit from the stylist employing their own Reflexive and Supplemental Charms in the style for them. The stylist can only normally attack immaterial characters within short range, but can also go for physical characters being followed by imps, and can use Shuffling the Pieces to discharge imps through the attacks of allies. The character pays for this by becoming vulnerable from a slightly longer range to attacks on the immaterial, and the Charm automatically ends if they end a turn with no enemies within attack range, only being able to resume it with Laughing Monster Form again. I\u2019m not entirely clear on whether the immaterial character can still move. The limit to Terrestrials is that their cloud form is still vulnerable to material attacks, but with better Evasion if they\u2019re not enhanced by magic to target the immaterial.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Laughing Monster strikes a good balance; it includes elements for attacking in a more social, esoteric fashion, but isn\u2019t strictly reliant on them, being perfectly serviceable as a distinct and stylized method of fighting in a straightforward manner. One thing I\u2019ll say is that, to my eyes, it\u2019s an odd case of an Art that might require some complementary Charms to maximize the value of some of its powers (including its Form), but I might just be missing something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T13:43:17-08:00","id":1292598,"title":"","content":"In previous editions, Laughing Monster was the Raksha Staff Shaping Style. They used it to become the archetypal Fool that stands outside society and tears it down with their mockery, in a fairly literal fashion, since Staff shaping combat was about messing around with societies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T15:58:25-08:00","id":1292635,"title":"","content":"Hey, fun fact; Graceful Wicked Masques was something like the second Exalted book I ever bought. I owned that before I did the core book.<br /> <br /> I know what the Shaping Styles are. Can't quite remember all their names, but do think they were modelled off of the main players of the Balorian Crusade... I think the Sword one was something like Universal Warlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T15:59:32-08:00","id":1292637,"title":"","content":"Okay, finishing off the Martial Arts in reasonably short order with Swaying Grass Style.<br /> <br /> <br /> The image of this one is interesting to me, being a more conceptually grounded one that is elevated a bit not so much by Essence but context and legacy, basing itself on the apocryphal origins of capoeira as it does. Even out of character, it has a bit of an interesting history, having been an Ink Monkeys product during a time of a bit of game drought, that drew some attention for its ideas but was hampered a bit by being Terrestrial; I\u2019d say it\u2019s among the more prominent to benefit from the overhaul. In any case, its internal history expresses itself in the thesis of using a lot of feint and misdirection to leave enemies open to heavy kicking attacks, as well as some more discrete weapons such as baton, boot and knives, although obviously not compatible with armour that would not have been available to originators. It\u2019s complements of Dodge and Performance are really a given.<br /> <br /> First Charm is Jubilant Battle Proposition, through which a character gets to open a fight in a suitably discrete fashion; Join Battle gets rolled with Appearance or Manipulation + Performance, which also gets to do double-duty as an inspire roll against all observers without multiple target penalties, and gets bonus dice under conditions where observing the stylist\u2019s feet would not be possible. To model the idea of the dancing covering the fighting intent, characters whose Resolve was beaten by the inspire roll get to treat the first attack against one of them in the fight as unexpected, with Mastery allowing attacks that would have already been unexpected to be ambushes.<br /> <br /> Reed-Breaking Banda allows a withering or decisive attack to take the form of a leg sweep, that in it does sufficient damage forces a check against falling prone, or else to make a smash attack with no Initiative cost and Defence penalty, as well as forcing the enemy struck that rises from prone or makes a disengage action to forfeit one Initiative to the stylist. In addition, Mastery allows attacks that are unexpected or stunted to have concealed footwork to impose a penalty to the roll to rise from prone, and automatic failure if it was an ambush. Then Sweeping Meadow Awareness Practice is used to half penalties to Evasion as a result of onslaught and unexpected attacks, with a successful dodge reducing the Initiative costs for disengages, gambits and Style Charms by one for a turn, although it can be stacked a few times. Those Charms with the Perilous keyword whose Initiative costs are reduced to zero this way can still be used in crash. Terrestrials get a different metric for their penalty reductions, only being able to relieve as much as half of their Performance.<br /> <br /> The Form Charm uses swaying rhythms between combat stances to protect from penalties while fighting prone, doubling 10s on damage rolled for decisive attacks made against enemies that are prone and didn\u2019t expect it, and there\u2019s no cost for attacking with improvised equivalents to the style weapons. Performance can be used in place of Athletics to perform rushes, and in place of Stealth for establishing concealment. It gets to be entered reflexively when an enemy\u2019s Resolve is overcome at close-range by a dance-based Performance roll.<br /> <br /> Rolling-with-the-Wind Method lets one match the rhythm of their movements to those of enemies, by way of reflexively disengaging in response to taking a hit, before the damage is rolled; if they depart successfully, post-soak damage is halved, and decisive attack damage is penalised by extra successes on the disengage roll up to a limit of the stylist\u2019s Performance, moving a range band away once the damage is rolled. It uses up movement action, but if such has already been used that round, it\u2019s paid off by removing a movement action in the next one. Terrestrials reduce withering damage the same way as decisive, and the Charm can\u2019t be used at all if the turn\u2019s movement action has been used.<br /> <br /> Teeth-in-the-Grass Strike is a major feint manoeuvre, allowing one\u2019s Performance to be added in dice to decisive attacks and distract gambits. An attack whose successes beat enemy Resolve becomes unexpected, but can also be an ambush the first time it\u2019s used in a scene, if benefiting from a distract gambit. It\u2019s limited to once per scene, but is reset by beating an enemy\u2019s Resolve with a dance Performance action, and Mastery allows a surprise attack to add half of Performance in dice to the damage or gambit Initiative roll.<br /> <br /> Whirling Rhythm Revolution evokes the fighter\u2019s passion, allowing a successful rush, disengage or dance Performance roll to be followed with a reflexive decisive attack, that doesn\u2019t count as the round\u2019s attack. Excellencies and Style Charms used to enhance the attack get discounted by the cost of Charms used to enhance the action that allowed for the attack. It might have one of the harshest Terrestrial drawbacks yet seen, withholding all bonuses aside from just the reflexive attack (to the point that it counts as the round\u2019s attack). Then Grass-Reaping Posture acts as a Permanent enhancement, allowing a stylist in the Form to use the previous Charm whenever a close range enemy tries to rise from prone or fails to disengage from the stylist.<br /> <br /> Last two Charms: Inescapable Tumbleweed Prana is Instant, but provides a benefit that conditionally lasts for the duration of a scene, that being that successful rushes allow the fighter to cross a range band towards an enemy every time they move away. The benefit is lost if an attack or rush is directed at a different enemy, the fighter moves away from the enemy, or experiences crash. The Charm can be used when rushing an enemy from concealment, with reflexive movement provided by such not requiring new Stealth rolls to be made.<br /> <br /> And finally, the Instant Charm Serenading the Reed. Feeling a source of inspiration and rhythm from ambient noises, the stylist is able to add the lowest out of their Appearance, Manipulation or Performance to their Evasion, unless they\u2019re actually in the presence of music, in which case they add the highest. If the dodge is successful, and the attacker rolls fewer successes than what is added to Evasion from the Charm, the enemy is forced to reset to base Initiative. As an alternative, it can be used to reflexively clash using a decisive attack, with the presence of music allowing 1s on an enemy\u2019s roll to be added as dice to the stylist\u2019s damage roll. Mastery allows the latter effect to make clashes against ambushes, while being Terrestrial means that clash counts as one\u2019s attack for the round.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Swaying Grass Style is another that feels decent enough, although its synergies don\u2019t stand out as much to me. That\u2019s not to say I doubt they\u2019re there, I\u2019d just need to look back over the Style one or two more times to have a full sense of how it builds up and slots together. <br /> <br /> <br /> Having looked at three of the Styles today, gotten an earlier start than I have for a while, and not expecting Sorcery to take very long, I\u2019m going to leave it here and then try to get through the rest quickly tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T17:23:22-08:00","id":1292651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From Essence 4, Chains-of-Silver Geas provides yet another path for dealing with truculent spirits and fae; they just need to overcome the being (which seems to need to present a meaningful opposition) in some challenge, physical, spiritual (i.e. exorcism) or social, which then becomes irresistibly bound to perform an inconvenient or serious task, or even a life-defining one if the Lunar\u2019s Essence is equal or greater. It\u2019s even a very compelling binding, from which the being can only meaningfully deviate to attend to another threatened Major or greater Intimacy, or use them in Decision points to win short reprieves from pursuing the task. It can only made to last more than a year if it entails a task that the being could meaningfully conclude, but automatically prevents them from attempting to harm the binding Lunar in any capacity but self-defence. And it can only be used <i>against</i> a character once per story; you can\u2019t readily put multiple bindings on the same figure, but you can hand out geasa left and right to many. This one looks really good on a number of counts, such as mystical binding rooted in a specifically Lunar method, engaging the function of guardianship, giving a bit more substance to how often the fiction has referred to them as bending gods and Raksha to their will. Good stuff all round. </div> </div> </div>Someday I'm going to force some jerk spirit to count every grain of sand in the Southern hemisphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T18:22:36-08:00","id":1292667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292651#post1292651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someday I'm going to force some jerk spirit to count every grain of sand in the Southern hemisphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really want to hear about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T19:39:15-08:00","id":1292684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292635#post1292635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, fun fact; Graceful Wicked Masques was something like the second Exalted book I ever bought. I owned that before I did the core book.<br /> <br /> I know what the Shaping Styles are. Can't quite remember all their names, but do think they were modelled off of the main players of the Balorian Crusade... I think the Sword one was something like Universal Warlord.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was <i>World-Devouring </i>Warlord Style, actually; the Sword as cunning, controlled general. Similarly, All-Consuming God-Monster is Ring as abandoning all logic in favor of passion and self-perfection, and Spirit-Twisting Obsession is Cup as manipulator and breaker of emotions. They actually don't have a backstory, going from the book.<br /> <br /> And now I want to see them as stolen Martial Arts too; Lunars rock Laughing Monster, but I can see Sidereals getting fond of All-Consuming God-Monster, and assholes in general as going for Spirit-Twisting Obsession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T20:04:14-08:00","id":1292687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292684#post1292684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was <i>World-Devouring </i>Warlord Style, actually; the Sword as cunning, controlled general. Similarly, All-Consuming God-Monster is Ring as abandoning all logic in favor of passion and self-perfection</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always conflate those names in some manner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They actually don't have a backstory, going from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes yes; what I meant by &quot;I think&quot; was that it always felt to me like the writing of those Charms opted to use very abstract pictures of those backstory characters as the model to build them around. I also readily admit that I might have been reading far too into the matter; it's a bit of a holdover from a different approach to observing the material.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T20:56:39-08:00","id":1292695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292684#post1292684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was <i>World-Devouring </i>Warlord Style, actually; the Sword as cunning, controlled general. Similarly, All-Consuming God-Monster is Ring as abandoning all logic in favor of passion and self-perfection, and Spirit-Twisting Obsession is Cup as manipulator and breaker of emotions. They actually don't have a backstory, going from the book.<br /> <br /> And now I want to see them as stolen Martial Arts too; Lunars rock Laughing Monster, but I can see Sidereals getting fond of All-Consuming God-Monster, and assholes in general as going for Spirit-Twisting Obsession.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit-Twisting Obsession sounds like it could easily be a reskinned Black Claw style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T00:06:48-08:00","id":1292714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292687#post1292687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I always conflate those names in some manner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes yes; what I meant by &quot;I think&quot; was that it always felt to me like the writing of those Charms opted to use very abstract pictures of those backstory characters as the model to build them around. I also readily admit that I might have been reading far too into the matter; it's a bit of a holdover from a different approach to observing the material.</div> </div> </div> </div>More the other way around. Those characters didn't exist as of Exalted: the Fair Folk apart from Thief of Words and Prince Balor. I can see someone thinking they are very clever in GWN.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T03:31:35-08:00","id":1292721,"title":"","content":"Huh; last night, I actually had a dream that <i>I</i> had become a Lunar. Never had that happen with Exalted before.<br /> <br /> Not in Creation, mind, it was set in the modern day; had this whole thing with Lunars coming back en masse, and some kind of weird conspiracy going on amidst the reforming Silver Pact. It was one of those kinds of dreams that doesn't stray more than about three meters from the setting of your own bed. Kept incorporating my Switch as a medium through which Lunars could communicate.<br /> <br /> But it also had some Brooklyn 99 characters; not the good ones, like Scully, Hitchcock and the Vulture. The fact that the Vulture had become a Lunar really shook my dream persona's still very new faith in his patron goddess.<br /> <br /> And Shadow the Hedgehog was there for some reason, having a whole thing where he was being slowly possessed by that Mephiles character from the 06 game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T03:36:10-08:00","id":1292722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1292714#post1292714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More the other way around. Those characters didn't exist as of Exalted: the Fair Folk apart from Thief of Words and Prince Balor. I can see someone thinking they are very clever in GWN.</div> </div> </div> </div>Princess Melusine, the Duke of Mirrors, and Incarnadine and Viridian are absolutely in Exalted: the Fair Folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T07:56:02-08:00","id":1292765,"title":"","content":"Warning: this one is especially long. I had underestimated the length of what to say on sorcery.<br /> <br /> Okay, up fairly early. Break me off a piece of that Sorcery, and then give myself a break for a little while.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorcery opens with some new shaping rituals, and of course one of the premier figures of Lunar sorcery is going to feature heavily there. I like the idea that Raksi\u2019s teachings can be somewhat eclectic and expansive because she\u2019s providing knowledge cribbed from the breadth of First Age knowledge. Plus some nice hallucinatory visions. What of the actual shaping rituals\u2026<br /> <br /> Balancing on the Edge: once per story, a player is allowed to suggest a twist for their spell, something that doesn\u2019t undermine its power but relinquishes a bit of control over its effect in a manner that inconveniences the character, and for which they\u2019re allowed to supplement a shape sorcery action with a reflexive repeat of that same action, benefiting for free from an Excellency spent and (if the control spell) any other enhancements. I like the sound of this one; I enjoy anything that can deviate spells a bit or make them somewhat wild, the means of reaping more sorcerous motes sounds particularly potent, and it has the feel of something with the Raksi backstory.<br /> <br /> Sigil-Skin Geometry: once per day, a character gets to make a difficulty 2 Intelligence + Linguistics or Lore roll (which, if working on the control spell, get at least three bonus non-Charm dice) to spend a few hours carving the formulae of a specified spell into their skin, creating a pool of motes equal to extra successes that can be spent towards shaping that spell. This one is interesting for rewarding the sorcerer that prepares ahead of time, possibly with a fairly large bank of sorcerous motes, and for a sense of playing off the imagery of the Lunar tattoos. Also marries together Raksi\u2019s schtick of elaborate knowledge of sorcerous theory with some of her more brutal experience.<br /> <br /> Terror-Relishing Art: once per scene, a character who successfully threatens or inspires fear in a narratively significant character gets sorcerous motes flat equal to the Attribute used in the roll, in addition to the difference in Essence ratings if the influence was on a higher Essence character. This one is just neat for harnessing a key quality of Lunar power, and how it encourages one to act in the presence of higher status figures.<br /> <br /> The initiation can also provide Merits for extra Resolve against fear and sorcerously produced influence, to represent conditioning from the experience of Raksi\u2019s tutelage, and a once per story capacity to cast a spell they haven\u2019t learned yet that they can later learn without tome or teacher, to represent the impression left by having read the Book of Three Circles (with an encouragement for Storytellers to adjudicate spells that logically wouldn\u2019t be in the book to be off the table).<br /> <br /> All of this together makes for a very compelling picture of why one would want to study under Raksi.<br /> <br /> <br /> The concept of the Jasmine Gems of Mishiko makes a return, albeit with a significant overhaul; I\u2019m pretty sure that the lore of previous Editions made Mishiko an outright Lunar (and somebody the Crossroads Society claimed as the actual first sorcerer), rather than one of their children (checks back} nnnnno, she was always the child of a Lunar, and that guy was referred to as the sorcerer, Mishiko was just very significant to his legend. The actual gems are very different, though; where once they were five, had a specific origin in the sorcery origin story, were kept by the Lunars, and needed to be gathered together and arranged in innumerable geometric formations to bring forth a simulacrum of her to recite mystically insightful poems, here it\u2019s a terms for spontaneously generated sorcerous relics that bloom forth from any number of liminal places and summon her literal ghost. Contrary to a prior notion in which their possession was closely guarded and let elder No Moons gatekeep sorcery a bit, this comes with the idea that young Lunars are gravitated towards the gem by unknown forces. She still has some of that same teaching method (albeit seemingly with more latitude) and inclination towards exploration and discovery. I think it overall makes for one of the more esoteric and mystical initiation processes. The shaping rituals are:<br /> <br /> Remembrance of Mishiko: the sorcerer gets to make an offering to Mishiko once per day, using mechanics very close to old prayer rules, and getting the threshold successes plus their own Essence rating in sorcerous motes that can be held until the end of the story, or reset with another offering. This just seems like a very straightforwardly potent ritual, probably commensurate to the implicit difficulty of acquiring one of the relics needed to perform it, although it can also be worth considering the hefty material and financial burdens of keeping it at a high rate.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer\u2019s Quest: learning of a location to which one must go to achieve a major character or story goal, or succeeding on Survival rolls to get there, immediately grants a sorcerous mote that can last for a story, and can be stacked with a bank of up to ten motes. In addition, once per story when upholding an Intimacy by entering such a place for the first time, the level of the Intimacy is multiplied by the sorcerer\u2019s Essence and granted as sorcerous motes, that can be held on to until departing from that place. I like the way that this one alludes to and incorporates Mishiko\u2019s old story, as well as the encouragement to follow in her foot steps, at least in principle.<br /> <br /> Twilight Koan: Mishiko\u2019s ghost reliably appears to offer strange questions or riddles, and players get to stunt an action with realization of its meaning, granting the better of Intelligence or Lore in motes that last for the scene. Doing so requires waiting for Mishiko\u2019s next appearance and new koan before getting the opportunity to do it again.<br /> <br /> And the Merits are for being allowed to confer with Mishiko once per story to introduce a fact without applicable background and with at least three non-Charm successes, and suggestions are given for Evocations for the jasmine gems, such as deeper communion with Mishiko, as well as themes of mystery, discovery and questing to enhance sorcery.<br /> <br /> Mishiko\u2019s place in Lunar story has always been at the margins of my awareness; looking back on it, I would judge the story to be fairly interesting, and the idea of how the gems were used was a bit cool, if a little limiting. I think this initiation does a very good job of taking the best parts of all that, and converting it into something a player can become really deeply invested in; a character\u2019s whole storyline can revolve around the guidance of Mishiko. It\u2019s actually one of the more vivid sorcerous prospects.<br /> <br /> <br /> And going even deeper down the rabbit hole of the esoteric and just damn weird is the simply named Root-Lore, by which one derives sorcery from deep insight into the patterns within trees, roots and flowers. The rituals are:<br /> <br /> Master Apothecary Enlightenment: a Lore roll to introduce a fact about herbs or Medicine roll to treat somebody using them grants sorcerous motes equal to Intelligence + extra successes on that role, which last for the rest of the story. Furthermore, basic or major crafting projects to create concoctions from plants allow a quantity of motes equal to Intelligence + awarded silver points + twice the awarded gold points, which also last for a story. It\u2019s limited to only being able to hold onto motes from one use of the ritual at a time, but still\u2026 I\u2019ll admit that I\u2019m starting to feel a hint of power creep in these rituals. Learning from Raksi and acquiring a rare relic was fair enough, but this one\u2026 either root-lore is supposed to be distinctly difficult and unusual to acquire or I\u2019m not fully appreciating the imposition of having to make a craft roll for herbal drugs, medicines and poisons that accomplish the objectives necessary for getting craft points.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer\u2019s Harvest: shape sorcery actions taken within medium range of significant plants such as trees or large gardens get to draw additional motes equal to the shaper\u2019s Essence, with any such source limited to once per day. It can also draw power from wood elementals, directly tapping the same quantity out of their own mote pools, although the shaping action needs to exceed their Resolve, and still limited per day. Powering control spells with the motes doesn\u2019t count towards the daily limit. This one feels more reasonable, and I like the impression it gives of how such sorcerers live and associate.<br /> <br /> Thousand Blossom Arts: with a few hours foraging for an efficacious plant, character can make a difficulty 2 Intelligence + Survival roll (with difficulty adjusted if appropriate to local verdency, or straight raised to 4 for foraging enough to provide a basically unlimited stock of material), and once per scene the foraged plants can be incorporated as reagents into a spell, contributing sorcerous motes equal to the highest of Intelligence, Lore or Survival, limited by the week-long shelf life of the plants for that purpose (as well as being useful only to the foraging sorcerer). This one I also think is neat and fair, for how it incorporates external materials directly into sorcery, at the cost of some tedious and inconvenient prep.<br /> <br /> This one has three Merits, one to let the character treat wood elementals, intelligent plants and any similar creature as though they have an affectionate Minor Tie, one for discounted cost on spells to create or manipulate plants or similar spirits (with the control spell getting the added benefit of a once-per-day waiving of the Willpower cost), and the last to let the character add their Occult to Survival rolls to forage for plants, Lore rolls to introduce facts about them, or Craft rolls to makes chemicals out of them, albeit only once per week and they count as Charm dice.<br /> <br /> I just like this whole thing for having a very earthy feel, in contrast to a lot of more lofty initiations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And now let\u2019s round it all out with these spells, starting at the Terrestrial Circle.<br /> <br /> First up is Blood Lash, which is exactly what it sounds like; a wounded sorcerer can draw their own blood out and shape it into a red whip with a black-barbed tip (in the dub we\u2019ll call it Crimson Lightning). The whip has decent attack traits, and for actions to attack or defend using it the wound penalty is halved. The actual cost of the spell entails taking a lethal wound, but that\u2019s waived for a sorcerer already wounded from another source. The whip also gets additional powers for the sorcerer with an Essence pool, as their wound penalty increases; at the lowest level, they can reflexively threaten enemies after damaging them, a roll in which wound penalty is waived and inverted into bonus dice, at medium it can extend the whip\u2019s range and, if grappled, has the option to pull them closer or leave them grappled at range (which leaves the grapple vulnerable to a simple gambit from the enemy\u2019s helpers), and the worst wound penalty allows the sorcerer to make a decisive attack in which the last develops a vampiric maw, allowing non-aggravated damage to be healed for every three levels dealt to an enemy, with a minimum of one, and the prior powers get to be used in combination with this for no cost; it can only be used once per scene, and is reset by taking at least 7 levels of damage in a decisive attack.<br /> <br /> I think that the interaction with wound penalties gives even the base spell something a bit more than just being a slightly odd way of summoning a weapon, and the powers from escalating wound penalties really sells it.<br /> <br /> Ah, right, control spell. Sorcerer is distinguished by really freaky veins, and gains a general capability to control the motion of their own shed blood, which can function as exceptional equipment, and at Storyteller discretion may be sufficient to create actions; it can be done at any range, but doesn\u2019t inherently convey awareness of the blood\u2019s situation or proximity. And distortion of the spell causes the whip to coagulate, reducing it to inflicting bashing damage and removing its Flexible tag, and treating the sorcerer\u2019s wound penalties as a level lower for the sake of accessing powers. Nice.<br /> <br /> Flight of Separation allows a sorcerer to convert oneself into a flock of tiny birds, guided by the caster\u2019s diffused consciousness, that will migrate to a designated location within ten miles. The birds use the sorcerer\u2019s traits, but are only capable of moving and dodging, for which they gain a +2 Evasion bonus against attacks that don\u2019t cover an area, and bonus dice for disengage and withdrawal. The top flight speed is designated as Dexterity + Athletics and then multiplied by two miles per hour, and the spell can be reflexively ended at any time, naturally ending with the journey or incapacitation. Having it as control spell allows one to communicate with birds (many of whom aren\u2019t good conversationalists), all of which (plus any similar spirits) treat as having a Minor Tie of fondness. This spell also has a special activation condition; upon gathering the necessary motes, the sorcerer can hold off rather than cast immediately, although doing so imposes a -1 penalty to everything as the sorcerer strains against the continuous effort to not explode into birds. It can be cast reflexively at any time, although close range enemies require disengaging first, or else the spell is lost. Distortion causes the flock of you to become disoriented and uncoordinated, forcing a Wits + Integrity roll every turn when fighting to prevent some of the birds from fleeing independently, represented as rolling a die of Hardness-ignoring bashing damage as they become too diffuse; when not in combat, the roll is for each mile of travel, with failure making the next mile half the speed.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a functional spell, nice and weird image of a means of travel, and compelling distortion effect.<br /> <br /> And the somewhat infamous Peacock-Shadow Eyes, now rendered as a Psyche effect, and cheaper in sorcerous motes than the norm (although costing two Willpower). The sorcerer\u2019s psychedelic and hypnotic eyes allow an Occult roll to be made against the Resolve of a target at up to medium range; if it wins, the target is put into a suggestible trance for a scene, in which their Resolve is penalised by 2, and they generally function as though sleepwalking, having no memory of time in the trance and rationalizing influence acquired under it as self-determined, although the trance can\u2019t withstand being attacked. It also fails outright against those without sight. Willpower can be spent to resist the memory suppressing effect if lacking such information could endanger a higher Intimacy, although social influence endures under those circumstances. Observers whose Resolve is not beaten can tell that the sorcerer is employing some kind of supernatural chicanery with a successful Perception + Occult roll against the sorcerer\u2019s successes. If the control spell, the sorcerer\u2019s eyes are permanently died with iridescent colours, with which they can treat their Appearance as one higher for rolls to inspire fascination with oneself or for any rolls against the hypnotised, although effectively disguising oneself becomes harder. Distorting the spell (which can target the ongoing trance effect) allows the target to experience cryptic flashbacks of their experience, which after a few days permits spending Willpower to resist the memory suppression even without concern for Intimacies.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say that the effect is less directly powerful than it was in the prior Edition, but is both more involved and potentially more rewarding. I think it feels both distinct as a hypnotic sorcery effect, and as something that might complement other social powers, rather than compete with them.<br /> <br /> Okay, onto some shiny new Celestial Circle Spells.<br /> <br /> Starting off with Cloud Trapeze, through which one can draw together vapour and Essence to manufacture a big cloud boat, which is sufficient to lift the sorcerer, cargo and willing passengers that are within long range with a combined mass equal to ten times the sorcerer\u2019s Essence in tons, and which can then fly at the same number in miles per hour, possibly helped or hindered by prevailing winds. Wits + Occult can be rolled to navigate obstacles or perils if necessary, and in combat the whole mass can be moved across range bands as a miscellaneous action, counting as the sorcerer\u2019s own move action for a turn. It benefits its passengers in numerous ways: they\u2019re protected from weather, temperature, and any other travails of aerial travel, and imposes a penalty on vision based rolls to find them (or the cargo) for anybody observing from the outside, an imposition not made on the passengers. The Trapeze can actually rise to the level of existing clouds, among which it is concealed to the point where it takes a difficulty 5 action of Occult or Survival or magic that can predict weather to make it out. The sorcerer has to stay aboard the ship to guide it, although they don\u2019t need to remain fixed to that task, and departing from the boat causes it to quickly descend, just carefully enough to minimize risk to those aboard before it vanishes. As a control spell, half of the caster\u2019s Intelligence is added to Essence for the sake of determining carrying capacity and speed, and bestows a capacity to make an Intelligence 2 Occult roll whenever in up to medium range of bodies of mist, for or water to take an action to shape vapour into structures like bridges or ladders the length of a range band. Distorting the spell causes it to be open to outside observers, while obscuring the vision of those within.<br /> <br /> I think this spell is interesting in the image and the kind of transportation capability it provides to a sorcerer, although I must admit that the control effect stands out a bit to me; I keep picturing a sorcerer turning a fortification\u2019s moat into a liability.<br /> <br /> Insidious Tendrils of Hate is a Psyche spell cast with a Ritual cost. The sorcerer spends a couple of feeding their malice into a fire until it is rendered as green as Ligier, and then adds something with a symbolic connection to an intended target, such as a body piece taken within three days or a personal item. Upon which the target will, no matter how far aware, be enveloped in acrid smoke that will seep into their soul, causing a roll of sorcerer\u2019s Manipulation + Occult against victim\u2019s Resolve (and anybody else within short range) to render anybody it overcomes paranoid and hateful, taking everything they hear in the worst way and suspicious of everyone they meet; it functions mechanically as an inspire roll for hatred that can\u2019t be resisted with Willpower, which lasts for days equal to the caster\u2019s Manipulation, and suppresses a victim\u2019s Major and Minor Ties by one level. As a control spell, the sorcerer is marked by such smoke being exhaled constantly, and they get to add their Essence as dice to rolls for inspiring hatred (including the spell) and influence targeting hateful Intimacies. Distortion targets a cursed individual, and allows them to spend Willpower to resist the hatred, although their Intimacies remain diminished.<br /> <br /> I think that it\u2019s an effective spell for sabotage, particularly with the range, and find the imagery and effect to scratch my itch for some really dreadful magic.<br /> <br /> Now, what would Prince of the Fallen Tower do\u2026 sounds kind of reminiscent of some demon titles. Creates a door of foul water, out of which emerges one of the titular creatures, a long ago sealed ogre of massive size, a rusty exoskeleton, and weeping sores, that is not very smart but serves faithfully and has a mystically bound Defining Tie of loyalty ala demon summoning, which remains for (Essence) hours. It can be summoned directly into combat, immediately rolling to Join Battle, and while more than one Prince at a time can be summoned, it can\u2019t be more than the sorcerer\u2019s Essence. As a control spell, a Willpower surcharge can be paid to summon a prince permanently (not counting towards the limit), which allows it to be treated as a familiar, and expands its powers by one Charm at the end of every story it\u2019s in. Only one prince can be held permanently at a time, but if it dies, a new one can be called with the increased powers. Distortion weakens some of the Prince\u2019s powers for a scene.<br /> <br /> Before reading their stats, I\u2019ll say that I\u2019m always happy to see some sorcery that can summon more distinct and idiosyncratic beings, and find it particularly interesting that the sorcerous mote cost gives this a more flexible range of conditions than calling elementals and demons have, particularly the application directly into ongoing combat.<br /> <br /> Okay, what can they actually do\u2026 decent mote pool, fifteen health levels, immensely strong, some good social stats and defences\u2026 not the fastest, but hits hard, has a good Parry and that chitin makes for a fairly hardy body. Huh, thing gets to have Special Abilities, Charms <i>and</i> Merits, let\u2019s see what they can do\u2026 its corrupting touch allows it to destroy ten cubic feat of mundane material with a simple miscellaneous action (or not very hard gambit for when it\u2019s something being worn or wielded), as well as being able to ignore some points of soak and Hardness from non magical armour (which also does aggravated damages to wood and earth spirits). Charms can allows its sufficiently heavy decisive attacks to waive some damage in exchange for imposing a corruption on target\u2019s Artifact that makes it a bit heavier and increases Evocation costs (requiring a repair project to dispel), double 7s on feats of demolition, and increase its Hardness by its soak, which destroys any mundane weapon that strikes it without sufficient Initiative to roll for attack. In addition to Legendary Size, has a Merit to completely disregard any influence that would make it stop destroying, even from its sorcerer. Between the name and some of the powers, these things feel as though they have an association with Octavian, but I think they overall distinguish themselves as their own nasty little buggers.<br /> <br /> Thorn of Cold Rebuke, lets you go all bad guy from Final Fantasy VIII (I never played it) by summoning a javelin of ice\u2026 ahh, it\u2019s not actually to impale people, it\u2019s thrown out to break into a cloud of sharp blue particles, although they still lacerate with an undiscriminating unblockable Thrown decisive attack, that gets Occult bonus dice and hits everybody within medium range of the impact site. It rolls the caster\u2019s Intelligence in Hardness-ignoring lethal damage, in addition to divided Initiative, while battle groups take a straight Intelligence + Initiative roll. On top of that, the area is rendered dangerously cold for the next several hours, creating an environmental hazard, causing difficult terrain from the slick frost, and if made by bodies of water, generating naval hazards of grinding ice, which can be sufficient to block up all but the widest rivers. The sorcerer even has the option to hold onto the javelin and wield it as a normal spear, and thereafter can elect to make a decisive attack to shatter it and unleash its cutting and freezing mist. As a control spell, its effects go from hours to days, the ice unnaturally resistant to melting for that time, and causing the sorcerer to become an object of Minor fear for spirits connected to wood and water, for which carrying the spear gets the benefits of exceptional equipment to intimidate them.<br /> <br /> I like it when sorcery provides unusual projectiles, and think this one does a very nice job with the combination of the scope and picture of its original attack, and its enduring after effect. Personally, I also like to imagine an Artifact that could be made around the core of this power (in and out of character) and the workings that might employ it as a Means.<br /> <br /> And finally there is Torrential Cascade. The sorcerer invokes something called the Storm Who Drowned the World in order to conjure a churning pillar of water, drudged together from any nearby bodies of water, which is then unleashed as a huge wave in a large arc in any direction from the caster, out to short range. It resolves as a not very high damage environmental hazard, but one that can put battle groups to rout, obliterates mundane buildings, and possibly tears up environmental features such as trees and crops. Being caught in the water also imposes a penalty on all actions besides resisting the hazard, and puts them at risk of drowning (with success against the hazard letting them get their face clear of the water enough to breathe effectively). What really makes the spell is the fact that it can be sustained after the initial burst, so long as the sorcerer devotes shape sorcery actions to it, requiring no rolls or cost. Doing so allows it to keep expanding its range, until it reaches long, and dragging along people that failed to resist the hazard (which gains additional damage dice if the wave is filled with debris). In cases where the Storyteller determines it encounters an obstacle it can\u2019t overwhelm, it becomes redirected. When the spell ends for whatever reason, the water discharges to create mucky ground that qualifies as difficult terrain, and might have other logical consequences. As a control spell, the shape and flow of the water can be more finely guided, able to change direction mid-course or go around troublesome obstacles, as well as avoiding things the sorcerer doesn\u2019t want to strike, as well as giving them a general quality of nearby water responding to their more extreme moods. When distorted, the opposing sorcerer and anybody within close range of them becomes protected by an opening in the water.<br /> <br /> I like this spell for some real wrath of God kind of destruction, and the more indirect ways it can be harmful to enemies.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the sorcery generally comes off well. Some very interesting additional rites and initiations, and good updates or expansions to the canon of spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T08:34:49-08:00","id":1292773,"title":"","content":"Overall I really liked the sorcery section; cool stuff, generally balanced, and while some of it is quite subtle and restrained, rather than big and flashy (for example, Mishiko), I think that it does so in an evocative way.<br /> <br /> I was a bit bored of the Celestial spells in the book; I've played a Celestial Sorcerer and seen two others played in 3rd ed, plus used an NPC with it as a recurring villain, plus our party has Mara as an ally.<br /> So it was nice to see some new spells, and I like all of them.<br /> I also liked that they had a nice variation in terms of theme, element, and type. They also seem balanced.<br /> <br /> I have to say though, I didn't notice the balance on the summoning rituals, but I have to agree with you now you point it out, a couple of them are getting quite a lot of sorcerous motes. Master Apothecary seems like maybe it should be limited in how often you can do it.<br /> As I discovered when I let a PC do a working to give themselves a magical heart of sorcerous flame that gave them sorcerous motes (hey, the concept was cool, so...), plus of course their rituals, letting sorcerers start a scene with a lot of sorcerous motes is actually a bit overpowered. So it's something to watch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T10:29:15-08:00","id":1292810,"title":"","content":"Okay, can afford a little bit of time to look at the Charm previews.<br /> <br /> All right, show me a lovely Manipulation Charm\u2026 Trash-is-Treasure Misdirection. An outright Psyche effect, the Lunar\u2019s successful Performance or Presence roll doesn\u2019t merely convince somebody of faulty value, they actually perceive it as whatever higher value (exact depending on the successes) object of about the same dimensions as it is presented as, and treat that as the basis for whether or not the bargain qualifies. That the perception doesn\u2019t change their sensory input, but rather instil in them the sense that such as merely incorrect in the face of the presentation, is an interesting way to imagine it being experienced and what it might say about this aspect of Lunar magic. Effect holds for hours based on the Lunar\u2019s Essence, though three Willpower can be paid to shake it off if the discrepancy is distinctly brought to a target\u2019s attention, and their Integrity preserves them against it being used again for that many days. Essence 4 lets it target multiple people.<br /> <br /> Yes, it\u2019s a higher Essence, but this is a nice one for a good bit of Lunar trickery and sabotage, maybe even a unique sense of distorting ideas of value.<br /> <br /> Labyrinth of the Beast: Sounds like a Guile Charm\u2026 yep, the Lunar can bring their own animalistic qualities to the surface and let somebody who couldn\u2019t get past their Guile see that instead, perceiving only base drives, and then ignoring the character thereafter. It\u2019s a neat picture of how Lunars might harness that part of themselves, employ Guile, the nature of how they could be perceived in social scenarios (particularly interesting to contrast with Appearance and Charisma), and maybe hint at some more off-kilter stuff the Attribute might do. Also has a cute Protean effect of letting a Lunar seemingly confirm themselves as just being a normal animal.<br /> <br /> Devil\u2019s Eye Brand: Ah, and here of course was what some of us were talking about, place a characteristic mark upon a person to make that person indelibly mistake for the Lunar. Right down to modelling the mark (applied with a gambit in combat) off of the Tell, for a number of hours. It\u2019s a lot more obvious then an actual Tell, even making regular disguise attempt\u2019s harder, and indeed needs a difficulty 7 action to realise that it isn\u2019t what it seems. Seeing Lunar and falsie together makes it harder to effectively read either. It otherwise has no benefits or drawbacks, regardless of appearance. Certain anti-shaping magic can resist it, and at higher Essence it can be made to last for days with mote commitment.<br /> <br /> (I had said it earlier in RPG.Net, because there had been conversation about misdirection where I suggested something like this, but I'll repeat it for here: I like the idea of being able to ape Bugs Bunny by wrapping a cloth on another's head that resembles rabbit ears, and pointing the hunters in their direction.)<br /> <br /> Now, what of Perception (another I have some excitement about)?<br /> <br /> Soul-Piercing Predator Gaze: Let\u2019s a read intentions or profile character action uncover somebody\u2019s greatest weakness, for whatever that means for them, and possibly even narrowing it to particular fields within a greater whole. It has to be something that might be apparent on the character\u2019s person at the time, and functions as a specialty to exploit it for whichever Ability is best suited. Doesn\u2019t need commitment to sustain indefinitely, but can only have one at a time. Protean allows a Lunar in a feared shape to use another Charm at no cost to use the Tie to penalize Guile. It\u2019s a lot like the kind of thing I once suggested for Intelligence, and in retrospect\u2026 yeah, obviously Perception.<br /> <br /> Dream-Delving Voyage: Psychically invade a character\u2019s dreams, using a read intentions action with a variety of possible Abilities and penalized Guile to see individual dreams that all reveal useful information. Can only be used once per day on the same person. Mostly I just like this for the sake of Perception as a whole, although it does have fun qualities of association with dreams in particular and a general quality of transgression.<br /> <br /> God-Body Consumption: Lunars can\u2019t turn into spirits anymore, but they can still partially consume them when they\u2019re truly killed to be able to internalize any of their Eclipse Charms that are qualified for, although doing so requires a mote commitment, at least before they spend the appropriate XP (at a fairly generous rate). While committing, limited to (Essence) Charms, can learn as many as they want, the first Charm acquired gets to be free. Oh, now this is interesting, getting to take Eclipse Charms from humans, including an actual Eclipse Caste Solar, for performing a non-lethal sacred hunt to get their shape. Presumably that can\u2019t be done repeatedly on somebody whose shape you already have. I overall find this to be a decent compromise for no longer getting spirit shapes, particularly since I think some of the powers were what people generally wanted anyway. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T11:48:19-08:00","id":1293106,"title":"","content":"All right, round out my beautiful Changing Moon Caste with some of those sweet, sweet Manipulation Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Argent Trickster\u2019s Rook is one of the few Heart\u2019s Blood Charms that had not been seen ahead of time. Allows a Lunar to get somebody to stake their face on a game of chance, whether knowingly, or through some misleading technicality or obscure language, that requires the Lunar to put up something they would consider of equal value. If the Lunar wins (without getting caught if they cheated), they get the shape. I think the concept is fitting for Lunars in general and this Attribute in particular, but I do have some notes. Namely, I think a little bit of guideline for resolving a game of chance in character would not go amiss, if only because I personally have often not been sure how to distinguish such a thing from general game mechanics in which everything consists of rolling dice. Furthermore, I feel as though the magic ought to enforce the Lunar that loses fulfilling their bet. But overall, it\u2019s a fine sacred hunt alternative.<br /> <br /> Now, for the Influence Charms, starting off with the nicely named Fox-Tailed Trickster\u2019s Grace. In stark contrast to all of the Charisma Charms based on aligning with or enforcing customs, this one allows one to make an instil roll against anybody who sees the Lunar violating a custom, in order to make them come up with their own rationalizations for not having a negative reaction to it (which mechanically entails being unable to form or change Ties from a negative inclination), and they need a Decision Point with a higher Intimacy to resist it, although it won\u2019t go so far as preventing the consequences of actually breaking laws. As an introduction, this not only gives a good feeler for what Manipulation might do, but also helps to give the Changing Moons a strong sense of distinctive contrasts, being able to develop the talent to dance back and forth along the lines of propriety as they please. Oh, and to be especially subversive, an Essence 2 repurchase lets the Lunar grant some extra dice to any observers who opt not to apply Resolve to the influence, which they can add to rolls to convince others against the custom.<br /> <br /> Forsaking-the-Blood Posture also allows them to harness some of the power of taboo by making an instil roll that doesn\u2019t experience multiple target penalties to create or weaken Ties as appropriate by accusing a character of having violated a custom of their own culture, with members of the same culture having weaker Resolve and being unable to unable to strengthen it with any Ties that would concern cultural solidarity. On the face of it, apart from the stuff with penalties, this would feel like a normal instil action, but it seems to me that it\u2019s one where the Lunar\u2019s power can override the need for evidence or complementary Intimacies where those would be necessary, which sounds like it can be distinctly useful.<br /> <br /> Going further, Tarnished Silver Imprecation allows one to spread harmful rumours by making an enhanced instil action to create negative belief about somebody else around in the scene, that simultaneously functions as a persuade roll to get them to spend the next several days to try going around spread the belief (which I presume generally consists of trying to make more instil actions) in the form of various social innuendos. It can also target the person who is the intended target of those negative ideas, which seems to kind of imbue the rumour into them, given how it makes other characters that read the victim\u2019s intentions are also exposed to the Charm\u2019s instil action (with their success at the read action being the limit of how much they can resist it), for a number of days equal to the Lunar\u2019s extra successes. I\u2019m thinking that some of these Charms will be ones I want to compare most directly to Solar Socialize Charms, to see how their capacity to sabotage a person\u2019s social standing match up.<br /> <br /> I also want to take this moment to note that Lunars have had a lot of effects that can endure for extended lengths of time without needing to commit motes, which I think may be more than what a lot of Solar Charms can do. Apart from being something that might offset the drawbacks of some comparable Charms that have slightly weaker effects, I also think it could lend itself to an image of Lunar flexibility, being capable of keeping more plates spinning at once. But again, been a while since I examined the Solar Charms in detail, might be way off base with this.<br /> <br /> Oh, I saw the name Generosity of the Cuckoo before, really interested to see what Lunars can get from those bastards. Lessee, make an instil roll benefiting from double 8s that, in lieu of an Intimacy, obligates those affected by it to accept a gift offered from the Lunar, that they can\u2019t wilfully throw away or abandon (although they can put it in storage, exchange it, gift it, or eat it as appropriate), and can only spend Willpower to resist this influence if the gift is clearly dangerous, or accepting would violate a higher Intimacy (might be hard to get somebody invested in a vow of poverty to accept precious jewellery). This Charm strikes me as interesting in that it doesn\u2019t strictly designate a purpose to something as simple as \u201coffer an object that can\u2019t be refused\u201d, but that\u2019s a premise that can have a lot of plasticity: give somebody stolen goods so that they take the blame for the theft; give somebody something that is covertly poisoned, or otherwise dangerous; give somebody an object that might be seen by another as indicating some relationship or affiliation (the target didn\u2019t know it was the handkerchief of another person\u2019s spouse); or hell, give something that is sincerely valuable or helpful to another, either to endear oneself to them or just improve their lives (under circumstances where, for whatever reason, they might not accept such a thing otherwise).<br /> <br /> Hmm, Laughing Raccoon Audacity; I presume this is going to be a Charm to enhance attempts to tell somebody that most of the other people living in their home are soooo stupid? No, it\u2019s an enhancement to the first Influence Charm, allowing a Lunar to reduce their own social standing by letting the Charm\u2019s effect instill Ties of scorn or disgust in addition to getting people to rationalize their taboos (I guess those things would intertwine a bit)\u2026 yes, interesting, it makes people kind of perversely accommodating to your actually performing the violations by finding them typical of somebody of your low quality, as well as making them all very evasive about doing something about you. That certainly feels very different to what many other Exalted Charms might do with one\u2019s social standing, and I\u2019m interested to see where the Attribute might go with it.<br /> <br /> Glib Tongue Technique is a much simpler Charm, doubling 9s on instil rolls and slightly reducing the penalty for implausible claims, to model the idea that the Lunar is talented at making deceptions sound like something an audience wants to hear. Following that concept is Heart-Snaring Deception, hooking into the desires of others to believe, in the form of instil actions that utilize an existing Intimacy getting to ignore the Intimacy\u2019s strength in penalties for implausible claims, rolling over into non-Charm dice if the difference favours the Intimacy. That\u2019s an interesting notion, being able to exploit prejudice to get somebody to believe in more absurd crimes (or even positive feelings to think something unlikely but desirable has happened). I think these might be the roots of the idea I had of Manipulation turning a person\u2019s Intimacies into weapons against them.<br /> <br /> I think I can guess a bit from the name Uncertain Sky Ambiguity. Right, special instil roll with bonus dice, yeah, succeeding causes the target to doubt the factuality of something. Going by the examples, seems to need to not be something too extreme; if you\u2019re in the right place, if something is as valuable as you thought, if you were really robbed\u2026 it seems vaguely familiar, but not enough to override assessing it here. They\u2019re relatively subtle doubts, but a Lunar can harness them as though they were Major Intimacies; you might get some surprisingly extreme things out of \u201cdid I leave the stove on\u201d. The drawback is that the influence can be resisted without Willpower if directly contrary evidence is presented, and it can\u2019t disrupt belief in something that any level of Intimacy encompasses; I do, however, appreciate the clarification of the wiggle room for that, getting somebody to doubt things that are kind of <i>within</i> the Intimacy. This is another one that feels very versatile, with a bit of extra oomph to it from that virtual Major Intimacy; apart from the influence it can give you over an individual, it feels as though it would be very effective at spreading general confusion. For the fact that it\u2019s Essence 1\u2026 I\u2019m getting the image of some audacious young Lunar who pops over briefly to the Blessed Isle, heads for somewhere like a large town or the main city of a minor prefecture, and just goes around breaking down anybody\u2019s certainty that they\u2019re where they\u2019re supposed to be or doing what they\u2019re supposed to be doing, causing normal society to grind to a halt, before the Lunar quickly bugs out (perhaps literally).<br /> <br /> Something a bit more overtly sinister is found in The Shadow Who Wasn\u2019t There, allowing a Lunar to interject in a conversation about some unknown entity or person who has such on their mind and insinuate that the person was <i>definitely not</i> the Lunar (whatever the person\u2019s current take on who the Lunar is should be). I\u2019d say that, on the face of it, this is minor enough to warrant not requiring a roll (although it does require mote commitment for a scene). However, I think the thing that really makes this Charm is the capacity to leverage the certainty as a virtual Minor Intimacy; it\u2019s more than just evading investigation or blame, it\u2019s that being suspicious of just about anything can create an avenue for a Lunar to establish unwarranted trust, that they can then take advantage of (even if the target can resist the power by spending Willpower, which probably mostly happens on occasions where the Lunar seems kind of suspicious or they\u2019re committed to trusting nobody). I like this one for both the subtle touch, the kinds of social doors a Lunar can slip into, and the admittedly absurd image of people discussing their suspicions in the presence of a really obvious Lunar with whom they\u2019re entirely cavalier. Appearance can get in on this act, for those Lunars with mimicry spirit shapes.<br /> <br /> (Heh, the end of that paragraph constitutes a solid 66,000 words written about Lunars) <br /> <br /> Of course they need to have it both ways, as Ever-Present Shadow Insinuation takes the opposite tack, allowing the Lunar to create a certainty that the unknown person under discussion definitely <i>is</i> the Lunar (\u2018s shape). On the face of it, that can be used for intimidation or misdirection (go in the shape of somebody you want people hostile towards, make Manipulation actions to persuade your targets to go after the person without saying it outright), although it should also be noted that people can have such discussions about actions they like, and the Lunar can take unearned credit. It also has the strange capacity to be compatible with the preceding Charm, said to create a general minor psychological penalty from trying to resolve the confusion, while the Lunar remains free to exploit either virtual Intimacy; overall that just creates a fun image of how Lunars might mess with people, and come across as wholly inexplicable.<br /> <br /> Heh, I keep thinking about that idea of Manipulating people into going after you in another person\u2019s shape\u2026 you take the shape of some traveller you know is heading to a town where there\u2019s been a murder, get in ahead of them and walk past people wondering who it could have been\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, stop; you look kind of suspicious, newcomer.\u201d<br /> \u201cWhat, who, me?! Nonsense! I was never even near the alley.\u201d<br /> \u201cWho said anything about an alley?\u201d<br /> \u201cWhat alley? I didn\u2019t bring up an alley, that must have been somebody behind me. Besides, I don\u2019t even own any knives, and I never saw that man before in my life.\u201d<br /> \u201cI think you\u2019d better come with us.\u201d<br /> \u201cOkay, the thing about that is-\u201c {runs off}<br /> {as a mob chases them, leads them out the front gate just as the actual traveller is arriving, rapidly shifts into something discrete, lets that person deal with it}<br /> <br /> Heh, outrageous. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For something coming at a society from a slightly different direction, there\u2019s Wayward Pariah Affliction, by which one can make a special instil roll to convince a character that they\u2019re secretly despised within their society; the flavour text addresses princes and elders, but the Charm can clearly be used on anybody. The affected character treats any of their Ties towards the culture or people therein as a step lower, and their suspicion and insecurity penalizes rolls for influencing or reading people in that culture, effects that persist until somebody from the culture assures them that they\u2019re welcome, in a manner using rules for overturning influence. It\u2019s not inherent to the mechanics of the Charm, but I\u2019d say it\u2019s reasonable for some characters to proactively engage in actions consistent with their new suspicions, particularly if other circumstances might make them seem more acute; if nothing else, if might affect the parameters by which their Intimacies adjust naturally. As a Protean effect, the target\u2019s Resolve is weaker is the Lunar is wearing the shape of somebody who actually comes from the culture.<br /> <br /> To help the Lunar function with subtlety, Inexplicable Mystery Incarnation is an Instant Charm that can be added to any action related to any form of influence, reading intentions, or applying one\u2019s own Resolve or Guile, to mute motes spent for those purposes. I think there might have been another Charm that did a similar thing for a slightly different process, but on the face of it I can see this belonging to Manipulation a bit more than Appearance, with the stronger focus at being discrete within an operation over general control of how one is perceived.<br /> <br /> With Subtle Speech Method, a Lunar is able to make their words have different meaning to two different listeners, i.e. a message (including influence) encoded for one listener is hidden within normal speech to another. Among these Charms, this might be among the most identical to a Solar Charm, but that\u2019s not really an issue here; the Charm set as a whole gets traction for having more distinct stuff packed in every direction, and even the basic fact of this being placed alongside other Manipulation stuff creates a very different tone to a Solar with Linguistics who may or may not also have stuff like Socialize.<br /> <br /> And finally there\u2019s Voice-Hurling Method, allowing a Lunar to imperceptibly throw their voice for the length of one influence roll or a few seconds of normal speech, which also allows them to speak without breaking concealment, and even imposing a slight penalty on rolls to figure out where they really are. This is another I could see with a variety of uses; leading somebody around, creating an impression that there are more speakers than there seems to be, Lunars should use their imagination with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That\u2019s only the Essence 1 Charms, but I\u2019m going to put a break here because I think there were a bit more of them than usual, and I had a lot to say about many of them. I\u2019ll see how the rest of Influence goes for deciding how to break it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T19:42:40-08:00","id":1293229,"title":"","content":"Okay, at least the Essence 2 and 3 Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hyena-Grinning Playfulness invokes an image for Lunars that I\u2019ve often found a compelling possibility for them and the effect\u2026 ah, interesting, I was thinking from the flavour text it would be a matter of hiding threat behind seemingly benign expression, but it\u2019s actually the other way around, being able to make threaten actions that gets the benefits of effecting action, but lacks the negative drawbacks of being able to negatively incline their Intimacies, or even feel general offence or hostility; so they take the threat seriously, but don\u2019t fully feel the violation of it (the flavour text refers to confusion and fear, but it can probably be played off in a number of other ways, such as the person laughing you off as not serious, but still with an underlying feeling that they really ought to do what you say). It\u2019s a pretty interesting take on Lunar applications of fear and ways in which they might generally conduct themselves, even if it can only be used once per scene (which can still really be fairly frequent). Still, I can see how it could be powerful enough for it to be reasonable to give targets a fairly accommodating means of resisting the Charm\u2019s effect to be able to fully feel the way that they\u2019ve been threatened.<br /> <br /> Now, Wolves-in-the-Mist Incitement, there\u2019s another fear-based effect, albeit a more direct one; the Lunar gets to make a fearful inspire action that can effect multiple people without penalty, doesn\u2019t need to be directly addressed to targets, and specifically excludes the Lunar as the source of their resulting fear. Instead, those affected will feel as though they\u2019re in immediate danger from <i>something</i>, and in addition to the usual effects of an inspire action, causes penalties to Resolve and Guile, and a separate, slightly larger penalty for any action that wouldn\u2019t serve the purpose of protecting from that danger, and is at its worst upon Join Battle and Awareness rolls to detect enemies; I particularly like that idea that fixation on a nebulous, and non-existent threat, distracts them from focusing on or noticing something genuinely dangerous, both as a described experience and suggestion of the potency of the Lunar\u2019s words. That makes up for the manner in which engagement in an actual fight won\u2019t be penalised.<br /> <br /> Something like this is really\u2026 not strictly broadening, but adding facets to the kinds of things that a Lunar might engage in publically. Appearance can do fear, but it emanates from the Lunar. Charisma can provide a sense of ecstatic liberation, and now this to just give people a general sense that they\u2019re under threat. It all weaves together to create a rich and vivid sense of what a Lunar at large in the world might do.<br /> <br /> Innocuous Rumormonger Remark has an interesting picture behind why a Lunar can make an instil action without target Resolve being improved by any negative feelings towards them specifically, that idea of being to pass the buck for their arguments away from themselves to the grapevine (even if I imagine that there are times in which the \u201crumours\u201d are just originating in the conversation). The fact that the target can\u2019t even recognise that the Lunar was influencing if they don\u2019t read or profile them is a nice bit on top. The whole thing gives me an image of a Lunar who openly instils some detrimental Tie in a Dynast, who comes under the impression that the Lunar wasn\u2019t making some argument themselves, just circulating some distressing information from back in the homeland.<br /> <br /> And then it gets an upgrade in Chattering Magpie Inflection, allowing Lunars the very strong image of obscuring themselves as the source of a statement, when standing amidst a crowd, and creating the impression that it just arose from the group as a whole\u2026 ah, and it plays delightfully off of the voice throwing Charm, to let the Lunar do it when slightly further away from the group. This all feels like a very effective tool in the arsenal of a Lunar shit stirrer.<br /> <br /> Heh, after the Appearance and Charisma Charms that let one get motes back from the sense of self-satisfaction for being themselves, there\u2019s something strangely humorous in the idea that Lying to the World brings motes from successful Manipulation influence and assertions of Guile because those function as a kind of prayer to oneself. The unusual kind of spiritual elevation of innuendo, misdirection and deception.<br /> <br /> So, Brother-or-Duty Dilemma: Lunar gets to weight influence in favour of the former of those, by disrupting the capacity of Ties to groups, or Principles in general, to be used against influence leveraged against a Tie to an individual, an amusing kind of genre enforcement. That they can\u2019t bolster Resolve is fair enough, but\u2026 it says that it prevents them from being employed in Decision Points if their intensity is lower than the exploited Intimacy. That\u2019s\u2026 already how Decision Points work? Fair enough that the Protean effect says that, if the Tie is towards the Lunar (in human or animal shape) they can\u2019t use such Intimacies at all, but for the base effect the benefit to Decision Points is either unclearly written, or based on misremembering the base rules and ultimately useless. I like the flavour of the power, but it definitely needs to be reworded a bit.<br /> <br /> Okay, moving on from that, errr, Faithless Wolf Strays, starting to provide a bit of social defence, and invoking that intriguing old image of Lunars doing so through a kind of manipulation directed at the self\u2026 and has an interesting element of Luna, of passions and relationships being prioritized over rarefied ideals. The Lunar thus gets to prevent Ties towards groups and Principles from weakening a Resolve that has been bolstered by a Tie to an individual that is stronger than them (although it\u2019s not enough to prevent them from being leveraged for persuasion), and if the Tie is to the Solar mate, requires those Intimacies to be even stronger. So a Defining Tie to a person would only let Defining Principles or group Ties to penalize Resolve, or to a Solar, none at all.<br /> Heh, although now I\u2019m considering the title, and how a more prejudicial view would see this less as a powerful loyalty to individuals, and more a sign of being unreliable.<br /> <br /> Countless Shadow-Puppets Dance enhances Shadow Insinuation and Shadow Who Wasn\u2019t There, to allow a Lunar to insinuate blame or blamelessness onto any human shape in the Lunar\u2019s library without needing to wear it. Doesn\u2019t really change the story premises inherent to those Charms, just gives the Lunar some more flexibility within them. There\u2019s also a helpful clarification that the cognitive dissonance of using both Charms simultaneously only applies if the provided assumptions are specifically contradictory; for the example given, the Lunar would need to make somebody think that the killer both is and is not the satrap. And mimic spirit shapes get to take it for Appearance again.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see\u2026 Empress-Grifting Confidences: enhances instil actions to provide Ties or Principles based around giving a character an inclination to believe the Lunar specifically, by preventing a character whose Resolve is penalised by an existing Intimacy from spending Willpower to stop its formation until at least the next scene, barring being shown direct evidence\u2026 okay, I\u2019m going to be honest, the wording of this one is throwing me a bit. I can\u2019t quite tell if this is about instilling an Intimacy, or aiding a lie with a virtual Intimacy\u2026 hang on, start over, break it down. A Lunar tells a lie; while lying, instils an Intimacy to make the listener believe them. Intimacy can\u2019t be resistant until next scene if the listener has an Intimacy that penalizes Resolve (representing the idea that they want to be lied to), unless shown evidence that the Lunar is a liar. If a scene goes by with nobody given such an Intimacy dispelling it, Lunar gets a Willpower point. It\u2019s an odd Charm, and feels a little bit niche, but I suppose that it can be fairly potent under the right circumstances. I guess the player just needs to know that they aren\u2019t creating an enduring belief, just a momentary certainty that they have to make the most of.<br /> <br /> Hmm, a longer Charm, hopefully it will be a bit less challenging to read\u2026 Gnawing Mouse Malaise: Lunar spends a scene engaging with an organization that they or their assumed shape-identity have authority over, consisting of various kinds of sabotage, then gets to make a roll using either Bureaucracy, Larceny or Socialize, with auto-successes equal to Essence, and opposed by the highest presumed roll of whomever is in the group, using Attribute and Ability suitable to contesting the Lunar\u2019s activity. If the Lunar succeeds, the sabotage gains a momentum that wracks the group with confusion for the rest of the story, represented with the idea that any 1s rolled while engaging in its business subtracts a character\u2019s successes, as well as doubling the time of any activity the group engages in, while the Lunar gets the chance of a Willpower point per day for when penalized rolls fail, and greatly enhanced Guile against attempts to figure out their roll in things. That\u2019s important, because the cursed group is given a potential out by uncovering the Lunar\u2019s roll in things, and then performing a project that counteracts their activity (although there are also Charms that can do it more outright). It can only be used on a group once per story, so they can\u2019t be subjected again if they shake it off.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been thinking of whether Lunars would get very much to interact with Bureaucracy; I feel they should get hardly any, and if they do, it should really come mostly in stuff like this. Not much else to say on it, just generally another nice picture of how they might spread discord.<br /> <br /> Ohhh, and a really nice portent for Grows-in-the-Telling Technique. Yes of course, Lunar gets to reset a failed instil roll for a lie, weakens the effect on Resolve of a competing Intimacy already used, and dubious claim penalties are halved. Basically, give the impression that, if a person is repeating a lie so emphatically, maybe it really <i>is</i> true. As a social reset Charm, it\u2019s certainly reasonable to limit it to scene. It\u2019s funny, a lot of this should be standard trickster fare, but it keeps giving me a much more sinister, even sleazy, impression.<br /> <br /> Next is Herd Subversion Approach which is fairly straightforward, make an influence roll to get somebody to act against a custom, with members of the culture practicing the culture getting a slight Resolve penalty, and it\u2019s not possible to use Ties to the culture to bolster Resolve or for Decision Points. It\u2019s not quite as sexy as a lot of other Charms to interact with cultural mores, but still seems fairly potent, and yeah, good to add a means of breaking down cultural respect in their repertoire.<br /> <br /> Secret Devil\u2019s Presence is another lengthy one aaaand ahahaha yes, Lunar generates fear by spreading stories about their own selves\u2026 after a manner of speaking. Lunar makes a contested roll of Manipulation + one of a number of Abilities, against a character\u2019s Charisma + Ability to accuse them f being an imposter, with the Lunar rerolling failed dice for all of the target\u2019s 1s (being able to accuse absent people at a penalty). With success, the extra successes\u2026 are they rolled against other characters in the scene, or just applied immediately? Either way, they function as an instil roll against those characters to create a Tie of suspicion, making people believe the target is anywhere from a confidence trickster in disguise to somebody possessed by a spirit; if they\u2019re already suspicious of imposters, it costs them more Willpower to resist. While characters have the Tie, read intentions actions against the suspected character can only ever give a sense that there\u2019s something off or false about the character, needing to beat the Lunar\u2019s Guile to see through the deception. Being used in combination with one of the previous rumourmongering Charms waives this one\u2019s Willpower cost, and it can also be used reflexively along with Wolves-in-the-Mist Incitement (normally being a Simple Charm). It seems a little bit convoluted, but looking at the full thing, I guess it can be potent enough to warrant it. I think I can see what it\u2019s going for, the idea of a Lunar who has been operating for an extended period somewhere that would be on the lookout for them, and takes some of the heat off by drumming up suspicion against somebody else. I\u2019m not sure why I never would have considered before a specialty of making people looking for shapeshifters think that somebody else was suspicious, as a means of keeping up their own ruses, but there it is.<br /> <br /> Ah, and we\u2019re up to the Essence 3 Charms. Let me just check something\u2026 hmm, more than two thousand words on the prior Charms. It\u2019s borderline, but\u2026 keep going. Jeez, who knew that there would be so much to say about Manipulation? I mean, it\u2019s only the Attribute that probably matches most closely to the basic archetype of the infiltrating shapeshifter\u2026<br /> <br /> Moving on. Creating-the-Wolf Attitude. Permanent Charm, allows Fox-Tailed Trickster\u2019s Grace to be used in response to being accused of violating a custom to make people excuse them, and if everybody present is influenced, reflexively follow up with Forsaking-the-Blood Posture without cost, which turns the accusation back on the person who made it, with bonus dice for every 9 and 10 rolled to evade the original blame. Apart from the delightfully childish quality of it, it continues the image of how a Lunar might tear down or deconstruct a society\u2026 that\u2019s it, that\u2019s why the trickster element feels more intense than whimsical, I keep getting the picture of people turning on one another as a society tears itself apart and the Lunar just watches, and it\u2019s incredibly unnerving. It\u2019s not a fun thing to imagine a Lunar doing. Especially for the degree to which they\u2019re messing around with particular people; like, the one to intimidate a person and deprive them of the agency to even properly feel outraged about it, that\u2026 might be one of the worst things I\u2019ve seen the Exalted being capable of.<br /> <br /> In a good way, mind, in a way that is all very compelling and dramatic and really helps the Lunar image, and is ultimately contributing to my new attraction to the Changing Moon Caste, it\u2019s just difficult to get through.<br /> <br /> Probably also the number of things that are getting into people directly in a harmful manner needing more mechanical intricacy to manage.<br /> <br /> (I think some of this may also be a bit reminiscent of some things in my own experience that were distinctly not fun)<br /> <br /> Okay then, next is\u2026 a Psyche Charm\u2026 should be a treat. False Burrow Pursuit, through which somebody else\u2019s attempt to influence the Lunar can be opposed with a Presence or Socialize roll against the speaker, to force a change of subject. If the successes beat both the other character\u2019s successes and their Resolve, then they whole-heartedly go along with the new topic, and try to influence the Lunar in that direction, forgetting what the original one was for a scene, unless somebody else reminds them and they spend Willpower. Can only be used once a scene, and in a human or animal shape the speaker has a Tie to, changing the topic to something related to the Tie\u2019s emotional character means that the influence can only be resisted with a Decision Point. This one is actually much nicer, and feels a lot more playful in its character; like somebody in Loony Tunes confusing an assailant by getting them spun up in a whole other line of conversation or pursuit, and it takes them a while to realise that they\u2019ve turned into a lollipop or a donkey and they resume the original attack.<br /> <br /> Oh thank God, I already saw Trash-is-Treasure Misdirection. All I have to say on it now is that it might have interesting synergy with the Cuckoo Charm\u2026 no, they\u2019re both Simple Charms; you can get somebody unable to refuse the offer, or to believe it\u2019s really valuable, but not both. All right.<br /> <br /> Wolf-Amid-the-Fold Approach is a bit curious as a non-Protean Charm focused on the matter of stolen shapes, or indeed a Charm that is focused solely on being within one. Just a flat boost to any (Major or Defining) Intimacies that are appropriated from being in those shapes, pay a mote and Willpower to make influence cost more Willpower to resist, and let the Lunar get their Willpower back if nobody being influenced attempts resistance.<br /> <br /> Hhhuh, just had a thought; you can get a person\u2019s shape without killing them in a number of ways. It might be possible for that person\u2019s loved ones to become aware of the fact that a Lunar can impersonate them, and appeal to them through their feelings for that person. Maybe they\u2019re even canny enough to know that a Lunar can act on those feelings even better than the original could. And while on the fact of it, such discovery might mean that the Lunar can\u2019t affect you, but\u2026 how can you <i>know</i>? How can you be sure the person in front of you is not the Lunar? The Lunar might have already displayed a capacity to have that person\u2019s memories. Maybe you can come up with identifying codes, but even apart from the possibility that the Lunar susses the code out, needing to recite something like that every time you meet up has to be exhausting. Just the general things that might do to a capacity to trust somebody\u2026 a lot of traction is given to the things a Lunar can do while very effectively imitating a person, but the mere act of revealing the fact that you\u2019re not (perhaps in an especially dramatic fashion, such as arranging for them to walk in on you and another) can be devastating, with minimal effort on the Lunar\u2019s part. Like a less intense and more focused version of the Charm to get somebody to be suspicious that everybody around them might be a Lunar.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sad again.<br /> <br /> Oh, this should bring me back up a bit; this Edition\u2019s version of Commanded to Fly! If somebody else has successfully hit a Lunar with a Psyche effect or mind-altering curse, the Lunar can use the Charm to add to it some additional quality equivalent to something less than a life-defining task, that the Lunar is giving themselves to pursue simultaneous to what the hostile magic does; it\u2019s not allowed to fully contradict it, but can make fulfilment of what the other does more difficult, or change some of its outcome. That\u2019s actually a very interesting kind of response, that idea that a Lunar can subvert even compliance, like going out of their way to fulfil a command in the most inefficient way possible. Also very Loony Tunes. It\u2019s also interesting as something with a lot more variation and investment than the Second Edition perfect social defence. Only usable once per story, but gets to be reset when a mind control effect is fulfilled in a way that upholds a Lunar\u2019s Major or Defining Intimacy, or just doing a legendary social goal.<br /> <br /> Ah great, more joviality in Coyote-Laughing Hilarity, allowing Lunars to resist influence by making a kind of Manipulation clash, which not only stops it, but gives any observers that it wasn\u2019t even meant seriously, that it actually intended the opposite\u2026 ohhh, the influence doesn\u2019t need to be targeting the Lunar, so they can not merely defend from it, they can use it to make something undesirable to the influencer. So it\u2019s like, somebody tries to inspire a crowd with some call to national greatness, the Lunar responds with some mocking and insincere agreement, and the crowd follows the Lunar\u2019s cue that the inspirational speech was actually an insult and they get all apathetic and demoralized. Actually, can the Lunar defend from it, or is it just to subvert its use on others, I\u2019m a little unclear. Even the stipulation about using the next Charm for when influence is made at the Lunar doesn\u2019t quite clarify for me if that lets the Lunar be defended at all, or is merely necessary to invert influence against the Lunar, for whatever purpose. At some point I\u2019m going to want to ask about a clarification on that.<br /> <br /> As for that referenced Charm, it\u2019s Whispering Silver Serpent. Okay, I think I get it in the other Charm; a Lunar can keep from being influenced, but they can only give themselves the impression that the person actually meant something different (which might have the interesting effect of getting themselves locked with a persuasion to do something harmful to that character) if they employ this Charm, allowing a Lunar to convince themselves of their own lies, whether they\u2019re mechanically enforced influence rolls or normal conversation. In normal uses of the Charm, that causes read influence, profile character, and even mind-reading magic to show that the Lunar was telling something they believed to be true. It can even thwart the truth-detecting magic of Solars, getting to make a Manipulation + Appearance roll with their own Essence in bonus dice. Very neat and weird.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s Cobra\u2019s Hypnotic Gaze, which I believe\u2026 let me check- yes, there was a Charisma Charm with a very similar name, based on making people just stop what they were doing and look at the Lunar. This, instead, allows a mesmerizing attitude so that Manipulation can substitute for Appearance in providing bonus dice on instil and persuade rolls, and as a Psyche effect, ensures that characters against whom there are bonus dice (I\u2019m not sure if that is for them being less attractive or less manipulative) are entranced enough to be unable to use their Intimacies in Resolve, in either direction, although they still get to make Decision Points. Not as intense as the others, but adds another edge to Lunar Manipulation, and can probably be especially useful against the right characters.<br /> <br /> (Also got a look back at old Commanded to Fly; Jesus, target yourself with an influence that has to overcome your own MDV, and then commit motes until the influencing effect elapses?)<br /> Okay, just\u2026 a couple of pages left. Forgetful Victim Prana: use at the end to make a special Instil roll to make a character to make a character forget the duration of that scene (no chance to resist with Willpower) and have no sense of the time elapse, resets any failed influence rolls specifically against that character, as well as removing the effect of any successful persuade, bargain or threaten influence rolls (barring circumstances in which the player who made the influence is against it, in which case it has to be resolved with rules to overturn influence). Instil and inspire still work, but the character won\u2019t realise somebody else brought them around to those feelings. Evidence that points towards the truth provides the opportunity to spend three Willpower to break free of the suppression, which also puts social consequences back in their proper state. Can only be used once per day, and the same person can\u2019t be targeted more times than their Integrity in days. This reminds me of a lot of stuff that happened in DaveB\u2019s Broken Diamond Mage chronicle, which sets it up as appropriately creepy to me.<br /> <br /> Shadow Faith Inversion improves instil attempts to weaken an Intimacy, making the character trying to harness it actually weaken their Resolve rather than strengthen it; can only be used once per story, being in a human or animal shape the Intimacy is directed towards makes resisting the instil require a Decision Point. Not as much of a story shaping one, just straightforward and powerful, the idea that it\u2019s easier to break down a Tie to somebody while pretending to be that person is horrific.<br /> <br /> Okay, Nameless Monster Embodiment is another very lengthy one, and Psyche to boot, let\u2019s get into it: Lunar gets to make themselves the antithesis of some deeply held conviction of a target they\u2019ve been interacting with for at least the last scene\u2026 scratch that, for the length of at least one scene whenever, in the form of a Manipulation + Presence or Socialize instil roll, to become contrary to one of their Defining Principles (the Lunar needs to know of it). The Principle can\u2019t improve Resolve against the Lunar\u2019s action, and Willpower can\u2019t be spent to resist. If successful, the target\u2019s Guile and Resolve are penalised against the Lunar, the Principle can\u2019t be employed for Resolve or Decision Points while <i>around</i> the Lunar, and while in the Lunar\u2019s presence, acting against the Principle causes loss of Willpower and gain of Limit (if the right kind of Exalt); if there\u2019s no Willpower to lose, acting contrary is not an option. It also costs the victim Willpower to read the Lunar\u2019s intentions, and the Lunar gains an innate awareness of any situation the character is in where the affected Principle is important. The only way to break that hold (while the Lunar commits the motes, at least) is for the victim to fully erase the Principle in question, or have some major victory against the Lunar; if the latter option is taken, the resulting catharsis grants a point of Willpower, gets rid of one Limit, and makes the Principle immune to the Charm in future. It can only be used on the same person once per story.<br /> <br /> It's funny, this one is also pretty nasty, but it\u2019s not really a downer, because it\u2019s just so <i>interesting</i>. The image of a Lunar gaining such power over a person and capacity to torment them by internalizing opposition to a life-defining belief, but also how there can be something edifying in that from the person overcoming the Lunar and reinforcing the significance of that belief to themselves. It\u2019s both mechanically and narratively very powerful, and whatever its application in the Realm era, I can imagine something like this being a staple of Lunars in the First Age; to harness their inherent discord in order to challenge the convictions of others, teach them about themselves and their beliefs, either to affirm the strength and value of them when the desire to hold on drives them to refute the Lunar in some manner, or else demonstrate the issues and weaknesses of their attachment and compel them to let go of it. And only at Essence 3. It was worth pushing this far into Manipulation just to see this Charm.<br /> <br /> Last of the Essence 3 Influence Charms is Taboo-Banishing Transgression, another enhancement to Fox-Tailed Trickster\u2019s Grace; when a Lunar violates a custom, they can pay a one-Willpower surcharge to make all of the witnesses forget the custom even exists, suppressing any associated Principles. It only lasts for a few hours, and can end early if somebody just reminds them of the custom, but the things they might do during that time (especially if the Lunar encourages them), that might not be stuff that you can walk back. It\u2019s really just rounding out the storyline of the Lunar breaking down some social walls, for whatever purpose.<br /> <br /> <br /> That\u2019s where I\u2019m going to leave it for today. For all of their intensity, the Manipulation Charms are proving very enjoyable to me, very much worth having waited for. So many of them provoke so much intrigue and possibility. They are actually feeling like some of the most formidable and intimidating things that Lunars are capable of. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T09:23:55-08:00","id":1293304,"title":"","content":"Okay, continuation of the Manipulation Influence Charms.<br /> <br /> First-in-School Assumption is interesting in giving the last social Attribute at least something to interact with battle groups without being part of a dedicated Warfare subcategory (at least I\u2019m assuming), albeit focused on opposition, given the Attribute. Or at least\u2026 opposition to start. So when an enemy group is about the check for rout, the Lunar gets to make a roll against their Resolve, and if the group routs and the Lunar succeeds, enough of the troops to form a group one dot of Size smaller will reform under the command of the Lunar, the flavour text describing this in terms of the least reputable troops flocking to the Lunar\u2019s side in the expectation of better prospects, the lost size dot constituting those who have no reason to do so. The group\u2019s members even form a Tie to the Lunar when the battle is over, of whatever appropriate emotional context. Can only be used once per day, but is reset if the Lunar commands a battle group to damage another enough to reduce Size. I think there\u2019s an interesting character to this in terms of how a Manipulation-heavy Lunar might sway the self-interested, of being able to mess with an army by drawing allegiances (which can probably synergize well with what Appearance and Charisma might do to break them down in the first place), and that a Lunar who is not necessarily good at commanding in war can end up with an army of misfits that might retain an attachment to them.<br /> <br /> As if Nameless Monster Embodiment wasn\u2019t able to do enough, Nation-Sundering Shadow is here to enhance it further; the Lunar is able to spend a week immersed in a society, and then add a surcharge to the activation of the prior Charm, targeting one of the culture\u2019s customs rather than an individual\u2019s Defining Principle, and rather than an instil roll makes an opposed roll against Charisma + Bureaucracy or Socialize of some important representative figure. If the Lunar succeeds, they get to subject <i>everybody</i> in the culture with Defining Ties to it or Defining Principles related to the custom under scrutiny, to the effects of Nameless Monster Embodiment. Furthermore, while still participating in the culture, once per story they\u2019re capable of automatically inflicting a botch on a roll for a leading figure in pursuit of some important social project. The disadvantage is that the Charm becomes subject of a larger pool of people triumphing over the Lunar to end it prematurely, in addition to some major person completing a project that affirms the significance of the custom under attack; this apparently renders that custom permanently immune to use of the Charm by that particular Lunar. It needs achievement of a legendary social goal to be used more than once per story at all (so a Lunar probably needs to be focused on one culture at a time). This covers a lot of the same values as its prerequisite Charms, albeit being able to effect greater social change with their testing. What\u2019s most interesting is that it doesn\u2019t strictly give a provision for the Charm ending by the society abandoning the custom, which I don\u2019t think would explicitly mean characters would lose their Defining Intimacies (particularly not since it\u2019s enough to have a Tie to the culture as a whole), so it\u2019s really something where the main outcome is the custom effectively being reinforced in the face of Lunar opposition. In any case, it\u2019s a very interesting sense of embodying the image of a major societal predator.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s Parade-of-Follies Deliverance, through which Lunars have a means of counteracting the mind control powers of other characters, getting to target people under the effects of such powers with a special persuade roll that needs no supporting Intimacy, which uses the rules for overturning influence. If the Lunar succeeds, it allows the controlled character to enter a Decision Point in which they\u2019re obligated to use either a Defining Tie that opposes the magic they\u2019re under, or at least a Major Tie to the Lunar or current shape. If the character spends the Willpower, the Lunar gets to add a mitigating condition to the control ala Commanded to Fly. It gets to skip over a lot of the conditions if used to help a Solar mate, both succeeding without a roll, and getting to immediately form a Major Tie to the Lunar to empower the Decision Point, and no character can have it used on them more than once per story. Apart from the utility of this, I like the image of it as another way in which a Lunar might provide somebody with liberation, a means of instilling them with an empowering contrarian impulse.<br /> <br /> Aaaand that\u2019s the Influence Charms. Probably could have finished them last night eheh. Actually kind of curious at the lack of an Essence 5 Charm, but I already had some ideas of my own about what those might be.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s only short now, but I\u2019ll accept the break. Overall, I think this facet of Manipulation has been very strong, lots of interesting and useful things to do, a lot that can really guide characterisation for Lunars and shape the course of stories, and some transgressive stuff that was genuinely affecting. Definitely interested to see the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T19:29:43-08:00","id":1293404,"title":"","content":"Took a little peek, and the Guile Charms only take up five pages, so I\u2019ll just squeeze those in now.<br /> <br /> Moonlight Curtain Drawn is an appropriately variable enhancement; on the face of it, it provides a +1 to Guile, but that goes up to +3 when the Lunar is in a different shape, against any action opposed by Guile that would suggest they\u2019re not who they appear to be. Kind of surprising that nothing with that focus was ever present in the game before. Essence 2 allows a repurchase to handily extend it to a day. Then there\u2019s Cat-Eyed Enticement, which allows one to reroll failed dice on an influence roll against somebody that has failed to see past Guile in the scene, to represent the idea that being a mystery makes them more compelling; I\u2019d want to look back over Appearance to see any that might help this image along. And Argent Deceiver Smile enhances MCD, allowing a surcharge to be paid to also add that higher Guile bonus to any effect or action that would show that they\u2019ve told a lie or have acted deceptively; I presume that this isn\u2019t intended to stack with the other one for cases in which one is lying about something concerned with their identity while wearing a different shape.<br /> <br /> Seven-Veiled Visage adds more layers to their concealment of motives, by spending a mote to make up to the Lunar\u2019s Essence in 1s subtract successes on rolls against Guile, although the Lunar needs to be aware of the observer. This one gets a bit of kick to it though, as well as dipping back into some of Manipulation\u2019s more uncomfortable territory with the Protean effect; in a human shape the reader has a Defining Tie to, a failed roll causes the character to suffer penalties to social and mental actions equal to their rolled 1s for the duration of the scene, as a representation of them being put into a funk over being unable to read somebody that matters to them so much. I notice it doesn\u2019t specify a positive Tie, so I wonder if that\u2019s a minor oversight, or the intention is that characters who hate you can also be deeply frustrated at inability to figure you out. I would lean towards the latter.<br /> <br /> Sublime Fa\u00e7ade Art serves as a permanent enhancement to the Lunar, permitting them to substitute Socialize for Integrity, Larceny or Performance in calculation of Guile, as well as spending a mote to eliminate one point of penalty from any source besides being unaware of an observer. I think this is helpful to allow Lunars, especially Changing Moons, to diversify their builds a bit, since investment in this or the other social Attributes can represent involvement in situations that still might not entail as much dedication to the Socialize Ability as a comparable Solar would have. Or heck, more than that, it provides its own kind of help to passing oneself off as something they\u2019re not; a thief can more effectively infiltrate high society despite everybody looking right at them. I think it just overall helps with the idea that a Lunar engaged in a similar pursuit to a Solar could be a very different kind of person.<br /> <br /> Anemones Conceal Clownfish\u2026 is probably going to trip up a lot of people declaring it in the heat of the moment at tables; I expect many an \u201camememies\u201d. As for the effect of this first Essence 2 Charm, the Lunar\u2019s own talent at dissembling allows them to project a sense of greater depth and complexity on allies, being able to increase their own Guile by one non-Charm enhancement, as well as raising their own cap for the trait by one, a power that has Muted motes if done to aid one\u2019s Solar Mate. Following that is Forgotten Self Wisdom, to further enhance the Lunar\u2019s dissembling in aid of shapeshifting; Intimacies incompatible with the shape\u2019s identity (human or animal) can be suppressed, which has the advantage of making it unreadable to reading intentions or leveraged for persuasion, but conversely removes its defensive benefits (although the Lunar remains capable of caring enough to act in a manner consistent with it enough to reveal that way). It ends if the shape is changed, and a Lunar who ends it deliberately to call the Intimacy\u2019s protection back makes it no longer usable for the duration of a day; I guess asserting your own identity makes it harder to talk yourself back into the other mindset. This is one that\u2019s intriguing for being technically less powerful than the Solar equivalent, but in a manner that is very fitting and interesting and I can hardly see much complaint about, as well lending itself to the image I have of a Lunar openly wearing different shapes around somebody who is in the know. It\u2019s like, you\u2019re going to meet with somebody you care about, and you don\u2019t want to be susceptible to their charms during the encounter, you go wearing the face of one of their enemies you slew for them. Heh, relationships with some Lunars must be friggin\u2019 weird.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, Labyrinth of the Beast\u2026 oh that\u2019s right, that was previewed, that Charm to conceal yourself behind a more animal identity. Good stuff. But it\u2019s the base for an enhancement (and first Essence 3 Charm) in Inconspicuous Feral Lifestyle, to deepen immersion in animal identity, as the Lunar gets to make themselves seem indistinguishable from an animal against intention reading for just one mote, without opposing rolls needing to make a 1, so long as the Lunar is\u2026 sincerely acting like that kind of animal. I\u2019ll want to review the read intentions rules to be sure, but I\u2019ve got to be honest, this feels like a bit of an air-breathing mermaid to me. I\u2019ll follow up when I see this other Charm it\u2019s referring to, but\u2026 if you\u2019re acting the animal for its own sake, is being found out really much of a risk? Maybe I\u2019m not giving enough credit to the dramatic underpinnings of a character using the action to realise that this housecat\u2019s heart is not really in their mousing, while that character is trying to stay on guard for shapeshifters. Mind, does just being around an aristocrat or something with an intention of spying in the first place qualify as an ulterior motive that invalidates the Charm?<br /> <br /> Going back to some of the emotional mirror stuff that Appearance did is River Reflects Desire; functions fairly similarly to Labyrinth of the Beast, but in addition to costing a few more motes, makes it so that the character who fails to read intentions sees in the Lunar what they would most like to see. The examples focus on things concerned with a disguised Lunar, but I think it\u2019s also interesting to imagine this in scenarios where the Lunar is presenting as themselves, while still generally being read by a companion in terms of what they want the Lunar to be. Probably really helps with a lot of rationalizations. Heh, getting a little bit uncomfortable again. Mind, not necessarily immune to backfiring, in the event that a person happens to really want the next person they examine or question to be somebody they can inflict violence or cruelty upon; being a mirror might rapidly turn to having inadvertently exposed your belly.<br /> <br /> Okay, Silver Mask Subversion, mentioned at the end of Inconspicuous Feral Lifestyle\u2026 when in the shape of another person to whom they have a Tie (which can readily be anybody whose shape they have) or an animal, get to complete rewrite one\u2019s own memories and Intimacies with something fitting the shape they\u2019re in; I presume that this doesn\u2019t grant the Lunar information that they didn\u2019t already have, and it\u2019s more like getting an identity consistent with what the Lunar knew of the person, and a general narrative that would\u2026 hang on, I\u2019m getting ahead of myself, start over: the Lunar forgets their real identity, and becomes under the impression that they\u2019re the person whose shape they have. The Lunar\u2019s own Intimacies are suppressed, and they get replacement Intimacies fitting to the shape\u2019s identity, probably mostly as it was known or could have been guessed by the Lunar. The Lunar doesn\u2019t actually lose memories outright, but they\u2019ll be reshaped to fit the narrative of the new shape being real; so I guess something like, you give yourself the shape of a Guild factor, you imagine the events of your mortal life in terms of something leading there, and further events in terms of the having served your Exalted factor motives; if you\u2019re several centuries old, everything longer than the factor\u2019s lifetime gets suppressed outright. Okay.<br /> <br /> The Lunar\u2019s Intimacies are suppressed, but they can still act in pursuit of their own motives, it\u2019s just that the experience of it will probably be weird; a lot of times of doing something without fully understanding why you did so, probably second-guessing your own meaning or intentions after the fact, and that\u2019s when your altered identity and Intimacies don\u2019t lead to you pursuing the goals in a manner that might\u2026 not be fully how you intended. Ah, so the Lunar memory distortion can be sufficient to conceal from themselves the fact that they are actually a Lunar, if using their own powers can surprise them or make them think it\u2019s something external. It\u2019s an Indefinite Charm, but it can\u2019t have the commitment ended voluntarily except at the end of stories, or if a threat to an important aspect of their real identity is encountered; otherwise, the Lunar needs to have defined a condition out of it when the Charm was invoked. And, per the caveat at the end of Inconspicuous Feral Lifestyle, having the Charm makes it impossible to discern the Lunar as anything besides an animal while in that shape, regardless of how they\u2019re acting (even if they\u2019ll often just be really acting as an animal).<br /> <br /> Okay, so this\u2026 covers a lot that was really intriguing about Solar persona Charms, but with sufficient differences in lots of little ways. First off, I like how it\u2019s phrased in terms of the Lunar telling themselves a powerful lie rather than anything else, just for the metaphysical and identity questions that doesn\u2019t muddy up. I like the way in which it can allow a Lunar to go for a really deep cover, or possibly go on a holiday from being themselves for a while. I like how it can incorporate a certain horror movie scenario in which a lot of weird things keep happening to or around the Lunar, seeming to actually emerge from them (possibly in an identity that would itself be hostile towards Lunars), before a realisation sets in that they are actually the Lunar and who they think they are isn\u2019t real (possibly right before it pops out of existence). And I think it\u2019s very interesting how, unlike the Solar persona Charms, these constitute no infringement upon the Lunar\u2019s true identity. Like, a Solar who styles themselves as somebody who cares about the Realm, possibly even with altered memories to that effect, and then acts in a manner consistent with that, that care might impress itself a bit upon who they really are. A Lunar can turn themselves into somebody who thinks they care about the Realm, acts in a manner consistent with that, but is also unconsciously doing all kinds of things that are harmful to it, but when the Charm ends that personality just vanishes, and need trouble the Lunar no more. There\u2019s got to be something very distressing in being a false identity that becomes self-aware, but can\u2019t ultimately do anything to stop itself from turning back into the Lunar, who may be a person they hate even apart from being somebody who is effectively killing them all over again. Oh shit, yeah; imagine coming to a realisation that you\u2019re not really you, you\u2019re the person who killed you and stole your face.<br /> It's absolutely horrifying, and I am completely in love with it.<br /> <br /> All right, let\u2019s get these last couple burdened with following that act out of the way.<br /> <br /> Will-Drowning Void is something much simpler, representing the unfathomable nature of a Lunar something emotionally draining to stare into, as somebody who fails to beat their Guile loses a Willpower point to the Lunar. Only gets to be used once per day, but gets reset by using the general character of the Attribute to uphold a higher Intimacy.<br /> <br /> And finishing off at Essence 4 is Mind-Shattering Mystery, in which the Lunar goes from being merely inscrutable to being outright dangerous to try figuring out, allowing a successful assertion of Guile to retaliate with a special, empowered instil action that imposes Madness, with varying intensities depending on how good the Lunar\u2019s roll was and whether or not the reading character already has the Derangement. The first time the person gets the Madness, they\u2019re forced to make the Willpower roll to resist it, with a one-off penalty of 1s subtracting successes; so it can alternately be something in which the Lunar seems inscrutable at first and then becomes a haunting nightmare, or else looking too closely at them revealed something you wouldn\u2019t want to see. Furthermore, having enhanced the Guile that the victim couldn\u2019t get past with the preceding Charm makes up most of the cost of this one, and being in a human or animal shape that the reader has a significant fear for lets the bonus dice for the instil roll not count to the Charm cap. It\u2019s impressive and all, but it does still ultimately need to play second fiddle to the Charm for rewriting one\u2019s own identity. I will say that it\u2019s a much more interesting form of psychic assault than Second Edition Manipulation got.<br /> <br /> So Guile did very well; going beyond the mandate of straightforward concealment of personal motives and identity into some very impressive powers related to twisting up subjects of identity. Kudos to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T21:51:38-08:00","id":1293415,"title":"","content":"I looked back on the Charm Inconspicuous Feral Lifestyle and the core read intentions rules, and can derive two things from it.<br /> <br /> One is that read intention, while it advises being reasonable on what information can be gleaned, is still fairly reasonable on what it affords for success. You don't need to judge the intentions of the specific action, you can get a sense of a person or animal's overall intent. In the case of a Lunar in animal shape, the specifics might elude a character who doesn't know that they're looking at a shapeshifter, but between the description of their prowess, its success, and a bit of dramatic license, they should probably derive that there's something about the animal that isn't what it seems. The Charm doesn't require the Lunar's overall presence to have no other motive, they just need to, at the time they're examined, be engaging in some natural behaviour that they don't intend to have any consequence beyond what it would for the animal.<br /> <br /> Second, Labyrinth of the Beast doesn't merely give a false impression of what your underlying feelings are, it compels a character to disregard you. So by being examined while doing something natural to the animal, the Lunar might then have more latitude to act unnaturally under a person's nose.<br /> <br /> I'd also missed that a Lunar using Inconspicuous Feral Lifestyle over Silver Mask Subversion need not be in animal shape, meaning that anytime a Lunar in a full-immersive false identity beats a read intentions action, they get to spend one mote to give off the impression of some base emotional urge, and then get ignored for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T00:41:51-08:00","id":1293425,"title":"","content":"Silver Mask Subversion kind of reminds me of that time the Doctor became John Smith. I mean, ok, it reminds me of Total Recall and every other version of that plot, but, most of the time with those plots, the fake mask becomes the real person by the end. On Doctor Who, they couldn\u2019t go that way, so they had to come to terms with John Smith \u201cdying\u201d and the horror of that experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T01:18:53-08:00","id":1293430,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to know how deep the ulterior motive thing goes. Like, for example, could a Lunar who's eaten a satrap's cat just lounge around on a cushion in the sun listening to their battle plans? They're earnestly lounging it's just in a place where they happen to overhear things. Is it just primary act that can't have ulterior motives? So for example you couldn't be a cat and knock some spice that the sultan is deathly allergic to into his soup because &quot;Hey, that's a thing cats do, knock things over for fun.&quot; so it's there to stop that kind of shenanigans?<br /> <br /> Also it could help defend against somebody specifically sussing out their disguise, for example if the war council specifically started talking about all the horrible things the Empress was probably doing at this very moment to the Lunar anathema's Solar mate, just to see if there was any response from the bird that was perched on the pergola?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1293425#post1293425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver Mask Subversion kind of reminds me of that time the Doctor became John Smith. I mean, ok, it reminds me of Total Recall and every other version of that plot, but, most of the time with those plots, the fake mask becomes the real person by the end. On Doctor Who, they couldn\u2019t go that way, so they had to come to terms with John Smith \u201cdying\u201d and the horror of that experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what the Exalted version of &quot;You really shouldn't have let me push all those buttons.&quot; would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T10:59:47-08:00","id":1293508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1293425#post1293425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver Mask Subversion kind of reminds me of that time the Doctor became John Smith. I mean, ok, it reminds me of Total Recall and every other version of that plot, but, most of the time with those plots, the fake mask becomes the real person by the end. On Doctor Who, they couldn\u2019t go that way, so they had to come to terms with John Smith \u201cdying\u201d and the horror of that experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>And John Smith didn't even need to grapple with a realisation that he was ever an identity that the Doctor had stolen and/or murdered.<br /> <br /> Really, it's the closest way that Lunars are probably ever going to get to becoming the Thing, if one takes that line speculating that people who have become assimilated might not even know it until they go full-monster.<br /> <br /> Mind, the part about being able to still act on one's true agenda without full realisation or comprehension puts me in mind of something from Devilman/Devilman Crybaby:<br /> spoilers for the end of that manga and anime series:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Towards the end of the story, the character of Ryou Asuka, who had recruited protagonist Akira Fudo into becoming possessed so that he could wield demon powers in combat with other demons, starts to find something unnerving in the way that the demon strategies seem to keep lining up with his own observations, and questions the basis of some of his actions and statements that ultimately only seem to be escalating the conflict. The manner of his investigation differs between media, but he ultimately discovers major holes in his own backstory, in the anime employs supernatural powers in his own defence intuitively, and is ultimately confronted by a demon with hypnotic powers who reveals that the Ryou identity was a complete fabrication (in the manga having been created fairly recently to allow him to infiltrate and understand humanity for the sake of more efficiently destroying them), unveiling his true identity as the fallen angel and leader of the demons Satan.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T12:11:09-08:00","id":1293519,"title":"","content":"Okay, bit of a late start even by my standards, but see if I can\u2019t get through these Subterfuge Charms before the end of the day. Maybe even get a start on Perception.<br /> <br /> Empowering lies and deception has been strewn throughout Manipulation, but it\u2019s probably going to be at its most direct in the likes of Moonlight-on-Mist Puzzle, allowing for double 9s on concealment of evidence and tracks, as well as allowing Manipulation to be used to roll for those actions. Gloaming Auspice Trickery improves sneaky hand actions for cheating at games of chance or setting poisons by giving them double <i>7s</i>, albeit only for the first Charm use of the scene, the second one just doing 8s, and all thereafter 9s. And Falling Leaf Distraction is where Lunars get their version of a power to keep people\u2019s attention drawn on their speaking, but for the purpose of distracting them from some other action that the Lunar or some ally might be doing under them; the Lunar makes a special instil action, and anybody taken in by it (being only able to spend Willpower to overcome it if otherwise a higher Intimacy would be threatened) has their attention fixed on the Lunar, and taking a penalty for Awareness or Investigation against actions of Larceny or Stealth (although the Lunar can\u2019t benefit from the Stealth, given how everybody is watching them). Protean allows animal shapes to make it sufficient just to be visible to characters, catching their attention with unusual behaviour.<br /> <br /> Hmm, nothing much to say so far\u2026 ah, Night Sky Burial looks more interesting, being able to supplement concealing evidence by adding extra successes and a variety of false leads for anybody who fails to successfully read the evidence, leading to clues such as the action having been a crime of passion, done by wild animals, something supernatural, proverbial act of God, or somebody who was in authority over either the victim or investigator. That last one in particular seems very good for helping a Lunar generate a subversive or anti-authority element, rolling some of the core Lunar theme into their general perfidy. There\u2019s a repurchase which allows those false leads to be apparent even if a person\u2019s investigation roll is successful, although it can only be in addition to true leads, it can\u2019t overwrite them entirely, causing even greater confusion for an investigator who\u2019ll understand that they\u2019re contradictory, but not initially know which is which; the smart Lunar probably sticks around a little bit to discredit the true evidence a bit. That part of it can only be done once per story, but can get reset by using criminal means to achieve a major goal.<br /> <br /> Second Shadow Forgery finally provides Lunars with their <i>second</i> Charm to do things with writing, this one allowing them to make effective forgeries upon making a successful difficulty 1 Linguistics roll; they can suffer penalties for things like only ever having seen a work once, or worse if they\u2019ve only ever heard a vague description, but a single success will still make it functional. A reader only gets the opportunity to realize it\u2019s fake if they have cause to doubt the authenticity, and even then are facing a difficulty of the Lunar\u2019s Essence + Manipulation (meaning no less than 4). With knowledge of the later Charm Mirror-Hand Stroke, the Lunar is able to not merely recreate, but forge entirely new works in somebody\u2019s hand and voice, although that requires a more comprehensive reference, although having that and the writer\u2019s shape makes the difficulty to detect the forgery 1 higher. In the spirit of Charm flexibility, it can even be used to make counterfeits of particular objects with Craft projects, including mundane facsimiles of magical objects, although detecting the falsehood is possible with any close examination, and not just when they have cause to suspect. I was thinking before about some of the implications of the limits of Lunar power with minimal things to do with writing, and I think this one still lies within those. I\u2019d say the main thing for this one would be able to more effectively keep up ruses, capitalise on somebody else\u2019s significance, or sew a lot of confusion and misdirection; that might not really make up for lacking the depth and variation of a Linguistics cascade, but it can make up a bit for having so few Charms.<br /> <br /> Shifting Silver Masquerade helps a Lunar to walk back missteps on maintaining the falsehood of an alternative shape (or any other disguise, if the Lunar goes for that), allowing them to subtract 1s from the rolled successes of somebody trying to see the Tell (or otherwise seeing through disguise) on the basis of the Lunar having acted out of character. That\u2019s probably the most basic and compromising way in which the Tell might be a liability, so I\u2019d say that it\u2019s very helpful to give the process a bit more back and forth by providing a means of counteracting it. And at any other time, they get to spend one mote to add a non-Charm success to acting Performance actions, whatever Attribute they use, so that\u2019s a neat way of keeping the Charm from being too niche (especially for anybody who might want later ones who aren\u2019t very into infiltration\u2026 or are simply pretty good at keeping in-character).<br /> <br /> Hmm, Many-Voiced Mockingbird Attitude, allows one to make a single influence roll or normal sentence perfectly mimicking the voice of somebody the Lunar has spent some time observing, or whose shape they possess (but presumably are not currently in). Repurchase at higher Manipulation allows a slightly higher cost to make that function for a scene. It\u2019s not a very expensive Charm, so I\u2019d say that a lot of the time it would be useful just for being a bit weird, or if you know a voice without the shape and want to misdirect from out of line of site. The Protean effect also helps this one from being too niche or obscure, as using it while in another person\u2019s shape allows 1s to rerolled when making influence to try and keep up the ruse specifically, or increase Guile against attempts to find discrepancies. Apart from furthering the capacity to offset that weakness, it gives me an amusing image in which basic Lunar shapeshifting doesn\u2019t quite perfectly mimic a person\u2019s tone or cadence, or something in the Lunar\u2019s natural speech patterns might occasionally slip through, but they can smooth that out a bit when somebody seems to be calling them on it. I feel as though there was an Appearance Charm that did something similar to this, but\u2026 I\u2019ll review later.<br /> <br /> Right, that Mirror-Hand Stroke turned out to be a permanent enhancement to the Lunar to allow them to internalize the handwriting and written voice of anybody whose shape they have, although only in languages the Lunar knows. Lets them make forgeries with the same skill and means of seeing through as the prior Charm, but they don\u2019t render each other redundant because that one allows forgery without heart\u2019s blood, and works in combination to make the deception harder to see through. It technically feels as though it ought to be a Heart\u2019s Blood Charm, but those categories are kind of arbitrary anyway, and it\u2019s likely more important to group these deception ones together for the sake of clarity.<br /> <br /> Okay, last Essence 1 Charm, and finish off Manipulation a little bit later\u2026 Laughing Devil Distraction. Lets a Lunar make a distract gambit at up to medium range rolling Manipulation + Performance, Presence or Socialize, to represent being able to irritate or draw attention in a fight with some good-humoured nonsense or ribbing. It\u2019s at the end here, but being its own thing doesn\u2019t need a prerequisite. Also has the special benefit of being able to be used in flurries, even though it\u2019s a Simple Charm. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T12:14:14-08:00","id":1293520,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, putting Charms, Martial Arts and Charms all in a row seems a bit mechanically intense and heavy.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, don't worry about that-&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, that's reassuring, thanks!&quot;<br /> &quot;No, I was saying don't worry about that, because it's going to seem like a cakewalk once we pack Artifact right in at the tail end of the week as well.&quot;<br /> &quot;_________________________________________________ __________________________________________________ _________________&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T12:45:53-08:00","id":1293526,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I was hoping for Dominions. There's enough charms to absorb! I'm trying to make a 400xp Lunar character, and I still can't decide what charms to pick, there's so many to choose from!<br /> <br /> But, to be fair, Artefacts do have more fluff than charms. And I should think we'll get Dominions on Monday. It looks like it's just a matter of packing everything in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T15:48:57-08:00","id":1293554,"title":"","content":"Right, our Essence 2 and up Subterfuge Charms.<br /> <br /> Starting with Clouds Cover Moon, a curiously specific Charm; the Lunar gets to make a special Larceny roll enhanced with double 9s when they put out lights, causing any onlookers who don\u2019t beat them with an opposing Awareness roll to experience a Psyche effect, in which they rationalize the darkness as something mundane, and to not be concerned about, to the point that they\u2019ll be compelled to not even try restoring the light if they don\u2019t need it for whatever they were doing at the time. There\u2019s a daiklave to generate darkness I\u2019ve had in mind for ages, and I can see this fitting very effectively alongside it. It\u2019s narrow, but also lends itself to a distinct image of a Lunar approaching with a bit of a horror movie scenario, in which it provokes some irrationality from others. It also fits in nicely with some of Dexterity\u2019s stealth Charms, even without being Totemic for smaller spirit shapes. Hmm, I wonder if that animal I\u2019m thinking of is small enough\u2026 Anyway, it also gets nicely built upon with Candle-Eating Rat Trick, allowing a Lunar to automatically extinguish almost all sources of surrounding light if they spend enough muted motes on other Charms, or something more specific at a longer ranger, with just the slight drawback that magical lights will re-ignite at the end of the scene. Clouds Cover Moon gets to be used at the same time, which in addition to extending the light removal for just spending two more muted motes on something, gives double 8s on the roll to his people with the Psyche effect. Only gets used once per scene, so a Lunar probably wants to place themselves very strategically to get as many of the right lights as they need.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Devil\u2019s-Eye Brand is another rather lengthy one. Break it down\u2026 you silly bastard, this was shown in the previews. I spent about three minutes searching for this around the rest of the Google doc, thinking that having seen it before meant it was accidentally reprinted or had different prereqs or something. Okay, this is already covered.<br /> <br /> Right, moving on, to Reflection-Twisting Theft, which\u2026 might be the oddest, most esoteric Charm that Manipulation gets, permitting them to draw an object\u2019s reflection out of a surface, resulting in a perfect imitation but for a mirror inversion quality, that can\u2019t be noticed anyway without magic and a successful Perception roll with a choice of Abilities; to add to the weirdness, it\u2019s said that even in cases where the mirroring would logically impede function, such as a book, it\u2019s still unnoticeable and usable. Last there\u2019s the fact that it literally extracts a reflection, leaving the original unable to cast one. It\u2019s not out of place as a power or in the Attribute, but I\u2019ll admit that a use for it isn\u2019t immediately apparent to me.<br /> <br /> But then Reflection-Shattering Stroke builds on the concept and takes it to an even more esoteric place; when a character is incapacitated with a decisive attack while in the presence of a reflective surface, the Lunar gets to activate the Charm to defer actual risk of death, and instead see the image of themselves dying in the reflection, resulting in the instantaneous formation of a Defining Tie of fear for whatever identity the Lunar is seen in at the time. Considering the things that a Lunar can do using such a Tie, the capacity to skip directly to imposing one by attacking somebody can probably be capitalised upon in any number of ways, and saves on some time for the Lunar. The weirdness here is compounded by permanently removing a mortal\u2019s reflection (I wonder if that means it can\u2019t be used more than once on them), and removing it form an Exalt or similar until the end of the story. And finally, a Willpower surcharge can be paid to draw the reflection corpse out, along with copies of everything on the original\u2019s person at the time (for Artifacts and the like, mundane replicas); it\u2019s somewhat easier to notice that everything is mirror-imaged, being able to do so at all without magic, although doing so is penalised. There are probably a few things that can be done with that; faking deaths, getting all of a person\u2019s stuff, all sorts.<br /> <br /> Heh, Wolf Cries Sheep is a hilarious name. Gets to enhance the false evidence Charm by letting it implicate specific people, as well as combine with one of the others to create the impression of a multi-tiered crime. Nothing much to say about this, just expanding the parameters of the shenanigans that the prior Charm can achieve.<br /> <br /> Yyyes, Butterfly Eyes Mirage; I\u2019ve been looking forward to seeing what something with that name might do when it came back up. Essence 3, and oh it\u2019s a lengthy one, actually will need to break this down. Okay, make a Manipulation instil roll against one person; if successful, a single thing within their presence becomes completely unnoticeable to them, so long as it\u2019s not large enough to stretch across range bands. The Charm is scene long, but maintaining the effect requires the Lunar to remain audibly talking throughout, constituting a reflexive action each turn. When a character is concealed by the Charm, they function as though having taken a successful concealment action, from which they get to launch surprise attacks, although doing so or any other obvious actions ends the Charm. If concealing something inanimate, renders it unable to be perceived with any sense besides touch, with a number of examples of ways in which that could be weaponised, such as making somebody unaware of their own equipment or features in the environment that threaten them, although the character gets to react quickly enough to contest such threats before they could harm them outright. And it becomes possible to spend Willpower to resist the effect if something being concealed would threaten a Defining Intimacy, but otherwise can\u2019t be stopped mundanely, although it\u2019s limited to one use per story on the same person. If that person should already have a Defining Tie of something that would impel them towards the Lunar, then the initial instil roll gets bonus successes equal to Essence.<br /> <br /> For the intricacy, it\u2019s actually a fairly straightforward effect, and one that can have significant plasticity in functioning as an ally or being able to sabotage others. Even just to maintain certain discretions. That it requires constant talking gives it a nice bit of extra character; a Lunar who wants to sneak a cart laden with an implosion bow doesn\u2019t merely wave their hand and go, they\u2019re required to keep fast-talking the gate watcher and whomever else the entire time it\u2019s being rolled past. Yes, I\u2019d say this carries forward the legacy of the Butterfly Eyes Charms very effectively.<br /> Hmm, what would False Moonrise Phantasm need to be stacked for\u2026 ah, when they\u2019ve given somebody else a facsimile of their Tell, they can also throw their growing levels of anima onto that person, either as the Lunar\u2019s own anima or their own if they\u2019re already Exalted. As with Lunars, that makes their fake Tell impossible to conceal and penalizes Stealth, and they don\u2019t even get anima benefits if they\u2019re taking the Lunar\u2019s. It\u2019s Indefinite, but ending prematurely while the fake anima hasn\u2019t mitigated immediately pulls the levels back to the Lunar. The stacking is for the sake of continuously shedding and making their anima grow.<br /> <br /> This one is absolutely wicked. Just picture the scene; you sneak up behind somebody, discretely style up their hair into something resembling animal ears, and hit them with Devil\u2019s-Eye Brand. You call attention to the false Tell throughout the crowd, and they all start rounding on and accusing the poor mark. As that person backs up into a corner protesting a mistake, the Lunar lights them up with an anima, seemingly putting the lie to them, causing much of the crowd to fall back in terror of the prospect of the accused being about to fire off some horrific Anathema magic, with maybe a few brave or enraged ones surging forward. The mark ends up fleeing for their life, pitifully sobbing and having no idea what\u2019s going on, while they can\u2019t even effectively escape or hide because they\u2019re blazing like a torch.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I found it funny until I got to the part where they were sobbing, and now I\u2019m just sad. I\u2019ve got to contrive this into a situation where the Lunar is contriving some event to set themselves up as a saviour or something, or just intend to teach some offender a lesson before talking the mob down (especially helpful if they have good Charisma). Still, lots of possible uses.<br /> <br /> And last of the Attribute is the Essence 4 Charm Inchoate Self Realization, and Jesus is it huge. And expensive, costs 15 motes and 2 Willpower\u2026 although it\u2019s Mute, so it will never trigger the anima. What does it do\u2026<br /> <br /> Aha, it took me a few reads of the first paragraph and a half, but it allows a Lunar\u2019s player to retroactively insert themselves into a scene by revealing somebody there to have actually be a shapeshifted them all along, so long as it\u2019s somebody whose shape they could have gotten, and actually granting the Lunar that shape. Doesn\u2019t have to be a person either, an innocuous animal is perfectly acceptable; so long as it\u2019s not a narratively important figure, the Lunar gets to declare it to have been them all along. For the duration of the scene, they can\u2019t be subject to read intentions, profile character or having the Tell seen, following the assumption that their effective infiltration signifies having already passed muster (although powerful magic can still unveil them). They even get the option to launch ambushes from their social prelude. The Storyteller apparently can\u2019t adjudicate any place as completely impenetrable (perhaps barring some that are truly unique and extremely plot critical, like the Bureau of Destiny), but if sufficiently implausible, can mandate a dice roll that can have some very high difficulties to represent them having overcome the challenge of infiltration. There\u2019s a whole thing about how even with a successful roll the players needs to explain how they got there, but under those conditions, they can go basically anywhere with somebody to replace. Can only be used once per story. If the Lunar also has False Moonrise Phantasm, at Essence 5 they get to make a repurchase allowing a very hefty surcharge of another 15 motes and one-Willpower to relocate themselves within a scene, retroactively revealing the person that was them to have been a misdirect, and placing themselves in the role of some bystander. Can even be used to \u201cdodge\u201d an attack whose damage has been rolled, although doing so requires a roll with difficulty of the dealt levels of damage.<br /> <br /> The idea of this is very neat, and I can even accommodate the idea of the mote cost as having represented the efforts to have gotten into place, but I\u2019ve got to be honest, it leaves me with the burning question of\u2026 how would you ever use this? Is the Storyteller supposed to be describing scenes in which the players are not present, to which a Lunar player can interject themselves, leaving their circle behind? Is it a thing that a player can declare while the circle is already engaged in something, to say that they were actually somewhere else, splitting the party and the narrative attention? Is it used when the party has a destination in mind, and the Lunar player gets to skip over most of the action and put themselves in place?<br /> <br /> I dunno, I\u2019m all for retroactive action Charms, but I feel as though they work most intuitively when you\u2019re changing something about the player character\u2019s person, or that happened far away from them that is just now entering the scene. I\u2019d want an example of how this might be employed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Overall, though, Manipulation has made a very strong showing. It\u2019s versatility is somewhere in between Appearance and Charisma, but it also has some of the most remarkable, chilling, and story-driving effects, while also retaining a sense of being very tight and focused. There\u2019s a remarkable depth and nuance to realising this avenue of being manipulative, ranging from playful to incredibly sinister, beyond what I would have considered even after having seen the prior two Attributes.<br /> <br /> And now the Changing Moon Caste is complete, more then it ever really has been; these Attributes have finally been calibrated to give them the feel of the social chameleons they were always billed as, and then some, and in a way that gives them a real texture that sets them apart from similarly focused other Exalted, even apart from the number of powers that are fully unique to them. It really has cemented them as very high in my esteem, brimming with story and character potential. Making Full Moons work is relatively easy, and even No Moons probably had some obvious, if unrealised, conceptual space, but I think the Changing Moon Caste ought to be remembered as the true success story of Third Edition Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T18:44:00-08:00","id":1293609,"title":"","content":"I think Inchoate Self Realisation is intended for when the party has split already, allowing the user to rejoin the group in case they are ambushed or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T19:47:18-08:00","id":1293638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1293609#post1293609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Inchoate Self Realisation is intended for when the party has split already, allowing the user to rejoin the group in case they are ambushed or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still leaves me with the question of what the experience is like in play.<br /> <br /> Like, if the group is divided, is the Lunar still engaged in action up until the point when they use the Charm to join the other group? What's the transition like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T21:17:04-08:00","id":1293655,"title":"","content":"Just to be able to say that I got a start on the Perception Charms before sleeping, I\u2019ll take a glance at the first few of them.<br /> <br /> The Heart\u2019s Blood one, for instance, of which I do not believe I have any prior inkling. Face-Taker\u2019s Gaze. Oh, now this is very interesting, having a certain call back to the portrayal of getting shape\u2019s by killing in the last Edition, with the process of learning about the subject\u2019s nature before the final blow. But it goes so much deeper here\u2026 that idea of becoming the person by a gradual transition of yourself to becoming akin to them in one of the more significant ways, knowing them and opening your heart to encompass and embody that knowledge. In some ways, I feel as though it might be one of the easiest sacred hunts to achieve, but it demands a lot of the Lunar, and can\u2019t be something they\u2019re casual about. Even if it doesn\u2019t end up portending a lot about what Perception might do, it\u2019s an intriguing process in its own right.<br /> <br /> (For the benefit of clarity: spend at least a week observing somebody to learn a Defining Intimacy, then form that same Intimacy and raise it to Defining; you get the person\u2019s shape, and can\u2019t change the Intimacy until the story ends. If the Intimacy in the target was not what you thought it was, hunt fails outright, and can\u2019t be tried again that way for the rest of the story.)<br /> Oh wow, I thought that another Charm was going to be in the same boat as Intelligence, but Whispering Heart Revelation actually constitutes Perception getting an additional sacred hunt. Let\u2019s see\u2026 right, acquire a person\u2019s shape by determining extremely important secret of theirs. Not really much to say about this besides how incredibly invasive it must be. This one actually feels like it would often be so much effort that it might be the kind of thing you go for mainly because you\u2019re really into acquiring somebody\u2019s shape by prying really deeply into their lives. Hell, it might be the Heart\u2019s Blood Charm of the technically narrowest application, if there happen to be a lot of people who don\u2019t actually have such important secrets\u2026 although they\u2019re tied directly to the scale of persuaded tasks, so it might be best to think of them less in terms of being actually, objectively important, and more things that they won\u2019t casually reveal about themselves. Although even then\u2026 eh, it varies. Still neat.<br /> <br /> Oh, although it's the unusual Essence 2 Heart's Blood Charm, so... yeah, got to kind of dedicate yourself into it.<br /> <br /> Those will do for now, I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T22:23:48-08:00","id":1293664,"title":"","content":"I wanna say this was a thing they did on Wild Wild West a bunch and it's probably been done on lots of other series. I mean, I can't imagine why they wouldn't have done it on Mission Impossible, but I don't remember any specific instances.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Wild Wild West had two main characters, James &quot;Jim&quot; West, a rough and tumble action hero, and Artemis Gordon, a master of disguise and gadgeteer genius. A good chunk of the episodes were &quot;We've discovered that [Bad Guy] is plotting something in [Location]. Go to [Location] and find out what [Bad Guy] is doing and stop it.&quot; Jim would usually take the direct approach and get captured. This would usually entail him being brought before the villain and then, when he needed help, it would turn out that Artie had been disguised as one of the guards the whole time.<br /> <br /> As such, the setup for the charm is &quot;Lunar with the charm goes off to pursue an objective off screen, while we follow the rest of the party.&quot; Play proceeds normally until something happens and a Big Damn Heroes moment is needed, at which point the &quot;disguised Lunar&quot; launches an Ambush attack or otherwise reveals themselves to save the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T23:25:42-08:00","id":1293670,"title":"","content":"I'm getting some serious Ender's Game flashbacks.<br /> <br /> &quot;Perhaps it's impossible to wear an identity without becoming what you pretend to be.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;In the moment when I truly understand my enemy, understand him well enough to defeat him, then in that very moment I also love him. I think it\u2019s impossible to really understand somebody, what they want, what they believe, and not love them the way they love themselves. And then, in that very moment when I love them.... I destroy them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:53:14-08:00","id":1293780,"title":"","content":"Good Lord was Ender full of shit.<br /> <br /> Probably a decent Lunar inspiration, though.<br /> <br /> Note that you aren't caring about the person, you're adopting one of their own cares to yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T18:03:58-08:00","id":1293932,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been interested in what Perception might do for a while with some of the ideas put forwards by the prior developers, which might not be <i>completely</i> defunct. That and how I think Second Edition Perception was one of the better cascades. It\u2019s of course starting with Senses Charms.<br /> <br /> Beginning with Ever-Wary Fox Technique, providing a non-Charm success to any Perception rolls opposing Stealth or detecting any hidden dangers, which can also be performed while asleep or incapacitated without penalty, which can awaken them or revive them from unconsciousness if their roll succeeds; it says that one still suffers the effects of incapacitation, but I\u2019d have to check back to see what those are. Distant Thunder Anticipation is something a bit more specific, being a Charm to predict the weather within the next few hours (but not magical changes), but in addition to establishing that Perception might include some Survival stuff, it would fit for the situation a lot of Lunars might be in, particularly because a lot of times they might use such prediction to make plans to harass or escape enemies and prey. It also goes further at Essence 2, in which a Lunar gets to respond to a mundane change in the weather by introducing a fact about having made some preparation or contingency in anticipation, so yeah, the writing is actually capitalising on that image of weather prediction as an avenue for achieving bigger things.<br /> <br /> Moonlit Sentinel Vigilance is a permanent enhancement to the Excellency and several other Charms for detecting threats, allowing a two mote surcharge to be made to let them last for a turn, applying those Charm benefits to any rolls to detect threats in that time, and only needing to use the surcharge once even for a combo of multiple Charms. Worry the Bone starts their means of opposing the Larceny of others, letting them add non-Charm dice to rolls to detect theft and becoming capable of contesting normally unnoticeable magic; I wonder if that\u2019s limited to theft, or can also apply to some Stealth effects that might otherwise be absolute. To get in some of the Rage image, successful detection allows for immediately rolling Join Battle, with threshold successes functioning as bonus dice, and even getting to launch a surprise attack if their Initiative beats the thief\u2019s and the first turn is used to attack. The Charm is themed about being protective of possessions, so it even gets to improve Defence and gambit difficulty against attempts to disarm them, allowing failed attempts to be hit with a decisive counterattack. Jeez, with benefits like that, it almost seems worth going around in a manner intended to <i>invite</i> attempted theft. It at least seems like a good way to draw a hidden Solar out into the open. Hell, use some of the Manipulation Charms to flare the Solar\u2019s anima, exposing them to all.<br /> <br /> Observed Prey Instinct lets their alertness safeguard them from hidden attacks, as they get to roll Perception + Awareness against unexpected attacks, removing their Defence penalty, and even against Ambushes, allowing them to apply a Defence at all; it starts off at the bare minimum, but more successes allow more Defence to be retained. Lunars get to take it with Dexterity if their spirit shape is a small prey animal.<br /> <br /> Sense-Sharpening Change conveys the idea that a Lunar can recalibrate their senses to fit a situation, in the form of selecting one sense (being able to stack for more than one, with costs discounted down to one mote) for which they get to reroll 1s until they\u2019re gone and ignore their Essence in penalty points, so long as those penalties are for overstimulation or understimulation; the given examples are sight being able to overcome too much or too little light, but not obscuring fog or things being far away. That penalty relief does get to apply to any rolls that would be messed up so, not just Awareness things.<br /> <br /> Heh, Stricken Calf Sense has a very quirky and novel basis for being able to reroll 5s and 6s on rolls to diagnose hurt and sickness and make the examination instant; applying a predatory instinct for detecting weaknesses. Has to make for a poor bedside manner, the sense that your doctor looking you over is pulling in an impulse to eat you. It\u2019s also one of the more unusual examples of a Charm applying to different processes, as the dice trick can also be applied to rolls to detect concealment or follow tracks, in addition to a non-Charm success if the quarry is afflicted with something that the Lunar has diagnosed in the past. So yeah, be careful not to piss your Lunar doctor off, or else they might <i>actually</i> chase you down and eat you.<br /> <br /> The name Spider-Amid-Roses Discernment puts me in mind of how being in that role might be something well suited to Lunars, creating an image that familiarity allows a Lunar to gird themselves against it, lending more to the whole apex predator mythos; the Charm itself doubles 8s for scenting rolls to detect poison or contamination, whether it be to protect oneself against a tainted foodstuff or diagnosing somebody else, in addition to sniffing out a trap or enemy that might try to poison or infect them. At Essence 3, they can even detect completely odourless substances, on the logic that they deduce them from surrounding smells being displaced or diluted, and when in an animal shape with a good sense of smell, they instead get to double 7s.<br /> Prey\u2019s Scent Discernment touches a bit on some of those ideas I alluded to around Intelligence, as it grants a permanent enhancement that lets a Lunar log the scent of somebody detected or examined in that way with Awareness, in addition to reading intentions or profiling, to be able to spend two motes automatically when in that character\u2019s presence to recognise them, either instantaneously or with a non-Charm success to see through magical disguises or scent concealment. The log only lasts for a day for most characters, but a Solar mate or somebody to whom there is a higher Tie can be retained indefinitely. A repurchase at Essence 2 even allows for the scent to be picked up and logged after the fact from casing a scene or tracking, so long as they\u2019re not too old, and being in the right animal shape allows the recognition to be made without motes.<br /> <br /> Heightened Sense Method expands a bit on Sense-Sharpening, although not in the form of a Permanent Charm; it\u2019s able to cover penalties that the other one wouldn\u2019t, and able to do it at a higher number while still at lower Essence, but it doesn\u2019t reroll 1s, and it\u2019s only an Instant Charm. However, if it\u2019s used while the other Charm is in effect for the same sense, the two together are able to fully eliminate penalties. It\u2019s a curious approach, but it doesn\u2019t fall into being a speed bump, and I think it\u2019s good for Lunars to be able to expand their senses so much even at the start.<br /> Echo-Drinking Awareness was previewed, straight up echolocation (albeit now with the context of being able to see how Sense-Sharpening Change gets to apply hearing benefits to vision-based penalties), and being able to double 9s for rolls in a shape with Echolocation. One thing that I don\u2019t think the preview version had was something unique among Protean Charms, being able to enhance a mutation in human form. I guess there\u2019s a question of it not being too powerful, and just the general feel of how echolocation should work for a character. Mind, the statement on how that can benefit the true human shape makes me wonder if my assumption that social Protean Charms can work for connections to your true identity has been in error. I\u2019ll try and find a clarification for that at some point.<br /> <br /> Into a lengthier one with Prowling Stalker Concentration. Hmm, make a roll following a lengthy examination of a discrete location like a building, and with bonus non-Charm successes if examining somewhere within a claimed territory, to store successes that can be naked for a day. They can then be applied as non-Charm dice up to Essence or 3 to actions within the location related to deep familiarity with it; concealed danger, Larceny actions to infiltrate it, Stealth within, Athletics around, Lore for facts about the place, Influence to get in or calm down confrontation, and resisting environmental hazards or traps. It\u2019s a real casing a location out kind of Charm, and I think the bonus to Lore especially can be very beneficial; do things like introduce ventilation shafts that a Tiny shape could sneak into or out of. Sure it can only be used once per day, but this feels like something in which you would want to put it on a focus for a session.<br /> <br /> Sense-Borrowing Method is an old mainstay, although I think the need to make a roll against the animal\u2019s Resolve to establish the connection through which their senses can be perceived is new. Plus the manner in which it designates being able to remotely get the use of the animal\u2019s sensory Merits. I\u2019m interested in the detail of being able to notice details an animal would overlook, and vice versa. But what\u2019s really interesting is the use on familiars; Lunars haven\u2019t had too much to do with them so far, but being able to make the Charm, that normally lasts only days, both Indefinite and have no mote commitment seems like it\u2019s a very significant incentive for a Lunar to have one. And then they get to go and also apply it to humans and magical animals, and then spirits or fae (who don\u2019t even need to be animalistic) as they make repurchases with growing Essence, which probably consolidates a few things that were spread out before. Mind, none of this allows one to actually direct the subject of your target, but I think that might be part of the fun, having to be discerning about who you connect to.<br /> <br /> Unwavering Predator\u2019s Eye is another straightforward Attribute substitution, being able to use Perception in rolling Join Battle, with the option to spend some motes to give the roll double 9s. That line continues with Wolf-Eye Advantage, to allow allow 1s on that roll, or in opposition to Stealth in combat, to be rerolled, with the special benefit of beating Stealth with the Charm while under Sense-Sharpening affording some Initiative. And then it\u2019s into Essence 2, starting off with the Permanent Charm Argent Goddess Eye, another instance of Lunar self-edification as they can draw motes equal to rolled 9s and 10s on Perception rolls that unveil hidden dangers, as well as to reading and profiling if they have the later Charm Understanding the Prey.<br /> <br /> Blood on the Wind provides some particularly good enhancements to tracking, to represent a Lunar\u2019s relentless pursuit; they get to add non-Charm dice for every rolled 10, reroll 1s, apply tracking to characters who have covered themselves magically, and in an animal with a good nose also get non-Charm dice equal to wound penalty. I can see this one synergizing very nicely with the power to pursue a person that smells of poison or disease, especially if you put it there. Mind, it\u2019s concerned with tracking, but now I\u2019m put in mind of the question of whether scent rules ought to account for things like wind direction; if a Wyld Hunt might give itself away by being upwind from an alert Lunar. Perhaps that\u2019s too much intricacy.<br /> <br /> Anyway, for something more focused on preternatural battle awareness, Instinctive Supremacy Approach allows the Lunar who wins in Join Battle to spend some Initiative to give their first action in a fight, whatever the Attribute, a free Excellency, and they don\u2019t even need to pay the Initiative if they had a Sharpened-Sense at the time; it really pays to be a Lunar who continuously keeps at least one of their senses at its best. And Shadow-Scouring Persistence, through which one gets to make a special gambit against characters in concealment of whom the Lunar is aware; probably often people who became concealed partway through the fight. The attack and Initiative rolls gets extra successes, rolled against a difficulty of the Stealth action\u2019s successes; if the gambit wins, the other character gets dragged out of concealment, leaving them exposed again to all combatants, so it\u2019s probably only really useful when in battle against somebody when the Lunar is alongside allies whose capacity to see through that Stealth isn\u2019t as good (might be helpful for when alongside battle groups). It\u2019s a Simple Charm, but can be used reflexively and without using up an attack if in a shape with improved senses.<br /> <br /> Already it\u2019s up to Essence 3, beginning again with a Permanent Charm, Fivefold Transcendent Insight to enhance Sense-Sharpening Change to allow it to function indefinitely with a surcharge of one-Willpower, which suffices to extend any number of activations for different senses. To further represent their growing divine sensory acuity, the Lunar gets all Perception Charms discounted, and Argent Goddess Eye doubles its reward, if all five senses are enhanced simultaneously. This feels like a certain subtle kind of growing transformation, or perhaps just a greater depth of instinctual alignment.<br /> <br /> Hundred-Eyed Watcher is another Permanent enhancement, this time for sense borrowing; if the Lunar pays another three motes and one Willpower to activate that Charm, it gets to establish a connection to all instances of a particular type of animal within long range. It\u2019s not just being able to switch between different individuals to look through, the Lunar is able to take in their information simultaneously, as their Perception rolls gets to add dice equal to the Size representing the group; it\u2019s a lesser benefit if they\u2019re a Miniscule animal, but it still amounts to being able to absorb and process information fed in by a large group of creatures, and get to ignore a sensory penalty if most of the connected animals wouldn\u2019t be blocked by it. In addition to the surcharge, the cost of it is that the connection will be broken with any animal that strays out of range, and the Lunar is obligated to remain in meditation, ending fully if they do otherwise; there\u2019s also not provision for this to work on anything besides animals. Still, even those might be countermanded a bit when the Lunar gets to repurchase it at Essence 4, and extend the range to several miles, or everything within a claimed territory; choose the right animal in the right place, and it might be just about impossible to approach a Lunar unannounced. Alternatively, place oneself in the middle of a city and link with all of the rats or spiders, and you can get insight into a lot of people\u2019s secrets (which, with the right other Charm, can also acquire their shapes). There\u2019s even a provision with a certain later Charm by which a Lunar can activate the Charm reflexively, waive the Willpower surcharge, and make it Indefinite (although I do wonder if that means that it will keep going while not meditating).<br /> <br /> The name Scent of Bygone Ages alludes a bit to something that prior developers would often suggest as a more cerebral Lunar power, although the realisation is looking a bit more grounded, as it\u2019s basically a casing action that can apply on something that happened in the recent past, occurs instantly, and has its roll take penalties for the number of days gone by, which the sense improving Charms cannot mitigate. If successful, they get to reconstruct the events that are being cased in terms of revelation conveyed by scents, such as recognition for familiar people, a general layout of strangers, and where and how the characters were; that bars them from information that would leave no such marker, barring very creative stunting; perhaps somebody with a strong smell on their breath would leave subtle variations from which a Lunar would get a vague sense of spoken words. The conditions to increase the interval of time represented by each point of penalty are actually more generous that I would have assumed; things like having a log of the scene of somebody present, stuff to do with high Intimacies, and being at least Essence 5. It\u2019s another one that, compared directly to a Solar equivalent, ends up a bit weaker, but is sufficiently characteristic to Lunars that I think it hardly matters.<br /> <br /> Okay, the much vaunted Watchful Spider Stance: a bit costly to activate, but significantly expands the range of a Lunar\u2019s senses while meditating. Eyesight goes in every direction and once and sees out to a mile at the least, hearing and scent extends to Essence miles, or fives times that for anything that would make a big impression, taste and touch gets double 7s (I guess that can be useful for examination of something that is brought directly to the Lunar). It can be further enhanced while within a claimed territory, being able to extend throughout the reaches of that boundary, and perceive from whichever angle as to ignore distance or obstruction; imagine putting a rock between yourself and the Lunar\u2019s citadel, unaware that the Lunar will be able to see (and smell and hear) you directly through the rock. There\u2019ll be another Charm, probably in Stamina, allowing for hibernation, and the Charm can be used at a greatly reduced (although still fairly long) range to provide information even while in the static form. And as one last special benefit, an Essence 4 repurchase allows one to enjoy the benefits of the Charm while retaining mobility if at least ten motes are committed to Sense-Sharpening Change, albeit at the reduced duration of a day (and I guess the benefit of combining this with sense borrowing is being able to add the Size of a group of animals to your rolls). Yes, this is a nice one both for its tactical value and giving a sense of what the general experience of being a Lunar might be, a certain spirituality to it.<br /> Continuing the means of tracking a person down, Inevitable Spoor Discovery is an Instant Charm allowing one to make a tracking roll with bonus dice, unimpeded by terrain or age of the tracks, and following somebody from up to half the Lunar\u2019s Essence miles away even if that should be impossible. If a tracking roll is successful, the Lunar can then choose to commit those motes to grant themselves a pool of non-Charm dice equal to rolled 9s and 10s, which they can then apply to further rolls to track, profile their quarry or examine their actions, or read intentions, dice which can be retained indefinitely until all are used up or the Charm ends. An appropriate animal shape extends the range by which somebody can initially be pursued to the Lunar\u2019s full Essence in miles. Just overall another nice addition to the Charms for pursuing undeterred.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Mystery-Stalking Pursuit applies much the same benefits to casing a scene, albeit with rerolling failures instead of bonus dice and only banking rolled 10s, although those get to be added as successes for rolls to pursue clues uncovered by the initial casing (also not needing the motes to be committed to holding them, although using the Charm again resets the bank, that otherwise lasts for the story). It can only be used once a day, but upholding a higher Intimacy by following up on the leads will reset it.<br /> <br /> Darn it, my mind won\u2019t stop going to Detective Pikachu.<br /> <br /> Not many left now\u2026 Red Visions Realized: make two Join Battle rolls, applying any benefits provided by Charms to both, keep the better one, and get Willpower if that wins the Initiative order. Dread Beast\u2019s Eye: get to roll Join Battle again after crashing an enemy who was at higher Initiative, getting to apply a free Excellency to the roll (can only be used once per scene, is reset by incapacitating an enemy with at least 30 Initiative). Both seem like good solid ways to harness that roll.<br /> <br /> And last of the Sense Charms, skipping straight to Essence 5, is Omniscient Instinct Concentration, which\u2026 was seen ages ago in preview. To recap, Lunar becomes permanently endowed with being able to spend one Willpower to preternaturally sense something that threatens or importantly affects the subject of a Defining Intimacy or the Solar mate, from up to 500 miles away, or the entire realm of existence if meditating in Watchful Spider Stance (as well as being inherently aware of the death and rebirth of one\u2019s Solar mate, with no cost or limit). Probably very useful for the Silver Pact leadership to keep on top of a number of important things, as well as general major sacred guardian beast stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sense Charms seem a bit fewer and the cascades a bit more direct than some of the prior Attributes, but they\u2019re still wringing a lot out of the concept, including a few that are immensely powerful, while generally things to effectively cover the basic idea of not having your sensory input and examination impeded.<br /> <br /> Normally I would call it a night here, but\u2026 who am I kidding, I wasn\u2019t going to be sleeping anyway, and I\u2019m already behind, I might as well push through the remaining Perception Charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T20:35:14-08:00","id":1293949,"title":"","content":"Okay, finishing off the Perception Charms by looking at the Scrutiny category. I\u2019ll admit, I\u2019m not quite sure to what to expect here that would be distinct from Senses.<br /> <br /> First Charm is Understanding the Prey, providing double 9s on rolls for reading intentions, character profiling and seeing through disguises, followed by Serpent-Revealing Savvy, which is used following a successful read intentions to discover a motive the Lunar opposes, allowing threshold successes on that roll to provide bonus Resolve against the character attempting to influence them in a manner that would serve that motive.<br /> <br /> So it\u2019s about figuring people out? Maybe situations as well? I won\u2019t nitpick that, given what the overall value of these subcategories is. For the Charms themselves, I think that the latter is giving this sense of being innately contrary and adaptation to that effect, which is cute.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Forked Tongue Discernment\u2026 might be that this is should be viewed as helpful for opposing things encompasses by Manipulation in particular, both in seeing through their dissembling and not being taken in by lies. That actually reminds me that I had thought Perception would be the one to help figure people out when assessing Raksi, but somehow I felt the subject had already come up\u2026 I think some of the topics might be bleeding together. As for this Charm, it\u2019s the Lunar method to judge whether or not a character\u2019s statement is true or not, in the form of a reflexive special read intentions roll with bonus successes, which I honestly like more than even the Third Edition version of Judge\u2019s Ear Technique. Mind, this one actually goes a bit further than even the Solar Charm does\u2026 wait, no it doesn\u2019t, it\u2019s just that continued invocations across the scene against a person that has already been judged by the Lunar work automatically without roll, representing having gotten a measure of their telltale signs. Even if a character employs an effect that lets Guile automatically win, the Lunar gets to oppose it with a dice roll again, this time with bonus dice instead of successes. Overall, though, it\u2019s a slightly more involved process for being able to get into a person\u2019s head enough to assess their honesty, so it\u2019s compelling on that front.<br /> <br /> Something a bit longer with Understanding the Herd\u2026 Lunar gets to supplement a regular read intentions or profile character action to get additional information on where the target\u2019s home culture is, and what their Ties to that culture might be. It\u2019s actually a Charm that can receive false information, as it will provide insight into the cultural background of a disguised identity, if the initial roll wasn\u2019t also good enough to exceed the disguise successes. There\u2019s good advice on how to convey that information in cases where the Lunar character might not be expected to be directly familiar with the culture in question, and even the notion that the player might be permitted to introduce a fact describing it, using the read or profile roll\u2019s successes to determine the extent of that. Furthermore, an Essence 2 repurchase allows one to not merely determine the culture, but use the Charm again to assess the character\u2019s role and status within it, <i>plus</i> hierarchical relationships to other characters from the culture in the same scene <i>and</i> the target character\u2019s Ties to those people. So the Charm can be very useful even if you\u2019re actually going around within the society that you\u2019ve connected people to.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve got to say, Perception is looking like a very useful backup to Changing Moons; not exactly unfitting to No Moons, but\u2026 actually, my first impression has changed, I can read this side of Perception as being more fitting to that Caste if viewed in terms of them also having more of a social intelligence side, which effectively rounds out that Caste in its own right, which might also bridge Intelligence to Wits (Perception being helped by also serving as a means of expanding avenues for absorbing raw information). A bit distinct from the Changing Moon thesis of insinuation, navigation and personal inscrutability.<br /> <br /> Fellow Hound Insight helps a Lunar assess the value of their human shape library, as it forms a special read intentions action with bonus successes, that will assess whether the target knows anybody that the Lunar can turn into, as well as the Ties to that identity (yet more that\u2019s valuable to the social Attributes). It apparently takes magic to apply any kind of Guile against that roll, so it\u2019ll just succeed straight up in the majority of cases. Ah, there\u2019s a bit of a mini-upgrade that comes automatically from reaching Perception 4, and I had misread the earlier part; the basic Charm requires the Lunar to try and find if the target has a connection to a specifically designated shape in the library, and the mini-upgrade is the one to get the measure of if a person knows <i>anybody</i> that the Lunar can turn into, although only one at a time if the person might know several. Still, even the basic version has an amusing connotation; it gives me the image of a Lunar opportunistically hunting a person who happens to be doing something of which the Lunar didn\u2019t approve (having done due diligence of assessing where they came from first), later deciding to visit the place for whatever reason, and then going around reading random people to try and find somebody who knows the shape, and work their way back into that life (or possibly know somebody to avoid). It takes three Charms and at least Perception 3 to get this stuff, but it feels like a worthwhile sideline for a majority of Changing Moons.<br /> <br /> Okay, this tree tops out its Perception min with the Permanent Expected Guest Insight, which enhances the prior Charm to allow it to instead assess whether or not an observed target has positive or negative Ties to any category which includes person or being that is within the Lunar\u2019s library. That is to say, if a target hates the Realm and the Lunar can turn into a bunch of officials or soldiers, or has a great fondness for wolfhounds, the Lunar will be able to know of it. They can still only get one insight at a time, although the Lunar is allowed to either ask after feelings towards a group that they specify, or just freestyle it to learn of any connection to a randomly chosen one. Hmm, okay, four Charms and a maximized Attribute takes it a little bit from a sideline into a dedication. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmm, with Taboo-Observing Reverence, I\u2019m getting an impression that a lot of the general purpose of these Essence 1 Scrutiny Charms is a means of providing some of the information that many Charms in a bunch of the other Attributes are dependent on. Not that there\u2019s anything wrong with that, and the realisation is actually a lot more invested when it could have likely gotten away with being more workmanlike. The minutiae of the Charm are still a bit different; rather than being automatic, the read intentions roll has a difficulty dependent on the obscurity of the custom that the Lunar is trying to gain an insight into. There\u2019s also a note on how it\u2019s a read roll that gets to use Lore instead of Socialize, but only if the Ability\u2019s background might encompass the culture in question. Success is described as giving a sense of the custom\u2019s nature and purpose, in a manner permitting flawless replication of it, to the point that performing it within the scene grants Willpower. The read intentions roll also gets double duty if it beats the Guile of participants in a practice that the Lunar had observed for the Charm, allowing them to know one Intimacy from each valid target related to it. The Charm only gets one use per scene, so the education might be a bit slow.<br /> <br /> Exquisite Heart\u2019s Taste can supplement a read intentions or profile action by allowing Intimacies that could support a character being open about their wants to penalize their Guile as they would Resolve, and there\u2019s actually a Protean benefit to elevate the flavour text about taking those cues from physical markers, by letting a Keen Nosed animal shape make the roll with bonus dice equal to the Intimacy\u2019s level\u2026 although given the phrasing in the Charm, I\u2019m just going to assume that in this case it applies only the highest level Intimacy.<br /> <br /> And I\u2026 am actually going to stop right here, abruptly in the middle of these Essence 1 Charms. I hadn\u2019t fully considered how much another ten or twelve pages worth would be, and despite my earlier comment it actually is getting late enough that my attention is starting to waver. I\u2019m hoping that I\u2019ll be able to start early enough tomorrow to finish these, and then work in my intended approach to the next preview portion<b>s</b>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T07:05:49-08:00","id":1294032,"title":"","content":"Okay, going to finish off these Perception Charms now.<br /> <br /> The next Charm up is Soul-Piercing Predator Gaze\u2026 which was previewed, I already talked about it. Next!<br /> <br /> Shadow Hunter Insight is a more mechanically cogent representation of insight into a person\u2019s weakness, and general positioning of oneself as a stalking hunter, by allowing a Lunar that has profiled or read a character who is unaware of the Lunar to gain non-Charm dice to a Join Battle roll against that character equal to 1s and 2s on that character\u2019s Join Battle roll, as well as the same number of dice to the first damage roll if the Lunar wins and uses the first round to attack, so long as they start a fight within a few days of having profiled their target. This just feels like a neat way to represent a Lunar approaching enemies in that manner, particularly the quality in which doing so entails having gained an understanding of an enemy\u2019s cares and motives, it\u2019s not just about examination for weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Far-Seeing Storm Crow is an enhancement on top of Soul-Piercing Predator Gaze, allowing the use of that Charm to be followed by getting to make a Lore roll (including threshold successes from the read intentions roll as non-Charm dice) to introduce a fact about the discerned weakness, with an allowance for relevant Intelligence Charms to enhance that action. It gives a few examples of what that might entail, basically allowing a player to further elaborate on and tailor the weakness (in particular contributing ideas about what its origin is), probably either to improve their capacity to capitalise on it, or lead it towards their interests. Possession of another Charm even allows one to attribute the weakness to supernatural afflictions such as the interference of spirits or sorcery, without the Lunar\u2019s Lore background needing to cover such subjects. It would be unusual as a Charm specific to a particular Ability, but I\u2019d say that relative narrowness is made up for by how it allows such an intrusion into other characters, as well as allowing Charms from a different Attribute to enhance the roll. And it\u2019s overall a fun-looking and tactical use of fact introduction that is very fitting to Lunars. Honestly, I feel rather remiss from having never once considered that mechanic myself as something helpful for Lunar cerebral powers in a hunting or harassing fashion.<br /> <br /> Cautious Rat Concentration helps a Lunar to know where they stand by getting to make a read intentions roll against all characters in their awareness (a little vague, but given the language employed in other Charms, I\u2019m going to assume this means known to be in the Lunar\u2019s presence), allowing the Lunar to know from everybody whose Guile is overcome whether or not they harbour any suspicions towards the Lunar, and roughly what those might happen to be, after which the Lunar can gain +1 to their Guile (likely representing them calibrating their guard to particular subjects). It can only be used once per scene, but considering the nature of scenes in which it might be used, once probably makes an effective prelude before throwing oneself around the movers and shakers as deemed necessary (if not cautious).<br /> <br /> Although speaking of, while many of these Charms seem valuable to Changing Moons, the notion that a lot might not have them does give me the amusing image that a lot of those Lunars go about their business with a certain wild abandon, preferring to learn the ropes of what they\u2019re engaging in by direct interaction and trial-and-error over pre-planning and observation, compared to a lot of No Moons who might be engaging socially with a more strategic intent. I don\u2019t mean this as broad stereotypes, more a possible derivation of trends and any interesting character possibilities that might arise therein.<br /> <br /> Hehehe, all right, the image behind Secret Sense Intuition, such as the Lunar who emotionally disarms pursuing assassins with cheerful greetings, is delightfully dickish, and lends an additional dynamic to my imagining of a long Wyld Hunt pursuit; the actual function of the Charm is to allow a Lunar to reflexively read the intentions of anybody that comes within short range of themselves while unaware, and on a success (which reveals them and their current emotional state to the Lunar), reflexively make an influence roll at the target against which their Resolve is weakened, with even a failed roll giving the Lunar a sense that somebody is nearby. If in possession of the Charm to perceive immaterial beings, it can even alert to their approach. It actually gives me an image of a Lunar who, on knowing that there\u2019s a general pursuit, specifically <i>doesn\u2019t</i> remain on the lookout for it, playing with letting the pursuers get as close to them as possible for the sake of doing something like spooking them or deflecting their attention; it fits my notion that battling against the Realm might often have Lunars dancing on the edge of a razor, although such would be a lot more by design than I would have been thinking. The once-per-scene use seemed like a frustration of my notion that it might be reflexively employed against multiple approaching characters in sequence, but the fact that the reset is the Charm actually succeeding just means that the chain of uses needs to not get interrupted before you\u2019ve winkled out everybody.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Uncanny Dreamer\u2019s Insight seems to actually still afford Perception some prophetic qualities, so I wonder\u2026 anyway, it\u2019s a Permanent Charm that applies whenever the Lunar goes to sleep, in which the Storyteller states to the player that there could have been an opportunity to make an Awareness or Investigation roll during the previous day which was overlooked (although only the most useful one if there were several), providing the opportunity to spend ten motes to roll for it in their sleep, as the Lunar\u2019s dreams recount events and their heightened awareness has an epiphany about a key missed detail. Hmm, in the end a bit more finely tuned detective than prophet, but still neat. I\u2019m going to take the Willpower acquired from success uncovering useful info as taking the form of the usual benefit of sleep and dreaming being ramped up a little bit. There are even a couple of Charms that can be reflexively applied to that memory examination; I\u2019m guessing that for one of them, a Lunar gets an opportunity to see if maybe something dematerialized was involved in proceedings, which leaves me debating whether to imagine that in terms more \u201cthe Lunar can actually experience the dream as though it was a capture of events\u201d or \u201cthere\u2019s a constant underlying awareness of the immaterial even when it isn\u2019t brought to the forefront of awareness\u201d. The Charm is also Mute, so no Lunar is at risk of blazing forth while they sleep.<br /> <br /> And converse to two or three Charms to assist writing, Untangling the Web actually gives Lunars some much needed assistance with reading; their basic reading speed is said to be multiplied by a factor of their combined mental Attributes, and they get to reroll a number of dice equal to Perception for rolling to decipher codes and forgeries, something allowing one to contest even Charm created encoding such as Letter-Within-a-Letter Technique. They can also reroll that many dice for read intentions rolls for characters who are supposed to be using obtuse language to conceal their motives, so\u2026 I guess I\u2019m going to have to add that to my considerations for how Guile might be portrayed or stunted.<br /> <br /> Into the Essence 2 Charms now, with Motive-Dissecting Eye providing some more social insights as a Lunar gets to reflexively read the intentions of somebody that they\u2019re seeing attempting an influence, to discern what their intentions behind the act are, with non-Charm successes equal to any 1s on the influence roll. That a Lunar can apply that information to selecting an Intimacy that would improve their own Resolve against an influence (which in combination with Serpent-Revealing Savvy makes the Resolve bonuses provided by that Charm count as non-Charm) roots it a bit in seeing the motives behind what is directed at the Lunar, the strongest impression I get from it is a Lunar flitting around a social scene and getting insight into the various characters intentions towards one another.<br /> <br /> Wolf Knows the Flock enhances Soul-Piercing Predator Gaze by improving its scope; the Charm becomes capable of assessing whole cultures, making a roll that might include Bureaucracy against a Guile provided either by a society\u2019s leader, or somebody prominent within it who would oppose their actions, upon which the Lunar is provided an insight into something that qualifies as the group\u2019s greatest weakness and a specialty for exploiting it. It\u2019s kept from being something that a Lunar can just roll into town and pick up immediately with a provision for how much interaction is required before the roll can be made, and a suggestion that it take longer for a group that would be harder to get the measure of due to size or decentralization. Despite the social quality of it, this one does actually strike me as a good deal more No Moon, because I wouldn\u2019t strictly assess the Changing Moon activities in terms of strengths or weaknesses, whereas this feels like the Charm of somebody that is gearing up for an attack. I actually think there could be some pretty cool narratives, possibly over a session, based around using this Charm to make an assessment and then formulating a plan to exploit it.<br /> <br /> Pack-Preserving Instinct is a somewhat unusual kind of Permanent Charm, although the underlying intent seems to be in-character for Lunars; if the Lunar sees their Mate or people for whom they have positive higher Intimacies in a situation where they might benefit from the Lunar\u2019s Perception Charms, the Lunar gets to pay two motes apiece to apply their own Charms to the other character\u2019s rolls and actions, representing warnings that the Lunar conveys to the character. There\u2019s a helpful list of Charms for which that might be valid, although given the overall wording it probably isn\u2019t comprehensive. I imagine this is something that you could only really get away with in this Attribute, seeing as it\u2019s so often a more passive interaction.<br /> <br /> Perspective-Shifting Persistence has an idea for a Lunar being able to get a more improved read on somebody by mildly altering their own point of view, being able to reset a failed read intentions roll, with an incentive to make the altered perspective more literal by rewarding a Lunar who changes shape before making the new attempt with what is basically a refund on the Charm\u2019s Willpower cost if the roll succeeds. This just makes me think back to other points about how being close to a Lunar might be weird\u2026 which I think also involved shapeshifting; for here, just the image of a First Age partnership is which the Solar was being very reserved about something, their Lunar scrutinised them very closely while trying to wheedle something out of them, and then halfway through the conversation turns into a dog or eagle or something for just a few moments while giving them a Look, before turning back. Hell, the Charm has no limit on how many resets it provides beyond the Willpower cost, maybe a conversation in which they cycled through four or five shapes before getting at the truth. Maybe include an elderly person and a child, both for invoking the image of either of their supposed wisdoms and just unnerving their Mate a little (I have to imagine that historically there have been innumerable Solars who, regardless of the nature of their relationship, asked their Lunar to please not turn into a child around them).<br /> <br /> Okay, back to weakness discernment, as Underbelly-Seizing Insight allows one to spend a Willpower point to give themselves a full free Excellency for any Attribute to enhance a roll benefiting from the specialty provided by Soul-Piercing Predator\u2019s Gaze (greatly compounding the value of that Charm) or the Join Battle roll enhanced by Shadow Hunter Insight. It can\u2019t be used on the same target more than once per story, but I wonder\u2026 right, the specialty provided by the former Charm does get fixed to a specific Ability, but the Lunar advantage is in flexibility in combining Attributes with it. Under a circumstance like this, I would even think that some unusual or unique combinations might be worth accommodating. And a specialty for exploiting a weakness might be more broadly applicable than it seems\u2026 if a person\u2019s weakness is their syphilis, give oneself a Presence or Socialize specialty related to that, and then maybe use this Charm a few times with different people to promote rumours related to their disease that greatly hurt their standing, building up towards some influence roll focused on them specifically intended to significantly emotionally harm them (or maybe offer them a relief at significant cost).<br /> <br /> So, up to Essence 3 now, and beginning with Razor Insight Tutelage, which appears to be taking some of the subtext I\u2019ve been reading about Lunars being challenging or subversive for instructive purposes and elevating it to text. When a Lunar defeats somebody through a revealed weakness (defeat being a fairly encompassing term here), they get to reflexively employ the Charm to target that person with a special persuade roll, that rolls Appearance or Charisma as the Attribute, but adds Perception as non-Charm dice (which probably also makes it a lock to stunt its actual Excellency in with whichever social Attribute is chosen), and which measures the strength of the virtual Intimacy the influence works through depending on the severity of the inflicted defeat, ranging from the Minor \u201ctarget gave up and failed to protect something of relatively limited significance\u201d to the Defining \u201cbrought character to unconsciousness or brink of death and/or destroyed or disrupted something of the highest significance or value to them\u201d; the persuasion itself needs to be focused on convincing the character to do something that will help them rise above or counteract their own weaknesses. It can\u2019t be used more than once per story, but if a Lunar opts to stick around as the person works on fulfilling the persuaded task, what a story that might be\u2026 although actually, I misread it, it\u2019s another Charm that can be used multiple times so long as it\u2019s on different people. Still, the image for this one is fascinating; it gives me the picture of a brash young Solar who meets their centuries old Lunar, who has been watching them for a while and is distinctly unimpressed, and offers the Solar an insult that leads to challenging to the death. The Solar gets slashed to ribbons, and awakens some time after, surprised and patched up and with the Lunar preparing a meal, and glumly acknowledges that they lost. The Lunar offers some tough love, and sets the Lunar on a course intended to redress some of their flaws. Or various other things; turn merchant princes into mendicant disciples, maybe show an officer of the Realm the error of their ways, likely a <i>lot</i> of things you could do with wayward spirits in lieu of turning them into accessories. Yes, the look of this Charm pleases me especially\u2026 it makes me want to watch videos of Asura versus Augus again.<br /> <br /> Oh, right, it has a Protean element\u2026 get to treat an existing Tie that would support the influence as one step stronger, or if Defining, add Willpower to the cost to resist. Sounds good.<br /> <br /> Dream-Delving Voyage was also seen in preview, get to examine dreams to learn info about a person. Next!<br /> <br /> Veil-Rending Scrutiny, which is\u2026 actually the last of the Scrutiny Charms. Okay, Lunar who is being examined by somebody they\u2019re not aware of reading their intentions, able to respond with reflexive roll of Awareness, Investigation or Socialize plus Essence bonus successes against the observer\u2019s Guile, and succeeding removes their own Guile penalty for being unaware of an observer; so something like the Lunar is instinctively put on guard against somebody figuring them out, even if they remain consciously unaware of being watched. If they read or threaten somebody who was watching them later in the scene, gets a bonus success. Seems sexy enough, but has the bad fortune to have needed to follow up the \u201coutdo somebody to make them let you teach them a lesson\u201d Charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And that\u2019s Scrutiny. Didn\u2019t have the biggest expectations, but turned out to be a fairly impressive cascade of information gathering, pursuit, and its own kind of influences.<br /> <br /> Hmm, only five pages of Mysticism Charms\u2026 but I did talk at length about some of the proceeding ones\u2026 almost three thousand words\u2026 eh, I\u2019m early enough, I can take a break for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T14:19:48-08:00","id":1294173,"title":"","content":"There is a lot of stuff in Perception, which is a Good Thing\u2122.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T18:06:26-08:00","id":1294259,"title":"","content":"Right, Mysticism Charms. Funny thing, these were a topic that, when looking back over the Second Edition Perception Charms the other night, I paid especial attention to, and they were prominent in a thought I had on those Charms that\u2019s been growing through the last few weeks of comparing them, which I might talk about later. But for now:<br /> <br /> The first one is your basic Charm to see dematerialized subjects, although with the unique twist of being in a shape with heightened senses being forewarned that a spirit is within long range, letting them know to use the Charm with certainty. Spirit-Rending Fury is\u2026 oh, so is basically all of the spirit attacking stuff going to be here? Mmmm I can get on board with that; does basically fit the Attribute\u2019s element of sensory enhancement on every axis. But yeah, Charm gives a tick-long enhancement to physical interaction and attack to get at the immaterial, although this one comes with a slight drawback of affording that same potential back to other beings.<br /> <br /> I like the imagery behind Demon-Drinking Fang as their spirit killing Charm, the extra damage dice to something lower on the Initiative order to convey the sense of slaughtering prey, feels very Werewolf the Forsaken Second Edition. Ohh, and Permanent Charms to keep enhancing that in even more proprietary directions\u2026 Shed Divinity\u2019s Nectar lets the Lunar spend Willpower with the death blow to internalise the spirit\u2019s Essence, acquiring mutations reflecting the spirit\u2019s nature and capabilities and nature, and the value of its worshippers for the duration of a story, with the mild cost of taking on a Major Intimacy to carry on some of the spirit\u2019s legacy, and an option to either digest it or spit it back out to reincarnate when the Charm runs out. Does it quite make up for not being able to shapeshift into them? Jeez, it\u2019s an Essence 1 Charm, and I already think it\u2019s more than some people deserve. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And hey, my ongoing quest to let a Lunar give their human shape functional wings with impunity continues (even if you\u2019d need to take down an Essence 4 winged spirit early on to manage this).<br /> <br /> From Essence 2, Devil-Restraining Grip allows a grapple gambit against an immaterial being that can use Perception and Occult for the control roll, and if successful lets the spirit be dragged into physical form, with additional power while in a shape with special grappling abilities or Legendary Size. I\u2019ve got to imagine the occasional No Moon who dealt with a troublesome local god by making a big show of grabbing their ephemeral form by the throat, pulling them into the world, and leaving them surrounded and unarmed by angry villagers, flying away Iron Man style.<br /> <br /> Scent of Midnight Dweomers (I\u2019m pretty sure that when I saw this name earlier, I assumed it was a typo) is their ticket into other worlds that people have often wanted Lunars to be roaming in; they get to make a roll to detect the presence of entrances to places such as sanctums or the Wyld, Malfeas or Underworld, and which one they go to (I presume the entrance needs to be in proximity), pulling double duty as a general weirdness detector as they get to try and sense the presence of ongoing sorcery or necromancy processes and identify their functions, and determine the nature and powers of hearthstones, demesnes and manses. To top it all off, they can determine the nature of spirits and fae by smelling them, although the roll to do so is a bit harder if they\u2019ve disguised themselves as a different manner of being.<br /> <br /> Hmm, Divinity-Stealing Whisper, eh? In the presence of a god or a place sacred to them, get to roll Perception + Occult against a difficulty based on the spirit\u2019s own strength and the size of their Cult, but with the benefit of doubles 8s and any magic that can aid hearing, in order to eavesdrop on prayers directed at the god; rather than taking them in individually or being able to process the many parts of the whole, Lunar is able to discern the basic gist of what worshippers are asking after. The Lunar is then afforded the means of co-opting the god\u2019s position if it\u2019s determined that they have no intention of answering the prayers, by providing the desired result in a manner that most worshippers can recognise; the reward for this is acquiring the entire Cult of lower Essence spirits, or taking one dot away from those stronger than the Lunar, as well as a capacity to gain the god\u2019s Eclipse Charms if they\u2019ve bought into another Charm. That\u2019s certainly one way for No Moons to make gods behave, or else Lunars to gird themselves for other battles, bring down the unfeeling and comfortable mighty, or set themselves up as divinities. It does feel rooted in the sense that many Lunars are objects of worship in their own domains.<br /> <br /> Claw That Rends the Veil at Essence 3 is a scene long enhancement to make some general spirit fighting a bit easier, bestowing a kind of foxfire aura to their regular attacks, a natural weapon, or one bonded to their body, to allow that means of attack to get decent discounts on the Charms for aggravated damage and grappling into the material, although wielding that aura so revulses spirits that they experience the Lunar as Hideous (also getting to use their Perception instead of Appearance to determining dice added to threaten actions, which they get to reflexively make against spirits upon activating the Charm). It adds a nice bit of flair to Lunar activity in that world, and I\u2019m getting an amusing image from picturing a Lunar applying their sensory acuity and discernment as a means of intimidation; perhaps making show of looking at the spirit through the flame, combining both its distressing aura and the implication of being watched very hungrily.<br /> <br /> I think Silver Curtain Parted (slip through sanctum entrances, cross realm of existence boundaries or get past sorcerous barriers) was previewed before. Not much more to say on it here beyond liking a Totem effect recognising migratory animals (which can be pretty damn broad) and admittedly becoming intrigued at the prospect of a new Wyld Migration Formation Charm.<br /> <br /> Devil\u2019s Hidden Footprints functions as an enhancement to Scent of Midnight Dweomers by allowing it to sniff out the traces of a magic that has elapsed or was more temporary, right down to a flaring anima, although the difficulty to do so grows as each month goes by. It\u2019s a bit more of a restricted Charm than usual, as the basic success only tells that something happened and how long ago, and getting more specific and useful information requires dedicating extra successes; from minor things like what the Essence rating of the user was or if it was one\u2019s Solar mate, up through things like the specific nature of the power, an Artifact it might have belonged to in general terms, and an overall character nature and profile, with one of the effects in between letting the scent be added to the library for later use.<br /> <br /> God-Body Consumption basically functions identically to one of the Intelligence Charms for acquiring Eclipse powers, the commitment and limit, the option to but them permanently, right down to being able to get them from appropriate human characters when their shapes are taken non-lethally. The Lunar just needs to permanently kill a spirit to internalise these powers. Not much else to say about it, despite its heavy implications.<br /> <br /> Two Worlds Penumbra helps out with the whole emissary to or for the spirit world angle, as the illumination of the Lunar\u2019s anima can become capable of rendering immaterial beings visible, or even tangible when close enough, although ones stronger than the Lunar can spend Willpower to become immune (although doing so requires a Decision Point if they fear the Lunar\u2019s current shape, as a Protean effect).<br /> <br /> And last of all, once again skipping straight to Essence 5, is Omen-Beast\u2019s Evil Eye, a Permanent Charm that denotes a whopping 30 motes (plus one Willpower) as a surcharge cost. The Charm enhances Far-Seeing Storm Crow (i.e. the Charm to introduce facts about somebody\u2019s weakness), with the additional cost allowing something between a prediction and a curse to make that weakness into something that will doom the character in a coming challenge. The difficulty for the fact introducing roll is the target\u2019s Essence rating, in addition to a modifier determined by how bad the doom will be; something that will only cause serious personal difficulties such as loans being called in or having a political challenger provide no modifier, a distinct danger such as being set upon by hired goons or hidden poisoners increases it by three, and a debtor becoming enslaves or a rebellion of breakout or something else that can alter the course of a life adds a full five to it. Jeez, and here was me thinking it would just be some kind of sabotage in a fight like a reserved botch, not the Lunar flavour of being a terrible prophet of doom. And part of that Lunar flavour is not being able to merely invoke it from afar; the target has to be forewarned of what\u2019s coming for them, and given a way out (although they only get five to ten days to achieve that). It doesn\u2019t seem to necessarily have to be something logically or thematically connected to the doom, making it a bit more uncanny and mystical; in basic terms it can\u2019t even be anything beyond merely inconvenient (I\u2019m guessing beyond time it might take to bring it about, even if within the realms of possibility), with more significant escape clauses requiring a decent number of threshold successes. The Charm also requires those motes to be committed, and the Lunar needs to reiterate the nature of the doom and the flaw resulting in it on a daily basis, lest they forget what lesson there may be. It\u2019s also helpfully noted that the nature of the achieved doom is not absolute; it can be adjusted a bit by the intervening circumstances (break all the spinning wheels said to be capable of pricking you and driving into deep sleep, and destroying all the wheels will probably just switch it to knitting needles or something, or even a fork). More than even that, the character and player who are facing the curse are afforded an opportunity to fight back in the moment it unfolds, with the right applications having a fighting chance to oppose or prevent it (also now considering how, unlike the Solar Charms, can only target individals). A once per story Charm that gets reset by accomplishing a legendary goal exploiting a character\u2019s flaw or helping them overcome their weakness.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the end of the Perception Charms. Not much else to say on the Mysticism ones besides effectively keeping spirit interactions and slaying interesting, or the Attribute as a whole besides it having been brought up ala Awareness into something whole character concepts could be built around.<br /> <br /> Mind, one thing I was wondering towards the end\u2026 ultimately, no return of Eagle-Fish Transition Prophecy. And really, good, we don\u2019t need it now anyway.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s late now, so despite being behind, I\u2019ll save my plans for the newest material until the morning. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T03:42:07-08:00","id":1294355,"title":"","content":"Oh, I forgot to ask before:<br /> <br /> Can somebody tell me the precise number of Dominions and Artifacts (and no other details)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T03:48:28-08:00","id":1294356,"title":"","content":"11 Artifacts (6 lvl 3, 3 lvl 4, 2 lvl 5) and 10 major Dominions, plus a short section with 8 lesser dominions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","name":"demonchilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T03:56:02-08:00","id":1294358,"title":"","content":"Huh, I didn't realise there were that many.<br /> (The 8 lesser ones are like 1-2 paragraphs each, Isator.)<br /> <br /> Also, the Dominions are arranged geographically, starting in the North and moving clockwise. So you could maybe do one direction at a time or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T04:12:22-08:00","id":1294362,"title":"","content":"I have received my information elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Seeing as they line up, I shall do each post consisting of one Dominion and one Artifact, counting all of the mini-writeups together.<br /> <br /> Should be able to effectively divide that between two days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T05:23:31-08:00","id":1294371,"title":"","content":"That's a nice way to break it up for yourself,it shouldn't be too mechanically overwhelming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T05:55:11-08:00","id":1294373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1294355#post1294355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and no other details?</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I'm sorry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T08:40:51-08:00","id":1294411,"title":"","content":"All right, finally a break from mechanics, and with some truly new setting information. Bunch of Dominions, ruled over by shapeshifters no less; getting\u2019 all Deep Space Nine up in here. Looking forward to this on several fronts.<br /> <br /> First off, love this running theme of depicting the Exalted in an abstracted manner with something inspired by Mesoamerican art.<br /> <br /> Okay, starts off with a little introduction to summarise the concept. The notion that a major thing driving support for the Lunars are people exploited by the satrapies for the sake of meeting their tribute obligations is something that I\u2019ve been expecting for a while, and putting that right up front helps to root the conflict in the excesses of the Realm (especially for any younger Lunars less invested in the legacy of the Usurpation or the Shogunate). Hmm, as an Irish person, those references to the kinds of people who might range out from their own lands for the sake of conquest; it\u2019s bad enough when that stuff is a matter of an official policy with some kind of supporting infrastructure, but when it\u2019s about letting losers and opportunists go out planting flags, I doubt it\u2019s never not been a human disaster, establishing a frontier culture of extreme hostility that future policy can only ever build upon and consolidate. The other stuff about the disease and the capital ventures, all makes sense as well, although it resonates less with me personally.<br /> <br /> That being said, I also think it\u2019s good how there are references to the picture being more complicated than universally generating opposition, or even fear; that there would be bonds created in such orbiting societies of greed and faith, even admiration. After all, the Dynasts are still Exalted, and between a potential human tendency to become invested in such impressive figures and their own powers to capitalise on that, it would make sense that they could become connected like that. And it creates groundwork for making the work of the Lunars more complicated, adding a bit more context to why they need to undertake it so gradually. It also creates some interesting scenarios for those social Attribute Charms to play off of.<br /> <br /> Now, while I have no objection to the corebook depiction of Dominions, I would say it paints them as a little bit uniform, and maybe not painted in the best light for people that have reservations about this depiction of the Silver Pact. More to the point, there was often preliminary writer statement about part of why they\u2019re able to fight the Realm so effectively is a diverse array of strategies, so it should really help people to point out several of the basic strategic formats that one might take. I\u2019ve got to admit, much as I like the asymmetrical war of attrition aspect of their war, I\u2019m most intrigued by that picture of some Dominions representing a military build-up from a distance to have armies in the future to engage in actual conquest against the Realm, perhaps partially because of the challenges such activity represents for Lunars.<br /> <br /> Last of all, a sidebar connecting the concept of Charm-created territories to the subject. Or\u2026 rather, summarise it a bit, with a point on how the dominion write-ups will reference territory qualities that they might include.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it\u2019s a good introduction. I think it effectively lays out the overall background and stakes of the conflict, and gives it a lot of moving parts to play off of, suggesting variety in stories and scenarios. Once we have The Realm, it should be complemented very nicely by the descriptions of actual satrapies (possibly even including some of their perspective on neighbouring Dominions).<br /> <br /> Now that\u2019s out of the way, let\u2019s look at the first new one: the Mountain of the Spider King. I\u2019d say that\u2019s starting off on a high note, since that guy was one of the more interesting new things in the core book to me; hopefully now more people will talk about it.<br /> <br /> Interesting to start off with a reference to an important nearby piece of infrastructure that the Lunar is effectively denying, this Black Shale Road. I also personally like the reference to it being aesthetically pleasing, just for the sense that gives of remains of the First Age. Something I liked from the corebook that I\u2019m glad to see repeated here is the idea that some Lunars exercise their power and harassment of the Realm and general offending institutions is by extracting taxes to profit off of their occupation of key arteries. I wonder what they might do with that silver; do they have contacts through which they can reinvest it back in their communities, or merely toss it away ala the alleged bandit in opposition to Alfred Pennyworth\u2019s service to either a colonial apparatus or military dictatorship? Eh, either way is probably good.<br /> <br /> I particularly like the description of the Mountain itself, owing to it challenging some of even my own picture of what a Dominion might be; not a land as most societies might inhabit it, not even people living in settlements on the surface of the mountain (although I imagine some of those are present, clustered around some tunnel entrances). It overall creates a good picture of a society that might be effectively maintained in the fallen Age in a manner unique to a Lunar, as well as a sense of what might draw new recruits (Lunar and mortal) to seek refuge there. It also casts a nice image of a stronghold that might stand in defiance of the Realm, an ominous geographic feature in which a Lunar\u2019s presence can be known, but does not present a ready avenue for legions or even Wyld Hunts to deal with (though I\u2019ve got to imagine that the occasional daring group tries conducting raids into the tunnels, never to be heard from again, possibly never even meeting the Spider King).<br /> <br /> So, a proper introduction to Aum-Ashatra, the Spider King. I like how, in contrast to a number of other really old Lunars and even the connotations of his own spirit shape (although I\u2019ve always been fond of spiders), he\u2019s presented as a more personable and somewhat easier going, even if the conflict has still affected him. I also enjoy the image of a monarch or similar figure publicly conducting themselves with dignified impassiveness while others speak for them; the description of employing favoured granddaughters for that purpose reminds me of a dynamic I enjoyed from the show Orphan Black, in which there was a gangster who didn\u2019t speak English, and had his niece as his interpreter (and was herself a bit nasty). It\u2019s nicely complemented by the idea that he\u2019s otherwise fairly playful.<br /> <br /> Heh, I\u2019d never considered before that a Lunar who primarily conducts themselves in the hybrid form could go unnoticed in their own society simply by going in their original human shape, especially if it might look far younger than one might expect of somebody who might be around a thousand years old. There\u2019s an interesting dynamic to it. And yeah, it\u2019s explicitly laid out that he keeps his Mountain open as a refuge for the desperate and the exiled; it makes me want to go back and read some things about a few Cossack groups again. The description of taking in war orphans in particular makes me imagine something like a one-shot game of playing those kids journeying in pursuit of rumours of a rogue divinity who\u2019ll take in people with nowhere else to go. And yeah, sounds like an all-around good situation, albeit not completely devoid of needing a bit of recompense; there is a war going on, after all. Speaking of, I meant to mention it before, I like the reference to how, for the most part, the tributes are scaled according to what a caravan can afford to pay.<br /> <br /> And a nice little description of his manner as a teacher and councillor within the Silver Pact. The idea that he specializes in espionage and intrigue does make me think that he actually would have contacts for the sake of spending his cash on supplies, although I have to imagine that a lot if also earmarked for bribes. And I think it\u2019s good to suggest the elder\u2019s mannerism and priorities when he meets up in council with other Northern Lunars; more than himself, I just like the reference to the idea that there might ever be any advocacies for minor or petty issues, that even with the conflict against the Realm they can sometimes get caught up in more personal vendettas.<br /> <br /> Huh, Aum-Ashatra is described as ancient, but his Dominion is surprisingly young. Mind, I guess that a lot of older Lunars might have gone through a few over their lives\u2026 and going by some of this description, it does seem that for all its security, even the Mountain might not be sustainable in the long run. The question of logistics has been on my mind through much of this reading, so I appreciate that the subject is actually addressed a bit here, and think it\u2019s interesting how this can create a bit of tension in their society; how the mandate of hospitality and taking in newcomers can grate a bit against lean seasons, and how that might be expressed by people. It actually puts me in mind of a different dimension to what could cause the Dominion to collapse; it\u2019s one thing to get to a point where the inhabitants can\u2019t be safely supplied and will either risk mass starvation or need to disperse, but what about cases in which large numbers of the inhabitants themselves ask Aum-Ashatra\u2019s leave to depart, and take their own chances? Hell, what if they start defying him en masse, either with things like larger and more frequent raids than he thinks is safe, or demanding that newcomers be turned away? He\u2019s described as punishing crimes harshly, but he doesn\u2019t seem to view the people as his subjects, so what might he do if there\u2019s some major act of defiance that clearly has popular support? I wonder if that\u2019s a possibility that ever haunts the Spider King\u2019s mind. Speaking of the punishments, I do like how, for all of his generosity and personable nature, he\u2019s still got a bit of Lunar edge to him in his responses to major crimes (although I have a sense that such a thing tends to more often fall upon newcomers who don\u2019t properly respect the rules).<br /> <br /> Heh, and a cute little sidebar describing the Dominion as dark, well-defended and labyrinthine.<br /> <br /> Yes, interesting to have an idea that a very old Exalt would have repeatedly had spouses and be surrounded by descendants; it\u2019s a notion I would have thought of as standard, and yet in the past has felt rather limited to me, with some vague lip service in Lands of Creation and old Lunars otherwise having almost felt asexual. I know some people would be of the opinion that \u201coutliving your spouse is cripplingly depressing, so most would avoid mortal romance or children\u201d, but, eh, dull. So anyway, Ashatra has often been attracted to the clever, determined and willful, fruitful enough to create four major families that hold sway in the Mountain\u2019s society. Interesting idea to have elected tribal leaders who serve as intermediaries between the community and the ancient demigod (although my overall impression is that, while venerable, the Spider King is more of a local celebrity than distant god or monster). As for the families themselves, I think the premise of them each being specialized towards social functions in a manner reminiscent of the new Scarlet Dynasty in particular, although something about the more specialized distinctions makes me think a bit about the tribes of Wakanda as depicted in the film; plus, there\u2019s something fun about the more financially powerful one being a tribe of mushroom farmers (I for one find the idea that anybody could get rich off of mushrooms hilarious, as though anybody would pay for them). And it creates a bit of structure for the process of refugees becoming part of their society, needing to actually be adopted into an existing family. And one final note that they don\u2019t take slaves, even to the point of allowing war captives who have nothing useful to offer and probably aren\u2019t too dangerous or offensive being allowed to flee (another thing that I could see possibly becoming a point of contention at some point in a chronicle). Mind, I will say that the basic social format of the Dominion being family of Aum-Ashatra makes the idea of a situation where they defy or reject him feel less suitable, although in a case where it did happen, it might create a stronger sense that he\u2019d sooner bend than abandon them. Besides, the adoption process might filter out spies and Realm sympathisers, but there could still be room for charismatic individuals who question a lot of their ways and bring a large section of the society around (although they\u2019d probably need the King\u2019s attention to be elsewhere); given my thought on more vigorous raiding, I\u2019m seeing the warrior Tehraihn family as forming a particular weak point.<br /> <br /> And a sidebar clarifying a bit on beastfolk, both for what the format and origins are, and the adjustments to relations with Lunars. Obviously the point on creating trials to bestow the mutations has already been provided in depth, but actual descent\u2026 I never had an issue with the zoophilic origins, and even like the mythic connotations, but must admit that the idea of it coming from just conceiving children while in the hybrid form removes a lot of the complications. I mean, the logistics of even having access to the Wyld, and the sense of needing to go out of your way to make children like that\u2026 it definitely works a lot less when they\u2019re no longer supposed to have fled to the Wyld and lived there for centuries. Plus, one benefit it might have is, in removing a sense that special Charms are needed to have such children without jumping through all the hoops, maybe people won\u2019t see pregnancy powers as a Lunar <u>Thing</u> anymore. Besides, it\u2019s not as if the matter of mating between human and animal in the Wyld isn\u2019t around anymore, it\u2019s right there in black and white.<br /> <br /> Okay, layout of the Mountain\u2026 every family has its own sections of tunnels, the actual settlements are located\u2026 actually, it does seem to read as though their actual living spaces are on the surface, even if they\u2019re high up and carved into the rock ala those Native American settlements named in a manner I cannot immediately recall. Oh I see, the tunnels are actually more of a fallback position. I like describing the manner in which they live and decorate their personal spaces, it recalls some of the best parts of Compass Autochthonia; need a lot of that in the books going forwards. Interesting that they sound like they\u2019ve got a thriving little market economy, and I particularly like the breakdown of types and sources of goods, and the whole thing makes me feel as though there might be other mountain dwelling tribes that might come for the trade or luxuries. Lower reaches filled with enough traps that even the boss can\u2019t remember all of them, probably filled with many Dragon Blooded skeletons, aaaand a sidebar about Ashatra having bred a variety of mildly giant spiders to serve as mousers.<br /> <br /> You know, I wonder if anybody who has anything to do with this write-up or the Lunar\u2019s original concept was drawing anything from the Vampire\u2019s Assistant book series, because the image of a society living inside a northern mountain with a spider association is really bringing to mind that depiction of vampires.<br /> <br /> Okay, a nice breakdown of the parameters for warring with the Realm around these parts. Also comes with a bit of history for how the Spider King came to take up residence, and\u2026 there seems to be an inconsistency in the timeline. Before it said he established the Dominion two hundred years ago, but now it\u2019s when the Realm was planning for the event of war with Bagrash Kol and designated the Black Shale Road as a major strategic artery? Or has Kol\u2019s reign been moved further along the timeline? Not sure what to make of that. Still, the history of their fight against Ashatra is more consistent: took time to trace him, have actually attempted siege in the past but never been able to overcome the defences or draw him out. Interesting that it\u2019s more than just a base for raids and a strong fortification, that the society actively tries to lure wayward people into the caves and tunnels to their doom, perhaps for the sake of maintaining the formidable reputation of the place (and illustrating the Realm\u2019s local impotence). Although perhaps I\u2019m misreading it, and the people taken while seeking refuge from rain are incidental casualties, and the luring fires are meant to draw in people for their own safety. Maybe sometimes a mix of both. Rounded out a bit with a nice description of the favoured war tactics of feint, traps and false weakness, with the Lunar occasionally taking the field personally to counteract enemy Exalted or ensure troops remember the power behind the Mountain.<br /> <br /> We get a breakdown of some local luminaries who I am very glad to find are not solely more Exalted: we\u2019ve got a fresh chieftain brought to authority by a good head for logistics (which in this environment is an obvious boon) but maybe a bit lacking in social intelligence and fully internalizing her patron-ancestor\u2019s values, a beastman warrior chief who earned renown for killing a Dragon Blood but was cost severe wounds in the process (bringing to mind some of Michael Goodwin\u2019s description of gunzosha warriors alongside the Exalted, which even I must admit was some compelling imagery) who seems to just be happy to be alive to train the next generation to take vengeance on his behalf, and a Lunar adherent who has become fairly prominent in the Mountain and tries to help out its people, but is also jealously protective of his esteem with the King in the face of Lunar students. Nice mix in there, good sense for some underlying disputes or agendas even while the society as a whole remains cohesive.<br /> <br /> Ah, and something I\u2019ve been waiting for for so long; detailing the setting through brief descriptions of a focused location\u2019s relations with neighbours, many of whom will nary be mentioned again. What have we got?<br /> <br /> Tantara, an old ornate coastal city sheltered in a bay not too far from the Mountain, long abandoned but starting to be revived by being adopted as an Imperial Naval base, particularly for the sake of safeguarding the sea routes that are increasingly necessary with the Spider\u2019s disruption of overland transport. Starting to suffer depression and piracy again as military forces are being drawn back to the Blessed Isle. This one\u2019s interesting on a few counts; it\u2019s a neighbour allied to the Realm, but despite its proximity to a vengeful Lunar (whose attacks might look a bit less shiny on an otherwise sympathetic local), all of its problems are actually local and even come more from the Realm not providing the support that they\u2019d like. Hell, it actually benefits from the manner in which the Lunar\u2019s activities drove traffic their way; it makes me think that the local princes would actually want to engage in machinations to help Ashatra, or at least keep him around, because the prospects for their growing prosperity are dependent on his presence. I like this as something feeling an impact in a manner more varied than making everything about the nearby Exalt, as it makes the setting feel more alive, and gives a picture of more complicated relationships between mortal and Chosen (particularly the idea that the satrap and local authorities are in a conflict not easily resolved by who can punch harder).<br /> <br /> Spray is a large but old cliffside fishing hamlet, part of a confederation united by common worship of local seabird gods; nice picture of a community background there, as well as focusing divinity on a subject where it might often be overlooked. Ah, further resolution to my question about trading matters of the Mountain, this place serving as an outlet for that in exchange for protection (although apparently some occasionally chance their arm at selling out or playing both sides, and need to be punished for it, in addition to ones who sometimes suffer the wrath of the Realm; I guess even a Lunar\u2019s protection can only go so far, without being sufficient to void the agreement). It\u2019s not heavily detailed, but it covers one of my queries about how the society could function, and gives an interesting snapshot of life caught in the middle of Exalted conflict. Plus an interesting sense of nuance; they remain under a protection that can\u2019t actually always save them, because what are they going to do, tell Ashatra they don\u2019t want him around anymore? Even if they had the nerve, what would that accomplish? I would suppose he sometimes compensates them for his failures, but that doesn\u2019t exactly bring back the burnt villages. This reminds me of why I so loved the first setting map I saw, dotted in shadowlands.<br /> <br /> And finally, a neighbouring mountain community called Skyborn, home to nomads who tame the really weird idea of large flying eels. Neat idea for a settlement consisting of descendants of a god, giving the God-Blooded a bit more to do than filling out some fighting ranks. Heh, I like the ruthlessness inherent to the idea that their isolation makes them vulnerable to economic exploitation from the actual Lunar, plus the idea that an offended god would turn to the Immaculate Order to seek redress for this. Turns a lot of assumptions about the power dynamics on their heads.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a good start this. I\u2019m actually relieved that it\u2019s interesting enough to have given me a lot to say without merely summarising what was already written (although I hope it\u2019s not too obtuse to somebody that doesn\u2019t have the manuscript).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, for the first of the Artifacts. In my usual manner, I won\u2019t break down the Evocations in as much detail as Exalted or Martial Arts Charms, although since I\u2019m only doing one at a time, I\u2019ll try to find a bit more to say than my usual summary. <br /> <br /> Oh good, starting out with a suit of armour, those are generally easier to process. I\u2019ll actually say, I\u2019m excited to see a variety of moonsilver Artifacts.<br /> <br /> Now, Eyebright: there are a lot of aspects to this backstory that I like, the aspect of a blind elderly person Exalting as a Lunar, a Celestial Exalt taking up service beneath a Dragon Blood and rejecting the prospect of succession on his passing. Ah, bringing back a reference to the Three Devil Princes, that\u2019s nice; oh for the days when Masters of Jade gave us our first tenuous hints of this rendition of Lunars.<br /> <br /> You know, I swear to God, somewhere around my reading of earlier previews, my head came back to the image of a suit of armour for a Lunar covered in substitute eyes. It was\u2026 when I was reading the Dexterity Charms, the picture of high speed fighting made me think of Kill la Kill, the first battle against the Blade Regalia Goku Uniform. I\u2019m quite delighted to see something like that presented here.<br /> <br /> Now, what can it do\u2026 basic function provides omnidirectional sight and removes the impediment to one\u2019s natural eyes, although obscuring the sapphires functioning as armour eyes can still mess it up. Has one of those unique categories for focusing action which I like, this time <i>Insight</i>, based on degree of understanding of an opponent in the form of knowing Intimacies that might be driving the fight (probably synergizes nicely with Perception Charms).<br /> <br /> And from there\u2026 the general picture is of knowing an enemy well enough for a preternatural awareness of their offensive manoeuvres. It\u2019s nice to see a power enhancing a Lunar Charm for once, with a nice method for using that observation to piggyback a read to get something to help Insight. Hmm, I think Essence 4 powers are unusual for level 3 Artifacts, but\u2026 consider that later. For now I like the capstone as a nice, vivid little method for keeping locked onto enemies no matter where they run or hide.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a nice Artifact to start on, although not the most evocative (not to its fault or anything). I\u2019ll admit that I most want to see some interesting weapon, and would be really happy with something whose powers express a really compelling thesis ala Pyre of Legions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T08:41:30-08:00","id":1294412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1294373#post1294373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I'm sorry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T09:44:21-08:00","id":1294431,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, when was Bagrash Kol's kingdom in 2nd ed?<br /> <br /> 200 years ago for its fall to the Realm seems reasonable for the Haslanti to be descendents, but I think it probably was further back in 2nd ed. Not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-06-2019, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T09:58:04-08:00","id":1294437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1294431#post1294431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, when was Bagrash Kol's kingdom in 2nd ed?<br /> <br /> 200 years ago for its fall to the Realm seems reasonable for the Haslanti to be descendents, but I think it probably was further back in 2nd ed. Not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bagrash K\u00f6l's empire fell close to 600 years before the current day, so this is a significant inconsistency in the text. We'll resolve it during post-KS development. Thanks to everyone who pointed it out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:01:18-08:00","id":1294439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1294431#post1294431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, when was Bagrash Kol's kingdom in 2nd ed?<br /> <br /> 200 years ago for its fall to the Realm seems reasonable for the Haslanti to be descendents, but I think it probably was further back in 2nd ed. Not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the prior Editions, Bagrash Kol rose somewhere about 150 years into the start of the Realm era, spent three decades building an empire fit to challenge the scope of the Scarlet Empress, and then it collapsed disastrously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T18:17:19-08:00","id":1294550,"title":"","content":"Okay, so having covered the general framework for what a Dominion write-up appears to be, I expect that I\u2019ll be a bit quicker on following ones, as I focus primarily on what is interesting about the specifics rather than general feelings on good priorities. With that, something called Skandhar-Bhal.<br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s curious that it would follow up with another Dominion focused on mountains in the North, but considering that I love icy mountain ranges and the image of travel around and life among them, I can\u2019t complain. In particular to that are the things like carvings and flags that might be intended to help out such journeys, or at least colour them, and the idea of some recurring strange iconography actually gives me a certain horror movie monster vibe. That\u2019s a setup that leaves me finding it leading towards it basically having finally given a nice Hidden Elf Village take on a Lunar domain a bit amusing to me.<br /> <br /> The mythology behind the existence of the valley is nice, enough that I don\u2019t particularly mind it attributing its unique and beneficial properties to something pre-existing rather than the efforts of whatever resident Lunar. I feel as though this kind of background, both in terms of a significant natural event and uncertain history behind it, is something whose absence felt very strong in much of the prior setting. And whatever the overall characteristics of the gods, I still have a soft spot for them occasionally being tasked with something more mystically significant and a bit abstract, and am glad to see it here. My initial take on the valley was that it was fairly small and its population concentrated, but at the point when it is describing resident monastic orders in the plural, I\u2019m curious about what the numbers within this place are supposed to be like. Wait\u2026 no, I hadn\u2019t been paying attention to the preceding paragraphs, basically everybody who lives there is monastic in some manner or another, that makes more sense. Actually, that\u2019s now putting me in mind of\u2026 well, there are a few fictional representations of a Shangri-la style place, but I\u2019m thinking particularly of one from the BPRD comics.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s nice to see a more spiritually focused Lunar. Let\u2019s see about this Vanamaithri Mirror-Soul\u2026 huh, even more spiritual than I had thought, if there\u2019s a whole element of having sought a relief from an innate drive to violence through it (also, person identifying with they/them pronouns). And here was me expecting a Lunar who had more co-opted the place or seized authority from its guardian spirits, not somebody who arrived as a student and rose in the resident esteem through a combination of their piety and actually being Chosen of Luna in a place defined by a moon relic. Heh, tortoise sensei; I wonder if they lean more Last Airbender or Kung Fu Panda. I take it this is one of those Dominions Eric talked about in which the Lunar\u2019s concern for the Realm has only become enflamed with the onset of the Time of Tumult.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, a nice looking breakdown of some of the resident monastic orders. I have an appreciation for the restraint employed here; we\u2019re shown enough to get on with, and have a sense of the place, but it doesn\u2019t go and name every resident god and describe their associated order. I also think it\u2019s interesting that there\u2019s room for specific dedication to other, lesser gods in that society. Of those, I like Jade Eagle\u2019s one just because I\u2019m fond on the whole to references to sky burial, and how the practices of Scarlet Doe\u2019s suggest a form of low level magic, or perhaps at least a unique characteristic Merit.<br /> <br /> Doing some more good with describing the layout and ornamentation of the place to help it feel more alive. I find the description of how the holy orders need to have lay people to cover a lot of infrastructural needs to be both logical and helpful for having a bit more to set games here. I like the descriptions of the ways in which even a relatively small and isolated community such as this can divide into cliques and possess meaningful conflict, even without much in the way of crime, endemic violence or a heavily stratified society. My comment about a Hidden Elf Village was a little bit ironic, but honestly, this kind of social texture is the kind of thing that I would have generally wanted in the past from descriptions of, say, actual Tolkien Elf societies. Or hidden villages.<br /> For all that there\u2019s a deeper and more genuine spirituality here, I also think it\u2019s good that there are still some political wrangling underlying their belief systems. Honestly, that just helps it to feel more real; sometimes designating something as spiritually malign actually <i>does</i> come from disputes of authority. It\u2019s also very interesting to see how that would create the circumstances for underground heresies even in a community this small, and there\u2019s something especially great in a tidy little reference to temple stores and exchange between households to give a sense of commercial activity at this level; there aren\u2019t shops and inns and the use of currency, there are the commons and families specialized to particular crafts, and it\u2019s all driven by social capital.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the picture being painted of this community is making me think of the potential for fascinating stories completely irrespective of the greater context of Exalted. It\u2019s like\u2026 imagine <br /> something between a soap opera and a prison drama, and add a sprinkle of period piece and supernatural elements to it, make sure to actually remove it from a lot of familiar modern conceits of commerce and government, and then run with it. I especially like the image of the one family who lives on the margins of the village, in the run-down and poorly furnished shack, because they\u2019ve been known or suspected to consort with darker powers; they don\u2019t really get invited to the festivals, and it\u2019s uncommon for anything to be provided for them, while the head of the family keeps scheming to employ local politics and clever little curses to ultimately bring more of the village into their social debt (or in fear of retribution), and soon <i>they\u2019ll</i> be the ones living in the big house in the square overlooking the nice statuary and getting the best of everything. Damn, I\u2019d watch the shit out of that show\u2026 book\u2026 whichever.<br /> <br /> Anyway; I\u2019ll admit, after the descriptions given in the first paragraph, I\u2019m a little bit uncertain about why there are longer ones for the orders back here. It\u2019s not a problem or anything, it doesn\u2019t mess up my point about not including more than are needed, I\u2019m just curious is all; I suppose I could read those as an introduction to the concept, before they are provided with a bit of focus. Besides, there\u2019s some good stuff in there. I like how the Order of the Moon-That-Fell regards Mirror Soul as a prophet of Luna not merely for being one of the Exalted, but because their own qualities align with what the Order sees and values in Luna, as well as the idea of martial arts training in this isolated context being useful primarily for its value in an avenue towards their process of self-actualisation, and in patrols through the more dangerous landscape to still help new people reach their home alive. What I liked about the Silent Acolytes in their intro isn\u2019t quite present in their description here (although it can be inferred a bit from the description of humanity trying to become divine), but I do think it\u2019s good to have a group with a stronger communal attitude. The School of the Pale Sky reiterates what I like with the sky burial, and the sense of communing with local ghosts helps root them as another facet of the overall social scene and local politics (especially the picture that sometimes a malevolent spectre needs to be rooted out and banished, to help keep life interesting). Annnd oh neat, one of these is actually one of the less significant traditions; the Silver Dragon Temple presents an interesting picture of how the Immaculate Philosophy might be appropriated to serve a different context, one that might not have anything to actually do with Dragon Blooded (it reminds me of some more off the wall interpretations of Christianity).<br /> <br /> Qualities of the valley as Vanamaithri\u2019s territory are what you would expect\u2026 Okay, I\u2019ll admit to having felt a certain mixed message about what the makeup of the society is, so I welcome a description of daily life to clarify some points. Ahhh right, the overall character of the place is monastic, but actually taking vows is often a thing reserved for later life, that straightens some things out. Plus maybe the general sense that the community of lay settlers might necessarily grow beyond what one might expect their orders to accommodate. They\u2019ve got a little mine sufficient to provide metal for the necessities, there\u2019s a nice shapshot of their overall diet\u2026 the description of their commerce, such that it is, is something I had already inferred, but it\u2019s good to lay it out directly like that. Sketching out the relationships between the monastic and lay people; I like the note on how temple authorities tend to be people who\u2019ve been in the orders their whole life, for the sense of how it has these powerful figures who might be a bit out of touch with the general population without disrupting the general dynamic. Ah, it took me a moment to understand that silver would be used for their prayer bells because of the whole Luna thing; not much else to say about their prayer activities, it\u2019s all fairly solid. It\u2019s also nice to have a sense of what a system of this size and isolation would do with its deviants, to round out the earlier image of how internal conflicts might arise.<br /> <br /> You know, apart from feeling a sense of callback to just about any Hidden Elf Village in fiction, something about the spirituality and location of this place felt naggingly familiar, but I just couldn\u2019t quite put my finger on it\u2026 but it\u2019s from the description of how they shun they outside world and discourage their own inhabitants from leaving with descriptions of the issues awaiting out there. It makes sense that new pilgrims might want to take up residence here, albeit tentatively; this land is peaceful, its inhabitants kind, but perhaps they do not belong. The fact that sometimes their own inhabitants do leave for the sake of preaching to the masses gives me two pictures; on one side, the bit of public ceremony in which everybody turns out to make a big deal about them taking on those burdens, warning them of the dangers of the big city, and to never forget who they are; on the other, that they might arrive in the cities to find a lot of other prophets preaching that they\u2019re emissaries from some hidden spiritual community, albeit ones who might be a bit more likely to be mistaken, deluded, or outright con artists.<br /> <br /> And finally, the prominent figures. Dancing Ceryneika sounds like an interesting type, on several fronts; that her divine blood extending her lifespan has allowed her to be somebody with youthful energy in being a kind of den mother for about a lifetime of the mortal inhabitants (I\u2019m picturing some people the same age as her, mildly frustrated or bemused by the memory of her as a bossy pre-teen, and still seeing so much of that in her as they start to weary), the substance of some of her reprimands around the community, that picture of something like people asking for treatment for something of which she disapproves getting passive-aggressively turned down. She seems like a very dynamic figure to have in an environment such as this, and a testament to the values of soft power.<br /> <br /> Ohh, a competing Exalt. You know, I was actually thinking that keeping Dragon Blooded out might be something of a priority, as their personalities and agendas might overturn the order of things, so it\u2019s interesting to see the writers ahead of me on this one. And yeah, just their bad luck (or perhaps something fitting to the nature of a place blessed by Luna) that the one Terrestrial they get is so at odds with the usual orthodoxy, despite being an Earth Aspect of all things. It\u2019s an interesting idea, that the pursuits and mannerisms of being Exalted might draw such respect, contrary to the usual strictures and standards, that could result in a severe schism if properly capitalised upon. Vanamaithri might be preparing to serenely lead her martial artists out for some kind of battle, but I wonder if Agallai Stone-Blessed, or anybody else, compromising the integrity of Skandhar-Bhal might just overcome her lessons and provoke her to Rage again (mind, the Great Curse might weight one of those options for her).<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s interesting to see that at least one of the gods, that sky burial Jade Eagle, assigned to watch over this sacred place chafes a bit at the duty, and would sooner by living a life that was less, well, spiritual. Like, I think this overall thing has been very good at depicting something genuinely religious surrounding some of the game\u2019s gods, but it\u2019s still fun to have a peek behind the curtain at at least one of them; they can provide a genuine inspiration and maybe even some truly meaningful guidance, but the fact that under it all they\u2019re not actually numinous and transcendental beings has some drawbacks. I like the depiction of the social impacts this has, such as being a good viewed a bit more uneasily by the worshippers and a temple to help out the stifled a bit by letting them serve as people who\u2019ll go looking for people not to help, but hinder. And to reinforce that element of Exalted being peers to gods, I think there\u2019s something very neat in depicting Jade Eagle as having a complex personal relationship with Vanamaithri and concerns therein, that just aren\u2019t mercenary; arising from a sincere concern tempered by a deep insight. Does inadvertently apply the wrong pronoun to Mirror Soul, though, probably a typo.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019d say that Skandthar-Bhal is the best example of its type of setting that I\u2019ve ever seen, for all of the reasons I elucidated on throughout. It falls very firmly into that category I\u2019ve discussed in the past; of not wanting to tell the book what I want, but for it to tell me what I want and then make a convincing argument for it. Lovely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm, getting a bit late\u2026 despite what I said before, I\u2019m kind of hoping the next Artifact actually does turn out to be reasonably straightforward. Let\u2019s see what Far-Ranging Eye can deliver.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what, are all of these Artifacts going to be eye-themed? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, forged by a usurped prince who had been a bit too na\u00efve and trusting of those around him, became Exalted while stranded in the wilderness and discovering a hitherto untapped reserve of strength, made with the intent of being a personal vow to be more vigilant in future. Again I like the reference to deferring temporal authority.<br /> <br /> I do like it when some Artifacts refer to a lineage of owners, just to fill out the history a bit more.<br /> <br /> No special preamble to the Evocations\u2026 ah, so it\u2019s going to be an Infinite Chakram focused on Investigation and, I\u2019m guessing, understanding motives? Assisted by striking with the weapon?<br /> Hmm, more like pursuit, focus and enhanced attacks against those the Lunar distrusts. I wonder if the weapon\u2019s power has been perverted a bit from vigilance to paranoia. Being able to negate most forms of supernatural disguise or concealment is neat though. And the capstone\u2026 lets you hit multiple people, including being able to ignore their being hidden.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, looks like I got my wish. No real complaints, it\u2019s still a solid Artifact, it just doesn\u2019t quite pop.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T23:01:17-08:00","id":1294616,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Far-Ranging Eye might have popped more if it was at the end of the Level 3s, rather than right next to the other eye-themed artefact.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think I've spoilt that the rest are not, in fact, eye-themed. Sorry Isator!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T23:14:43-08:00","id":1294619,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, one of the pieces of fiction was starring The Mirror-Soul.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2418474\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2418474</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:23:12-08:00","id":1294727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1294439#post1294439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the prior Editions, Bagrash Kol rose somewhere about 150 years into the start of the Realm era, spent three decades building an empire fit to challenge the scope of the Scarlet Empress, and then it collapsed disastrously.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I swear, you cast your empire, army, and all your loyal people into the sky <b>one</b> time, and that's all they ever remember about you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T09:58:22-08:00","id":1294780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1294727#post1294727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I swear, you cast your empire, army, and all your loyal people into the sky <b>one</b> time, and that's all they ever remember about you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going into the sky was Manosque Viridian's trick. Bagrash Kol went in rather the opposite direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:00:27-08:00","id":1294782,"title":"","content":"Okay, got another eight entries to do, let\u2019s see if I can manage before the next Charms preview comes out.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Touman Clans. Much as I appreciate something utilising the fallout of a conquest by the Realm, particularly for making use of the interesting backstory of the new entry that is Medo, I do have to mildly question why three of these are in the North. I mean, there are only seven full entries left, so at least one Direction is being left out a bit. That being said, I\u2019m interested in seeing what the exiled clans do that makes them a terror to both the cities and the pastoral nomads.<br /> <br /> Glad to see the example of a Lunar who is distinctly far travelled from native lands, just to emphasize that the activities entailed by the Silver Pact can entail a lot of roaming. It\u2019s also interesting to see something in terms of the Lunar kind of lining up with an exiled group, rather than them flocking into the Exalt\u2019s sphere of influence. Wasn\u2019t expecting them to re-conquer a new city-state, though. The actual layout of the city, and political structure of the clans, sound fairly standard. Ah, here\u2019s something to distinguish a bit, that this is a very recent development and that not all of the settlers are happy with the arrangement; I\u2019ll admit, the preceding elements seemed functional but a bit workmanlike, this bit not only sets it apart from the standard fantasy backstory, but gives the situation some teeth. It actually touches off of some notions I had in the previous entries, except here the tension to break apart is not being offset by a lengthy status quo and a more powerful Lunar (I\u2019m assuming).<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see about Wake\u2026 referred to as \u201cshe\u201d, was wondering considering the lack of pronoun earlier\u2026 another Full Moon\u2026 I find the notion of somebody who finds one of the standards of the Silver Pact, to have continuously used one\u2019s own people up in fighting the Realm, to have grown wearisome and is seeking activity with a different people in their own marginal situation as a bit of a vacation. Like that she\u2019s another one not automatically setting herself up as an authority, and find the description of how she interacts with the people endearing; she strikes me as having the status as a kind of honoured houseguest, who just happens to be capable of sticking around for two or three generations. Kind of makes me think of the relationship between Theoden and Aragorn, where the former is the one who looks elderly and has significant status and responsibilities, even though he remembers the latter riding off to war with his father while still a small child. Ah, it solidifies that impression by describing her as a kind of community hero-aunt, a term I find very evocative. I like the description of the relationship from the mortal leaders\u2019 end, where the sense of deference is not from exertions of power or even necessarily awe, but because of the common background generating endearment; I also especially like the reference to how there have been ones among them capitalising on that respect by manipulating her into support of endeavours favourable to them, it\u2019s a good dynamic to introduce to people\u2019s thinking about the setting. It\u2019s an interesting notion that, despite this more interactive attitude, the people have still sometimes tried adding her as an outright deity; given the rest, I like to imagine that some of Wake\u2019s methods for resisting that include acting in a distinctly un-deific manner.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the prior entry might have ultimately been a bit reserved in describing what Mirror Soul wanted to go back out and fight, but this one is setting up the compelling dynamic where the vacation has been good for reviving the Lunar\u2019s spirit for fighting in its own right, but she\u2019s left uncertain about whether or not to use the people she\u2019s currently embedded with for that. That she\u2019s only been presented with a short window to decide to try leading them out of the city and into attacks on the Northern satrapy adds a useful Z-axis to the existing dispute within their own culture, and I like how there are actual systemized elements to play some of these conflicts out in a way that favours the nobility; Wake surely has strong Intimacies that would compel her to leave the Touman out of the fight, and if the leadership appeals to this, while maybe also working on weakening whatever Ties or Principles would represent her desire to lead them into battle so they wouldn\u2019t be valid for Decision Points, then her own decision on the occasion might be a bit moot. She has, after all, spent decades specifically trying to avoid being a formal authority over them, there isn\u2019t a firm basis for her to simply command them into it; such a scenario would have to play out in interactions with their courts and councils, perhaps initially underestimating their desire to stay put, and that\u2019s something that could not end favourably for her.<br /> <br /> And what happens then? She abandons her principled stand against the Realm? Or perhaps she finally says goodbye to the Touman clans, and tries to set up a new dominion elsewhere, except that between her conflicted heart and maybe trying to make up for lost time and a sense that the window is closing her efforts in that respect are a bit inelegant. A bit too easy for a Wyld Hunt to take note of and hone in on. A bit too fixated on not letting that project be a complete wash to cut and run if surrounded. I wouldn\u2019t really call that Last Stand Mode myself, it\u2019s too much based in compromised priorities and a few mistakes.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the Touman would actually decide to go out and make war after all if they learned that their dear auntie was killed? Or perhaps a locked down underclass would explode in revolt first.<br /> Anyway, enough about her, what of the clan culture. Another nice picture of their style, and I particularly like the idea of dying cloth in richly vibrant colour; I won\u2019t get into a whole thing about misconceptions about Medieval peasantry, but I will say that it contrasts distinctly with even my own sense of aesthetics in the North. Also nice to see a reference to wagons, which often feel like an overlooked element in describing nomadic people; that they decorate them with historical scenes is a nice touch. The Meets sound very pleasant, and I think the wrestling matches make for a good adaptation of Medoan duelling culture to have fit it more into their current circumstances, where going so far as to kill one another wouldn\u2019t be practical.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d almost forgotten to consider that the city itself would have its own culture, not least because it\u2019s only been occupied a short time. Let\u2019s see\u2026 I like the sense of history (distinctly carrying the character of the Northern Direction) in the idea that Carnelian itself is also formed from the remains of a previously collapsed state. I find the picture of the culture here to be a very interesting way of giving the sense of something lavish while still present in its environment; the focus on fire in iconography, festivity around seasonal cycles, that their more decadent practice has some of the format of a steam room and that smoked and pickled stuff is a luxury food item. It\u2019s also neat to see a picture of the occupied city being one of adaptation through syncretism rather than distinct conflict. It has the values of being both fitting, to the North in general and the description of Carnelian\u2019s history in particular, and in making for an interesting social and aesthetic layout. And it\u2019s yet another nice depiction of soft power.<br /> <br /> Carrying the Medo practice of ancestor worship seems sensible; indeed, I\u2019m currently imagining ancestor worship in the context of the North, in a whole new light, whether for nomads or the settled\u2026 might come back to that. Here, though, I appreciate a bit of elaboration on the mechanics of how those cults might function, such as funereal practices intended to keep the ghosts close at hand and the principles that keep the dead from outnumbering the living. The description of the process by which the ghosts and Wake ousted the Carnelian gods and the people appropriated their temples as resting places for ancestral remains, is good for giving an example of how that function of the setting plays into matters of conquest, as well as being effectively evocative of similar practices in reality. The manner in which they would view Wake feels like it has some background and context in their general short-term syncretic practices with the gods of lands they\u2019re currently passing through; I think the description of some gods leaving their own homes and worshippers to follow nomads is intriguing and it makes me wonder what the attraction was, if they felt they were getting a deal or simply found the Touman more to their liking or something else. And I\u2019m amused by the image of the displaced gods who won\u2019t make new deals cursing their luck that the conquerors would be accompanied by a damn Lunar of all things.<br /> <br /> Nice to see the Immaculate Order involved in a situation, and the dynamic that the Wyld Hunt might establish with a Dominion that is less secure, and with a Lunar less powerful.<br /> Okay, a picture of how the cultures have started to merge\u2026 distinct differences in marriage practice seems like an effectively direct way to illustrate the difference, and there\u2019s another great depiction of soft power in the manner in which some of the Carnelian practice is winning out due to the manner in which it is enriching powerful Touman, at the expense of their clansfolk. It\u2019s interesting to see an overall economic transformation in the society, and who this is included in the basis of the divide, that it\u2019s not all about traditionalism versus something new. The fact that they\u2019ve been around long enough for children, particularly of mixed marriages, to not only grow up into it but be the first generation having to deal with it, to me that adds a strong sense of stakes to a coming conflict; I think it\u2019s particularly fun how there are some new people being brought up in a Carnelian fashion, but who are compelled with the stories of how their parents or grandparents may have lived. Indeed, some of the broad strokes of this scenario feel very resonant to me culturally. <br /> <br /> And I like how, sitting atop all of that, you\u2019ve got a voivode whose ambitions stand somewhat between and apart those divides, informed a bit by her legacy as the inheritor of their original monarch\u2019s bloodline and mantle. A kind of middle way between the desire for nomadic conflict and settled wealth, in service of trying to build a new empire. It has a note of how her perspective would be that such a project would benefit everybody, and yet I can readily see how both sides would find something objectionable in even the part that would nominally service them. I think it\u2019s fun how the description of Carnelia\u2019s surroundings creates a ready pool of candidates for conquest, and the whole scenario is a grand illustration of how monarchy is something distinct from being merely the most powerful aristocrat.<br /> <br /> Good little sidebar to lay out the specifics of the generational difference; whatever the outlook of the people born since the conquest, the city is the only home they\u2019ve ever been familiar with, the fact that their parents value things that simply can\u2019t be effectively passed on\u2026 I wonder if somebody with first-hand experience of being the children of immigrants had any influence on the writing of this chapter.<br /> <br /> Not much distinctly to say about the clan write-ups beyond the general observation of it being helpful for getting a picture of the political and cultural layout, and there\u2019s some fairly vivid personality here. I like how the Five Arrows have a distinct relationship with Wake, and think the premise of the Nevaz, people politically Touman, but not ethnically or particularly culturally, is interesting. Plus the manner in which their intermarriage is not focused on the wealthy and powerful; it is overall good to see a picture of how a conquering people would incorporate all class strata, and the process of conquest would not necessarily improve everybody\u2019s livelihood. <br /> <br /> Mind, the Minor Clans all bring at least one interesting thing with them; the Avakhorana, the sense that, in the past of the people, the ruler of another polity might have actually departed their seat to go along with their Touman spouse, the Iron Flame that there is actually an inroad for the Immaculate Order in this setup, which sounds like it would be intriguing using this Dominion as a target in a game focused on Terrestrials, and the Kuchinte both the very premise of a clan consisting entirely of the dead and the manner in which this is getting them involved in local shadow politics now that the people are settling down.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, the prominent figures\u2026 nice to get a bit more background on voivode Sangerel and the basis for her ambitions, that idea that city life is not merely to her profit but has allowed her to find her calling, plus that some of her basis for conquest isn\u2019t merely mercenary or driven by ancestral legacy. In embodying some of the conflicts driving the society, I particularly enjoy the notion of her being close friends with Wake while probably needing to be the strongest advocate against leaving the city, let alone going off to fight the Realm; very latter day Roman Republic, I think.<br /> <br /> I like the tragedy inherent to the idea of Ganzorig as a big advocate for returning to the nomadic life who is getting on in years and dreads succumbing to old age without achievement worthy of his people and ancestors, that\u2019s another very Theoden kind of thing. There\u2019s a good dynamic to the idea of one of the clan leaders being a ghost from before the conquest, this sense of an innate stasis undermining his own desire to try and reconcile the dividing people, plus the prospect for good conflict in the idea that the clan isn\u2019t wholly satisfied with such a leader reigning in perpetuity. Good to see native Carnelians represented here, and an underground high priest no less; the place feels more lively if the axes of conflict are more than just internal disputes of the Tournan, especially considering that such may prove to be a distraction from fomenting revolution beneath them. I particularly like the idea that the priest as revolutionary leader is starting to become more popular than the actual goddess he represents. Same goes with an outside of the Guild who is looking to profit off of local ambitions.<br /> <br /> So, finally the neighbours. For all that it\u2019s the target of Sangarel\u2019s expansionistic ambitions, it\u2019s nice to see that Thetra has a distinct character of its own, and is hardly a passive actor in this subject. Indeed, that they aren\u2019t merely sitting around waiting to be conquered but proactively have their own ambitions against Carnelian helps to make the subject seem even more precarious, and adds another edge to Wake\u2019s situation. Supposing she actually did convince a sizable number of Toumans to depart with her, or even had to settle for leaving in her own right, but then later learned that her adopted people were being menaced by a neighbour who had struck first while they were resolving their own disputes. How might that test her resolve? I thought of Toumans who might depart in vengeance at news of her death, but here\u2019s a scenario that could turn that dynamic on its head. Mind, the distraction of it might produce tragedy all round; I have the unhappy image of a Wake, tentatively establishing a new Dominion when she learns of Carnelia\u2019s danger and finally resolves to abandon her current situation, leaving her open to being accosted and cut down by a Wyld Hunt. The stationary Toumans get fully destroyed, never aware of the fact that Wake wanted to come back to them. How\u2019s that for a shaggy dog story?<br /> There are a couple of cities that are recovering from devastation inflicted by the clans, that\u2019s a nice bit of local tension. Aaaand a little summary of the lifestyle of those Touman who have more or less separated completely to try and maintain their nomadic lifestyle, as best they can with reduced numbers.<br /> <br /> There are a number of things for me to love here. Where the Mountain of the Spider King and a lot of the shahan-yas were polities defined by the presence of a Lunar, this is a good picture of an already complex, culturally rich situation in which a Lunar is inserted as just another feature (albeit a very prominent one). The Touman Clans feel well realised without just being another Mongol-expy, rich and coherent but not monolithic. There are a lot of threads to keep track of here, a lot of conflicts that could arise and play out in a number of ways on their own even before player Exalted crash into it. It\u2019s a lively scenario that I think could offer memorable games to people willing to engage with it on its own terms.<br /> <br /> I do have to say though, these new setting write-ups just aren\u2019t playing fair; I\u2019ll never again be content to do a location write-up as a White Elephant gift in the style of Scavenger Sons, and yet a format such as this would really stretch me to breaking point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, what is the next Artifact up? A dire chain, haven\u2019t seen one of those yet in the books, should be interesting for the novelty alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, the Hundred Rings of Hadam-Ul, there\u2019s quite a mouthful. Another nice Artifact made from a bound entity, always like me one of those. I like the mythology behind this one, not only for the weird nature of the creature itself that sets it apart from the usual monster of more obvious strength, and the premises behind how a given Lunar could best it; both in terms of the characteristic adaptive way of engaging with it, and the sense that having achieved a unique and renowned feat didn\u2019t need to entail being the best Exalt around. I also like the ambiguity inherent to the actual process of converting it into a dire chain, reinforcing the sense of mystery behind the First Age, and some texture to arts that may be lost or forgotten in the contemporary setting.<br /> Okay, you\u2019re off to a good start, give me some interesting powers beneath.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve a soft spot for moonsilver Artifacts that change size to conceal themselves, so using the mythos of the serpent as a basis for that is a decent start. Scathing Torment Coils stands out as an unusual process for dealing with a grappled enemy, possibly covering a form of attack that there might be limits against elsewhere. Let\u2019s see, the overall character seems to be a moonsilver chain that is adaptive and has an eagerness to ensnare enemies; modifying length to get them when they\u2019re further away (as well as for other utility purposes to which I do not object in an Artifact weapon), and modifying features to hold or punish them once they\u2019re caught up. Mind, the character of the weapon lending itself to something as simple as spinning a caught enemy around and flinging them away is also fun. Indeed, something like being able to stretch to the point of grappling enormous enemies (with other mechanical benefits to empower the effect)\u2026 that should feel like a much more basic application of a moonsilver chain, but the personality to it, the sense of vigour and enthusiasm from the origin story, that gives it a lot more bite.<br /> <br /> Ah, but a power by which the chain can actually come alive to an extent and gain a capacity to maintain a grapple all on its own, that feels like something that could only belong to a weapon of this backstory, and gives the prior powers a nice sense of building up to this kind of awakening.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is a much better weapon; in place of an ideology, it\u2019s got a nice bit of personality to it, which feels very much like it could serve as a kind of partner to a wielder. Nice job here, looking forward to more like it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T18:55:11-08:00","id":1294947,"title":"","content":"Next up is Iscomay, the Empire of the Bear, which is finally to be situated in the West\u2026ern part of the North. Seriously, did some Northern Lunar slip the writer(s) of this chapter a twenty? I\u2019m sure I\u2019ll enjoy it, but in the interests of comprehensive analysis, I do have to be a bit critical of it being weighted like this.<br /> Anyway, it\u2019s looking like one of those stay put and build a powerful nation style of Dominions; seems like it\u2019s being set up as facing an issue of long-term sustainability with limited resources.<br /> Wait, it\u2019s located near the Fang Lakes? Those are in the Northeast. Sounds like somebody made a little error again. That can be corrected of course, just noting it. Otherwise, decent little summary of the environment and agricultural output. If I\u2019m reading this right, the geomancy that allowed the place to be so accommodating despite its geographic location was undertaken by mortals, which I have a couple of thoughts about that I\u2019ll reserve until I get more information. I do like the setup in which the cities are of a more timber construction, and it\u2019s got my attention with that line about how a lot of artistic and scholarly citizens are in the capital without a choice.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I\u2019ve never considered before that you might get a lot of ruling families throughout Creation establishing legitimacy through claiming descent from Shogunate Exalted; it does establish an amusing dynamic in such places where a dynasty might maintain itself with the promise that one of the Chosen might appear among them some day. I wonder if its presence here in a group that is actually descended from the blessed children of a Lunar (one shaman named True Voice) is a matter of a mistake on their part, or a cover story for their intermittent supernatural powers. The history and process of their expansionism seems fairly standard, although their plenty compared to neighbouring scarcity gives it a certain distinct quality with their food-based hydraulic despotism, or something along those lines. The establishment of control over provinces looks fairly ruthless. I do like the idea of demesnes to cap as a motive for expansion, but considering what their geomancy already did for the Oma Valley I wonder what the value of more of them is supposed to be; can the ones closer to home run out? Does it continuously make their own climate and output even more luxurious? I wonder if it\u2019s not a bit of an advanced technology for the later Age of Sorrows\u2026<br /> <br /> Maintains a large army of janissaries that is pushed to its limit keeping the overexploited provinces in check, and that the empire struggles to finance without making the problem with maintaining order worse. Another standard breakdown of the military organisation. Being raised to view the ruling dynasty as their authoritative family members is kind of interesting. And yeah, lays out some of the shortcomings of a slave army.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m gonna be honest, three sections in, and this place hasn\u2019t particularly grabbed me. It\u2019s not bad or anything, it just hasn\u2019t yet done anything that makes it stand out, and its sense of internal conflicts\u2026 they\u2019re not absent, but I don\u2019t quite feel invested in them. It\u2019s not exactly helping with my thinking that too many of these are in the same Direction.<br /> <br /> The religious traditions\u2026 I guess I\u2019m interested in the idea that the religion in its current form is comparatively new on the basis of having compiled and codified an earlier oral tradition; seems to be part of an ongoing trend of more consolidation of power into hierarchical institutions. With that in mind, I do like how the priests themselves are not formally ranked and organised, with standing and weight given to sacred interpretation being a matter of cultivated relationships, and I think it emphasizes them as the maintainers of a state religion for an increasingly centralised power for most of the trainee priests to come from wealthy or powerful families. Okay, finally picking up colour here with what the main nature of its religious text is, a system of codes governing the manner in which it\u2019s permissible for people to seek the intercession of spirits, and that anybody can do the praying but they need their khojas to tell them when the rules allow it. Kind of asking Rabbit Krustofski if it\u2019s right to by a Chrysler kind of thing. That and how their text covers a number of other topics, and being the basis of law imposed upon provinces, extends the authority of the khojas, so there\u2019s a bit more implication and drive to the expansionism.<br /> <br /> I think the description of their architecture and ornamentation at least gives their cities a lot of visual flair; I can readily picture these places with their large buildings and all of the sculptures and stelae around, and I think they\u2019d stand out a lot on those practices. And I do find some strong character in the descriptions of their fashions, both the idea of emphasizing their comfort with lighter fabrics than typical in this Direction, and their expansionism with incorporating heavy furs suggestive of the growing frontier. I think the references to incorporation of bears throughout has been just understated enough, while the ubiquity of it does give me a sense of what might distinguish an Animal Avatar as a patron deity for an urban culture, to what it would be for nomads or what might be found with alternative gods.<br /> <br /> Okay, been this far into the description of this Lunar Dominion before getting very much about the Lunar Exalt, so let\u2019s see what this True Voice has on offer. Rrriiight okay, it\u2019s getting interesting here. So you\u2019ve got a Lunar who actually originated from the culture of the Dominion herself, and put together a whole regimen of insight into spirits and some other kinds of technical and organisation knowledge to help them advance. But it\u2019s also not really done out of a personal sense of loyalty or obligation, since she\u2019s more invested in the Silver Pact and wants to use her homeland as an eventual weapon against the Realm. Because of that, she leaves after not very long to take the fight more directly to them, leaving the growing empire as a reserve force, and has now come back to try and hatch her nest egg to turn on the vulnerable Realm, only to find that this Dominion has grown a bit beyond her capacity to control. The line about having put passages into the sacred text that conventional theological interpretation has appropriated to other purposes in the meantime is great.<br /> <br /> Yes, right, it\u2019s coming together now. Boring would not have been the right term for it, but in its own right it\u2019s\u2026 straightforwardly a polity that came upon an unusual degree of power, that has become a basis for dominating its neighbours. About what you\u2019d expect of such a scenario far away from the Realm. The dynamic of it having been set in motion by a Lunar who is coming to collect, but it evolved in her absence into something of its own, it\u2019s very, how do I put it\u2026 specifically in terms of a story related to Lunars, I think it\u2019s a good strong idea for the format and challenges of a Dominion, particularly one intended to flourish at that distance. And it\u2019s probably an unprecedented scenario, because there hasn\u2019t exactly been another opportunity in which somebody might call a reserve force in to attack a vulnerable Realm.<br /> <br /> Right, so with that in mind, I can make my way through the rest of the features of this thing, in terms either or what True Voice has to navigate to try and redirect it, or just how it functions for its own games set in that theatre.<br /> <br /> High Sila sounds nice and lively, and I think the picture of it as a site for theological debate sounds like a particularly interesting feature. In the end, I guess the point on how not all visiting foreigners are there* by choice refers to the premise of how, having their lands conquered, they would end up drifting towards the new capital. I think it makes the place particularly inviting as a setting for play to have that element of being so cosmopolitan making it a hotbed for intrigue and revolutionary movement, and that among the subjects of concern for the congregating khojas is the manner in which such a consolidation threatens orthodoxy.<br /> <br /> Former capital Karaqa sounds intriguing with its kind of iconoclastic and debauched refuge status; if they can get in before any scheduled clearance of squatters and resettlement according to official policy, I imagine that a group of players could have a wild time set there. And I like Burdock as an example of the consequences of the empire\u2019s ruthlessness that might just come back to bite them; considering how much of its power is predicated on the food surplus, I imagine a particular dramatic irony to vengeful ghosts who might come bearing weapons of famine. All they need is the right champion to lead them.<br /> <br /> Port cities such as Spur are always useful for their own kind of cosmopolitan character, both in travellers and hard goods. I often enjoy the image of rebels in the setting adopting outside patrons, so I\u2019m glad for this idea of an ousted Raksha tyrant who finds themselves an object of some kind of reverence again when the new boss is perceived to be even worse. And Storm\u2019s Breech sounds good for some frontier survival stories and working class unrest, and in the spirit of unlikely benefactors, I like the idea there of a Guild factor trying to convince the workers to help subvert control of the mines in exchange for better working conditions.<br /> <br /> Karaqa\u2019s qualities as True Voice\u2019s territory gives me a sense of it being a good reason you don\u2019t abandon one for centuries (plus, a quality such as crime-ridden is just going to make that state self-perpetuating), and I can\u2019t help feel that her decision to try claiming the new capital rather than attempt to clean up the old one and leverage it against the centre is the wrong choice.<br /> <br /> Right, there was a mention of the child emperor, named here as Ajurai Siladar II, before, and as I suspected it would seem his status is on account of having inherited a good strain of Moon-Touched power; I\u2019d present that as some obscure law saying that somebody who inherits such is immediately given the throne. Not much to say about him otherwise, his status as being the focus for lots of other people\u2019s influence and agendas is another fairly boilerplate element. His religious tutor Habja is in a similar boat, although I like the idea that she\u2019s at the centre of tensions surrounding her agenda of trying to encourage a crackdown on heterodoxy, with opposition being partially on the grounds of it being something that just makes their new provinces harder to hold. Isipho Spear-Grace and Qismai are just okay as additional features of the palace intrigues. Might have been interesting to have a figure unrelated to the capital.<br /> <br /> And for the neighbours\u2026 I like the premise of one of them being a successful rebel state that is dealing with the attempt to reconstruct and constantly worried that they\u2019re going to be reconquered, and think it\u2019s a distinct dynamic for there to be debate in Inscomay on whether to bother, since doing so would really only be for show as Sulat isn\u2019t really worth much anymore. Similarly the idea that the relatively young empire has taken a few too many liberties with some of the neighbouring nomads, whom they might end up driving into alliance with the liberated province.<br /> <br /> Dazul having a trapped demon as their ruler, with the aristocracy consisting of exorcists to both speak to it and keep it locked up, is delightfully weird. I think that\u2019s nicely balanced by the more mundane concern of a major trade neighbour\u2019s expansion having devalued their exports. Aaaand I like that them being shifted more to the east means they\u2019re on the border of the giant weird forest, just for the geographic distinction (I find the idea that their folklore refers to scary bear-killing witches cute).<br /> <br /> <br /> All right so overall, Iscomay\u2026 it holds together, and it\u2019s got a decent amount going on in and around it. It just shines a bit less to me in comparison to preceding write-ups. I do sincerely hope that somebody else with different tastes and priorities gets more out of it than I did (which, to be clear, is not nothing, it\u2019s just less; it\u2019s like the second Artifact to me).<br /> <br /> *Up to 100,000 words of review.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of Artifacts, next we have\u2026 Nightbane, a powerbow. That should be nice.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, that\u2019s a fairly dark backstory for it, with Luna in the plague victim shape and all of the murder and making the bow from somebody\u2019s spin extracted and cleaned by partially eating a guy\u2019s corpse. I\u2019m looking forwards to seeing its balance of curative and corrupting powers. Given the impact of the Great Contagion on even Lunars, reiterated by things like Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s trauma and the Lunar third generation, I\u2019m glad to see it play into the backstory of an Artifact being lost to Lunars who keep trying to find it again. Particularly for the ironic element of it having been a healing Artifact that was likely mostly powerless against it.<br /> <br /> I wonder if you\u2019d have to be doing anything with Nightbane to get those rerolls for diagnosis rolls and medicinal rolls. Like, carry it like a staff or something, or just enough to have it strung over your back. Probably doesn\u2019t matter. What about the more important powers\u2026 heh, the whole time I\u2019m reading Argent Panacea Arrow, I kept thinking about shooting the contagion out of somebody being a gambit would entail needing to get into a fight before curing somebody, and then it notes that doing it outside of combat doesn\u2019t require rolling Initiative and I think \u201cof course the gambit stuff is to give it a utility for curing people when poison or disease are being wielded as weapons against you\u201d.<br /> <br /> Ah, makes sense that the concept would extend as far as being able to mess up creatures of darkness and fae, gives it a bit more to do in a fight. Actually\u2026 okay I get it, the whole thesis of the Artifact is about being curative, and it takes that to extremes in attacking people; creatures of darkness, individuals who, in being contrary to the wielder\u2019s Principles, are viewed as metaphorical blights on the world, rolling in some of the murderous origins. It\u2019s a solid premise so far, but it would really hook me if it did any particularly interesting things with it.<br /> <br /> Okay, being able to remove a certain class of Intimacy immediately and fully is a good start. Given the mechanics for succeeding with it, I\u2019d almost wonder if it\u2019s a bit too powerful for an Essence 2 power; I would suppose that would be kind of all right as something with a very narrow scope and only available from possession of the one Artifact, but it does mildly concern me with the precedent it sets. I do appreciate that the Resonant power for dealing with mental illness also can\u2019t remove it completely.<br /> <br /> Hmm, keeps going with a power to remove curses and shaping effects\u2026 and finally a power by which a character can impose curses of their own against the kinds of people that some prior Evocations can injure, to permanently trap them in animal shapes. As an end point, I like how it ties in a more directly Lunar theme for the moonsilver weapon, as well as how it ties into their own power to impose transformations by potentially lowering the threshold for damage required to do that. It\u2019s kind of\u2026 cruel, in a manner suggestive of a predatory quality even in a moonsilver item made for a more benign purpose.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ultimately, I find Nightbane to work effectively as a weapon that has a consistent line through its attacks, and is kind of weird. I\u2019m getting a running sense that powerbows might be weapons for shooting things in a more abstract manner, and maybe some other utility tool stuff. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T23:20:16-08:00","id":1294981,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I pointed out the north-west/north-east references, Eric said the north-west is a typo.<br /> <br /> Back to the Toumans; one thing I liked about this chapter (of a number; it's my favourite fluff chapter) is that it presents a number of different models of &quot;barbarians&quot; that were common in real life, but previously not mentioned much in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Skhandar-Bal and Iscomay are &quot;barbarians&quot; purely in the sense that the Realm has labelled them as such. One is a monastic community, the other a feudal empire built on a central fertile farming area. The Mountain of the Spider King is a raiding culture based in an area that isn't comfortable, but provides safety.<br /> And then you have the Toumans, who are nomadic refugees pushed out of their homeland who've gone looking for another place to conquer. Like the goths and vandals.<br /> <br /> It also has a variety of models of Lunar interaction with their societies.<br /> <br /> You also make a good point about how dynamic it is. I didn't find the Toumans the most original, because it felt a bit like a Northern Chiaroscuro. But the conquest is more recent, giving more sources of stories. And just generally, it has lots of good detail.<br /> <br /> On Iscomay;<br /> I've often used dynasties (small d) that trace themselves to the Shogunate. It just makes sense to me. I've even had one with mortals and elemental-bloods claiming to be Dragonblood (the players liked the pelagthrope who called himself King Aquos Danaadsson and went on about how he was a water aspect, hence the gills) and desperately looking for real DBs to marry in.<br /> But I've never had Moon-Children claiming it. It made me wonder if a Lunar might hear about the magical bloodline of Kings who rule Iscomay and how they're descended from the Shogunate, and decide that this evil Realm-esque example of an Empire must be destroyed and its Dragonblood rulers toppled.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I'm planning to run a Lunars game a bit north of Iscomay, at the top of that bay, and I wanted some kind of empire of city-folk to the south to battle or intrigue against the PCs rugged and free barbarians. But not the Realm (our antagonists in my friend's game).<br /> So it works out pretty well for me.<br /> I also like how their warmer lands make them rich and attractive, despite being so far north.<br /> Might have to kill off True Voice though.<br /> And I'm sure the PCs can have fun pretending to be bears and trying to manipulate Iscomay via omens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-08-2019, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T00:01:27-08:00","id":1294985,"title":"","content":"On the weight of northern satrapies: it might be because the far north was previously less developed than other areas. The North-East, home of Iscomay, had nothing at all, whereas the South-East has Prasad, Ysyr, Volivat, Palanquin, etc.<br /> <br /> My view of the White Sea coast has changed from a desolate icy wilderness to one inhabited by a whole bunch of coastal trading cities and fishing towns.<br /> <br /> Or, maybe it's just coincidence. Probably depends on what ideas the writers had. Certainly the South seems to lose out a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T00:19:05-08:00","id":1294987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1294985#post1294985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly the South seems to lose out a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sssssssshhhhhhhhhhh<span style=\"font-size:8px\">uuuut it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T00:21:46-08:00","id":1294988,"title":"","content":"All right, it is way too late, and I have had some disruptions, but I still want to knock out one more Dominion before tomorrow. Finishing is going to have to overlap with starting the next (final?) Charms preview.<br /> <br /> I am hoping that the Nameless Lair of Ma-Ha-Suchi demands less of me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, first off, I think it\u2019s a good counterweight to all of Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s fresher, more melodramatic qualities to still have a bit of hostility inherent to where he makes his home, although that is effectively tempered a bit by reinforcing the notion that he is not merely open to negotiation, but notably inclined to and skilled at it. I never had an issue before with Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s Caste (that ire was reserved for Red Jaws), but I appreciate it being a bit more overt rather than needing to infer the details of it. And while my notion that his placement was meant to serve as a blockade between the Threshold and the Southeast isn\u2019t exactly rocket science, I do enjoy seeing it laid it clearly here.<br /> <br /> That Changing Moon quality to him is also effectively reinforced with the description of how he ingratiated himself to the now named locals, the Chante-Sa. I think it would be easy to fall into a trap of using his situation to avoid really giving him much in the way of an achievement, so I\u2019m glad that it establishes his acceptance in terms of performing a great fight of combat and negotiation in making good with the local goddesses by eliminating troublesome monsters. I don\u2019t want to read too much into the running element of established Lunars being ascribed familial roles, but it\u2019s a picture of authority, divinity and even celebrity that I find endearing, so I\u2019m happy to see it repeated here.<br /> <br /> Also, I have a certain soft-spot for the scenario of people shunning a character who is probably kind of okay because of a monstrous appearance (it\u2019s the basis of one of my favourite Xenoblade 2 characters), so I like that being folded into Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s backstory here. That and him not being a big asshole about it.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there\u2019s a little description of the Three Mothers. I think it\u2019s a good call to not make them super long; I might even say that more cases could do with just describing a purview and iconography. Considering the environment, I think my greatest fondness is for the Lavish Mother, both because the apparent colour scheme makes her sound very distinct looking, and because how it folds together what bright colours tend to signify in a jungle.<br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s interesting for the Chante-Sa culture to make unity to the point of being effective for the Lunar\u2019s purposes an ongoing and slightly fraught goal, and I\u2019m intrigued to learn more about what it means for each tribe to be dedicated to one of the goddesses. Sorry, bands. It\u2019s an interesting governing setup they\u2019ve got there; a matriarch appointed by divinity, but who delegates a lot of governing authority to chosen intermediaries and whose spiritual authority is not absolute. It sounds like a system developed on a lot of complex precedent and compromise, and I find it very believable; more than a lot of depictions of simpler systems, really. In the spirit of wanting there to often be depictions of mortal princes and chieftains that the Exalted need to treat with rather than simply dominate, I\u2019m happy to see the idea that Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s authority is considered no greater than that of the band leaders.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a word for the kind of limited agriculture that the Chante-Sa engage in, but it currently escapes me\u2026 ah, I\u2019ll probably find it again, since this write-up is really making me want to read things about the peoples of the Amazon rainforest again. I\u2019ve got to say, between the change of Direction, the relations with the local Lunar, and their own layout of spiritual background and challenging environment, reading this write-up is really reinvigorating my interest.<br /> <br /> I like the sound of the religious practices, with the reference to communal prayer putting me in mind of lavish ceremonies. And it\u2019s nice to see a description of ceremonial cannibalism that doesn\u2019t demonise the process or its practitioners, and gets the subject closer to its more common practice.<br /> <br /> For the descriptions of the individual bands, the Gap gets off to a good start. Their aesthetic, particularly the skulls on which they encourage the growth of phosphorescent fungi, sounds like it makes for some very vivid scenes, and I\u2019m glad that they\u2019re described as living in ornately carved towns, just because it makes for a more accurately diverse picture of the kinds of people that are probably the inspiration here, of their lifestyles and processes. Like their goddess, the land of the Chuwe sounds like it has some very compelling colour schemes. The notion that the East has flora of unique properties has often felt like an underutilised idea to me, so I\u2019m happy to see it prominent in this band\u2019s purview, as well as how that ties into them having the greater economic savvy; the picture of them selling goods and services to merchant outposts is cheerfully bringing me back to Masters of Jade. And for the Mahni, first off I like how they incorporate menstruation imagery into their mythology, and from there the idea that clay-work and river running leaves them as the most widely travelled and richest band. I just get something out of the image of them crafting ornate pottery in large quantities, and then having things to put it in. I really need to get pottery into my head more, considering it anthropological and archaeological significance.<br /> <br /> Ohhh, I like the Blood Seasons, for a few reasons. First is that it\u2019s an intriguing way for Ma-Ha-Suchi to establish a system of resolution to allow the people to maintain a kind of unity while retaining their separate identities. The fact that one of the suggested tasks to determine authority being playing a trick on Ma-Ha-Suchi suggests to me that he has a certain willingness to be a bit open to mild indignities for the sake of keeping the system running, himself integrated in it, and maintain an endeared status. Mind, I will say that although I wouldn\u2019t want to think of the system as being rigged, it strikes me as possible that he might occasionally confer with the Three Mothers to suggest tasks that might be favoured in one band\u2019s favour, and perhaps sometimes send his adherents out to very lightly and subtly interfere, in cases where he thinks the good of the Chante-sa requires the season to be devoted to a particular course; he might not be dominating them, but he\u2019s still Exalted, and there are methods for him to exert power through that. That said, I ultimately like the picture of a month of competition ending in a season of communal dedication to some particular specialty; it gives me a picture of each band having members who\u2019ll go among collected groups to use their expertise in leading them collectively through the season\u2019s efforts. I also like the connotations of the beastfolk only getting to lead when the Chante-sa collectively fail in their tasks, rather than getting to compete directly.<br /> <br /> Okay, that gets the jungle and the people out of the way, now on to the Nameless Lair itself. The backstory of being some minor fortress whose name is forgotten is certainly more fitting to his current ethos, but I also think some nice holdovers like that are given some interesting expression in the idea that Ma-Ha-Suchi has repurposed a lot of the place to be more accommodating, even comfortable. I\u2019ve always liked to see him as being somewhat analogous to the Beast of the French fairy tale, and I\u2019m happy that a bit of that comes through in the idea that his personal quarters are very dark and private. I also enjoy the sentimentality underlying him maintaining a catacomb for prominent descendants and fallen students.<br /> <br /> Considering my thoughts about the description of his initial approach, I\u2019m glad that being considered a holy figure hasn\u2019t completely divested the Chante-sa of wariness concerning him, just recontextualised it a bit. The way it describes him as not resenting the petitions of the bands, that they\u2019ll only make at direst need, gives me the compelling image of him being fairly genial when holding audience with petitioners who\u2019ll still shake a bit, won\u2019t meet him in the eye, and hear even the mildest pronouncements in his bleating voice as carrying an edge of threat. I mean, that\u2019s what I\u2019d impose on it, I\u2019m sure the basic concept is that he doesn\u2019t mind when the people need his aid or intervention on something. Considering the difficulty of approaching, I wonder what kinds of people even would intrude upon him, but I suppose that even discounting Wyld Hunts, there might occasionally be people who seek an audience that don\u2019t care to seek Chuwe guides are wait on his permission, and are strong enough to be capable of making it through the jungle and be a bit beyond the perimeter guards. I\u2019m imagining something like the occasional merchant prince who might come with a well-armed expeditionary force to impress themselves upon making a deal for easier passage to the Dreaming Sea, or perhaps even the occasional outcaste or Exigent who has some words to exchange.<br /> <br /> Yes, with the references to beastfolk before, I admit that I briefly forgot about the capacity to transform existing people. I like the way that the whole thing is framed around and incorporated into the existing mythology, and the spiritual nature of a present religious feature, that\u2019s all really cool. Plus not restricting itself to what might be some of our pre-conceived gender roles by ascribing Ma-Ha-Suchi the role of doula in the process. I\u2019m glad that the resulting beastfolk are now divided into separate castes of wolf and goat (I know it was kind of the point, but I always found that whole thing of wolf-goat folk who kept feeling an urge to eat each other was going a bit too far), as well as how both of them have big communal roles; just get a kick out of the wolffolk\u2019s purpose including additional hunting to help the people through lean times. And it\u2019s good to give a shout-out to the admiral qualities of the goat. I get a real kick out of the basis for the premise that a lot of outsiders encounter inhabitants of the area in terms leading to an assumption that they\u2019re all beastfolk.<br /> <br /> Aw damn, we\u2019re almost at the end? I kind of want it to keep on going. Oh well. So I Mahiya and Red Cat both individually, and as a partnership; her as somebody in this context who has big mercantile ambitions out of a love for luxury (plus the idea of somebody having divine favour due to a good eye for flower offerings), him as somebody who cut his teeth from experience garnered in Guild caravans (I can just imagine him being perceived as some mysterious stoic tribal warrior type), and the sense of partnership from complementary interests.<br /> <br /> Hmm, the Inan of the River Band is a man? I could have sworn I read before that they were invariably women\u2026 well for now, I like how Aan Jander represents a bit of a fly in the ointment in the current peace arrangements of the Chante-Sa, leading to both some inter-band tensions and slight conspiracy within his own ranks (which I adore taking the form of wanting to petition the goddess to appoint a new leader, rather than murder him). I\u2019m also glad of the diversification inherent to the idea of a tribal warrior leader being somebody physically infirm but a good tactical planner.<br /> <br /> Not so much to say about Gap leader Greenheart. Her premise, a thaumaturge encouraging her people to raid more to acquire more luxuries for their home, is all right and all, and does have an interesting connotation of their more isolated quality leading to trying to diversify their practices, causing tension as that steps on another band\u2019s caste role\u2026 huh, I guess I did have something to say about her.<br /> <br /> For the beastfolk, I like the sense that goatman shaman Uakka\u2019s authority within the dominion actually allows him to rank higher than some of Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s students, as a sense of the basis for him calling upon their greater strength in dealing with some more dangerous spirits. At the very least, I would imagine that any who might disrespect the shaman in the course of doing so might receive harsh words from the boss; besides, I\u2019m sure even he can still teach them a thing or two. And in the spirit of tensions in the homeland, I think there\u2019s something interesting in accusing a beastfolk of retaining original kin loyalty.<br /> <br /> (It is just now occurring to me to see all of these systems and relationships in terms of this originally being Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s retirement plan)<br /> <br /> And last of them is the wolfwoman general Six Day Storm. This one I actually do have the least to say about, beyond wondering if her polyandry is a practice unique to her within this society.<br /> <br /> Little sidebar on the beastfolk traits\u2026 I kind of feel as though the goatfolk get the slightly better deal, but perhaps I\u2019m not giving due consideration to the benefits of Enhanced Scent and a two-dot hide.<br /> <br /> Now to finish it off with the neighbours who are surely the subjects of these raids and trade expeditions\u2026 huh, had not considered how the remaining separations between the bands would lead to both relations with the same group, as they do with the woodworking Vuloth; they trade carvings for petal-leather with the Flower Band, but are often subject to River Band raiding. I hadn\u2019t considered that any of the Chante-Sa would intermarry with outsiders, but I suppose such groups would sometimes have to, and particularly the most external ones. Hell, considering some things I\u2019ve read about African tribal trading practices\u2026 I\u2019ve got to say, after having read everything about their layout, something about the idea of Immaculate missionaries coming to the Vuloth to offer assistance against Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s supposed raiders really stings; somewhere between the manner in which they would reduce the River Band to nothing more than pawns of a Lunar, the misplaced blame for independently undertaken activities\u2026 but the worst is the fact that they have friendly relations with the Flower Band. I keep picturing some canny monk trying to keep the Vuloth onboard by excusing the Flower Band from blame for Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s actions, real or imagined, and shrugging off any of their own protestations with condescension; some horrible scenario in which the petal traders are shoved to the side while their own spiritual kindred and their Undying Uncle are dragged into battle with a group to whom they have blood ties being galvanized by emissaries of the Realm.<br /> <br /> Hmm, nice for the jungle to have some overgrown, haunted ruins. Annnd a nice fortified trading outpost; the main thing I\u2019m getting from that is the idea that it could make for a really neat staging ground for a chronicle, a gathering spot for adventurers and mercenaries and criminals and canny merchants, and all of the associated services, standing on a frontier with raiders from a Lunar dominion on one side and traffic flowing in and out of the opulent Southeast on another. I think I\u2019m actually salivating a little bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Nameless Lair has done more than just a really good job of updating the features to a new milieu. The society it\u2019s developed feels very rich and compelling, drawing a lot that is impressive and worthwhile from more accurate anthropology rather than just resorting to cheap stereotypes. It very nicely complements the dynamic shown in Ma-Ha-Suchi as shahan-ya; that side felt strong for its own internal dynamic of a dysfunctional family, and having these people and situations as the neighbours really strengthens that; alternatively, a story focused more on the Chante-Sa side of things, with the inhabitants of the Nameless Lair as the occasional weirdos who venture out on some business from Undying Uncle. Overall, very enjoyable to read.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What Artifact is next on the docket\u2026 a set of moonsilver panpipes, what?! :0<br /> <br /> <br /> Made for an independent Lunar during the Shogunate, partially from the bones of a demon harpist\u2026 heh, I like the description of Nabira having succeeded in earning Alia\u2019s gratitude and admiration with her craft skill and the gift of the instrument, but such things still didn\u2019t bring her into the Silver Pact. I actually find something very moving in the image of her having actually saved her own precious home, and more besides, by playing the pipes; it\u2019s not a thing I can read without imagining the kind of music that would be played. Still, poor Allia; being a demigod hero keenly aware of how many died in spite of the ones successfully saved must be a unique kind of survivor\u2019s guilt. Even if one didn\u2019t play out a story of seeking her out and trying to offer some comfort, I think there\u2019s something sweet in the premise that the Silver Pact honours her by occasionally cycling her returned gift out to other independent Lunars.<br /> <br /> Right, it\u2019s an instrument, so of course it wouldn\u2019t have weapon stats\u2026 given its legend, seems very fitting that the fae are more susceptible to its performances. I\u2019m going to suppose that the capacity to wield Silver Voiced Nightingale through it to gravely hurt them is the addition of a later wielder.<br /> <br /> Oh dang, first Evocation to empower music convincing an attacker, especially a fae, not to hurt the player or something they care about\u2026 general things for music to calm hostility or non-intrusively ward off the Fair Folk and the Wyld\u2026 but still a bit of edge in it to empower the Lunar magic for leading allies into battle (although still acknowledging its core, with driving them not just with rage for what they fight, but love for what they protect).<br /> <br /> A bit of calling upon the natural world to fight off the Raksha, if need be\u2026 being able to use a power to affect things cared about besides a claimed territory sounds very strong, and I like how it can lead to a Lunar losing Limit. And all ending in a capacity to transform a fae being into a more genial form, while still retaining its characteristic magic, but lacking a will to harm people. I think there can be interesting scenarios arising even from those who change back after a year, and not altogether vengeful, although there\u2019s also something compelling about the idea that there are beings with Wyld powers out there who found they preferred being what the pipes turned them into, and wield their magic for more benign purposes.<br /> <br /> Can\u2019t find much else to say about these, other than being really delighted to find such a pleasant little surprise amongst the Artifacts. This one is a strong contender for this book\u2019s equivalent to Pyre of Legions.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Jeez, they\u2019re really knocking it out of the park) <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T00:37:19-08:00","id":1294989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1294981#post1294981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't find the Toumans the most original, because it felt a bit like a Northern Chiaroscuro.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe in the broadest strokes, but what matters to me is the details. When I look at the Delzhan, I'm not just seeing yet another culture of horse-riding pastoral nomads that took over a city and established an empire (of which, historically, there have been a <i>lot</i>, even if the Mongols end up overshadowing a lot of them due to just how successful they are), I'm seeing a bunch of the little things such as how they opportunistically seized Chiaroscuro at a time when all of the native factions who had been knocking the shite out of each other for two hundred years had been left completely exhausted, and the manner in which they shrewdly leveraged the city's strategic and economic value into beneficial relations with the Realm. I'm seeing the cultural practices, I'm seeing the manner of dress, I'm seeing the Dereth. The city itself has such grandeur and intrigue to it, and the Delzhan have spent close to six hundred years soaking that up.<br /> <br /> The Toumans feel sufficiently different, with their history of exile, with their ghosts, with their painted wagons and their Meets, and sure, yes, the fact that a Lunar has been living it up with them for a couple of decades. That's all stuff that would have made them interesting and unique to me even before they got to a city that they conquered in a very different way, are holding in a different way, and have very different relations with their neighbours. Not to mention the Lunar caught between conflicting loyalties.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T00:41:22-08:00","id":1294990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1294987#post1294987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sssssssshhhhhhhhhhh<span style=\"font-size:8px\">uuuut it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Spoilers?<br /> <br /> Look on the brightside, there is only 2 more previews to drop: Charms 4 (Sta, Str and Wits) &amp; QCs. Only a little more before it is done.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T08:20:06-08:00","id":1295049,"title":"","content":"Sorry about that, I didn't really think that through.<br /> <br /> I really liked how much they'd changed Ma-Ha-Suchi's role, so that he's part of an interesting culture, rather than simply its ruler. A visit to the area by PCs is no longer simply about meeting/fighting Ma-Ha-Suchi. And it was good the way the writers integrated the beastman-tests into the culture.<br /> <br /> There's another small point I liked from this, but I'll leave it for later.<br /> <br /> As to the pipes, I always like to see non-weapon artefacts, and these are well supported. I can definitely imagine the character who uses them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T10:11:12-08:00","id":1295074,"title":"","content":"I hadn\u2019t really twigged to the idea that Ma-ha-suchi might have arranged the Blood Moon so that he could rig things if he wanted to, but the fact that it becomes \u201cRaid the Realm\u201d season if everyone fails and that he could theoretically influence the difficulty of the assigned tasks, both directly and indirectly, does not seem unintentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T14:54:35-08:00","id":1295131,"title":"","content":"Fuck I\u2019m behind\u2026 yesterday was really weird, it messed me up quite a bit. Not sure what I\u2019ll do to line it up.<br /> <br /> Heh, might be no better mindset to approach Raksi\u2019s domain. I\u2019ve had some thoughts about her mannerism, I\u2019ll be interested to see if they line up with Mahalanka.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the introduction, apart from setting the scene with a picture of Sperimin\u2019s characteristic spires, a like the description of Mahalanka as being in the former city\u2019s shadow; even if it\u2019s metaphorical (although I\u2019m a bit excited at the prospect of a description that makes it feel more literal), it\u2019s a nice image for how the nature of the place has changed over the Ages. Grounded a bit in the sidebar adjusting the backstory a bit to include Ma-Ha-Suchi, and attribute the current state of the place to inter-Lunar conflict rather than extended decay or deliberate design.<br /> <br /> Mind, descriptions of Mahalanka as a living city have often felt a bit\u2026 scant to me, so I\u2019d like to see something more comprehensive\u2026 Okay, good start with a big clearing having been made in a manner that causes the spires to stand out, and they\u2019ve got some agriculture going. And yeah, the city sounds nice and functional; like, considering the approach before, for the core of it to be <i>just</i> a city is a significant step up in any case, that it\u2019s inhabited by people with families and businesses and manner of dress just living their lives, and touched up a bit with some good infrastructure and the odd sorcerous benefit. I like the idea that inhabitants of different classes have a consistent family structure, and the idea that permission to undergo the trials to become apefolk generally require the approval of a family\u2019s elder council. Plus the nod to the idea of a temple economy, operating at a larger scale than the Northern commune, but also existing alongside something more market-oriented.<br /> <br /> Makes sense for a sorceress queen to have a proper tower, and for somebody of Raksi\u2019s opulence to have two. I\u2019m getting a good sense of the decaying nature of the place, which is an image I always find compelling, and I like a lot of the particulars of the descriptions; Raksi\u2019s private laboratory, the extent of her court\u2019s luxuries (particularly the private museum), the idea that the guest quarters contain abandoned places that they might wander into to explore. There\u2019s a real tactile sense to this description, I can almost taste it. Oh, also that idea that the land leading up to the area has all been arranged in parks, that makes it sound like it would make for a very nice description of the journey up to it.<br /> <br /> Between this and the Tangle, I\u2019m getting an interesting sense that one of the most significant things about becoming beastfolk here is not in the actual benefits of the mutations themselves (although they\u2019re probably nothing to sniff at, even in an enhanced experience of day to day life), but that they denote people whose dedication led them to go through severe trials to prove themselves before the reigning Lunar, and being remade a bit in that Lunar\u2019s image is primarily a signifier of the duty and status conferred upon them for having done so. So it\u2019s an interesting way to present this idea of a caste system that privileges the beastfolk, particularly for its contrast on how prior Editions would often default to with them (especially around Lunars). On its own, that they form Raksi\u2019s bureaucracy continues to add to the sense of Mahalanka as a living city, and then you add their bestowed transformations and it creates a kind of Planet of the Apes vibe, a contrast between their appearance and intellectual sophistication.<br /> <br /> Heh, I like the way that Raksi\u2019s chief justice has the title of Dread Arbiter, and then the current office holder, Eskrin Fal, is somebody restrained and dignified and scholarly who finds serving under somebody as seemingly mercurial as the Queen of Fangs to be terribly frustrating. Jakun Qobal being somebody who takes the fact that they\u2019re living in the ruin of an actual First Age archive as a basis for trying to draw upon ancient mystical social sciences and apply their principles to profoundly transform life in the city is really neat, and sounds like it could be a good example even to Solars (and I like how the opposition from his fellows isn\u2019t just about being conservative, but argument that such lofty projects would disrupt cohesion enough to make them vulnerable to or inefficient against the Realm). And for the generalissimo Feroz Kutari to be scorned by his soldiers while he\u2019s more of a staff officer concerned with the efficiency of logistics then an inspiring commander well, gives me a picture that these warriors don\u2019t quite understand the Lunar that is reigning over them.<br /> <br /> Does say something about the attempt to keep a military readiness by having the army sectioned off in their own city quarter. Ooh, an industrial district, that should be nice. I always like some breakdowns of manufacturing processes, so I\u2019m happy that there\u2019s some insight into the city\u2019s factories and the goods they produce. It\u2019s also nice to see that the physical prowess of the apefolk finds an application in that sector as well; feels a bit reminiscent of The Last Airbender. Honestly, a lot of Mahalanka feels more Ba Sing Se to me than some Dragon Blooded strongholds have. And I\u2019m always a real sucker for people repurposing construction in a post-apocalyptic state.<br /> <br /> The Roaring Market sounds good, but the scope of its commerce, particularly the reference to imports from the Dreaming Sea and the activities of mercenaries, does put me in mind of a certain shift of priorities. In the earlier days of Lunar discussion, Mahalanka was generally referred to in terms of a ruin that needed to be kept in a state of poor development so that the Realm Legions would be hard pressed to come in and seize it, while it\u2019s treasures still served Raksi\u2019s purpose. Here we have a very elaborate city-state that has trade contacts with neighbours, and the idea seems to be that it thrives without concern for Realm attack from a combination of distance, a military supremacy (and accommodating environment) that could contest the Realm\u2019s finest, and the formidable prowess and reputation of its queen. I\u2019m ultimately okay with that, partially because I think a lot of other Dominions are effectively covering the other image and so this place needs something to set it apart a bit, it serves the adjustments to Raksi\u2019s character to allow more diverse engagement with her, and it is neat to get a snapshot of what an unmolested Lunar could achieve.<br /> <br /> Also like that image of spoils from the official war parties being liquidated with the aid of civilian contractor merchants.<br /> <br /> The Road of Idols is very neat, both as an image to illustrate the diverse extent of Raksi\u2019s domain and for the snapshot of some of the colourful local gods (I like the cat god who defends granaries particularly). It\u2019s also fun to use it as a contrast to the style of worship for Raksi herself, and that her own particularly brand of acting as an intermediary to the spirit world amounts to \u201cdon\u2019t make me come over there\u201d.<br /> <br /> Does a good job of making the townlands surrounding the city sound lively and diverse and interesting; I think even some of the better parts of the game, even a bit of Autochthonia, can leave such places feeling like window dressing, but here they effectively convey being vital parts of the community and areas with their own distinct characteristics. It\u2019s an especially good touch to give some of the local customs, triumphs and business sidelines (and I\u2019ve got to hand it to himself, the description of Daughter-of-Fox means that his point about using one of those Intelligence Charms to bind an entity to some menial task indefinitely was right on the money).<br /> <br /> Hmm, interesting that the Thousand Fangs Army consists of a mix of beastfolk, not just the ones empowered by Raksi and those descended from them. That the apefolk are empowered to punish others does speak to their caste stratification, and I find it rather fitting that they\u2019re still wary of doing so under Raksi\u2019s gaze. It\u2019s a good illustration of the extent of her power for her to have multiple testing grounds, and the descriptions of what some of their trials pertain not only makes for good reading of her freaky sorcerous authority, but give a nice sense of how they\u2019ll draw and empower people for a variety of social roles, and not merely the warriors. Also think it\u2019s neat that, in contrast to Ma-Ha-Suchi, the ascended apefolk are expected to maintain certain family ties that help prevent the elevated caste from becoming <i>too</i> separated. And yeah, fun bit of internal stratification based on whether one\u2019s state was something attained through trial or what one was born to, a kind of reversal of what is usual in depicting such internal divisions.<br /> <br /> Yes, extending my renewed picture of Mahalanka is upgrading the Total Control Zone from just neighbouring tribes aware of and fearful to Raksi to a sizable empire under her sway. It\u2019s interesting to picture how it seems to be held together less by uniform administration and more by religious awe to the sorcerer queen herself, and the manner in which they mythologize her (and how even their picture of her as a terror ascribes some socially reinforcing purpose to such). The description of how limited the process for petitioning Raksi for intercession is contrasts against my own assumption that such a thing could be accommodated regularly, but the picture of what it\u2019s like when she actually descends to work magic to resolve some of their problems about fits what I would imagine, especially the point about her not requiring any kind of repayment for doing so; in my mind, this would still be less about altruism and more about Raksi revelling in the assertion of her own power to solve problems and exert dominance, whether those be blessing or bane to those that experience it. The actual feats themselves sound sufficiently sorcerous.<br /> <br /> Good to be given a picture of some of the peoples within her Dominion\u2026 nice to see a callback to Dark Eyes\u2019 action and influence with the point of there being a triad of tribes in conflict of one of them that is heavily engaged in slavery; it occurs to me that a lack of administrative uniformity means that there isn\u2019t really much to stop Raksi\u2019s vassals from fighting amongst one another, so long as it doesn\u2019t escalate to a point that disrupts Mahalanka. The example of what happened to Jaciral of the Endless Branch sounds like another good instance of how Raksi\u2019s random acts of kindness can effect profound transformations. I like the way she keeps the nature of her powers close to her chest to enhance her mystique, and that even in the Total Control Zone, a grateful beneficiary encouraging worship of Raksi can cause tensions with local gods.<br /> <br /> Zanzannec has a lot of interesting connotations; being another elaborate city-state as something of a peer to Mahalanka, another instance of internal struggles being allowed to play out without central oversight, and the manner in which Raksi\u2019s self-sustaining sorceries might shape local politics. Like, the idea of one of her favoured apemen overthrowing the government, and then being under threat from one of the deposed royalty having overcome a trial to become transformed, that\u2019s really cool. Mind, I imagine his petition to Raksi would find that she favours a bit of a Michael Scott approach to management: \u201cI don\u2019t care, everybody reports to me; the rest, just sort out amongst yourselves\u201d.<br /> <br /> Heh, interesting to see how the Zone is not <i>quite</i> Totally Controlled, although if you have to flee to a Wyld Zone for refuge\u2026 The best thing I\u2019m getting from this is the manner in which the place\u2019s name informs the manner of it being part of the Wyld, how the mutations are diverse, but not merely random, they\u2019re constrained within a theme defined by the place that has become contaminated. It\u2019s a good example to draw from for any other Wyld Zones\u2026 also makes me really want to actually watch Annihilation properly.<br /> <br /> By the way, dummy that I am, it\u2019s taken me about this long to fully grok that Raksi\u2019s Dominion is vastly beyond the scope of any other thus far. Hence why, apart from her three chief ministers, it\u2019s just too big to do something like give examples of important personages. Really good for setting it apart.<br /> <br /> Okay, last of all are the important neighbours. Let\u2019s see, an appropriately ominous spirit court to give a bit of local colour in the form of the dangers of deep jungle, and emphasize the significance of Raksi\u2019s reign by her having brokered protection deals for caravans. And giving them a sense of contact with the neighbouring empire of Ixcoatli through a buffering tributary, who have differing opinions on the sensibility of pissing off a mighty Lunar empress.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mahalanka has advanced considerably, feeling like a more vibrant, living place in its own right rather than just the backdrop for Raksi\u2019s depravities. There\u2019s a whole surrounding world for any of her adherents to have activity in while being slightly apart from her (and indeed, lends a bit to the question of what might draw them in the first place), and I find it gives a lot to Raksi\u2019s credibility as one of the mightiest Exalted of the Second Age to have her maintaining this outside the reach of the Realm. I also think it does a good job of setting itself apart from other imperial structures, both in terms of a form of unification and administration fitting to the environment, and the manner in which being governed by a sorcerer would be experienced by its people. I think this should really do a lot to help the credibility of the Lunar Exalted in the Time of Tumult.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, nice to finally see some daiklaves. What might Phaessa and Deinon be capable of?<br /> <br /> <br /> Another nice example of mysticism underlying the creation of an Artifact, particularly entailed by something therapeutic in the face of losses to the Usurpation. It\u2019s interesting to see the idea of beings bound into daiklaves consensually, and the idea that a Lunar might involve themselves in what have to be the especially esoteric politics of spirit courts closest to Luna; it touches off of things that I really liked in Glories, some elements I enjoy in Werewolf: the Forsaken, and kind of makes me want them to hit the stretch goal that would expand upon that side of things. The short daiklaves themselves sound very good looking, with their crescent moon shape and being distinguished by the light they emit.<br /> <br /> It'll also be nice to see something utilising the imagery of lunar cycles with a bit more sophistication than the core book\u2019s Moonlit Huntress. Yes, has one of those great internal systems, this time based on the blades being <i>waxing</i> and <i>waning</i> (and the state between either). Hmm, an interplay between dazzling light and confounding shadow, I might be able to make use of some of this for my own purposes\u2026 Considering the conditions for shifting the cycle of the blades, I appreciate how resonant wielders get to start them off in a chosen state if they win Join Battle.<br /> <br /> Oh, the Evocations themselves will partially include ways to shift that state, okay. I think that would make the process more dynamic in an actual fight, and it feels like a good way to incentivize style a bit; also seems like a good way of shedding some pesky anima levels. Right, so the general theme seems to be one in which the waxing warrior pursues the foe relentlessly and with an ecstatic terrifying presence, and the waning fighter falls back and into shadow, so it\u2019s also a good complement to general Silver Pact emphasis on hit-and-run.<br /> <br /> Non-Charm bonuses to Resolve or Guile are nice, as is the idea of being able to use those powers repeatedly for waxing or waning, although the real thing that stands out for that power is the unique element of the persisting consciousness within the swords being capable of communicating with and offering advice to resonant wielders. It adds a very distinguishing element to them, particularly from the sense that they\u2019re more cooperative with the wielder, compared to the more servile Adorei and some more malefic Artifacts that might require some give and take. Oh, and it\u2019s also only Essence 1, so characters can get in on that fun from the get go, nice choice.<br /> <br /> Ohh, a really like how the blades provide a means of shooting off weird moon fire, with its own special properties, largely because I like Lunars to get a few energy attacks. Nothing much to say about the capstone other than liking how it expands upon that imagery, and the way that it gets awakened by earning the respect of the bound gods.<br /> <br /> Yes, a nice little set of swords. I do like when paired weapons are given distinct and complementary powers, and this one touches off of a few things I think would be really nice to equip Lunars with. The powers themselves aren\u2019t exactly moving, but I find some of the basis in their origin to be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T15:40:46-08:00","id":1295138,"title":"","content":"Just want to say that I've been reading all of these and enjoying them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T18:41:29-08:00","id":1295173,"title":"","content":"Oh God I should not have reread the description of Mahalanka in Compass East. That's gonna be a lubricant for my accelerating descent into madness...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T21:51:26-08:00","id":1295211,"title":"","content":"Okay\u2026 I\u2019m going to get out one more Dominion now, get a proper sleep, be up properly tomorrow, get the other three done early, and then blast through the Stamina Charms while my brother is playing Resident Evil 2. After a couple of revivals for old familiars, it will be nice to see something new (as far as I know) in the Eskari.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, we\u2019ve been shifted down to the South. A group of savannah inhabiting, camel-riding nomads, descended from a destroyed city that rebelled against the Realm. I wonder if these ones will actually stick with that, rather than being attached to a new city. A bit of description of the logistics of their travel between water sources, including the limits in size of groups that can effectively move like that. Their marriage and household structure\u2026 matrilineal and polyandrous, permissive of same-sex marriage (but make a big deal out of deciding who\u2019ll count as the matron). Ah, I was wondering how that might work in a nomadic society, but it makes sense for them if they have an attitude that women run the household (such as it is) and men tend to the animals, so it\u2019s useful to have two husbands who can alternate their time between home and herd. I think the idea that the family of a woman who dies without suitable daughter to take over becomes absorbed into the family of the mama\u2019s sister could make for some very distinct and possibly a bit fraught family situations (even if I would expect their families to not exactly be huge). I wonder what the attitude of men is to the children of the other co-husband.<br /> <br /> Wait a moment\u2026 I thought the Eskari sounded familiar before, but are they just straight up\u2026 no, that group from What Fire Has Wrought lived with a persistent fear of the Shogunate, not the Realm. This just happens to be a group in a <i>very</i> similar boat. Gonna put that to the side for the moment\u2026 I like how this is a nomadic society divided into multiple distinct groups, some of whom are semi-settled, it just helps to make them feel more real. Elevating the desire to rebuild their lost homeland into a holy mission, that\u2019s a very intense societal premise, I think. The description of their cuisine resolves a question I had had from reading a summary about traditional Mongolian food just a few days ago and wondering where they got the ingredients for the dumplings from, and I feel rather silly for not having considered that they might buy it from farming neighbours. It generally sounds like they eat fairly well, some nice rich dairy foods.<br /> <br /> I was wondering where the Lunar might show up, and the description of the storytelling including \u201cZamisha stories\u201d in which they\u2019re pursued by a punishing devil hints to me that this is going to be a very different kind of Dominion, albeit of a kind I\u2019ve speculated upon in the past; where the Lunar is less of a leader and more of a disaster that drives the nomad people to chase the Germanic tribes into Rome, so to speak. Also particularly like the idea that the more settled ones dedicate themselves to convert their oral histories into tapestries, just for the depth it gives to any of their decoration that might be seen around there.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I feel as though I\u2019m missing a little something in the description of their religion\u2026 but I think the basic distinction is supposed to be that these gods are closer than is usual for a society, whether nomad or settled. I guess the idea is meant to be that both having originated in a relatively recent exile created rites structured around that closeness of their gods being exiles as well, and newly adopted spirits are drawn into that right. I especially like the description of how some of those gods have changed in nature to fit their new situation, although some of the descriptions of their original natures sound very cool; I like the idea of a marketplace god having lots of hands in particular, and I guess a feline god patronising granaries is just a thing now (it\u2019s really clever, and it makes me wonder if any real society has ever drawn the connection).<br /> <br /> Okay, tell me more about this Smiling Zamisha and what she\u2019s doing to these unfortunate people.<br /> <br /> Oof, she\u2019s had a very rough time of it. Might just have had one of the worst early experiences of any Lunar who didn\u2019t come from the Shogunate. Can\u2019t exactly fault her for being hard-hearted verging on cruelty following all of that. Also makes the name ironic, and not in the fun way\u2026<br /> <br /> Right, so the purpose of her torments is in trying to harden the Eskari in a similar manner to herself, hoping to turn their pastoral lifestyle to raiding and their fear into a martial hatred that will have them turning back upon the Realm. It\u2019s a horrible sounding, if understandable, strategy, although I will note that the description suggests that she can wield her power to rely more upon rumour and innuendo that grows in the retelling, without needing to actually do half of the horrors attributed to her. As I thought, this method allows her to be more flexible in relating to this Dominion; she can pop in occasionally to keep her myth alive and continue refining and cultivating it to her purpose, and freely depart to engage in other business elsewhere. I imagine that such a thing can be fairly common as Dominions go (come to think of it, True Voice was rather similar).<br /> <br /> What can I say about the system of government\u2026 the gyula, the overall leader of the people, doesn\u2019t sound like a very powerful, which I think is good, I think it\u2019s worthwhile to have societies in which the\u2026 local equivalent to a head of state does not have extensive powers while functioning as normal, and not because there\u2019s a lot of resistance to their authority. Like, they\u2019re a widely diffuse people, of course they won\u2019t have a lot of power in a centralised leader. It mostly just reminds me of things I\u2019ve read about old Irish kings. But still not a merely ceremonial leader, since their attitude concerning the Realm (and perhaps other enemies) gives a unifying force something to do.<br /> <br /> But what\u2019s really interesting about the system are the husband-advisors, the kundu; utilising their polyamory as a basis for creating an intertwining network of familial connection and diplomatic communication, which might ultimately knit them together more closely than their decentralised structure might imply. I think navigating that system of overlapping marriages would make for some especially engaging and unique scenes for Socialize. I also like how the gyulas tending to favour kundus with priest, shaman and thaumaturge skills gives Zamisha a strong avenue to influence the society, as she can present herself in the manner of a divinity to them in particular, and they get to transmit their insights up and down the nominal chain of command. Plus the way that she can distribute her Moon Marks to sometimes influence the selection of the gyula, even contrary to traditional norms.<br /> <br /> Like the sidebar describing the evolution of the institution, both for giving a sense on how the Lunar\u2019s influence has shaped the society to fit her purposes (and might continue to do so in the future), as well as their internal trends. It\u2019s just good to have anything that keeps these societies from feeling too static across centuries.<br /> <br /> Good, lay out some of the influences in the clans\u2026 I think it\u2019s really fun to give the Dzhenifa clan a custom that traces back to association with the Varang states, but they would refuse to acknowledge such a kinship over hatred of the Varangians siding with the Realm. Still, I think it\u2019s a missed opportunity to not at least say what the omen behind matriarch Olanka\u2019s name might be; do like her more spiritually driven agenda, though. The tutelary god, Glass Razor, is just okay. While the Leila military raids and history of blood feud with the Realm sounds like a good form for some first contact with the Eskari to take. I like how those ones have an emphasis on youthful vigour and a devil-may care attitude, too many fantasy societies place too much emphasis on the older. I think that\u2019s embodied well in the idea that Gyula Zita is a younger woman than the norm, and considering Zamisha\u2019s usual relationship with the Eskari, find some fascinating implications to the idea of her having acted as a mentor to the warrior chieftain. That the Leila matriarch schemes to replace the current gyula with her own daughter calls some of the Harkonnen intrigues from Dune to my mind; I just love those dynastic schemes based on advancing the position of your heirs rather than yourself. Ohh, and First Flint is grand in being a Bloody Hand who has advanced in the world by having a higher position through the esteem of an associated tribe. I want more instances like that in the game.<br /> <br /> For the Razhiin, it would be good enough to have a clan that acknowledges and is tolerant of intermarriage with other societies, but I think that making it a practice intended to extend their own power by assimilating groups on the whole takes them a step beyond. It does an especially huge part to keep the Eskari from feeling homogenous with that idea that many of their own customs have changed as a result of that assimilation, even if the result is that they\u2019re derided as lacking the proper identity and pride from a lot of their fellows. With the gyulas having a larger number of husbands than the norm, I was wondering how they would relate to one another, so I\u2019m glad to see the idea that the Razhiin kundu is engaged in a relationship with one of his fellow husbands, suggesting the possibility that their poly marriages could become even more crossed over. I\u2019m amused by the irony of their own god having encouraged their intermarriage with other people, but being unhappy with the more diverse worship that brings with it.<br /> <br /> Just taking a peek ahead\u2026 normally I would object to detailing all seven clans, but in this case I\u2019m giving it a pass on two grounds. One is that, since the setup of the Eskari is that they have relatively little, it seems to me that such writing would be necessary to fill them out, and saves on elaboration on minute details. The other is that I\u2019m really liking the flexibility in these Dominion write-ups, how they\u2019re not strictly bound by a consistent template, both because it makes them more engaging to read when you\u2019re going through a lot of them, and because it emphasizes the diversity that they represent, both in their own right and how Lunars might interact with and utilize them.<br /> <br /> So, next ones, the Szonia, a more isolationist and puritanical group. Ohh, the idea that they\u2019ve ranged far enough away that their Realm enmity has become transferred to Prasad is very clever. And then it goes and turns some of the assumptions of that on its head with the idea that matriarch Idoska is engaged in peace negotiations with a Prasadi tributary because they\u2019ve come off a bit worse for wear in their conflict, helping to keep the clans from just being a stereotype, emphasizing that they can be adaptive and pragmatic in response to circumstances. Ah, I was wondering how their traditionalism would play off of Zamisha\u2019s influence, and think that some really good conflict could come from the fact that she\u2019s less of an apparent presence to them and they\u2019re not happy with how she\u2019s influencing the other six.<br /> <br /> I think there\u2019s something very fun in the idea that the Tezelyke preserve knowledge of a bunch of crafts and practices for the time in which they might reclaim a metropolitan homeland. I think the idea of maintaining rites for dead gods is an especially compelling picture of an exiled people, and sand paintings of the lost city feel like they would be a really great application for craft projects and something to make a big deal out of unveilings. Does logically sound like a group in which revanchism (i.e. revenge as an ideology) would surge up. Heh, I love the minute (but probably meaningfully felt) distinctions between traditionalists supporting a gyula trying to conquer a new Eskaridam, and revanchists pushing for reclamation of an old one. But\u2026 ohohoho, that\u2019s great, that\u2019s inspired, a young firebrand passing herself off as being driven by visions from the lost patron god of their city, who is in actual fact the Exigent of a self-sacrificed mirage god who empowered somebody for vengeance against the Realm for destroying their cult. That\u2019s a detail I tip my hat to. And oh dear, even their poor tutelary god believes that she\u2019s getting real visions, and keeps trying to find a trace of the dead city father. This could either be a basis for the clan\u2019s ascendancy or a recipe for absolute disaster, and I am <b>here</b> for it.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve got the Varoniikh, whose nomadism just consists of them moving back and forth between high- and lowland with the seasons, remain in fortified camps otherwise, and are close enough to the Varang for their to be consistent conflict between them. They maintain raiding distance to a major pass through the Summer Mountains and all. I think there\u2019s a good format for their internal tensions regarding the question of whether or not they\u2019re letting themselves become <i>too</i> aggressive against an enemy that outguns them (Zamisha\u2019s influence is probably not helping), and it feels like a clan that is going to need some major changes to survive in the long term. I like how the granary god Damet is adapted to this situation, particularly drawing wildcats in to assist in raids north.<br /> <br /> And finally, the Vevyehn, largely settled down in riverside villages and with a willingness to accommodate foreigners. Just for a brief aside, I\u2019ve not fully considered how some of the others might extend nomadism to temporary habitation in other people\u2019s towns, but that seems like it would fit for some of them (especially the Razhiin; it seems to me that a lot of those marriages would occur while living in a town, and when they leave their spouses go off with them, especially if children are involved). But yeah, the inverse of that is a group who are themselves setting up the towns in which others might start settling down. Let\u2019s see, they\u2019ve got a claim to strength and wealth with the benefit of iron deposits\u2026 yeah, considering the significance the people place in reclaiming Eskaridam, it makes sense to include one of them who\u2019ll say \u201clook guys, we found it, let\u2019s all just settle down here and build a new life\u201d. I\u2019m glad how the basis for rejecting that isn\u2019t purely from other clans having contrary ideas of what Eskaridam entails (although I do love the paradox inherent to the stance that recovering the homeland from which they were exiled into nomadism is incompatible with ceasing to be nomadic), but there are also practical concerns about the vulnerability of the new towns to other raiders, and competition from the Guild. The gyula might not be a ceremonial leader, but I find it fitting that the matriarch of the clan that has started settling into townships would be, even if she is presented as having brought the town governments around to the idea that they need to oppose the gyula\u2019s agenda as a threat to their own stability. Ahh, and of course the former marketplace god would be the patron of people that would take up this position.<br /> <br /> Okay, the neighbours. There\u2019s already so much to the Eskari, spread over multiple fronts, that it seems there\u2019s less need for a dedicated section here, so I think it\u2019s the best call to focus on two of their most iconic satellites. First is giving a name to the Varang state that betrayed them, Haqad, with their basis as a source of Eskari animosity solidified with the point that they were enriched by possessions of the razed city being handed over to them. That they\u2019re protected by sizable military resources really feels like something that would fill the exiled people with disgust at their comfort and wealth, and a sense of hateful impotence in the face of them. It really sounds like any Exalt or other power who could open the city to Eskari vengeance would effectively win the loyalty of the clans as a whole (if not all of the interest groups within them).<br /> <br /> The Kazhur have been mentioned a lot, especially as intermarrying the Razhiin (to the point of introducing a new major god to worship) and being subject to a lot of raids from the Szonia, so it\u2019s a good choice to elaborate on them a bit. I wouldn\u2019t have expected them to also be a raiding culture (the idea of raiding nomadic raiders makes sense, and is a thing I\u2019ve often read about, but doesn\u2019t quite feel intuitive to me, which feels like a very strange hang-up). Mind, considering how they have a custom of providing recompense when confronted by people that they have stolen from, it actually sounds a lot more like a kind of trading ritual that may have evolved out of a purer raiding practice or is an adaptation to their neighbours to match commercialism with shows of military strength. Either way, it\u2019s a very unique kind of practice, but one I could believe having ever existed in some form in reality, so I\u2019m glad that it\u2019s been included here.<br /> <br /> And finally, the Sands Where No Man Walks, a kind of haunted wasteland which feels very reminiscent to me personally of times when I imagined adapting the Gerudo from Legend of Zelda (as they were in Ocarina of Time, as I didn\u2019t yet have an inkling of their great portrayal in Breath of the Wild) to the setting. It\u2019s a more interesting sounding shadowland than the norm, with a very compelling icon in the form of that smoke tree and the idea of it unleashing all kind of elaborate horrors of the dead into the world. I particularly like the idea of a people responding to the threat of proximity to such a thing by meeting it head on; the funeral practices of sending in the remains of the dead to add the ghosts of their people to help combat the horrors would be grand enough, but the idea that the living would sometimes brave the wastes to save their own tormented ancestors is a really great image, really lends a lot of esteem to the people.<br /> <br /> I think nomadic cultures have often been underserved in Exalted, so it\u2019s wonderful to see one given such carefully designed detail here. I think the best part about the Eskari is their diversity; they still feel like a consistent people with a common background, while also feeling like a very real people from how they\u2019re covering lots of different angles and have many different ideas. I find their backstory with the Varang and the Realm to be compelling, and really enjoy them showing one of the darker sides to the Silver Pact and the concept of Lunar Dominions, even while those things don\u2019t completely overwhelm the portrayal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All right, up to the four-dot Artifacts, starting off with the slayer khatars given the not in the least bit ominous name of Ichneumon Blades.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeesh, these things were born from an ill-fated encounter with Balor himself. It would be bad enough for the weapons to have their presumed nature in their own right, but I love the sense of transgression inherent to the idea that they\u2019re successors to the spirit of a weapon held in a higher esteem; that\u2019s especially fun for transgression as a theme of Lunars and their material, here turned against the will and ideal of the Lunar who put them together trying to salvage something more noble. That they bear a resemblance to ovipositors is a good look for them, and it of course makes sense that there would be a lot of Lunars less reserved (to say the least) to harness their dreadful nature.<br /> <br /> Speciality for piercing attacks, annnd yes, right off the bat, the expected quality of them partially shattering to leave fragments that burrow within the bodies of enemies. The capacity to partially ignore Hardness sounds like a good way to start the battle out with this, and then capitalise on the results. Also like how those embedded splinters require surgical removal, rather than being sustained by Essence. And the Resonant effect seems to overall say that the wielder should use them for piercing without reservation.<br /> <br /> Wouldn\u2019t have expected a power for the splinters to give things like the position or intentions of the victim away. Ah jeez, I thought it was going to be focused on messing up the body, but the idea that those larval fragments can also assault the mind\u2026 and with a fairly diverse application of mental illnesses. The Icheneumon Blades don\u2019t seem to want their wielders to fight to the death, but to the pain; stab enough to leave lots of fragments, and then leave to let them work their horrific magic, that will also call the wielder back to see and further their handiwork. I\u2019ve been wanting a few dread weapons, and this one is living up to that beautifully.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s all just at Essence 1, it gets a lot more overt the next step up when the damn things start erupting as jagged masses that further maim and hook themselves in to become more difficult to extract. And then drag the body around as a meat puppet if it should die while fragments are embedded in it. Yes, I think I prefer this Artifact as a Lunar method for creating zombies than some of the Ink Monkeys Charms were. And the description of Ravening Swarm Consumption is genuinely uncomfortable to read, particularly imagining those erupted splinters scything through a person\u2019s flesh as they make their way to the vital organs. Yes, this Artifact is recalling the memory of having ticks embedded and removed, in all of the best ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the Ichneumon Blades get the level 4s off to a good start, conveying\u2026 not so much a fighting style as a process for assault and torment, feeling effectively cruel and grim. I think it has room for a bit of expansion seeing as it only goes to Essence 3, but I\u2019m not critical of that, and actually think there are some merits to an avenue for its greater powers to fall to the imagination of players; it certainly sets a good example for itself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:28:22-08:00","id":1295225,"title":"","content":"I don't have much to say about the Eskari, other than the concept of refugees adapting to desert life and debating whether or not to retake their homeland is a good one.<br /> <br /> But Mahalanka... it's great.<br /> <br /> I found 2nd ed Mahalanka pretty dull. It's Raksi, a library, and Raksi's goons. As much as you can have fun singing &quot;Oh, I'm the king of the swingers, oh, the Jungle VIP...&quot; etc, it's a sorceress and her ruined city... and that's it.<br /> One of my friends said he liked that, and so wasn't so keen on the new one, but as far as I'm concerned, a ruined jungle city with a mad Exalt in is a)something I could easily make myself, and b)not that different from Rathess.<br /> I also wasn't that enthused by Raksi in the Silver Pact chapter.<br /> <br /> But Mahalanka is great. It's a whole society of interesting stuff, and Raksi is simply the tyrant. Like Ma-Ha-Suchi, this is no longer &quot;the elder and their goons&quot;, it's &quot;a city with a bunch of interesting stuff, one of which is a Lunar elder.&quot;<br /> <br /> I liked:<br /> How it's a rich and powerful city, that looks completely different from a &quot;civilised&quot; city.<br /> The thought put into the economic effects of beastmen and sorcery.<br /> The various actors, and their varied views on Raksi<br /> The names. All the names are great.<br /> The adaptations of First Age ruins, for example turning a fallen tower into a horizontal apartment block.<br /> <br /> Mahalanka is actually an interesting place for PCs to interact with, rather than just the name of the place you go when you want to meet Raksi.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, you may remember when people were discussing the Ma-Ha-Suchi vs Raksi war, that I felt it was weird that Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi fought a war when their bases are 3500 miles away (further than the distance from London to Samarkand, and much of it jungle).<br /> <br /> But, as this chapter reveals, actually Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi both used to live in Mahalanka. It was only due to their feud that Ma-Ha-Suchi left, and travelled all the way to the other end of the Scavenger Lands to find himself a new base. Firstly, it makes more sense, and secondly, it gives you more of a sense of them being really close until they fell out, as they had been living together and working together in Mahalanka.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:55:25-08:00","id":1295231,"title":"","content":"I need a break.<br /> <br /> I need a break because I am straight up not sleeping, a scenario that was going before the book was around, but has become exacerbated by my endeavour.<br /> <br /> That and I want some time to let my computer rest, and for me to be away from it.<br /> <br /> I shall post nothing today. I shall set myself up to try and get a proper night's sleep. Maybe I'll finish reviewing before the Kickstarter ends, maybe I won't. For now, I need to try taking this in hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:59:47-08:00","id":1295236,"title":"","content":"You've been at it pretty intensely. Have a good rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T01:32:44-08:00","id":1295263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1295231#post1295231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need a break.<br /> <br /> I need a break because I am straight up not sleeping, a scenario that was going before the book was around, but has become exacerbated by my endeavour.<br /> <br /> That and I want some time to let my computer rest, and for me to be away from it.<br /> <br /> I shall post nothing today. I shall set myself up to try and get a proper night's sleep. Maybe I'll finish reviewing before the Kickstarter ends, maybe I won't. For now, I need to try taking this in hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more than than fair. Good night and sweet dreams, friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T03:30:23-08:00","id":1295272,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I made that observation because it was something like 8 in the morning. I'm not actually going to be sleeping for hours.<br /> <br /> Plus some computer stuff that will bum me out for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T07:10:26-08:00","id":1295305,"title":"","content":"Well that is less than ideal. Sorry for your suffering","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T05:17:18-07:00","id":1295538,"title":"","content":"Okay, finally up bright-eyed and bushy tailed and eager to try and push through a whole lot of this. The Bronze Tide is a more unusual name for a Dominion, so it has my immediate attention.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Heh, first impression I got from reading the introduction was that those bells being referred to with the city of Steep were made of bronze, and there was going to be something magical about them that would ward off the Wyld. But nah, this is introducing the Dominion by way of first bringing up a city that is under an apparently unstoppable assault, which is quite a tone to set. I think the detail here most intriguing for me to find a follow up on is\u2026 the polished armour being worn by the Bronze Tide raiders.<br /> <br /> Yes, as I suspected from the introduction being set at a coastal scene, this is a subject of the setting\u2019s far Southwest, another more newly developed part of the world. In particular the Cinder Isles, which puts it <i>very</i> far from the usual sphere of the Realm. The description of the Isles being home to scores of nations makes me want to look back at them on the map and get a sense of what those nations might entail, their possible scope and relations, but. The big thing I take from it, though, is the point of a force originating in its eastern quarter and moving west, which makes me wonder if the Bronze Tide is necessarily concerned with the Realm at all.<br /> <br /> Okay, it\u2019s setting the scene of the historical background to the Isles; kind of sounds like another instance of a place beyond the Realm\u2019s hegemony being subject to continuous tumults, albeit with seemingly more turnover and scattered diversity than what might be found by the Dreaming Sea. It feels like a very different environment, both in terms of climate and geography and the local power dynamics (kind of reminiscent of the Indian Ocean or South China Sea, things that the Western Archipelagos never quite covered) in which to set games, and even if it seems to be driving at the rise of the Bronze Tide putting a lot of these events in the past, it can give its own sense of background and legacy, a basis for old feuds and alliances and lost treasures that might be sought out and utilised in a Time of Tumult game.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s a lot to get from the picture of the region that the Dominion is crashing into (I\u2019m particularly liking the idea that a lot of the dominant coastal cities are being affected by migrations that the new growing power is pushing up towards them), but still need to get to the subject in focus\u2026 which still seems to be being held off for a bit, as it\u2019s also giving us a picture of what the mainland further south has been doing with greater proximity to the Wyld. I\u2019m not complaining, but this write-up is giving me the impression of something that would have been written very differently had the book order been something else, and the new Southwest had been introduced elsewhere, but that\u2019s just a stray observation. What matters to me here is that the question of people living <i>very</i> close to the edge of the world is something I think has never been given much attention before, seeming to be primarily conveyed and conceived on in terms of low population density, low infrastructure people in a hunter-gatherer lifestyle, relating to the Wyld largely in terms of being preyed upon, subjugated or using it in shamanistic rites. So it\u2019s interesting to get a more in-depth look presuming a greater variety of social formats, of what Southeast Asian maritime societies would be like if they were situated at the literal edge of the world from which strange beauties and horrors emerge.<br /> <br /> Oh, actually jumped the gun a bit; it\u2019s more like being referenced before getting to our subject, one Spear-Empress Bhadri, whom I\u2019m guessing to be the Lunar in this scenario (unless she\u2019s a raksha queen that the Dominion is going to be raised against). Was this character mentioned earlier in the book? There are some judgements I\u2019ll defer until I have more of the facts, but for the time being I think it\u2019s an effectively striking picture of people facing the threat of a major force from the Wyld, which feels distinct from other instances in this and other books of a regional status quo being overturned by more mundane conquerors. The descriptions of what slaves are used for and how the advance is being aided by strange vessels and crafts gives it that added texture of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Ah, okay, finally comes to the point; that the Bronze Tide is the poetic name for the manner in which the coastal states have managed to unify in the face of mass migrations and an oncoming Wyld assault and are being driven out for their own conquest of the Cinder Isles. As an aside, I\u2019ll note the concept of Yu-Shan ending up as a refuge for Terrestrial gods driven from their home sanctums, which isn\u2019t something I\u2019ve imagined before but now find to have strong possibilities in characterising the divine city.<br /> <br /> Okay, now the whole thing is coming together; Bhadri is a raksha empress of unusual power who is driving a new conquest in her quarter, and this Lukha Palash is a relatively new Lunar, Chosen as a result of his actions as a charismatic leader in this crisis, whose focus is on resistance to her rather than anything to do with the Realm, with the Bronze Tide being his per project to save the people from the Wyld. The relative shortness of his introductory section is giving me a sense of what sets this Dominion apart; one in which the Exalt is an active driving force, visible and commanding, while remaining only a singular element of a much bigger picture (emphasized by the fact that he can\u2019t govern alone and needs the assistance of all the newly united princes). That\u2019s good for two major reasons, both to provide a contrasting example to the likes of Mahalanka or Luthe where the openly commanding Lunar is somebody ancient and nigh unassailable, and it gives a nice example of how characters of the type that players could be running might conduct themselves in such a scenario.<br /> <br /> I would have liked a description of the culture focused on an element of disparate elements being pushed together for the first time, but the idea of a common standard owed to a shared history as provinces of a greater empire has its own charms (and conveniences). That one of the commonalities of fashion is widely wearing caps helps add to the sense of the area\u2019s distinctiveness, and I do like the details of local variations. Likewise, the idea that even utilitarian metalwork is embellished with culturally significant imagery furthers the area having a unique aesthetic, something that I think could have an advantage to future fiction or games in which one could establish the location just by describing elements of everyday life. There are some nicely thought out economic implications to the forced migration, such as the significance of being able to keep large herds of higher value animals growing as a status symbol, and I think it ends up having <i>enough</i> of a reference to the people still being highly fractitious, even in the face of their shared crisis and an Exalted leader, to give the sense that this is all still something very new and unstable. That further distinguishes it as a Dominion; none of the others have existed in this state of crisis, with the challenge of holding together a diverse coalition, and I think it hints a bit at some of the limits of the format; I can\u2019t shake the feeling that Lukha Palash is in for a bit of a tragedy (barring getting some extra muscle from some player characters wanting to go help out).<br /> Mind, even his success constitutes a major tragedy for some neighbouring peoples, but I suspect he cares less about them.<br /> <br /> All right, being given a breakdown of what the Bronze Tide is up to. So basically, their intention is to generate an atmosphere of terror, alternating between grand displays of martial fury as their ships approach island cities in the hopes of cowing them into surrender, and if made to fight destroying infrastructure that can\u2019t be taken with them (i.e. basically everything but ships) and slaughtering fighters and leaders, enslaving people with valuable skills, while forcing inhabitants to flee into neighbouring islands to keep building up their own legend, in the hopes of ultimately allowing them to conquer without the need to fight. It strikes me as a strategy that would make a lot of sense to the people involved, driven by their desperation and perhaps a need to keep a constant forward momentum lest their coalition fall apart, and is absolutely terrible in the long run, both for the enduring traumas it\u2019s likely to inflict and probably wasteful in a manner that presents even the conquerors with problems. And I like that, I like that sense of fallibility and people being driven by powerful emotions and immediate exigences, as well as a picture of growing crisis that really feels like it needs some interventions, or at least powerful added voices (one could always play other Exalted arising from within it).<br /> <br /> Ah, okay; where the culture section was giving some of the aesthetic background, the section titled Life Among the Tides is getting into the meat of tackling the subject of how all of these newly connected disparate peoples are struggling to function together. I think it does a very good job of presenting this not as an empire or even a confederation; it\u2019s an alliance of convenience created in the most thoroughly ad hoc circumstances, and there\u2019s not only been insufficient time to formalise a lot of the components through diplomacy, the manner in which they\u2019ve been pushed together likely precludes effectively doing so in the future. That Lukha Palash is trying to keep a sense of unity through moving between the numerous cultures and equally celebrating their customs, to generate a sense that none is supreme over the others so they can remain cooperative, that is a detail I really like as making his leadership feel not just very distinctly Lunar, but distinctly Changing Moon, and having seen the Charms for that Caste gives it a very firm sense of credibility. That\u2019s really good social and personal characterisation there. Finally I like the descriptions of how the people have prioritised adopting new religious practices, such as the offerings of sweet and pure liquids in hopes of making good impressions on new gods they have to ingratiate themselves to, as well as how those gods themselves are exploiting the opportunities (the idea of gods appropriating cults by taking on the names of deposed, or possibly killed, gods is absolutely wonderful and a manner for bringing in that element of real life cult ascendancy that I\u2019ve never considered before but is just so elegant; hell, it makes me picture an Exalt doing the same, something that feels particularly fitting for Lunars who can outright make themselves resemble, in form and in power, the gods that they slay). Combine it all with references to how they\u2019re handling cultural elements acquired from subjugated isle peoples, and I think this section validates the entirety of the Bronze Tide on its own.<br /> <br /> Okay, I was ready to think the sidebar describing a few of the prominent component cultures of the Tide was a good idea just to give a deeper sense of some of the parts, but giving them all some particular hangup with their new situation was really inspired. The particulars of each are pretty great and all; you\u2019ve got the Lunar\u2019s native culture, whose princes are annoyed at a sense that their authority has been usurped by an Exalt, a group of people that are being forced into an entirely unfamiliar geographic environment and have had their traditional pantheon completely destroyed, forcing them to try and rebuild a new one from scratch, a society that is not only resistant to external authority on principle but has an old grudge against beastfolk and feels an anxiety about being governed by a Lunar, and the historical rivals to Lukha\u2019s people, who for all of his attempts at maintaining togetherness and a sense of egality, are still bothered that a member of that culture had to be the one Chosen. All of that is delightful stuff for how, with limited wordcount, it gets across the sense of these being real people, that the plights of the parts are distinct from the plight of the whole and may prove to be major dealbreakers, and that even somebody Exalted can have a lot of hassle to deal with from various people\u2019s cultural baggage. If there\u2019s any mercy in Heaven, somewhere out there Lukha will have an Eclipse Caste mate waiting for him, with whom he might be able to get some extra oomph to prevent these people from falling apart. I especially like the points about how being Exalted does <i>not</i> make you transcend native culture, and can actually prove a major liability <b>even within your own culture</b>.<br /> <br /> And finally, in place of the usual sections on prominent individuals and neighbours (the latter of which is a bit redundant when the whole point is that basically all of the neighbours have been invited into the house), there\u2019s a description of the council of leaders that Lukha has surrounded himself with to try and govern this mess. First off I just want to say that I like the details given to what functions the council actually performs, since I like anything that helps me to envision the actual functions of a government.<br /> <br /> Ah, of course there\u2019d be another Lunar here; somehow, despite him having been described as a Changing Moon from the very start and my own frequent references to him, imagining Lukha\u2019s isolate has kept me thinking of him as somebody without tattoos, so it helps to solidify that by saying that he\u2019s got one other Lunar sent as a Silver Pact emissary to back him up. I like how, even while Jural Three-Trees has been sufficiently won over by Lukha\u2019s charms that he\u2019s opted to remain and help him out, he maintains a bit of his own agenda concerning service to his shahan-ya (and even one that might incidentally help out the Bronze Tide). Plus the general fun of a Lunar venturing out with the intention of dealing with some big bad, and on the threshold of its lair worrying that it might be more than he can handle.<br /> <br /> It makes sense that there might be a Dragon Blood somewhere in that leadership, but Leja\u2019s story sounds like an effective microcosm of the whole human tragedy underlying this situation. I think her trauma is a compelling element to reinforce the basic humanity of the Exalted, and the description of her nightmares is not only ominous in its own right, but gives an intriguing sense of what the powers of the Fair Folk might be; more than the possibilities of them actually being able to create such changeling creatures, or even assault somebody with such twisting of their dreams, is the idea that when it comes to the raksha, it might be hard to tell which one they\u2019ve done. I\u2019m suddenly struck with a hope that one of their major themes will be uncertainty about what is the reality of a situation; it makes me think of the comic where a raksha confronts that Solar from Whitewall with a prophecy from some of his manikins, and while the Solar dismisses the prophecy as a product of the fae\u2019s narcissism, the noble assures his creatures that the point is that, having heard it, the Solar will be haunted by the possibility that it contains truths.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s mostly getting off track; let\u2019s see if any of these councillors are mortal. Yes, Sufek the bard looks like a very useful addition; somebody more stable and native to help Lukha navigate unfamiliar matters of state, as well as being a propagandist who can work on the subject of keeping the people together and countermanding threats to Lukha\u2019s actions and authority at the end of a pen rather than a spear. I know I keep harping on the book\u2019s portrayal of soft power, but it\u2019s a subject that became of interest to me in the game\u2019s interim period, and I\u2019ve been really glad with how this one has been emphasizing it.<br /> <br /> And an elderly strategist Parav, to round out youthful fervour with some practiced caution, to help keep the Tide from overstretching itself, while also benefiting from a lifetime of contacts across the membership if this new coalition.<br /> <br /> Ah, I had actually misread my little peak ahead, there is still a reference to some of the Bronze Tide\u2019s neighbours. There\u2019s a description of one of the city-states of the Cinder Isle, Argidos, that is in the path for conquest, desperately seeking allies and finding none going because it has a history of rapacious warfare itself and using mercenaries hired from one of the former states of the Tide against its neighbours, and they\u2019re happy to leave it to their mercies. It\u2019s a short description, but I find something very sad about it, just from the picture I\u2019m getting of a once proud and confident edifice being left in absolute terror for its future, something that\u2019s hard not to at least get a twinge from my sympathies. Mind, it also seems like ripe territory for a desperation breeding willingness to treat with some darker powers.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a pair of literally connected islands, Melanthes and Ipera, presenting a further complication for the policies of the new coalition, as they\u2019ve historically had cordial and dynastic ties to one of the nations, who may prove unable to protect the old allies from the pressures and needs of the new one.<br /> <br /> Okay, yeah, I should have expected that the neighbours section would provide some of the details on the Cinder Isles that are dealing with the Bronze Tide. Next is Tenai, one that managed to effectively fight off the Tide\u2019s assault, albeit with great human cost and the creation of a shadowland, left in the unenviable position of trying to get their lives back in order following that ordeal, remaining terrified that the invaders might come back for them, and if I\u2019m reading correctly, distracted from the fact that an invasion force of Fair Folk is still on the move, and might be now closer to them than the Bronze Tide is.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s the island Sayfar, home to the capital of an empire among the Isle that has alternately been able to stand against the Bronze Tide, and been fractured a fair bit by some of their possessions using the opportunity to rebel, only for the new invader to sweep them up. They also have an interesting local mythology and ecstatic religious practices in an affinity for the sea. I like these ones for presenting the idea that the Bronze Tide aren\u2019t the only game in town, even if they\u2019re currently acting at a bit of a disadvantage.<br /> <br /> And finally, a sidebar covering some of the nature of Spear-Empress Bhadri herself, and the court that accompanies her. Bhadri is relayed as a creature of violence and an unrelenting hunt, given such iconography as the power to summon legions from the earth, having a pet bird that mutilates the souls of fallen enemies, and a spear of ash and sapphire to cause those it\u2019s cast at to wither. She\u2019s referred to as having twelve companions, of which we get descriptions for two; Zalak of the Wave-Cutter Chariot, who rides a mare of living fog wields a triple-bladed daiklave of ivory and pearl that summons sea monsters, and is inherently fickle, capricious and given to bouts of wanderlust that can even distract her from pursuing the Bronze Tide, held to the course by a bound oath of service from Bhadri having beaten her in a duel; and Gelyb the Song of Fire, a poet-blacksmith driven by a wish to burn away ugliness and impurity, a creature of envy and vainglory paradoxically matched with a meticulousness in pursuit of his actions (which to him are a craft), who creates the camps for his fellows at rest by singing up great buildings from cold fire and fragrant smoke, and incinerates ships with fists wreathed in crimson fire.<br /> <br /> Okay, so this picture of the raksha nobles is <b>super</b> exciting, on a few fronts. For one thing, the pattern in the descriptions; that a noble consists of an iconic pursuit in its existence, around which it has a characteristic power and panoply, utilizing metaphorical or broadly applied aesthetics, so you can give them visually distinctive and very unusual expressions while still being tied to a coherent idea. Of the three, I think Gelyb\u2019s is the most expressive of this, while Zalak\u2019s has the most flair. Then there\u2019s the implications of how they relate to one another, which sounds like it\u2019s going to consolidate and streamline a lot of the old shaping combat functions down to the basic idea of \u201craksha can have interpersonal conflicts from which they wring binding oaths to determine their hierarchy\u201d. Both of those together feel like they\u2019re being presented as things the raksha would have in place of a genuine personality or real inner life. And finally the sense that the force assaulting the states of the Bronze Tide is not really an army as such, but just twelve nobles (albeit possibly among the stronger of their kind); armies are employed, but they seem likely to mostly be the conjurations of several of the nobles involved. If they can pursue this idea to a full expression, with some mechanics that might live up to it (reminding that I need to look back at the raksha in Adversaries), I think it might make the Fair Folk the most interesting and threatening that they\u2019ve ever been, and ticking a lot of the boxes that I\u2019ve always wanted from and struggled to fit even their best mechanics to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Bronze Tide has kind of shot up there for being one of the most interesting Dominions yet. On the front concerning the Lunars specifically, it hits a number of good marks; showing an activity taking place in a sphere far removed from and unconcerned with the Realm, showing the big endeavours of a much younger Lunar so that Dominions don\u2019t feel proprietary to ones at least a few centuries old, and really feeling like it\u2019s being managed by the Lunar in a way that plays to their strengths besides subterfuge and manipulation. As a society in its own right, the Bronze Tide is immensely compelling as this huge, messy bloc of human activity being forced to respond to a crisis really unique to the setting, which is effectively balancing an understandable drive with some really horrific methods. It does a very good job of making the group feel genuinely multi-faceted and struggling to deal with the problems of that, which also helps to make the element of simple human society and interaction feel like a challenge worthy of the Exalted, <u>even while it\u2019s in the shadow of a major supernatural threat</u>. And there\u2019s real pathos to the way that, on the face of it, success and victory for the Bronze Tide comes at the expense of the peoples of the Cinder Isles. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, next Artifact up is Penumbra Gleam, and it\u2019s nice to see another Thunderbolt Shield, and I\u2019ll be interested to see a four-dot one that doesn\u2019t have a world inside of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Heh, it\u2019s deliciously fitting that, after my encounter with the praiseworthy raksha facing the Bronze Tide, the story behind this Artifact should open with another description within the same pattern; Maja of the Starling Song, driven by a pursuit of martial perfection, in possession of a magic looking-glass in which to refine her technique, and whose precise method in combat resembles a dance, with the added benefit of hubris in giving herself a title challenging the Sun.<br /> <br /> Or rather, she was, before a group of young Lunars cleverly stole her glass away and fashioned it into a shield that could reflect all her failings and mistakes, in the face of which her ego was broken and she submitted. Setting aside the mystical implications of it, that\u2019s just really cool as a story for how the Exalted might deal with supernatural enemies, particularly the raksha.<br /> <br /> So the end result is a mirrored shield in which the flaws of those it reflects are revealed, not discounting the wielder, leading to a practice of granting it to younger Lunars who need to be taught a lesson. I\u2019ve not yet had an opportunity to comment on the manner in which several of the Artifacts have been referred to as serving a cause in the community of the Silver Pact, but it\u2019s been a through line I\u2019ve enjoyed, both for the sense of methods for them influencing and instructing one another, and for a bit more detail for the processes and benefits of their intercourse.<br /> <br /> Huh, interesting that the shield\u2019s first power is not based on it being used as a shield, but something to train in front of. The mechanical expression of that method for correcting one\u2019s own flaws is very interesting; use it to make Instil actions against oneself to erode Intimacies of pride or bravado or create and strengthen ones representing humility or frustration with oneself, to generate a resource called <i>Reflection</i>, which can be spent to reroll failures on dice for Melee attacks or to make full defence actions, with resonant wielders getting a higher pool of Reflection to hold. This is making me excited to see the scope of this Artifact, as I really like the idea of such a flavourful powerset that is also extremely subtle in its methods and purposes.<br /> <br /> Ah, of course there would be powers based on using the corrective reflections to undermine or confuse enemies while wielding it as a shield. I really like the resonant effects in these, for making the severity of various effects depending on how far below Parry an enemy\u2019s hit roll was, just to drive home the point about them being assailed with their own failings. Heh, I find it particularly in the spirit of Penumbra Gleam\u2019s raksha roots for it to be not entirely honest about the flaws it reflect back, in the power to weaken even successful hits based on flaws in the initial attack.<br /> <br /> Still, it\u2019s a four-dot Artifact, the occasional overt manifestation wouldn\u2019t go amiss. As this level goes, being able to create a kind of distorted image effect of various defensive manoeuvres is still fairly low-key, and I like how it allows Reflections to be used as a fuel for improving defence. That an enemy can spend Willpower to overcome the effect seems reasonable as a balancing factor for what is technically a die adder is dependent largely on spending something other than motes that could be stockpiled before a fight, although with that in mind I actually feel as though Silver Phantom Phalanx\u2019s actual mote cost may be a bit too high. Unless I\u2019m misremembering something about the dice cap rules for static values, the fact that the bonuses to Parry for using this aren\u2019t non-Charm makes me feel as though the five motes it costs would be better spent on just your regular Excellency, for a bonus that can\u2019t be dispelled by spending Willpower, and saving on a resource that can have valuable use elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the more I think about this, the more I feel as though you\u2019d be a lot better served by reserving that Reflection for the power that can remove damage dice, rather than use it for a Parry die adder that is still fairly mote expensive and requires you to be Resonant and take a full defence action for enemies to not be able to ignore. But like I\u2019ve said elsewhere, I\u2019m not the best to assess these things.<br /> <br /> And finally the expected power to respond to an enemy\u2019s attack with a reflection of them doing it, which can turn damage back on themselves. I quite like some of the mechanics in this one, such as being able to use an enemy\u2019s own Initiative as the basis of the decisive clash attack, the capacity to use Reflection to add dice as if to say that the mirror is not merely reflecting the attack, but correcting its shortcomings, and what I think is a not <i>too</i> expensive Reflection cost to copy the enemy\u2019s attack-enhancing magic.<br /> <br /> You know, it\u2019s super weird that several of the three-dot Artifacts went to Essence 4 and both of the four-dots go only to 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is another very enjoyable Artifact, from a nice origin story over to some very evocative powers that don\u2019t need to be all gimmicky visual flair. It\u2019s always nice to see Thunderbolt Shields find interesting ways to elaborate on defensive applications as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T05:32:15-07:00","id":1295541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1295305#post1295305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that is less than ideal. Sorry for your suffering</div> </div> </div> </div>Believe you me, on any occasion in which I find myself up for the entirety of the night and keep going past the dawn, it's not from the inability to sleep, but having neglected to do so. Hell, I would have gone to sleep then were it not for the fact that I found myself on a day in which there were errands and engagements. I did manage to find a couple of hours in the afternoon for a good nap, but even before that I didn't find myself drained or fatigued while going about my business.<br /> <br /> My problem isn't with insomnia, but an excess of distractions and alertness making sleep frequently a thing I have to consciously elect for (on which I'll drop off completely in about fifteen minutes). It's only whenever there's something actually important that I'll need to be sure to wake up early and fully energized for that my body puts its foot down and starts creating an overpowering sense of tiredness against which a capacity to stay up is both futile and unwanted.<br /> <br /> So the main thing about all of this is in having had an especially big diversion to keep my attention. Really, my main problem with having been up all of that night was a sense of disappointment more than anything physical. I wanted to assert my self-control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T07:47:50-07:00","id":1295557,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been thinking that using the Bronze Tide as a lure to bait Bhadri into attacking Faxai and then letting Sha\u2019a Oka\u2019s army take down the winner feels like an appropriately Lunar method of fighting as well as being a fairly epic task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T08:14:50-07:00","id":1295561,"title":"","content":"So, I think it's interesting the Cinder Coast made you think of the South China Sea or Indian Ocean. The names made me think, actually, of Greece and the pre-Roman Mediterranean.<br /> (Though of course it's near An-Teng.)<br /> <br /> But saying that, I think this kind of island-city intrigue and jockeying over trade is maybe something they both share, that the old West set-up didn't really do a ton (it did a bit). Pirates of Polynesia was a good, but different, kind of genre, as you mentioned. One reason I was glad to see the Dreaming Sea was that I thought rival Empires around a small-ish sea was something Exalted lacked.<br /> The Cinder Coast is, I think, somewhat between the West and the Dreaming Sea, so is a useful part of the setting.<br /> <br /> I also liked having a refugee horde, just because that was what happened with the original &quot;barbarians&quot; who invaded(/were invited to) Rome. The Vandals and Goths coming from inland down to the Mediterranean, being pushed by those behind them.<br /> <br /> I have to say as well, I thought of the Cinder Coast as, well, a coast, and was quite surprised to read about all these countries inland. But of course, on the map, there is actually a huge section south-east of the Cinder Coast, it just doesn't have anything marked on it. I guess I kind of thought of it as just the hinterland of the coastal states, but there's no particular reason it couldn't have it's own thing going on (or at least, it did. Now it's full of Raksha I guess).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T16:28:22-07:00","id":1295683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1295561#post1295561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I think it's interesting the Cinder Coast made you think of the South China Sea or Indian Ocean. The names made me think, actually, of Greece and the pre-Roman Mediterranean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like many elements of Exalted, it would be rather syncretic. The parts that say that to me are the cultural diversity and the importance of ocean channels, but the Hellenistic Mediterranean is probably found in things like the ship design, the use of bronze and the diversity of warring states... plus some of the particulars of how much of a culture you can pack onto an island. Let's say it strikes me a bit as what you would get if you merged those geographic and historical zones together.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the ones I'm talking about are really interesting and don't get enough attention in my media or general world view, so I'll take any excuse to absorb and apply more information about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Though of course it's near An-Teng.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that you could fit the entire Blessed Isle in the distance separating the Cinder Isles from An-Teng.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also liked having a refugee horde, just because that was what happened with the original &quot;barbarians&quot; who invaded(/were invited to) Rome. The Vandals and Goths coming from inland down to the Mediterranean, being pushed by those behind them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And were probably being pushed by other people that were even further east.<br /> <br /> Huh; I wonder if it says something about the power dynamics of the modern age that strong polities formed east early and kept generating migrations towards the west. On the other hand, Islam, Buddhism and Hinduism effectively expanded east and had major defining effects on the societies they encountered, so it's probably more of a continuous interchange that could have gone either way, and perhaps in the next few decades that pendulum is going to swing back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say as well, I thought of the Cinder Coast as, well, a coast, and was quite surprised to read about all these countries inland.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is an island but a coast that doesn't have any continent to back it up, and yet look at how many countries Britain has hosted, now and throughout its history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But of course, on the map, there is actually a huge section south-east of the Cinder Coast, it just doesn't have anything marked on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just there; the narrowest section of the southwestern map is still about six or seven hundred miles long, and about a third of that is coloured green. You could put something like Turkmenistan, Uzbekistan, Tajikistan and Kyrgzstan comfortably in there, and put Kazakhstan and Afghanistan to either side rather than above or below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there's no particular reason it couldn't have it's own thing going on (or at least, it did. Now it's full of Raksha I guess).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there might literally just be twelve Raksha nobles going around there, maybe each with a retinue of about a few dozen commoners. I think the armies are put back in their toybox when not in use, and the depopulated land they leave behind readily has the Wyld flow into it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T16:48:36-07:00","id":1295689,"title":"","content":"All right, finally up to the last of the full Dominion write-ups, Sunken Luthe. The description of Leviathan already did a lot to improve my interest in this place, so I\u2019m excited to see what a dedicated description of its nature and people can bring.<br /> <br /> <br /> That opening description is nice and focused in its brevity, not spending too much time elaborating on the concept on it having been a city that sank, and making clear that the place has mostly been drowned out. The fact that it hangs on the edge of a precipice adds a nice bit of native tension, to keep the city from feeling like a place that could comfortably opt to sit out Creation\u2019s conflicts entirely.<br /> <br /> Luthe\u2019s population is going to be one of the oddest of any Dominion, so it\u2019s a good idea to dive right in to the nature and history of the people. I have a vague sense that the past depictions made the city more habitable to people lacking mutations, so when there\u2019s supposed to be a lot less available real estate for them, and intermarriage has left only a few dedicated holdouts, I\u2019ve got to wonder at the psychological state of those people. Just think about it; numerous generations without access to the sun. They\u2019ve got to be kind of weird. On the beastfolk side, I\u2019m hoping it will drop some of the caste distinctions that were around previously, they always felt a bit much. The fact that the city has become a destination for immigrants provides a bit of insight into a vibrant undersea social network.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a description of how Leviathan has been around, but having always been a very distant figure the immigrant population needed to develop their own process for government, the Luthian Council; what was originally an ad hoc body to allow multiple clans to leave together in peace that evolved into a formal legislative parliament. By no means a democratic system, mind, with councillors choosing their own successors; the closest thing they get is when a very large majority of the citizens vote for the removal of a member, and even then it\u2019s the other councillors who get to select and vote on their replacement, so it sounds like a very concentrated form of power. It mentions how that was the means for otherwise outside candidate Blood-Dimmed Deep to get in, although the biggest thing I\u2019m wondering is how and why Leviathan found the time to sire a daughter, considering he spends virtually all of his time swimming around as a big dolphin, unless she\u2019s supposed to be <i>really</i> old, or\u2026 a shapeshifting orca.<br /> <br /> Ah, but in contrast to a few of the other Lunars who try to maintain mutual respect with surrounding governing bodies (and even with Raksi\u2019s outright autocracy), that Leviathan is back in the game and looking to use the city as a war Dominion presents problems for the council, as despite his nominal respect his stature is sufficient that he can merely issue commands and the people and authorities feel obligated to comply (that his daughter is on the council to curtail their complaints and resistance can\u2019t help). Given how Leviathan was described before, I\u2019ve got to imagine that a lot of this is a simple matter of his lack of social grace.<br /> <br /> Luthe\u2019s condition creates some unique bases for its cultural development that are good to explore. Their cosmopolitan nature and safety relative to their surroundings is said to allow them to form a very elaborate artistic oeuvre, to the point that the majority of people engage in at least some level of creative output, of which apparently one of the most popular themes is coming up with elaborate ways to depict the city having sunk (leading me to picture a trend in which people try to outdo one another with how overwrought and extreme they can make it while still keeping in good taste). Religion is an element that is influenced by the nature of Luthe from before it fell; it was earlier given the title \u201cCity of a Thousand Gods\u201d, which is elaborated on here by the point that, in addition to bringing and cross-pollinating their ancestral gods and the guardian deity of Leviathan, the people have taken to the gods depicted in the native sunken temples, and I\u2019ve got to wonder what any of those gods think about receiving such an extra source of prayer.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a description of their cuisine favouring raw fish (as well as aquatic plants), and I\u2019m suddenly imagining Luthe and its people as having a resemblance to Zora\u2019s Domain in Breath of the Wild, just because that game gave them a very good aesthetic which I think would be a good place to start from. Then there are a few points about Luthian value and craft materials: how they have little care for silver or gems as units of exchange, instead mostly using a system of credit and debit referencing a defunct ancient currency called the deben, and that they place great value in trade for materials hard to manufacture underwater, with glass being the favoured substance in weapons, corrodible metals disregarded entirely, and jewellery consisting of shell, sea ivory and precious stones, with the addition of gold for the wealthiest. There are notes on some particular concessions in everyday life for their underwater existence, such as how writing is used by carving into plates of gold and lead, as well as seashell writing and whale bone scrimshaw; I\u2019m guessing that the metals are for more official documentation, and the more mundane, readily available stuff are for personal notes and references, and maybe more transitory documents like receipts. The people can\u2019t get much use out of clothing, so they basically go by Barsoom rules by sticking to bags and belts from which to hang personal items. It\u2019s said that the new war footing has led to a transformation of the economy to focus heavily on creation of things like weapons and armour, but I\u2019m curious about the description of the funding coming from a major deben infusion by Leviathan; considering the deben being described as a largely fiat currency and that Leviathan has been in virtual isolation for a thousand years, it kind of sounds like he\u2019s basically devaluing the currency be decree. Either that or he\u2019s got some source of trade goods he\u2019s been holding out on for centuries that he\u2019s suddenly made available for liquidation, but I feel as though even that would dramatically affect the deben\u2019s value. I don\u2019t know, on the face of it, it sounds like a rather crude method for financing armament supply, but something in the wording of \u201cvast outpourings\u201d leaves me wondering if that\u2019s actually supposed to be the intent, that Leviathan\u2019s fixation is harmful to the city in the long run.<br /> <br /> Okay, with those points about how the undersea culture works out of the way, it gets into a description of the actual layout of the city, starting with a point on how Leviathan personally lacks the talents or interests to restore its shattered form (having no sense of value for its more cultural treasures in the face of warring with the Realm), and hence much of its current nature is the result of embellishments provided by the newer aquatic inhabitants.<br /> <br /> First off is the Drowned Quarter, starting off on the amusing note that, by the standards of the aquatic inhabitants, intact buildings are held in lower esteem, with features such as doorways and corridors being restrictive to swimming (further recalling some Zora aesthetics, although their city is not located underwater) and staircases derided as worthless, leaving them to be relegated as slum areas, while others get to luxuriate in spaces that provide privacy and security while being more accommodating to their natural lifestyles. It\u2019s a nice way of making the environment and its inhabitants a bit more alien. Added to this is the description of their own building materials and methods, using local varieties of what sound like particularly large varieties of kelp and coral to bind breaking walls together to form versatile pods, from which necessary extensions are simply grown. There\u2019s a nice point about how the choice between the building materials is largely aesthetic, with kelp regarded as cosier and coral as sturdier and more colourful, which helps get one into the mindset of the inhabitants and feel their basic humanity. There\u2019s some helpful elaboration on their infrastructure, not just on how some indoor underwater illumination is provided by phosphorescent algae, but of the parameters for coral tunnels connecting structures that does double duty in giving a greater sense of the population; spaces that need to be made large enough to accommodate whalefolk, as well as some that are so narrow that only flexible cephalopod people and the diminutive \u201ctetrafolk\u201d (who have a major municipal function as the general maintainers of their constructions) can generally get through them. I\u2019m not quite sure what to make of the tetrafolk, so I\u2019ll need to see if there\u2019s anything in the suffix to make sense of it later. We\u2019re finally told about the central structure of the Palace of the Luthian Council, a huge structure of red coral that also functions as the home of the city\u2019s main police force and standing army, the Siaka Guard (although I\u2019m guessing they\u2019re not literally all sharkfolk) commanded by Blood-Dimmed Deep.<br /> <br /> Ah, now here\u2019s something particularly relevant to my interests; about a year ago, I asked the developers if living underwater would be presented as imposing an impediment to speech, inspired as I was by one of the Flat Earth books in which such people are depicted as needing to using magical ear pieces to hear one another, so I\u2019m very happy to see the point that the common language of Luthe is a form of sign language (another thing I considered in that query, and which I also really like as an image), in addition to more exotic forms such as people derived from cetaceans having a forms of speech, a few using controlled bioluminescence, and I would personally imagine that some with cephalopod features would be able to use controlled skin colouring for it. It\u2019s a really nice way to make the people feel more adapted to their environment, both in the sense of it shaping them into something distinct, and in the use of ingenuity to overcome its limitations. And some of the implications to it\u2026 it\u2019s got to really have an impact on oratory, considering that sign language doesn\u2019t quite project the way that a voice would be able to. There are probably a few interesting workarounds one could come up with for that.<br /> <br /> Next is the Sunken Hall, the remains of the meeting hall of the old city\u2019s priest-kings found in the centre of the city, which has been appropriated as a meeting place for Lunars of the Silver Pact. We\u2019re told one of the assets in the possession of the Western Lunars, a rather valuable sounding Artifact map of the Western ocean that can track the movement of fleets (even if it depicts them across outdated features), and to offset some of his more withdrawn qualities we\u2019re informed of how Leviathan personally attends every meeting of his adherents and councils of his fellow shahan-yas (presumably needing to compress from his giant orca form), although still generally of an attitude of domineering pronouncements. It also says that members of the Luthian Council occasionally get invitations to meet with Leviathan or adherents for discussion of matters of city politics (I guess that, on occasions where the citizenry vote out members, he might have thoughts on who the council should nominate as replacements) and the grand strategy against the Realm, with him favouring Blood-Dimmed Deep in this function. I like the point about how part of the basis for that is her being his daughter, since it gives him some extra-warmth, and that the relationship between the two is complicated by her wish to start making war openly faced with growing frustration at his reservation; that seems to be a bit of a recurring theme with Leviathan, either his reputation or familial ties drawing a lot of people into his orbit, where they find his underlying personality very difficult to deal with.<br /> <br /> Okay, going to try and compress the next few of these locales. Ooh, the description of the temple district having been constructed to resemble a map of Creation sounds really cool as an endeavour of artistry, spirituality and civil engineering; it sounds like there\u2019s the mildest callback to some of Leviathan\u2019s Second Edition personality in the note that he defiled the temples to the Elemental Dragons in his rage at the Usurpation. I\u2019m always glad for descriptions of the people\u2019s religious rites, and I\u2019m happy to see another instance of the recurring intriguing notion of people maintaining rites for gods that have died off, it\u2019s just a really nice personable sense of Creation\u2019s growing diminishment. Likewise towards another depiction of Lunars viewing their patron in religious terms, and I like how there\u2019s a unique tension to the priesthood that attends the temple to Luna actually disliking Leviathan owing to his treatment of their order\u2019s founder. If any part of the city was most appropriate to sit on the edge of that abyss, this would be it. While it might be that on other occasions I would gripe about the idea that characters believing the slow collapse was due to natural causes is a misconception, and it\u2019s actually a result of the Wyld is at the bottom of the fissure, on this occasion I\u2019ve got enough general good will, a basis for seeing it as a logical necessity, and the general love of the new raksha that plays nicely off of the idea that they\u2019re pulling temples in to feed off of the echoes of prayer within them, to be willing to set such enmity aside.<br /> <br /> Heh, I like the reference to Mesoamerican sacred ball games in the original function of the Poet\u2019s Court, and I\u2019m really happy to see even a brief exploration of how their distinct language affects their cultural expressions. I particularly like the idea that they would supplement the experience of watching a form of poetry based in sign language and body movements with drugs to induce synaesthesia; it gives me a sense that the only time people are liable to ever \u201chear\u201d anything is when they\u2019re watching a poet\u2019s hands flash through verse, and their brains are translating that into a sensation of sound. It makes me think it would be interesting to have an exchange between a Luthe native and a surface dweller (including some Lunar immigrants adjusting to life in the city) on the superior art form, as I\u2019m imagining dedicated underwater poets decrying speech as a limited and inferior expression to the combination of their own language with an appropriately high audience.<br /> <br /> And there\u2019s finally a reference to how the inhabitants who still need air (whether to live or, in the case of some Lunar crafters, practice their works) get by. It\u2019s mostly just a point on how even some of the aquatic inhabitants, such as those derived from mammals, need to stop in for air sometimes, that there are luxury quarters for those Lunars who\u2019d prefer to stay in their true forms (which I have a sense belies a typical Luthian derision for such people), and some of the variety in methods for actually providing and purifying such air, from sophisticated artifice to stale old filters for the poorer inhabitants. Come to think of it, I actually wonder if remaining separate from the beastfolk in Luthe conveys wealth, for such people to be capable of funding the necessary infrastructure of their survival; it\u2019s not elaborated here, so I guess it depends on whether or not one would assume that such people are maintained by government subsidy. Yes, I can see two ways to go about that; one in which municipal obligation devotes resources to maintain their survival, provoking griping from the general citizenry on how their tax debens go to preserve folks of limited productivity who refuse to integrate, or else that between old money status and being able to engage in some industries limited in the rest of the populace, they\u2019re distinctly wealthy and able to maintain their own necessities. I wouldn\u2019t imagine the air-breathing population is large enough to incorporate both.<br /> <br /> Last of the described districts are the Outposts, which are more properly Luthe\u2019s surrounding townlands to help provide it with necessary resources, as well as homes for the poor and iconoclastic. We\u2019re given a picture of the integrity of the Siaka Guard by the fact that their patrol priorities are determined by the availability of bribes. Mind, it may be that their system of finance is not exactly formally developed, so it might be that bribery is just an integral function of how they\u2019re kept in the black.<br /> <br /> All right, the Prominent Figures list is giving us one last picture of Blood-Dimmed Deep\u2026 who I had not been cognisant enough to realise that she would be an orcawoman; between that and the point about how he\u2019ll meet with his adherents in person, I guess that solves the mystery of where she came from. But there are more important things than that, she\u2019s a power player! Oh hey, that desire to not be defined by her father is actually a theme of her write-up, makes sense. I like the idea, for herself and elsewhere, that having such authority in a key location of the Silver Pact and being the Moon-Touched of a very powerful member makes her basically a member of the Pact, and the fact that she actually isn\u2019t means the Lunars don\u2019t exactly listen to her. I\u2019d almost want to play a Lunar who would share her viewpoints just to get some things going. Or hey, give her a connection to Sha\u2019a Oka, that should create some drama.<br /> <br /> Nice to see a genderfluid character included in the mix. The description of their anglerfish features sounds familiar to me, I wonder if we\u2019d had beastfolk like that Inanja before, or if it\u2019s just similar to one of the Pole mutant peoples of Autochthonia. Still, they sound good, and I imagine the luminescent hair makes for very good displays at poetry jams. I also like the idea that the best time and place to meet Leviathan is when he turns up to listen to somebody\u2019s poetry.<br /> <br /> Ah good, final nail in the coffin for Leviathan the Dragon Blood eater by having one active in Luthe\u2019s society\u2026 oh hey, quite the contrary from him actively defending Gevan Batahul from some more overzealous adherents. I actually find something adorable in the idea that he (and by extension, much of Luthe\u2019s population) doesn\u2019t\u2026 wait, how can he never have heard of the Realm, who does he think that the city is being put on a war footing for? Okay, setting that aside, I think it makes for an interesting character to have a kind of amoral businessman and lawyer in this environment (particularly to help along the industry for arming the city), makes me think of him as a kind of underwater Morland Holmes.<br /> <br /> Oooh, a First Age ghost hanging around. She\u2019s described as having been one of the priest-kings, so I really want Lady Forever-Drowning to have not been Exalted when alive. I thought the idea of the people worshipping at the alters and idols of forgotten gods was really cool as it was, so the idea that those rites have been enabled by the ghost of one of their original administrators (for which she herself is venerated) is just a nice cherry on top. <br /> <br /> Okay, finish off with the neighbours, starting with an allied spirit court, the Hollow Court. Hmm, the leader has the title of Storm Father (Halid) and is referred to as a storm mother, so I wonder what the implications of that are. Still, that aside, seems quite sensible that Leviathan would associate with some gods to assault Realm shipping with storms, and the payment in sacrificed sailors founds very Death\u2019s Master. Oh what, now you choose to be a censor Fakharu? Yeah, I\u2019m sure you\u2019ll be wrathful right up until the point when they give you a cut. What about the ghosts of Galbadan? The overall character of that settlement sounds fairly standard, but the image of an underwater haunted city consisting of a ship graveyard is a pretty cool addition to underwater society.<br /> <br /> With Luthe\u2019s background, it sounds like a very interesting point of contact to have a cousin society consisting of land-dwelling refugees from the city. Heh, considering the history of the Realm\u2019s expansion, it must have been fun times to come across this island and discover that their mythology despises the Dragon Blooded; makes me think that Dolaron was subjugated more on principle than because it had much of value to offer.<br /> <br /> Aaaand a little point to touch off the history of the Niobraran League, and a first hint at the nature of the Spoken; apparently they were big. Obsidian sounds like a good counterweight to Luthe\u2019s place in undersea society, and I enjoy how there\u2019s a big source of weird lore for people to form religious beliefs around that is unrelated to the Old Realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And that\u2019s it. Luthe is another one that I think has updated well, effectively coming across as alien. Even if it\u2019s not a place in which to set whole stories (should people not be able to manage the difficulties of the underwater setting), I\u2019d say it at least makes for a very compelling backdrop for any stories in which Lunars or other potential allies against the Realm come to petition Leviathan or seek to attend council.<br /> <br /> Right, good, finished, aaaaand there\u2019s still the Caul left to do. I miscounted the men Liz! I\u2019ll get to it a bit later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Back up with another suit of armour, this time a big ol\u2019 suit of full plate by the name of Seven Furies Caged.<br /> <br /> <br /> The origin story of this one sounds very reminiscent of one of the armours in the core, but being forged in the middle of the heedless battle out of moonsilver to encase an angry Lunar will convey some very different lessons. I often wonder at the origins for malevolent Artifacts, so it\u2019s interesting to see one that was made with the best of intentions but under circumstances that inclined it towards something horrific. Heh, of course the thing would be spiky, although the main thing I like in the appearance is the idea of it having broken bits of sword and bone embedded from enemies in the course of being forged. Nice to see an instance of interchange between wildly different factions of Lunars.<br /> <br /> Oooh, where would it go from increasing its protection based on how badly injured the wearer is? Let\u2019s see, using wound penalties as bonus dice to go into battle\u2026 an enhancement for the as yet unseen Relentless Lunar Fury (makes complete sense for the theme)\u2026 extra power for attacking people that have managed to hurt you\u2026at Blood Moon Ascendant, I feel as though I\u2019m not going to be able to fully appreciate this without having seen Relentless Lunar Fury, but I\u2019m getting the general idea of stoking rage from growing injury and the offence of successful foes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, this looks good overall, but it\u2019s not got anything that really jumps out at me, and I think I need to look at it again when I\u2019ve seen the Stamina Charms. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T18:17:43-07:00","id":1295704,"title":"","content":"They did a special update with the Realm section on the Caul. You may want to read that before going into the Lunar writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T19:22:21-07:00","id":1295719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1295704#post1295704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did a special update with the Realm section on the Caul. You may want to read that before going into the Lunar writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div>What?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T19:48:30-07:00","id":1295723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1295719#post1295719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the Kickstarter updates (the March 4th update, specifically) is an excerpt from <i>The Realm</i>, specifically its section on the Caul. BrilliantRain is suggesting you read that before you read the <i>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate</i> section on the Caul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T20:02:33-07:00","id":1295726,"title":"","content":"I would note, the Luthe section very very much suggests that Leviathan's long period of seclusion was much more &quot;swimming around as a whale god, indulging in some investment, and taking in the occasional poetry slam at the poet's circle,&quot; as opposed to &quot;swimming around as a whale god and napping on his throne holding his trident, but otherwise, never doing anything.&quot;<br /> <br /> Leviathan seems to have been the distant protector of the city, a symbol that the people looked up at and saw, who gradually got more and more attached to this weird city that kind of grew up around him and started to become more and more of a part of it.<br /> <br /> Though my favorite bit was, far from being her Father's voice on the Council, Blood-Dimmed Deeps is in active OPPOSITE of Leviathan, and wants to go hardcore balls to the walls &quot;DEATH TO THE SURFACE!&quot; style war. Which both her father and the silver pact oppose. Much like you, my first impression of him having a daughter on the council was, &quot;Oh, she's his voice to the Council,&quot; but no, she seems to entirely be her own person. XD<br /> <br /> It's perfect and I love it.<br /> <br /> I think of it as New York that just happens to be Underwater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T20:58:22-07:00","id":1295732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1295723#post1295723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the Kickstarter updates (the March 4th update, specifically) is an excerpt from <i>The Realm</i>, specifically its section on the Caul. BrilliantRain is suggesting you read that before you read the <i>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate</i> section on the Caul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it different from the section released during the last Kickstarter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T21:06:25-07:00","id":1295733,"title":"","content":"It occurred to me when imagining a new Lunar arrival being introduced to folks, that strictly speaking common Luthian shouldn't have pronounceable words, since it includes no aural component.<br /> <br /> My resolution to this is that the written form consists of characters employed in ancient times, and while trying to pronounce things like sentences by articulating the sounds those characters represent will usually produce nonsense, common convention is that the spoken pronunciation of a person's name is an acceptable substitute if ever dealing with somebody who speaks (although an extended engagement will have most prefer you to at least sign their name).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T21:23:02-07:00","id":1295736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1295732#post1295732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it different from the section released during the last Kickstarter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here you go:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2432121\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2432121</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T21:35:51-07:00","id":1295739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1295732#post1295732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it different from the section released during the last Kickstarter?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was much longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T02:29:20-07:00","id":1295748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1287173-isator-levi-reads-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1295736#post1295736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here you go:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2432121\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2432121</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I would have found it unnecessary to read something that is not actually in Fangs at the Gate in any case, particularly considering how much I already have piling on top of me.<br /> <br /> A